window.AKK_THE_LITTLE_DARLING_WIFE_WHO_IS_A_DIVINE_DOCTOR_SAVED_THE_ENTIRE_FAMILY_OF_THE_DUKES_MANSION_CHAPTERS=(window.AKK_THE_LITTLE_DARLING_WIFE_WHO_IS_A_DIVINE_DOCTOR_SAVED_THE_ENTIRE_FAMILY_OF_THE_DUKES_MANSION_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":201,"title":"Chapter 201: An Ignorant bumpkin.","paragraphs":["After all, these things could all be made into various pretty jewelry.","After haggling with Henry for a while, He Zhiran bought these gems for eight hundred taels of silver.","Henry never imagined that He Zhiran would be so wealthy and generous.","So he took the initiative to market the small mirrors and telescopes.","\"He Zhiran, these are my most precious things, won't you consider them?\"","He Zhiran didn't even think about it and refused directly: \"I'm not interested in those.\"","Seeing that the other party really refused, Henry simply stopped marketing.","At the same time, he also identified He Zhiran as an uncultured country bumpkin.","He Zhiran didn't care what others thought at all. She directly handed over several boxes containing gems to Mo Jiuye, and then urged Henry to go inquire about the prices of glass and other items.","In the end, He Zhiran bought a small amount of glass, a small amount of plastic cloth, potatoes, sweet potatoes and some crop seeds from Henry, spending another 150 taels.","It was said to be a small amount, but it looked like quite a lot.","If transported by ox cart, at least five carts would be fully loaded.","Henry asked with great concern: \"He Zhiran, have you figured out how to transport these things?\"","\"It's figured out. I plan to rent a warehouse near the dock and move them there when your ship is repaired and docked.\"","He Zhiran had just finished speaking when everyone felt like the cargo ship seemed to have moved.","At the same time, Henry's companion also excitedly ran over: \"Henry, that master is very powerful and repaired the ship so quickly!\"","\"That's great, notify down that the cargo ship will dock immediately!\" After Henry finished speaking, he urged Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran onto the deck.","Hu Cong had already stood there first, waiting for Henry to pay him.","Henry was very excited. Seeing Hu Cong, he wanted to enthusiastically give him a hug.","But as soon as he opened his arms after getting close to Hu Cong, Hu Cong dodged away.","\"The ship is fixed, the fee is ten taels of silver,\" Hu Cong said with a straight face.","Henry awkwardly turned his head to look at He Zhiran and asked her to help translate what Hu Cong had said.","He Zhiran told him that Hu Cong was asking him for ten taels of silver for his labor.","Now Henry was even more embarrassed.","He had just arrived and hadn't sold any goods yet. He Zhiran hadn't paid for the goods either. He simply couldn't afford Hu Cong's fee.","He Zhiran also saw his predicament and said, \"Go ashore with me first to get some silver.\"","She also explained it to Hu Cong for a while. At this time, the cargo ship had been steadily docked at the pier.","With the ship docked, they didn't need to take a small boat and went directly ashore.","He Zhiran immediately dove into the carriage. When she lifted the carriage curtain again, a thousand taels of shiny silver appeared before everyone.","She was also very thoughtful to introduce Henry that these silver ingots were ten taels each, with a total of one hundred in front of them.","Henry directly picked up two silver ingots and gave them to Hu Cong.","Hu Cong only took one.","\"I only accept due compensation,\" it was evident that he was absolutely strict in his work.","This time, without He Zhiran's translation, Henry also understood Hu Cong's meaning.","He simply put the other ingot back.","After getting his payment, Hu Cong did not leave in a hurry.","Having met someone he could chat with for a few sentences, he had earned silver today and felt like treating them.","He Zhiran and Mo Jiuye did not know Hu Cong's thoughts, thinking that he was going to leave with them.","What the two of them had to do now was to rent a warehouse at the dock.","With Hu Cong's help, they soon rented a medium-sized warehouse for one tael of silver for three days.","Immediately afterwards, Mo Jiuye also hired several workers at the dock to help move the goods He Zhiran had purchased.","Hu Cong had originally wanted to treat the Mo couple to a meal, but seeing that they had purchased these items from the foreigners and still didn't know the exact quantity, with so many things still to be moved to who knows when, it was obvious that his treat was unlikely today.","After watching the workers move goods to and from the warehouse several times, Hu Cong bid farewell.","\"Master Mo, since you still have things to do here, I won't disturb you. If we have time another day, we can make an appointment to go drink.\"","Mo Jiuye clasped his fist: \"I live in Xiling Village on the westernmost side of Yuncheng. Brother Hu, if you have anything, you can come and find me there.\"","After Hu Cong agreed, he left.","This was just right. Hu Cong saw them buying these items from the foreigners but didn't know the exact quantity.","A solid witness...","He Zhiran could sneakily add items to the warehouse without any pressure.","In order to save time, Mo Jiuye had hired more than 20 workers.","In less than half an hour, the goods they had purchased from Henry were all moved into the warehouse.","Before locking the door, He Zhiran placed the large amount of glass, tiles, plastic cloth, and various grains, potatoes, sweet potatoes, fresh corn and other items she had purchased from Taobao and produced from her space inside.","With Tang Mingrui joining the doll business, it also made a small profit. He Zhiran took this opportunity to purchase large quantities of plush fabric again.","In addition, considering the seasonal issues, He Zhiran could not take out fresh fruits to show people, so she processed those fruits into various dried fruits and stored them here.","At the same time, she put all the gems in Mo Jiuye's arms into her space.","After taking care of these and seeing that nothing was missing, Mo Jiuye locked the warehouse door.","Henry knew he was about to leave this place. He tentatively said to He Zhiran, \"Miss He Zhiran, I plan to set off early tomorrow to head to the next city of Dashun. Can you continue to help me translate?\"","He Zhiran shook her head: \"I'm sorry, Henry, I can't leave with you. I still have a lot of family members here who need me.\"","Although Henry already knew the answer, he was still reluctant.","\"But without you, I simply can't communicate with the people of Dashun here.\"","He Zhiran could understand Henry's helpless feeling.","She pondered and said, \"Wait for me for a moment.\"","After speaking, she went into the carriage.","He Zhiran purchased some thick xuan paper and writing brushes and ink on Taobao.","She cut the xuan paper into 20 cm square pieces, thought about it, and wrote down some common English phrases, labeling them with the corresponding Chinese characters.","When Henry wanted to say something, he could show these cards to the other person.","After receiving these handmade translation cards from He Zhiran, Henry was so moved he almost cried.","\"He Zhiran, I'm so grateful to you. With these translation cards, I won't have to worry about communicating with the people of Dashun.\"","He Zhiran humbly said: \"It was nothing.\"","Henry didn't know how to repay He Zhiran. He had originally wanted to give her some silver as payment.","But he had already seen that she clearly didn't lack these things.","Seeing that He Zhiran hadn't purchased those beautiful fabrics he brought, he ordered his companions to take some over to give her.","He Zhiran also did not stand on ceremony, and placed the fabrics in the carriage.","\"Henry, I'm very happy to meet you. We have to go back now. My home is in Xiling Village. If we have another chance, let's meet again.\"","\"Alright. If I have a chance to come back here, I will definitely come to see you.\"","Out of habit, Henry was about to step forward to give He Zhiran a hug, only to be deterred again by Mo Jiuye's unfriendly gaze.","This also made it clear to him that the people of Dashun did not like hugs..."]},{"number":202,"title":"Chapter 202: Why did you Buy so many things","paragraphs":["It was getting late, He Zhiran and Mo Jiuye were driving a mule cart back to Xi Ling Village.","Along the way, He Zhiran was busy the whole time.","Having found a real foreign backpacker, how could she miss such an opportunity?","She entered her space and processed some more dried fruits, packing them neatly with oiled paper.","Potatoes, sweet potatoes and tender corn from the space, a sack full of each.","There were also some vegetables that were easy to store, like onions, pumpkins and so on, she prepared some of each type.","Of course, her favorite chili peppers were a must. Fresh ones would be hard to explain, so she took the dried ones. In any case, having the spicy taste was better than not having it.","Looking further away at the cattle, sheep, and fat pigs in the ranch, they had been fully grown for a long time, and the poultry had also bred many next and next-next generations.","Seeing the increasing number of living creatures in the ranch and breeding grounds, overcrowding had occurred.","He Zhiran operated the control panel and started slaughtering chickens and sheep, even the various kinds of fish in the ponds did not escape.","To save trouble in the future, He Zhiran directly operated and removed the bones and segmented the various meats, and cleaned all the fish thoroughly.","In addition, there were also chicken eggs, duck eggs, goose eggs, 100 of each type were prepared, if not for considering the capacity of the carriage, she could have prepared more.","Although there was no snow yet in the northwest, the outside temperature was already very low.","She believed that bringing these things back and storing them outside would be completely fine.","Therefore, she did not need to worry too much about not being able eat them all.","He Zhiran prepared all the items to be taken home, and took them out from the space using her mind.","She knew clearly that the amount of things prepared was large.","Therefore, after Mo Jiuye sat down beside her, she got out from the carriage and took out the prepared supplies bit by bit.","The things He Zhiran prepared filled the entire carriage, it could be said that there was almost no gap left in the carriage.","Even so, each of them was still holding a basket of eggs in their arms...","With so many more things suddenly added in the carriage, plus two live people, the mule obviously had a very hard time walking.","Luckily they had arrived at the village entrance, He Zhiran and Mo Jiuye simply jumped off the carriage and led the mule back.","They first passed the residence of the Cui clan. It was obviously very quiet there, they did not dare to go out and walk around casually without the order of the county magistrate.","On the contrary, the Zhao and Zhou families seemed much more active now without the suppression of the Cui family.","After yesterday's events, they had already recognized Mo Jiuye. When they saw the couple, no matter who it was, they would enthusiastically greet them.","The two also politely responded.","From what they saw, the members of the Zhao and Zhou families were very enthusiastic, and did not show any signs of rejecting outsiders.","Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran were even more convinced that choosing to live here was the right decision.","Just as they arrived at their own yard, they heard the voice of Mo Hanyue.","\"Little bunny, don't run, I won't hurt you.\"","As they opened the yard door, they saw Mo Hanyue chasing a rabbit around the yard.","Eighth Sister-in-law was blocking it from the opposite direction.","\"Hanyue, chase it towards me, I can block it.\"","Then, they saw a black shadow seeming to descend from the sky, and grabbed the rabbit by the ears in one go.","For a rabbit, Eighth Brother even used his lightness skill...","\"Eighth Brother, Eighth Sister-in-law, Hanyue, we're back.\" Mo Jiuye greeted.","Seeing them return, Mo Chuhang handed the rabbit to Mo Hanyue and strode over to take the rein from his hand.","\"Ninth younger brother, why were you two gone for so long today?\"","Eighth Sister-in-law also ran over, \"That's right, you two were out for so long, if you didn't come back again, your Eighth Brother would have gone out to look for you.\"","He Zhiran smiled and pulled Eighth Sister-in-law's arm, \"Eighth Sister-in-law, there were many things today, I’ll tell you about it later.\"","There really were quite a lot of things, especially about preparing so many goods, they would have to arrange to transport them home tomorrow.","Eighth Sister-in-law touched He Zhiran’s hands which were somewhat icy cold, \"Ninth Sister-in-Law, go inside and warm up first.\"","According to ancient etiquette, after returning home, they had to greet the elders first, so He Zhiran went to Old Lady Mo’s room first.","At this time, Mo Hanyue also ran over with the little rabbit in her arms to show her.","Seeing the little rabbit, He Zhiran realized that she didn't see Rice Ball.","\"Hanyue, where’s Rice Ball?\"","When Rice Ball was mentioned, Mo Hanyue sighed.","\"Ninth sister-in-law, you don't know, this little guy just likes sticking with you. When you're not around, it runs up the mountain.\"","\"I wanted to stop it at first, but Fifth Elder Brother told me that Rice Ball likes to play in the mountains, and will come back by itself at night.\"","As soon as she finished speaking, they saw a round black and white ball running back to the gate.","Rice Ball rushed towards He Zhiran and hugged her ankles in front of everyone, starting to act coquettishly.","He Zhiran affectionately bent down and picked it up.","\"Rice Ball, where did you go play today?\"","\"Mmm... mmm...\" Rice Ball rubbed against He Zhiran, also making comfortable sounds.","He Zhiran knew that the little guy was acting coquettishly with her, so she cuddled and tossed it up and down in her arms.","Whether it was because the little guy was too tired, after tossing it a few times, it fell asleep.","He Zhiran simply carried it along to Old Lady Mo's room.","Hearing the voices, the other sisters-in-law also rushed over.","Since everyone was here, He Zhiran carefully told them what happened today.","In the yard, Mo Chuhang was completely stunned the moment he lifted the carriage curtain.","\"Ninth younger brother, why did you buy so many things?\"","\"Eighth Brother, many of these things were bought from the foreigner, as well as the seafood bought from the fishermen. The meat was bought at the market...\"","At this moment, Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran were doing the same thing.","He also told Eighth Brother about what happened today.","While talking, they unloaded the goods from the carriage and sent them directly to the storeroom in the backyard.","At this time, after listening to He Zhiran's account, the sisters-in-law also prepared to go see the fresh food she talked about.","Mo Hanyue hugged the little rabbit, while He Zhiran simply let her take care of Rice Ball as well, and took Old Lady Mo and the sisters-in-law to the backyard storeroom.","The evenings were much colder than the daytime this season.","At this moment, as they came out from the warm room, they couldn’t help but shiver.","Second Sister-in-law couldn’t help but say, \"The weather in the Northwest is really cold enough.\"","He Zhiran also felt very cold.","What does one eat in cold weather?","Hot pot, of course.","She had been here for several months already, and still had not eaten delicious hot pot.","Today they brought back tender beef and mutton, just right to enjoy.","When the ladies arrived at the storeroom and saw so much food piled up, they were extremely surprised and delighted.","Even when they were at the Duke's mansion, the storeroom had never been stocked with so many delicious things."]},{"number":203,"title":"Chapter 203: The man is quick on his feet.","paragraphs":["Just now, Ninth Sister-in-Law said that much of the food they brought back today was bought from the foreigners, and they were all things the sisters-in-law had never seen before.","Seeing so many delicious ingredients, the gluttonous Eighth Sister-in-Law was the most enthusiastic.","\"Ninth Sister-in-Law, tell us what we should make for dinner tonight. Let's get started right away.\"","Old Lady Mo also agreed with Eighth Sister-in-Law's words: \"Yes, let [He Zhiran] and Ninth Sister-in-Law decide the menu. You all can help them prepare.\"","She had already seen that this ninth daughter-in-law was skilled at whatever she did.","If the task was left to the other sisters-in-law, such good ingredients would likely end up wasted.","According to [He Zhiran]'s understanding, hot pot had not yet become popular during this period. Of course she would not leave the preparation of this novel dish that no one had tried before to anyone else.","[He Zhiran] first went into the storage room, and picked out some suitable beef, mutton, pork, chicken and some offal.","The offal had already been cleaned in her personal space. Currently they only needed to cut the ingredients into pieces.","[He Zhiran] did not need to do this herself. She could leave this task to her sisters-in-law.","Although there were many ingredients to prepare, there were also many sisters-in-law. With everyone pitching in, it did not take long to get the ingredients ready.","The only green vegetable suitable for hot pot right now was cabbage, which happened to be [He Zhiran]'s favorite.","Especially when the cooked cabbage had absorbed the red oil - dipping it into the tasty sauces was simply a delightful experience.","The potatoes and sweet potatoes they brought back today could also be used as ingredients. This would let the family try these two kinds of produce.","After handing over the tasks to her sisters-in-law, [He Zhiran] took out the seafood she had bought from the fishermen's village earlier.","Lobsters were not suitable for hot pot, but shrimp were perfectly fine and tasted great too.","Therefore, [He Zhiran] divided the shrimp into two portions. One was for the hot pot, the other for cooking Sichuan style sautéed shrimp.","As for the lobsters, she kept a few for tonight’s meal, and put the rest into her personal space to preserve freshness.","As a side dish to go with the hot pot, [He Zhiran] felt there was no need to make things too complicated. Hence, she decided to steam garlic lobster.","After getting all the ingredients ready, she deliberately walked into the carriage compartment in full view of everyone.","Pretending to rummage through the storage cabinet inside, her consciousness had already entered her personal space.","She opened Taobao Treasure Trove and purchased a large jar of sesame paste, scallion flower sauce and fermented tofu.","Then she quickly changed the packaging of these seasonings to match this ancient time period.","In truth, there were many options for hot pot dipping sauces, like the seafood sauce, fragrant oil and oyster sauce she often had in her past life.","The reason why [He Zhiran] chose sesame dipping sauce was mainly because she considered that these could all be produced locally.","For instance, as long as there were sesame seeds and a small grinding stone, sesame paste would be easy for her to make.","Scallion flower sauce was also easy to explain. Scallions were already available in this period, and farming families were familiar with scallion flowers too.","The only reason they didn’t make scallion flower sauce was likely because salt was too expensive then to waste in this manner.","As for fermented tofu, it would be more troublesome, but once they could make tofu, fermented tofu would not be far off.","Additionally, [He Zhiran] had another motive.","She wanted to test the palatability of these seasonings to the people of this time.","If they were well-received, it could become a money-making business for the family in the future.","Of course, that was something for the days to come. She was just making some preparations in advance.","[Mo Jiuye] was carrying firewood from the backyard with Eighth Brother when he saw [He Zhiran] emerge from the carriage holding several bottles and jars of differing sizes.","[Mo Jiuye] quickly put down the firewood and strode over.","He knew these were just his wife's tricks to hide her abilities.","In front of Eighth Brother, he deliberately exclaimed, \"Oh how forgetful I am, I actually forgot there were still things inside the storage cabinet.\"","As he spoke, he had already taken the items from [He Zhiran]'s arms.","[He Zhiran] secretly laughed to herself: This man's reactions are really quick.","She played along and said, \"I didn't see these things in the storage room just now, so I guessed you must have forgotten them in the carriage.\"","They had to admit, this brief exchange between husband and wife completely eliminated [Mo Chuhan]'s suspicions.","When he first saw Ninth Sister-in-Law emerge from the carriage holding those items, [Mo Chuhan] had wondered how there could still be things inside when the carriage had already been emptied.","So those were the things kept in the storage cabinet.","They were probably more strange goods bought from the foreigners.","The other sisters-in-law witnessed their conversation as well, and had the same thoughts as [Mo Chuhan]. Everyone still believed these were odd items Ninth Brother and Sister-in-Law had purchased from the foreigners.","[Mo Jiuye] directly brought those seasonings to the kitchen, while [He Zhiran] found a container to mix the sesame dipping sauce.","The ingredients prepared by the sisters-in-law were also ready. Eldest Sister-in-Law came to ask what the next step was.","Naturally, the next step was to lay the food on the table and start cooking in the hot pot.","But this question left [He Zhiran] momentarily stunned.","She had only considered what to eat, and did not think about the current situation of the household.","They had only just moved into this rented courtyard last night. Other than some cookware purchased en route and their luggage, they did not even have chairs for people to sit on, let alone dining tables.","Thinking of all this, [He Zhiran] was instantly furious with herself.","The ingredients were prepared but they had neither dining tables nor charcoal stove.","[He Zhiran]'s troubled expression did not escape [Mo Jiuye]'s notice.","In his perspective, Ranran was a clever girl who never seemed troubled over anything before.","Something major must have happened.","[Mo Jiuye] walked over anxiously with a tense look on his face, grasped [He Zhiran]'s hand and pulled her out of the kitchen.","Only when they reached a corner did he ask, \"Ranran, what's the matter?\"","[He Zhiran] was led away by [Mo Jiuye] with an urgent demeanor, and thought something had gone awry.","She assumed he would say something after bringing her to this corner.","But instead, he was the one asking what had happened to her...","What could possibly have happened? It was just a slip-up on her part!","But on second thoughts, this was no small matter either.","Everyone had been busy for so long preparing the ingredients, but now she had to inform them about a change in tonight's dinner plans.","[He Zhiran] felt she truly could not bring herself to say those words.","Seeing that she still gave no reply, the anxiety and tension [Mo Jiuye] felt grew stronger.","\"Ranran, tell me quickly, what exactly is the matter?\"","Faced with that impatient expression, [He Zhiran] shrugged and said,","\"It's about tonight's dinner.\"","[Mo Jiuye] looked puzzled. \"Dinner? Wasn't preparation going smoothly?\"","\"Oh dear, you don't know - hot pot requires at least a charcoal stove, plus tables and chairs. And we have none of those.\"","She really had been negligent in forgetting to purchase some furniture when they went out this morning.","Although [Mo Jiuye] did not quite understand why the meal Ranran spoke of absolutely needed tables, chairs and a stove, these were not difficult issues for him to resolve."]},{"number":204,"title":"Chapter 204: We eight brothers and sisters eat the old habit again.","paragraphs":["“This is no problem. I can go to the clan chief for help and ask him to help borrow some tables and chairs from the villagers,” Mo Jiuye said confidently.","Mo Jiuye was not speaking nonsense based purely on imagination. When he was leading troops in battle, he also had a lot of contact with the common people. Those country folk living in poverty would often make charcoal themselves and then sell it to wealthy city households to make a living.","Moreover, when following the two clan chiefs to look at houses yesterday, Mo Jiuye noticed that several villagers had simple charcoal kilns in their yards. This was proof that there must be charcoal here.","Upon hearing his words, the worried frown on He Zhiran's pretty face immediately relaxed.","\"Mo Jiuye, you're so smart. How could I not have thought of that?\"","Seeing her smile, Mo Jiuye indulgently patted her on the head.","\"Alright, be good and wait at home. I'll take care of this.\"","After speaking, Mo Jiuye went out of the yard.","With the problem resolved, He Zhiran returned to the kitchen to continue working.","This time, she was making garlic steamed lobster and spicy pepper shrimp herself.","The sisters-in-law were seeing these ingredients for the first time. At first, they were somewhat afraid when they saw the big lobster.","Unexpectedly, the young sister-in-law cleaved it in half with one stroke of the knife...","He Zhiran completely ignored the surprised expressions of her sisters-in-law and busied herself with head lowered.","The garlic paste was prepared by He Zhiran when the sisters-in-law were busy, as was the sauce for the pepper shrimp.","She skillfully spread the garlic paste evenly over the lobster before putting it into the pot.","Right after, He Zhiran went to another stove in front of everyone and started stir-frying the pepper shrimp.","In no time, the rich, spicy aroma spread out, even drifting through the door cracks farther away.","Eighth Sister-in-Law took a deep sniff.","\"Although I don't know what dishes Little Sister-in-Law is making, the smell alone has already whetted my appetite.\"","Second Sister-in-Law joked, \"Look, Eighth Sister-in-Law's gluttonous tendencies are acting up again.\"","Immediately, everyone burst into loud laughter...","Just as the two seafood dishes had just come out of the pots, the sound of footsteps came from the gate.","He Zhiran went out with the sisters-in-law to take a look.","They saw Mo Jiuye walking in front, working with a villager. The two were carrying a large round table.","Behind them were several other villagers, each holding two chairs.","Walking last was Zhou Clan Chief.","Old Zhou Clan Chief held a bag of charcoal in his hands instead of carrying tables and chairs.","Before they even entered the yard, Zhou Clan Chief couldn't help but ask, \"Old Nine, what delicious food is being cooked in your home? It smells even better than restaurant dishes in the city!\"","Mo Jiuye also knew a little.","\"Hehe...it should be dishes my wife made with spiny lobster and mantis shrimp.\"","\"Spiny lobster? Mantis shrimp?\" Zhou Clan Chief was clearly very surprised.","As someone who had lived most of his life in Yun City, how could he possibly not know about seafood?","It was just that these two kinds of seafood held no appeal for them.","If it wasn't because their family really had nothing to eat, no one would go eat things like spiny lobster and mantis shrimp.","Although that was the case, he had eaten them several times during the years of famine when he was young.","Not only were those things hard-shelled, they were prickly to eat. Most importantly, they tasted extremely fishy.","\"That can't be. I've eaten spiny lobster and mantis shrimp before, but they didn't smell like this at all.\"","Mo Jiuye also didn't know how to explain and could only smile it off.","The Zhou Clan members set the table and chairs down in the yard and went to get another set.","Mo Jiuye pulled Zhou Clan Chief along to He Zhiran.","The tables and chairs were borrowed but the charcoal needed to be paid for. He wanted to get money from He Zhiran.","\"Ranran, give twenty coins to Zhou Clan Chief.\"","Although He Zhiran still didn't completely understand commodity prices in this era, she knew in her heart that twenty coins for such a large bag of charcoal was truly very cheap.","The wood used to make charcoal had to be chopped in the mountains, and afterwards was artificially carbonized.","This made He Zhiran think of the poem about the old charcoal man, allowing her to sympathize with their hardships.","Therefore, she directly gave Zhou Clan Chief fifty coins.","When Zhou Clan Chief took the copper coins, his first thought was that his new daughter-in-law understood the ways of the world.","For such a large bag of charcoal, it was exactly fifty coins if sold in the city.","Zhou Clan Chief directly counted out twenty copper coins to pocket, giving the rest back to He Zhiran.","\"Young daughter-in-law, we're all villagers here. I only charge cost price for charcoal.\"","He Zhiran felt distressed about the hardships of the peasants and didn't want him to work for nothing.","\"Zhou Clan Chief, you've put in effort and it's only natural to earn some money. Just keep it!\"","When Zhou Clan Chief saw her trying to give money, he retreated several steps back.","\"Us crop farmers value sincerity. Over so many years, the villagers have always bought charcoal at this price.\"","He hadn't expected the old man to be so stubborn.","Since that was the case, He Zhiran did not insist.","She looked towards Mo Jiuye, \"Husband, since we've come to Xi Ling Village, the two chiefs have helped us a lot. Why don't we invite them over for dinner tonight?\"","Mo Jiuye had also been thinking this. After all, they were going to live here long term in the future so it was very important to get along well with their neighbors.","\"Alright, I'll go invite Zhao Clan Chief over later.\"","Zhou Clan Chief had intended to decline. During such impoverished times, which family had excess to spare? If their own family members had enough to eat, it was already considered very good. If he stayed to eat here, this family would have less to eat.","However, the scents from Mo Family kitchen were too tempting. Also, taking this chance to become better acquainted with the new neighbors wasn't a bad idea either.","Therefore, Zhou Clan Chief did not decline.","\"Since this is the case, this old man will stop being courteous.\"","As his words fell, he took out the twenty copper coins he had just pocketed and gave them all to Mo Jiuye.","\"I can stay and eat dinner here, but I can't accept money for the charcoal.\"","What Zhou Clan Chief was thinking was that Mo Family could use the money to buy some grains. He would be eating one meal here so they surely couldn't suffer losses because of him.","When Mo Jiuye saw Zhou Clan Chief's actions, he found it somewhat funny but also distressing.","He pushed the copper coins back, \"Zhou Clan Chief, does it make sense to charge for dinner? Could it be you look down on Old Mo here?\"","\"No, no, no, I didn't mean that. I only...\"","\"If that's not what you meant, then keep the money,\" Mo Jiuye directly cut him off from explaining and brought Zhou Clan Chief into the main room.","This was the largest room in the entire yard, suitable for putting tables and chairs. They would also choose to eat dinner here.","Old Lady Mo called for the women to carry tables and chairs into the room.","While everyone busied themselves, the previously missing Mo Chuhan had at some unknown point returned with Liang Hao and the others in tow.","The several men all carried game in hand. It was clear from their travel-worn appearances that Liang Hao and the others must have been up in the mountains hunting all day."]},{"number":205,"title":"Chapter 205: Eat Hot Pot","paragraphs":["In addition, the gains were quite substantial.","Six wild chickens, a wild mountain goat, and everyone was holding a live wild rabbit in their arms.","When Patriarch Zhou followed Mo Jiuye to check out the situation, they saw all these hunting spoils in front of them.","The old man couldn't quite believe his eyes and rubbed them forcefully.","Having lived here his whole life, he naturally knew there was game on the mountain.","The hunters from the village would gather and organize trips up the mountain that would last several days.","Even so, it seemed the game they hunted back was not as much as what this Mo family had obtained in one day.","Patriarch Zhou was so envious, he was too envious of the Mo family.","With such great hunting skills, even if the Mo family spent their whole lives as country bumpkins like himself, they would never have to worry about food and clothing in the future.","At the moment, everyone's attention was focused on the game, especially the wild rabbits held in some people's arms, which no one could take their eyes off.","Mo Hanyue simply couldn't resist such cute creatures. At this time, the little girl was smiling from ear to ear.","\"Big Brother Liang Hao, you guys are too amazing to have caught so many little bunnies.\"","Liang Hao grinned foolishly, \"Miss likes them, so we tried our best to catch more to bring back.\"","Mo Hanyue pointed to an empty room to the west. It had already been turned into a place for her to raise Rice Ball and the little white rabbit they just caught.","\"Dear brothers, please first put the wild rabbits in there.\"","When the door opened, Rice Ball immediately bared its teeth at the few men approaching them.","It was as if it was a door god, as long as you dare come near, I will bite you.","Liang Hao and the others all knew this black and white furball was Madam Nine's darling, so of course they had to indulge it.","Liang Hao was the first to make a gesture of surrender, \"Little ancestor, don't bite me. We promise not to go in.\"","Mo Hanyue ran over with an amused smile and picked up Rice Ball to bring it into the room.","\"Rice Ball, they are all our own, don't be so fierce, okay?\"","When facing Mo Hanyue, Rice Ball could only reluctantly tolerate her and did not have the same good attitude as towards He Zhiran.","It was seen wagging its little butt and slid off Mo Hanyue's body, then swaggered away.","This was also considered tacitly approving Mo Hanyue's words.","The few men laughed to themselves, then put the rabbits in the room before closing the door and leaving.","Mo Jiuye saw Eighth Brother had come back and told him to accompany Patriarch Zhou inside to chat while he went to invite Patriarch Zhao over.","Just as he walked to the front door, the Zhou family servants came over again with a large round table and some chairs, plus two braziers.","Everything was ready except for the leading actor. It was time for He Zhiran to make her entrance.","She directed her bewildered family members to place the two braziers in the center of the two tables. Then she fetched two large copper pots from the kitchen that they had bought on their exile journey.","As the copper pots were filled with clear water, she added the hot pot soup base she had purchased from Taobao Treasury.","By this time, Mo Jiuye, who had gone out to invite people, had also returned.","Following him were not only Patriarch Zhao, but also Xie Tianhai and Fang Chuanzhou.","Fifth Sister also helped Fifth Brother over.","Seeing the red-hot braziers and copper pots placed on the tables, everyone was somewhat at a loss.","Especially the few outsiders.","While the Mo family was hospitable in inviting them for a meal, cooking with braziers on the table was a novel way of dining.","The two patriarchs, Zhao and Zhou, were particularly puzzled but did not dare ask out of politeness. They assumed it must be some fancy, modern way of dining practiced by rich noble families in the capital.","If they asked, it would make them seem unsophisticated country bumpkins...","Eventually it was Xie Tianhai who voiced what everyone was wondering.","\"Nephew Jiuye, what are you having us eat?\"","Mo Jiuye smiled.","\"Uncle Xie, this is a new way of dining my wife came up with called hot pot.\"","Having said that, he went on to usher everyone to their seats, with men at one table and women at the other, perfectly dividing up the space.","Still confused, everyone had just sat down when He Zhiran led a group of women to start bringing up ingredients.","Seeing these ingredients made them even more bewildered.","Before anyone could ask, He Zhiran took the initiative to explain, \"Everyone, this is a new dining method I read about in books. You cook the ingredients in the copper pots and eat them as they simmer.\"","As she spoke, the water mixed with spicy hot pot soup base in the copper pots started boiling. The aromatic smell of numbingly spicy flavor permeated the entire room.","After hearing He Zhiran's explanation and smelling the tantalizing aroma from the pots, some could no longer restrain their eagerness to try this novel way of dining and picked up their chopsticks.","They had picked up their chopsticks but still did not quite know how to eat this hot pot without seeing someone demonstrate first.","Therefore, everyone could only watch Mo Jiuye longingly.","In fact, this was also Mo Jiuye's first time seeing this new dining method. However, as the host he had to \"lead by example.\"","So he used the chopsticks to grab some of the ingredients and put them in the copper pots.","He Zhiran also timely prepared the dipping sauce and distributed it to everyone.","Seeing the water in the pots boiling again, she reminded, \"You can eat now after dipping it in the small bowls of sauce.\"","Everyone followed her instructions to grab some cooked ingredients into their bowls and dip them in the spicy sauce to eat.","As Da Shun did not yet have chili peppers, the tongue-numbing spiciness that hit their throats as soon as they put it in their mouths made several people cough uncontrollably.","After coughing, an tantalizing, rich, and irresistible flavor lingered in their mouths for a long time, making them crave more bites with rising fervor.","Then everyone grabbed more ingredients from the simmering copper pots into their bowls again and wolfed them down with great relish.","Mo Chuhan kept nodding in praise, \"I don't know what spices Sister-in-Law put in the soup, but it's so delicious that I just can't stop.\"","Fang Chuanzhou chimed in in agreement, \"That's right. Having been in the capital for so many years and eaten all kinds of delicacies, nothing can compare to the delightful flavor of this hot pot.\"","Xie Tianhai also laughed, \"With such delectable flavors, it would be even better if there was wine to accompany the meal.\"","Speaking of wine, He Zhiran had really been negligent today. She had prepared so many tasty dishes but had completely forgotten about the wine.","The mule cart supplies were already completely moved out so if she conjured up wine now, it would definitely arouse suspicion.","So for today, she could only let everyone have some slight regrets.","Seeing that everyone had gotten the hang of eating hot pot, He Zhiran called a few sister-in-laws over to help bring out the garlic steamed lobster and spicy shelled shrimp dishes that had been prepared in the kitchen.","Patriarch Zhou was a bit more composed since he had already heard Mo Jiuye mention this stuff when he came over to deliver firewood earlier.","Patriarch Zhao reacted differently. He asked in puzzlement, \"Elder Nine's wife, what is this? The hot pot ingredients are so good and your Mo family doesn't seem short on money. Why make such lip-burning stuff to eat?\"","Out of courtesy, Patriarch Zhao kept the latter words to himself in his mind.","Instead of explaining, He Zhiran directed Mo Jiuye to ask everyone to try some.","She wanted to prove with facts that these seafood they did not regard highly could indeed become irresistibly tasty delicacies in her hands.","And so it was. Bound by propriety, everyone resolutely ate a bite that Mo Jiuye had grabbed for them, only to find, as He Zhiran expected, it made them crave for more bites."]},{"number":206,"title":"Chapter 206: Just stay home and be your mother.","paragraphs":["Especially the two clan chiefs Zhao and Zhou, they were not unfamiliar with these seafoods.","A few years ago, Yun City suffered from drought, which led to much reduced crop yields.","At that time, even if one had money, it was very difficult to buy grain.","Therefore, in desperation, many people could only go to buy those seafoods that people usually didn't like to eat from fishermen to fill their stomachs.","When the seafood was bought back, people were already hungry. Such food was difficult to eat in large bites. It was simply torturous.","What's more, they didn't have the skills like Old Jiu's wife. The seafood they made was sometimes fishy and smelly. It was almost impossible to swallow, and several people even got vomiting and diarrhea from eating seafood...","But it’s different now. These seafoods that they looked down upon, when they got to others’ hands, they could actually be made into such delicious food.","Also those animal internal organs used for hot pot, how could they be so delicious?","They really lived up to being people from the capital city. They were absolutely unambiguous about food and drink, which was not comparable to them country bumpkins.","Chief Zhao ate with a flushed face, and had even forgotten the restraint he should have as a guest.","\"Old Jiu, if you take these foods to the city to sell, you will definitely make a lot of money.\"","Speakers have no intention, listeners have their own intentions.","Chief Zhao didn't lower his voice, so the women could hear it very clearly.","After the second sister-in-law heard that she could make big money, she immediately became interested.","\"Ninth younger sister, what do you think if we go to sell such food in the city?\"","He Zhiran didn’t object to this, but currently the ingredients and seasonings for making hot pot could not be exposed in large quantities.","Moreover, she heard that there weren't many rich people in Yun City. Just talking about these ingredients and seasonings for hot pot, the cost was very high. If the selling price was too low, they certainly couldn't make much money. If the price was too high, I'm afraid not many people could afford it.","So He Zhiran was not in a hurry to run this catering business.","They had just settled at the foot of Xi Ling Village. The first thing they should do was to settle their family first.","Although she didn’t know much about business, after all she had seen many things in her previous life that didn't exist in this era. With the help of space, it wouldn't be difficult for her to find some money-making ways.","Moreover, Tang Mingrui had also come to live in Yun City. After stabilizing, she would come up with a small business to cooperate with him, and develop step by step in this way, so as not to attract too much attention from others.","After all, their identities were special. Even if they had arrived in the place of exile, it was hard to guarantee that no one would pay attention to them in the imperial court.","Not to mention, there was Meng Huaining on the surface. He was entrusted by Fei Nanyu to take office here to take care of their family.","She didn't believe that Meng Huaining wouldn't tell Fei Nanyu about their situation.","Right now, it seemed that Fei Nanyu posed no threat to them, but who could completely guess the mind of people in higher positions?","Therefore, He Zhiran planned to observe carefully before making plans.","Of course, with such a large family right now, it was inappropriate to do nothing. After everyone was settled, she would come up with a win-win idea.","\"Sister-in-law, I know you are in a hurry to make money for our family, but before that, you have to look at the ingredients we used today.\"","He Zhiran knew that the second sister-in-law was straightforward, so she didn't need to beat around the bush when talking to her.","Old Lady Mo, who seldom expressed opinions in front of daughter-in-laws, spoke up.","\"Xie, what your ninth younger sister prepared today, let alone other things, just the spicy seasoning that makes our mouth tingle, we can’t even get it. Without raw materials, how can we talk about making money?\"","After hearing Old Lady Mo's words, He Zhiran had to give the old lady a compliment.","Among all the Mo family's women, Old Lady Mo was the most sensible one. At a glance, she could spot the key issue that made this business impossible to do.","\"Mother is right. The peppers I bought from the foreigners are limited for our own family's consumption. If used for business, I'm afraid the stock would run out in just a few days.”","The second sister-in-law was obviously very disappointed: \"It's such a pity that such a good money-making business can't be done!\"","\"Don't worry, I bought a lot of seeds from foreigners, including chili peppers. Next spring, we plant them on several acres of land. By then, we will have enough chili peppers to use.\"","As soon as the second sister-in-law heard this, she immediately became all smiles.","\"Is it true, ninth younger sister? When the time comes, I will definitely not be lazy and grow a lot of chili peppers.\"","When it came to planting, Mo Hanyue was also interested: \"Sister-in-law, when I was reading the pharmacology books you gave me, I discovered that some medicinal materials are not only easy to cultivate, but also very valuable. I want to go to the city after a while to buy some medicinal seeds to plant medicinal materials next spring. It must be able to increase income for our family. \"","The other sisters-in-law saw that the young auntie had thought of ways to make money for the family, and they were obviously anxious.","But when they were in the capital city, they were all spoiled. Apart from being able to make some embroideries, they had no other skills.","The eldest sister-in-law tentatively asked, \"Younger sister-in-law, we sisters-in-law don't have as much knowledge as you. In the future, whatever money-making business you come up with, just give us a heads up and the eldest sister-in-law will definitely help out.\"","The other sisters-in-law also stated that they meant the same thing as the big sister-in-law.","In short, from now on they would all listen to the ninth younger sister-in-law. If the ninth sister-in-law points to the east, they would definitely not go west.","He Zhiran really liked such an atmosphere. For any matter, everyone in the family should work together towards the same goal.","\"Okay, when I come up with good ways to make money, I will definitely inform my sisters-in-law first.\"","The women chatted without hiding anything from anyone else. Of course the men could hear what they said.","Although the fifth brother had lost his memory, after getting along for these two days, he had completely accepted this group of loving family members.","Hearing that the female family members wanted to make money for the family, he, as the man in the family, had to pitch in willingly.","\"Making money is men's business. You just do housework.\"","Eighth brother also echoed: \"Yeah, with so many grown-up men, even if we go hunting in the mountains every day, we can earn enough for the family's food and clothing. You just need to take care of mother at home.\"","With both elder brothers making themselves clear, Mo Jiuye should have also expressed his stance.","However, he did not do so.","He knew his wife's capabilities. When He Zhiran wanted to make money, their lifelong hunting probably couldn't catch up with her.","Liang Hao even patted his chest and guaranteed: \"From now on, we brothers will take turns hunting in the mountains to ensure that the family can have rice and meat every day.\"","In the eyes of these older people, as long as an ordinary family could eat their fill and dress warmly, it was already a comfortable life.","Especially for Liang Hao and the others, they had been wandering orphans since childhood and had no high demands for quality of life.","It had to be said that the two chiefs Zhao and Zhou were so envious of them.","Just look at them, so confident in what they said. Based on the many prey they brought back from the mountain today, their words were by no means an exaggeration."]},{"number":207,"title":"Chapter 207: Potatoes and Sweet Potatoes","paragraphs":["Especially Zhou Clan Chief, after seeing those hunted preys, he had already roughly calculated their prices.","Speaking of that wild mountain goat alone, if sold to restaurants in the city, it would fetch at least a few taels of silver.","With such an abundant harvest in one day, it was enough for these people to eat their fill, and there would even be some left.","Xie Tianhai and Fang Chuanzhou were also listening enviously.","By now, they had thoroughly accepted the fact of becoming an ordinary commoner. The Mo Family's manpower grew increasingly numerous, and each was highly skilled.","Relying on hunting to support a family in the future would be no problem at all.","Thinking further of their own circumstances then, they were formerly scholar-officials. Even if there were quite some manpower, none was able to go up the mountain for hunting.","It seemed that after they returned, their whole families had to gather together to carefully discuss the problem of their future livelihood.","He Zhiran was listening to the men's discussion without rebutting. She would simply do whatever she ought to do in the future.","Seeing that everyone had just about eaten their fill of meat, she put the sliced potatoes and sweet potatoes into the pot.","These two items were the first time the people present had seen them.","They had wanted to ask what these were when they first saw them, but faced with so many delicacies, they were reluctant to stop their mouths from eating to speak.","Now seeing He Zhiran putting these two foods into the copper pot, they raised their curiosity once more.","For asking this kind of question, the Eighth Sister-in-law as a foodie was most adept.","\"Ninth younger sister-in-law, we cut for half a day in the kitchen just now, and still didn't know what these are.\"","He Zhiran smiled as she explained, \"These were all bought from the Westerners by me. One is called potato, and one called sweet potato.","I also heard that these things not only taste good, but have very high yields too. I kept some seeds, and we can try planting some next year.\"","Upon hearing He Zhiran say that these two foods had high yields, the two clan chiefs were the first unable to keep still.","They had been tilling the soil their whole lives, and there was no news more exciting than the topic of high yields.","Zhou Clan Chief笑着 asked, \"Ninth young household, you said these things have high yields, so just how high could they yield?\"","He Zhiran thought about the sweet potatoes and potatoes planted in her space. She didn't know if it was an issue of cheating, but the yield per mu could reach two thousand jin for potatoes, and even more for sweet potatoes, close to five thousand jin.","To play it safe, she did not report such high numbers.","\"Zhou Clan Chief, according to what that Westerner said, potatoes can yield up to a thousand jin per mu, and sweet potatoes will be more, with at least two thousand jin per mu.\"","As soon as she finished speaking, the two clan chiefs were no longer able to keep their cool and stood up.","\"Ninth young household, is what you said true?\"","Zhao Clan Chief turned red in agitation. They must know that planting crops their whole lives, they had never heard of any crop with such high yields. Could the Ninth young household have been tricked by those Westerners?","He Zhiran also could not boast too much regarding such matters.","\"Hehe... Zhao Clan Chief, whether it can really yield as high as that, we'll have to see after planting them.\"","Zhao Clan Chief nodded and sat back down.","Seeing the Ninth young household's nonchalant manner, she clearly didn't care whether she was being tricked. What was he getting all worked up for?","At the same time, the two clan chiefs also extinguished their original intention to ask for some seeds.","These unknown things, they didn't dare try indeed in case the yields weren't so high after all, that would be an entire year's time wasted in vain.","Their attitude did not impact He Zhiran at all.","Seeing that the potatoes and sweet potatoes in the copper pot had softened from cooking, she urged everyone to have a taste.","This time, her action elicited another round of exclamations.","\"Ninth younger sister-in-law, this sweet potato is sweet and delicious!\" Eighth Sister-in-law ate while smiling and praising.","Even the usually composed Sixth Sister-in-law couldn't help but appraise, \"That's true, these two new snacks do seem rather filling too.\"","The table with the men was similar, as they all vied to praise the potatoes and sweet potatoes for their unique flavor.","Everyone present feasted merrily on the delicacies. They felt that they had never eaten such delicious food in their lives.","When Mo Jiuye saw that everyone had just about eaten their fill, he then asked Zhao and Zhou, the two clan chiefs.","\"Two clan chiefs, may I know if you have any spare land for sale?\"","Zhou Clan Chief raised his brow, \"Ninth lad, you plan to buy land?\"","Zhao Clan Chief echoed, \"True enough, for country folks, tilling land is fundamental.\"","Mo Jiuye nodded, \"We will be living in the village in future, so planting crops is a must.\"","Zhou Clan Chief contemplated briefly.","\"In our Xi Ling Village, if we talk of good land, most are in Cui Manor people's hands. Luckily after being tended these few years, though not comparable to Cui Manor's fertile soil, our family's land had also improved vastly.\"","Mo Jiuye knew his wife's space-produced seeds weren't particular about soil conditions at all. Thus he didn't care if the land was fertile.","\"Land conditions matter not. Good land is nurtured. We can take it slow.\"","At the same time, Xie Tianhai and Fang Chuanzhou also stared at the two clan chiefs.","They shared Mo Jiuye's thoughts. To live in the countryside, they would have to do what country folks ought to.","After exchanging glances, Zhao Clan Chief said,","\"There isn't much farmland in both our families. Only those near the foot of the mountain have been left fallow for years. Such land would take at least three to five years' time before it can be nurtured fertile.\"","The indigenous villagers of Xi Ling Village naturally understood this kind of land. Even if seeded, the harvests wouldn't be great. It was likely they would toil in vain.","Zhao Clan Chief suddenly recalled Cui Manor.","\"Ninth lad, Cui Manor has the most land, far more than their tribesmen can farm.","In the past, relying on Cui Wen's power, they forced our two families to send people over as unpaid labor.","Now that the new fair County prefect is in power, Cui Manor had been punished. I supposed we no longer have to work unpaid at their place. Much of their land would surely be left barren.","When that time comes, Cui Manor people will surely want to sell off their farms. You can then buy fertile land from Cui Manor.\"","That was indeed a good plan. But Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran hoped to own more land, no matter the condition, preferably adjoining parcels.","Whether fertile land or those left barren for years, they wanted them all.","\"The two clan chiefs, no matter the land quality, we hope to buy them.\"","In suggesting that Mo Jiuye buy farmland from Cui Manor, the two clan chiefs actually had no ulterior motives. They were thinking about harmony since they were going to live together in the same village. They didn't want to do anything that would invite criticisms.","What they didn't expect was that even after they had said so much, the other party remained just as determined.","Since that's the case, they shouldn't be blamed for not warning them. When it came to money spent, no one had the right to make demands how it should be used.","Zhou Clan Chief said, \"There are about twenty mu of fallow land at the foot of the mountain in our Zhou family. That area was opened up through land reclamation by our clansmen, and we have the title deed registered officially.","The deeds are still in our hands presently. If you want to buy them, based on the wasteland price back then, it'd be one tael of silver per mu.\""]},{"number":208,"title":"Chapter 208: A Lot of Money for a Fool","paragraphs":["Anyways, those lands have been lying idle, so it's better to sell them at a low price.","When the Zhao Clan Chief saw this, he said, \"The Zhao family also has twenty-six mu of barren land over there. Like the Zhou Family, we'll sell it for one or two taels of silver per mu.\"","Mo Jiuye first looked at Xie Tianhai and Fang Chuanzhou.","After all, they had all come to Xi Ling Village for their own families, so naturally they couldn't fall behind others when there was land being sold.","When Xie Tianhai and Fang Chuanzhou heard that it was land that had been barren for many years with low yields, neither of them were very interested.","They weren't very knowledgeable about farming to begin with. If they went to cultivate land like that, it might end up a fruitless endeavor.","Therefore, the two of them shook their heads at Mo Jiuye at the same time, indicating that they did not want to buy such land.","If possible, they wanted to buy some of the Cui Family's good farmland.","It was just what Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran wanted to hear that the two men did not want to buy the land that had been barren for many years.","They had planned that if possible, they would buy all of the land at the foot of the mountain and build their future house there too.","That way, their family property could be managed together.","Mo Jiuye immediately decided, \"Clan chiefs, I've decided to buy all of that land from you.\"","As soon as his words fell, He Zhiran brought over a large silver ingot, worth a full ten taels.","\"Clan chiefs, this is the down payment for the land. After our family settles down in the next few days, let's go to the yamen to process the land transfer formalities.\"","Such a large ingot of silver yuanbao placed on the table suddenly gave a sense of great wealth.","When the Zhou Clan Chief saw this, he smiled and said, \"Young Lady Mo is really too kind. Just give a little symbolic down payment to show your intentions. After all, we’ll be fellow villagers in the future. How could I not trust you?\"","By now, the two clan chiefs had determined that the Mo family were foolishly wealthy.","Not only did they want all of that land, but they were also so refreshingly willing to take out silver...","He Zhiran would not try to guess their thoughts at this time. She smiled and replied, \"The silver will be given sooner or later. This deposit also shows our sincerity in buying the land.\"","\"Very good, very good. Since this is the case, we will gladly accept it.\"","The Zhou Clan Chief was quite modest and pushed the silver to the Zhao Clan Chief. \"Zhao Clan Chief, you can hold onto the silver first. We’ll divide it after we finish the formalities at the county yamen.\"","The Zhao Clan Chief smiled and responded, \"Okay, I'll arrange it as Elder Zhou says.\"","It could be seen from this that the characters of both clan chiefs were quite good - they were modest and not greedy for money.","Having settled the matter of purchasing the land in their hands, Mo Jiuye then asked, \"Also, I heard that many of the houses we were assigned here originally belonged to your clan members?\"","The Zhao Clan Chief explained about the ownership of those houses.","Mo Jiuye asked again, \"I wonder if those compounds are for sale?\"","Hearing Mo Jiuye's intention that he seemed to want to buy those dilapidated compounds, the two clan chiefs were completely stunned.","\"Young Mo, you want to buy those compounds too?\" Clan Chief Zhou said somewhat incredulously.","You have to know that those compounds were very much an eyesore where they sat. Not to mention they couldn't afford to repair them, the government kept using them to provide rent-free housing for those exiled people.","Although no one could live there long-term, having that kind of thing still felt a little irritating.","Mo Jiuye laughed and said, \"My family likes quiet. I feel it’s more suitable to build houses there.","Also, it's close to the land we bought which makes it convenient to take care.\"","The two clan chiefs both felt that his words made sense.","\"Mm, that idea is not bad. It's just that with so many compounds at the foot of the mountain, have you decided which ones you want to buy?\"","\"If possible, I plan to buy all of them.\" Mo Jiuye's words were completely unambiguous.","\"Buy all of them?\"","The two clan chiefs were shocked by his words again.","If it was one or two compounds, it would have been fine for him to buy them. After all, the Mo family didn't seem to lack people either.","But to buy all of them, what on earth did they need so much space for?","\"Y-Young Mo... You have to know, although those compounds are a little shabby, they’re still much more expensive than buying land. Are you sure you want to buy them all?","Also, the reason we moved away is because it’s hard to avoid harassment by the barbarians there.","Take a look at the houses in our village. No matter how dilapidated, the courtyard walls are all built over ten feet high.","Being far away from the foot of the mountain, there’s a chance to detect barbarians coming and make preparations.","If you build houses at the foot of the mountain, even if the courtyard walls are repaired to be high again, once the barbarians come, you won’t even have time to make defensive preparations.\"","Although the Zhou Clan Chief was extremely eager to turn his family's dilapidated houses into silver, he still felt it necessary to remind them.","Making money was secondary. If the Mo family lived there unsafely, they would feel uneasy even if they took the money.","Mo Jiuye knew that both clan chiefs were kind-hearted people and was very grateful that they could sincerely remind him.","However, he didn’t care about harassment by a few barbarians at all.","As long as there was one man at home, the barbarians would retreat fruitlessly.","He smiled and said, \"I have my own plans for this. If possible, I would like to buy all of the compounds at the foot of the mountain.\"","Not only were the two clan chiefs stunned now, even Mo Chuhan was a little anxious.","Before going up the mountain today, he had specially checked the foot of the mountain.","The dilapidated compounds of various sizes added up to at least twenty.","Had Ninth Brother gone crazy? Was he planning to let each family member live in a separate compound?","\"Ninth Brother?\"","Mo Jiuye knew that Eighth Brother had doubts, but with so many outsiders around at the moment, it wasn’t good to explain too much.","\"Eighth Brother, I'll tell you about it later.\"","Even if Mo Chuhan still had endless doubts, since Ninth Brother had spoken like this, he could only repress them for now.","When Madam Mo saw that her eighth son had objections, she quickly helped Mo Jiuye speak.","\"Chuhan, listen to your Ninth Brother. Our Mo family is currently headed by the He family.\"","Mo Chuhan knew that his Ninth Brother's wife was the head of house.","Ninth Brother was also acting on his sister-in-law's intentions in doing this.","But he just couldn't figure out that with less than twenty people in the whole family, including Liang Hao and the others, what exactly did they want to do with buying so many compounds?","Since the old mother had spoken up for Ninth Brother, it meant that she also supported Ninth Brother and his wife.","Therefore, Mo Chuhan decided to keep silent and watch.","Knowing that he had lost his memory, Fifth Brother decided not to participate in major family decisions until he remembered.","The two clan chiefs had thoroughly discovered that the decision makers in the Mo Family, apart from Young Master Mo Jiuye and his wife, were also that old lady.","Since the heads of the household had this intention, it would seem pretentious if they tried to advise otherwise.","\"Young Mo, the Zhao family has seven compounds at the foot of the mountain, big and small. Let’s look them over first and discuss the price afterward, alright?\"","The Zhou Clan Chief also said, \"Our Zhou family has nine compounds. We’ll do the same and talk again after checking them out.","As for the remaining five, they belong to the Cui family. If you want to buy them, you’ll have to talk it over with the Cui family.\""]},{"number":209,"title":"Chapter 209: A Meal for the guests and Hosts","paragraphs":["Mo Jiuye nodded: \"Okay, there's no rush with the matter of the courtyard, we'll discuss the specifics again after the Cui Family's case is settled.\"","Xie Tianhai and Fang Chuanzhou saw that the Mo Family had bought so much farmland and courtyards in the time it took to have a meal, and they immediately became anxious.","However, when they thought about those tattered courtyards at the foot of the mountain, they really didn't dare to buy them recklessly like the Mo Family to rebuild.","After all, the silver they had was limited. If they bought those dilapidated courtyards at the foot of the mountain to rebuild, it would be like spending twice the amount.","It would be better to ask if the courtyard they were currently living in was for sale, at least they could save some silver to buy farmland.","Since Mo Jiuye had brought up buying houses, they simply asked about it too.","\"Chief Zhao, I wonder if the courtyard we are currently renting is for sale?\"","Chief Zhao replied: \"The courtyard that the Xie family is renting belongs to our family, so I can make the decision. If the price is reasonable, of course it can be sold. As for the courtyard where the Fang family lives, it belongs to our clansmen, so I can't make decisions for others. You'll have to ask them before I can give you an answer.\"","When Xie Tianhai heard that the courtyard they were living in could be sold, he let out a sigh of relief in his heart. At the same time, he asked, \"How much silver do you want for the courtyard we live in?\"","Chief Zhao calculated in his heart and said, \"My courtyard occupies more than one mu of land. I spent a total of twelve taels of silver to buy the land and build the houses back then.","The courtyard is also old now, so I'll sell it to you for twelve taels.\"","Xie Tianhai thought about it. Chief Zhao's courtyard was large enough for his family to live in comfortably. Although twelve taels was not a small amount for their family, it would still be cheaper than rebuilding.","Not only that, they could also avoid the hard work of building the houses.","\"In that case, my Xie family will buy the courtyard.\"","As he finished speaking, Xie Tianhai also took out two broken silver coins from his arms and handed them to Chief Zhao.","\"This is the deposit, keep it safe.\"","Although Second Sister-in-Law didn't know Mo Jiuye's specific purpose for buying so many dilapidated courtyards at the foot of the mountain, she was very clear that every decision made by Mo Jiuye and Lady He was absolutely right.","She sincerely hoped that her father's family would follow Mo's lead and buy houses at the foot of the mountain.","But seeing that her father was already impatient to pay the deposit, even though Second Sister-in-Law was anxious, she didn't think it was appropriate to remind him in front of so many people.","She could only wink desperately at her father, but Xie Tianhai didn't even glance at the women's table.","After winking fruitlessly for half a day, Second Sister-in-Law could only give up...","Mo Jiuye and Lady He were happy to see the Fang and Xie families planning to buy the courtyards they were currently renting.","It wasn't that they were selfish, but that they had already made preliminary plans for the utilization of the land and houses at the foot of the mountain.","If the Xie and Fang families followed their lead and bought land and houses at the foot of the mountain, they would have to adjust their plans again.","It was great that both families were buying houses in the village. Not only would it save them money, it would also make their plans easier.","The sumptuous dinner not only resolved the matter of purchasing land and houses, Mo Family's generous hospitality today also made Chiefs Zhao and Zhou realize Mo Family's capabilities.","In the past, those who were exiled to Xi Ling Village usually didn't have money to bribe Cui Wen, so Cui Wen would deliberately arrange for them to come here to be bullied by his clansmen.","But the Mo Family was different. It wasn't that they didn't have money to bribe Cui Wen, they just disdained to do so.","The same went for the Xie and Fang families. On the surface, they didn't seem to have Mo Family's deep foundation, but families who were able to buy houses and were planning to purchase good farmland surely wouldn't lack the bit of silver required to bribe Cui Wen?","Also, today the Mo Family bought over forty mu of land in one go. And from the looks of it, they seemed to have plans to continue buying good farmland.","It was very obvious that they were planning to become the local tyrants of Xi Ling Village!","In the past, the Cui Family in Xi Ling Village was like local tyrants. Not only did they own so much land that they couldn't even finish planting, they would also ask people from their two clans to provide free labor.","If it had been other reasonable tyrants, they would at least pay ten coins per day for the villagers' help.","Hopefully the Mo Family could become reasonable tyrants. Their clansmen helping out more in the future could also earn some money for household expenses.","Thinking of this, the two chiefs felt that it would be very important to maintain good relations with the Mo Family in the future.","Today's dinner was a very good start.","With this in mind, the two chiefs stood up in tacit understanding, and spoke more politely than before.","\"Young Master Mo, thank you for your hospitality today. If you need help with anything in the future, just say the word. As long as we can do it, we will definitely go all out to help.\"","\"It's getting late, and you've been busy all day, so rest early.\" After he finished speaking, Chief Zhao bid farewell.","Seeing this, Fang Chuanzhou and Xie Tianhai also stood up to express their gratitude to the Mo Family for their hospitality before following the two chiefs to leave.","After sending off the guests, the sisters-in-law worked together to clean up the bowls and chopsticks.","Carrying two empty plates to the kitchen, Gluttonous Eighth Sister-in-Law kept praising today's dinner.","\"Sister-in-Law Mo, I really don't know what's in your brain that allowed you to come up with such a way of eating, bringing raw food directly to the table and cooking it on the spot.","The lamb and beef were tender and delicious. At first, I didn't know how to swallow those smelly organs, but after taking a bite, I couldn't stop eating them.","The sweet potatoes and potatoes were also delicious. I especially liked that texture.","Also, Sister-in-Law Mo, how could you make those hard-shelled things so delicious? When you have time, you must teach me so that I can show off my skills to my Eighth Husband...\"","Eighth Sister-in-Law talked endlessly, saying almost everything in the sisters-in-law's hearts.","Although the other sisters-in-law didn't express it as straightforwardly as Eighth Sister-in-Law, they were thinking the same.","While washing dishes in the kitchen, the sisters-in-law didn't forget to pick up some sweet potatoes and potatoes to observe them, as if they had obtained some incredible treasure.","Seeing the sisters-in-law's interest, Lady He jokingly asked, \"Sisters, is there still room in your stomachs for more food?\"","\"Are you going to feed us something delicious again, Sister-in-Law Mo?\" Second Sister-in-Law patted her round protruding belly and said with a smile, \"Second Sister-in-Law still has room here, but only for delicacies.\"","Second Sister-in-Law's words made everyone laugh.","Everyone said that if there were delicacies, they could still eat a little more.","Seeing this, Lady He directly threw a few sweet potatoes and potatoes into the still burning stove fire.","This kind of stove fire was the most suitable for roasting sweet potatoes and potatoes. The flames were not strong and it would not go out for a while.","Seeing Lady He's actions, the sisters-in-law were immediately shocked.","\"Sister-in-Law Mo, throwing such good food into the stove fire would be a waste!\" Eldest Sister-in-Law held an iron hook in her hand, distressed that those sweet potatoes and potatoes were in the fire. She was about to hook them out of the stove.","Lady He quickly stopped her: \"Eldest Sister-in-Law, I'm also making a delicacy here, I won't waste the food.\""]},{"number":210,"title":"Chapter 210: Please don't Sell them.","paragraphs":["The eldest sister-in-law was still rather puzzled. In her understanding, anything thrown into the stove would eventually be burnt to ashes. How could the ninth younger sister claim to be making delicacies...","The sixth sister-in-law, who was usually the most taciturn, came forward and pulled the utterly confused eldest sister-in-law to the side.","\"Eldest sister-in-law, you have to trust the ninth younger sister. When has she ever done anything she wasn't confident about?\"","\"That's true. The ninth younger sister has always been steady in her actions. I'm overthinking things.\" Somewhat embarrassed, the eldest sister-in-law tossed the iron hook aside and went back to washing dishes.","Mo Jiuye was also kept busy, along with Liang Hao and the others, carrying over borrowed tables and chairs to return to the village.","Mo Chuhan, on the other hand, went to the backyard to prepare the game they had hunted.","He had figured out that while the ninth younger sister at home was no doubt the one in charge, the silver spent was also from her.","Since he had not yet taken up his post at the government office, he planned to go hunting more during this farming off season and exchange the game for silver, which he would then hand over to the ninth younger sister to manage.","As the eldest brother, spending his younger sister's money made him feel awful no matter what. He was unwilling to idle around if he could help out in any way.","Seeing Mo Chuhan walking purposefully toward the empty room after having finished preparing the wild goat and pheasants in the backyard, Mo Hanyue panicked.","\"Eighth brother, the little bunnies are so cute. Please don't sell them,\" she pleaded.","Mo Chuhan did intend to tie up the wild rabbits with rope and deliver them into town tomorrow morning along with the rest of the game to exchange for silver.","In the past, with only one younger sister in the family, he and his brothers would have simply doted on her.","But things had changed. They were no longer some aristocrat living in the capital city, and their sister was no young lady from a prominent household.","They would all have to work hard together to maintain their future livelihood.","\"Hanyue, you're a young lady now. Don't make trouble.\"","Mo Hanyue pouted and stood blocking the door, refusing to let Mo Chuhan enter to get to the rabbits.","\"Eighth brother, even if I have to beg you this one time, please don't sell these rabbits, okay?\"","Seeing his sister relapse into her willful ways, Mo Chuhan could only patiently reason with her.","\"Hanyue, be good. We can't possibly keep these wild rabbits.\"","Mo Hanyue did not understand. \"But they're lively and jumping around. Why can't we keep them?\"","\"Rabbits have formidable teeth. Even caged, they would gnaw through and escape. We might as well sell them for some money, which would be more practical.\"","Mo Chuhan was not just repeating hearsay. When stationed at the border pass, he had hunted some wild rabbits himself, planning to keep them for a while and add something extra to the soldiers' meals when they triumphantly returned.","But in less than two days, the rabbits had all escaped, leaving bite marks all over the place.","Though Mo Hanyue wanted to retort, she knew deep down that her eighth brother must be speaking the truth.","At a loss for words for the moment, she instead began to sob in agitation.","Hearing Mo Hanyue's cries, Old Lady Mo rushed over with the sisters-in-law who had been busy in the kitchen.","They arrived to see Mo Chuhan flusteredly trying to comfort a bawling Mo Hanyue.","Needless to say, everyone present assumed that Mo Chuhan had made Mo Hanyue cry.","\"Husband, don't bully Hanyue,\" the eighth sister-in-law said as she strode over to stand between the two.","Hands on her hips, she looked about ready to fight Mo Chuhan for justice on Mo Hanyue's behalf.","With someone backing her up, Mo Hanyue promptly ceased her crying. She had only been putting on a show anyway, so she stopped as quickly as she had started.","\"Eighth sister-in-law, just look at what eighth brother is doing. He's so cruel to want to sell those cute little bunnies for money.\"","Now everyone understood what the dispute between the siblings was about.","Old Lady Mo and the sisters-in-law were formerly noble ladies who had never so much as lifted a finger, let alone knew anything about keeping wild rabbits.","So they unanimously decided Mo Chuhan was in the wrong.","The third sister-in-law even dramatically fished out five taels of silver from her sleeve and stuffed them straight into Mo Chuhan's hands.","\"Eighth brother, I'm buying all these wild rabbits. Take the silver.\"","How dare he bully their sweetest little sister? Absolutely unacceptable.","While the other sisters-in-law were not as drastic as the third, they too demonstrated their defense of Mo Hanyue.","The only exception was He Zhiran, who did not react like the others.","She already had plans for those wild rabbits upon seeing Mo Hanyue hugging one.","To that end, after seeing Mo Hanyue holding a wild rabbit, she had purchased a hundred baby rabbits in her space and started raising them.","It was the first step in her money-making endeavor without needing to be out and about. She could do it at home.","She knew a little about the nature of rabbits. Truly wild rabbits were indeed difficult to tame, and preventing their escape attempts was virtually impossible.","But the rabbits from her space were different, having been caged since young and already accustomed to such a life that escape was likely the furthest thing from their minds.","What's more, the space-grown rabbits were less prone to illness and easy to keep alive.","She just needed to plant some cabbage and carrots occasionally, then add cornmeal after the autumn harvest. During summer, it was even more convenient with the mountain at their doorstep - she could simply uproot some grass to feed the rabbits.","Additionally, rabbits reached maturity in six months and reproduced swiftly.","Right now was the agricultural off season, so running a small-scale rabbit farm at home was a good idea.","Most importantly, in her hands, rabbits were of immense value beyond imagination.","Their fur could be used to make plush toys - something He Zhiran had planned even while on the road.","In Tang Mingrui's hands, the toy business had thrived phenomenally. If not for the supply shortage on her end, their partnership would have been making money hand over fist.","Moreover, she already had proof from her previous life that rabbit fur plush toys not only sold for higher prices than synthetic fiber plushes, but also looked more appealing.","She was certain that plush toys made from rabbit fur were guaranteed profit with no risk, without having to worry about wear over time either.","As for rabbit meat, the simplest way was to produce chilled rabbit meat for sale, easily doubling or tripling profits.","Even just directly selling the meat by weight was a steady long-term source of income.","Therefore, He Zhiran's plans were sure to generate considerable profits for the family.","Just as Mo Chuhan was at a loss over how to counter the sisters-in-law's endless stream of words, He Zhiran finally spoke.","\"Sisters, Hanyue, I also feel there is no need to keep these wild rabbits.\"","All eyes instantly turned to her as her words fell.","\"Ninth sister-in-law, you agree with eighth brother selling those cute little bunnies too?\" Mo Hanyue asked in a choked voice.","He Zhiran stepped forward to gently pat Mo Hanyue's shoulder and softly said, \"Hanyue, the ninth sister-in-law once read in books that wild rabbits are difficult for us to raise. It would be better to exchange them for money.\""]},{"number":211,"title":"Chapter 211: Can be responsible for raising Rabbits","paragraphs":["The women had always believed He Zhiran's words without doubt.","Seeing that the ninth younger sister had said so, everyone closed their mouths that were criticizing Mo Hanyue.","He Zhiran continued to comfort Mo Hanyue: \"When I came back today I haven't had the chance to tell everyone yet. Not only did I buy some novel items from the foreigners, I also bought a lot of live rabbits.","These rabbits are different from wild rabbits. They have been kept in captivity since they were young, so they won't escape.\"","Speaking, she held Mo Hanyue's hand: \"Tomorrow, Hanyue will have a lot, a lot of rabbits, and those rabbits are snow white, much better looking than wild rabbits.\"","Mo Hanyue was still a child at heart. Hearing what the ninth sister said, she immediately became all smiles.","\"Ninth sister, you didn't lie to Hanyue, did you?\"","\"When has the ninth sister ever lied to you?\" He Zhiran said, pretending to be unhappy.","Now, Mo Hanyue was completely no longer thinking about those wild rabbits.","\"The ninth sister really hasn't lied to me before. I can be responsible for raising rabbits at home from now on.\"","Raising rabbits at home can also be sold for money in the future, and they even have to kill them themselves.","When that time comes, He Zhiran doesn't want Mo Hanyue to come out and stop it like today.","Therefore, she plans to buy some special rabbits for her to raise alone in the warehouse.","For example, the Angora giant rabbit and Mini Lop rabbit.","She really liked these two breeds of rabbits in her past life, the kind of like where you can't take your eyes off them when you see them.","Buying these two rabbits is partly because Mo Hanyue likes them. Of course, if these rabbits can also successfully breed, they can be completely sold as pets to rich people, which would be killing two birds with one stone.","With the whole plan in place, He Zhiran saw that Mo Hanyue had already obediently given way at the door.","Considering Rice Ball was still in the room, He Zhiran decided to push the door open herself.","The moment the door was pushed open, everyone was shocked.","They saw seven wild rabbits lined up neatly against the wall, shivering.","Rice Ball was sitting in front of them somewhat proudly, like a drill instructor, even fiercely patting the ground a few times with his front paws.","Even when someone came in, those wild rabbits didn't dare move a bit.","This scene really shocked everyone.","Mo Hanyue laughed behind her hand.","\"Ninth sister, Rice Ball isn't setting rules for these wild rabbits, is he?\"","\"Uh... it seems that he really is.\"","In He Zhiran's cognition, silly animals like pandas didn't have it in them to do this.","However, the scene in front of her made her have no choice but to believe this was true.","\"Rice Ball, did you line them up?\"","\"Mm hm!\" Rice Ball let out a heavy quadruple sound, answering very crisply.","This action once again drew a sigh from everyone.","Rice Ball looked at those people impatiently for a moment, then turned around and slapped the ground with his fleshy paws at those wild rabbits before hugging his mistress' leg with his round butt.","At the same time, he let out a \"whine whine whine\" cry. Anyone with eyes could see he was acting coquettish.","The women all looked at He Zhiran, hoping Rice Ball would also come act coquettish with them.","Unfortunately, Rice Ball had always ignored their enthusiasm, only getting along well with the ninth young lady.","Mo Chuhan took the opportunity to enter the room and called those sisters-in-law to come help bring those wild rabbits to the backyard.","After the sisters-in-law came back from the backyard, He Zhiran felt it was about time and the roasted sweet potatoes and potatoes in the stove should be cooked. She beckoned the women to come taste them together.","Old Lady Mo ate very full tonight, but somehow, seeing the lively scene of her daughters-in-law, she also wanted to go join in the fun.","She thought this in her heart, so she did it.","He Zhiran peeled the roasted sweet potato she had hooked out with an iron hook and handed it to Old Lady Mo: \"Mother, try this roasted sweet potato, it's very delicious.\"","Old Lady Mo also didn't stand on ceremony. She took the sweet potato, blew on it, then took a bite.","\"Hmm, sweet and sticky, even better than hot pot.\"","Seeing the usually most dignified mother-in-law praise it like this, the others believed this stuff must taste very good. Although their stomachs weren't hungry at all, they still couldn't help swallowing their saliva.","He Zhiran knew they still didn't understand how to eat these roasted sweet potatoes and potatoes, so she demonstrated peeling off the charred skin in front of them one by one.","She handed the peeled sweet potato to Old Lady Mo: \"Mother, try this roasted sweet potato, it's very tasty.\"","Old Lady also didn't stand on ceremony. She took the sweet potato, blew on it, then took a bite.","\"Hmm, sweet and chewy, even more delicious than when boiled.\"","Seeing even the usually most dignified mother-in-law praise it like this, the others were convinced this stuff must be very tasty. Although not hungry at all, they still couldn't help swallowing saliva.","Following He Zhiran’s example, they each went forward to taste it.","For a while, words of praise did not stop ringing in the kitchen.","The baked potatoes were also unique in flavor.","They said it was just a taste, but no one ate less. Now the women were completely stuffed...","Old Lady Mo saw their pathetic state and gently blamed: “Look at yourselves, all born to big families, yet see your bearings. It’s late, go embarrass yourselves in your own rooms.”","The sisters-in-law and Mo Hanyue laughed and responded, then each ran back to their rooms.","He Zhiran was the last to come out of the kitchen. She had just stepped out the threshold with one foot when Mo Jiuye came back with Liang Hao and the others.","Seeing everything at home had already been dealt with, they each returned to their rooms.","Rice Ball naturally had to stick to its owner. Wherever she was, it definitely had to be there too.","He Zhiran indulged the little guy, bringing it with Mo Jiuye into the space.","Since she had already talked about raising rabbits, she had to prepare for it before going to the warehouse tomorrow.","The baby rabbits raised in the space had obviously grown a lot bigger. Estimated by tomorrow morning, they could grow even more.","Even so, if these rabbits were taken out of the space, they probably wouldn’t be fully grown for a few months.","In order for the family to see the income earlier, He Zhiran simply bought another hundred adult rabbits from the built-in mall in the control panel.","Although the price was a bit higher than buying from the Taobao mall, the rabbits here had special physiques, superior in ease of raising and less prone to illness.","Such rabbits could breed quickly in a short period of time. By then, the sisters-in-law and Hanyue wouldn’t have to worry about being bored.","In addition, she also purchased two pairs of adult Angora giant rabbits and two pairs of adult Mini Lop rabbits as planned.","It had to be said, pet rabbits really had an attractive appearance that made people want to hug them as soon as they saw them.","Especially the Angora giant rabbits, which looked at least 20 catties.","With the necessary rabbits purchased, what was left were the cages.","It was unrealistic for so many rabbits running around loose in the warehouse. The foreigners who brought them wouldn't do that either.","Therefore, rabbit cages had to be arranged.","This could also solve the problem of having to find a way to build cages after transporting the rabbits back. Might as well get it done all at once.","He Zhiran selected professional breeding cages sufficient for raising 1000 rabbits in the Taobao mall.","Rabbits breed rapidly, preparations must be made in advance.","Anyway these rabbit cages can be folded up and are very convenient to store."]},{"number":212,"title":"Chapter 212: You can leave this to your mother.","paragraphs":["While the appearance of the rabbit hutch was quite plain and looked like something from this era, there was also that foreigner Backpot Hero there, so they weren't worried at all about drawing criticism.","With the cage bought, Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran busied themselves with the installation.","First they installed five small cages, able to hold twenty young rabbits.","In addition there were ten cages for the adult rabbits, with ten rabbits in each cage.","There were plenty of cages, so for now they would let the adult rabbits squeeze together temporarily to make it easier to transport tomorrow.","Once they were settled in, they could redistribute them then.","As for those pet rabbits, they were a gift He Zhiran intended to give to Mo Hanyue, so of course their cage couldn't be makeshift.","Each pair would have their own cage.","Having witnessed Rice Ball's \"management capabilities\" today, He Zhiran wanted to test it further to see if the little guy really had such skills.","At the moment, Rice Ball was sitting in front of the warehouse door, gnawing on a carrot.","Hearing its owner call, it reluctantly threw aside the carrot and trotted over in front of her.","First it acted cute for a bit, and once it saw its owner smile, the round little fellow then sat up straight, waiting for orders.","\"Rice Ball, can you herd these rabbits into the cages?\"","\"Mm-hmm.\" After four sounds of affirmation, the little guy sprang into action.","One could see it waving its furry little arms, calling out a few times at the rabbits frolicking in the grass.","An astonishing scene occurred.","All the rabbits stopped moving. First they looked warily in the direction of the sound, then they all scrambled like bees into the cages.","While they all went into cages, they were completely disorganized and ignored He Zhiran's plans.","The rabbits paid no attention to age or size - as soon as they saw an open cage, they darted inside, completely mixed up.","Even those few purebred rabbits acted the same way - the huge Angora and a group of bunnies less than a month old were packed in together, not even daring to move a muscle.","This scene thoroughly amused both Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran.","Although Rice Ball hadn't done a great job with this task, at the very least it proved that the little guy did have some skills.","By this time, Rice Ball had already proudly made its way back to He Zhiran, burying its head in her embrace while whimpering a few small bleats, as if requesting a reward.","Such an adorable little creature certainly deserved a reward.","He Zhiran looked at the bamboo grove she had planted - although it hadn't grown very tall yet, it didn't affect the size of the bamboo shoots.","She willed a great many fresh, juicy bamboo shoots to appear - so many they nearly buried Rice Ball's round body.","As one would expect, bamboo shoots were what this kind of animal loved best.","When Rice Ball saw so many fresh, delicious bamboo shoots laid out before it, it instantly forgot about its owner.","The little guy swiftly grabbed a shoot and began happily feasting away.","He Zhiran took the opportunity to use her mind to completely reorganize the rabbits' quarters.","With that task complete, she and Mo Jiuye finally went to wash up and rest in their long-absent big bed.","After being busy the entire day, the young couple truly was exhausted. Not long after lying down in each other's embrace, they fell fast asleep.","The next day, He Zhiran intentionally rose early.","She planned to use the spiny lobsters stored in her spatial dimension to make lobster porridge for her family.","Due to time constraints she didn't plan anything too elaborate - in her former world, just being able to eat a nice big bowl of porridge packed with lobster meat early in the morning would have been sheer luxury.","And the Mo family had by now grown accustomed to frugality. Making some lobster porridge, frying up a few scallion pancakes, adding a refreshing side dish, such a breakfast was both economical and satisfying.","The sisters-in-law had grown used to getting up early to prepare breakfast for the family, so they were quite surprised to find the little ninth sister beating them to it today.","The whole family gradually drifted into the kitchen to lend a hand, and before long they had this special breakfast ready.","Naturally it earned unanimous praise from the family.","After breakfast, Mo Chuhan made to accompany them to the warehouse to transport back the goods they had bought from the foreigners.","In principle, with such a large quantity of goods in the warehouse, having more people along would be a good thing.","But Mo Jiuye didn't plan on bringing his eighth brother. He Zhiran had prepared so many live rabbits yesterday - they couldn't very well keep them outdoors with no real shelter.","Without proper hutches at the ready, they would need to hastily construct a makeshift grass canopy to at least block the wind and rain.","\"Eighth Brother, I'll go into town with Liang Hao and the others. I'll have to trouble you today to hire some men from the village to come build a canopy in the backyard.\"","Mo Chuhan didn't quite follow. \"Ninth Brother, why build a canopy?\"","\"Has Eighth Brother forgotten? We bought so many rabbits from the foreigners yesterday. Naturally we'll need a canopy built.\"","He was somewhat disappointed at not being able to accompany his ninth brother and sister-in-law to haul the goods back, getting a look at the local conditions in town.","Ever since he had relocated to register as a resident of Xiling Village, he still hadn't gone into town to observe the customs and practices.","Especially since he would be working as a county sheriff in a little while, not even being familiar with basic local circumstances here.","But the task his ninth brother spoke of was also important. At present not only had his fifth brother lost his memory, his health hadn't fully recovered either.","In this family currently only he and Ninth Brother were men capable of handling things, so it was reasonable enough for him to take care of these matters.","Just as Mo Chuhan was about to verbally agree, Old Lady Mo walked over.","\"Jiuye, why not bring your eighth brother into town with you. It's just building a canopy, I can handle arranging that.\"","No one in the Mo family would deny the old lady's capabilities.","Hadn't she single-handedly supported that entire Prince's manor in the past? Arranging a simple canopy should be no trouble for her.","But she was getting on in years, and had endured such a long exile - Mo Chuhan couldn't bear to let his old mother continue laboring.","\"Mother, let your son accompany you to speak with the clan elders first. Once they've made arrangements on their end, you'll just need to oversee things a bit with the daughters-in-law.\"","Old Lady Mo knew her caring son didn't wish to tax her unduly.","\"Your mother is still quite hale and hearty, making arrangements is no strain.\"","With the old lady speaking thusly, Mo Chuhan and Mo Jiuye gladly accepted.","Mo Jiuye led Old Lady Mo to the backyard, choosing an appropriate location and detailing the desired size of the canopy.","He Zhiran took the chance to release Rice Ball from her spatial dimension.","She had discovered that the little fellow didn't like solitude - leaving it alone in that space put it in low spirits.","She and Mo Jiuye were going out and couldn't bring it along, so for now they could only leave it temporarily in Mo Hanyue's care.","With household matters seen to, the couple headed out with Mo Chuhan towards the mule cart bound for Yuncheng.","Liang Hao and the rest stealthily followed close on their heels by means of qinggong.","Once the mule cart entered Yuncheng, Mo Chuhan immediately went about arranging to first sell off their hunting spoils.","This perfectly aligned with Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran's intentions.","They could take this chance to first go to the warehouse and release the rabbits they had prepared in advance inside."]},{"number":213,"title":"Chapter 213: Madame Mo also thought of a good way to do both.","paragraphs":["Liang Hao and others were sent by Mo Jiuye to the city to hire ox carts, the more the better.","The mule carts were left to Mo Chuhan, while the husband and wife went on foot towards the direction of the warehouse.","The two tacitly looked at the location of the pier. Henry's big cargo ship had already sailed away, presumably it had already set off yesterday.","Henry's departure was also a huge convenience for Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran.","The items He Zhiran purchased in Taobao Mall had completely no evidence.","Mo Jiuye went forward to open the door of the warehouse, while He Zhiran put the rabbits and prepared cages in the empty space at the fastest speed.","They had just finished tidying up here when Mo Chuhan drove the mule carts over.","The moment he entered the warehouse, Mo Chuhan was completely stunned.","Not to mention how many goods were stacked in the warehouse, how much silver did the ninth brother and sister have in their hands!","They actually bought a warehouse full of stuff.","I'm afraid the goods of that cargo ship were all bought by the two of them...","The two had already anticipated what the eighth brother's reaction would be like when he saw these things.","Mo Jiuye lightly coughed with his fist against his lips.","\"Eighth brother, Zhiran and I felt that these things could be put to good use at home, so we bought them all.\"","Just then, the ox carts hired by Liang Hao and the others had not yet arrived, so Mo Jiuye introduced these items to Mo Chuhan.","\"Eighth brother, this is called glass, which serves the same purpose as our local window paper here, but it is transparent and does not block light like window paper.","There is also this, called plastic cloth, similar to the oilcloth commonly seen in our Da Shun Dynasty, the difference is also in transparency.","These are tiles used to pave room floors and look very beautiful.","These are all kinds of fruit made into dried fruit. Although they have lost moisture, they are easy to preserve and taste especially good.\"","As he spoke, Mo Jiuye had already handed a piece of pineapple to Mo Chuhan.","\"Eighth brother, try it, it’s sweet and sour and very appetizing.\"","Mo Chuhan was still immersed in astonishment at these things. He took the pineapple somewhat stiffly and bit off a piece.","Then unintentionally, he ate a whole slice of pineapple.","\"I have to say, the dried fruit made by the foreigners is really delicious, I just don't know what kind of fruit this is made of.\"","\"I heard that this thing is called pineapple. Zhiran thinks it tastes pretty good. She bought some seeds from the foreigners and plans to try planting some.\"","Mo Chuhan kept nodding as he listened: \"Well, not bad, not bad. If we can also grow such fruit, it will not only be a treat for the family, but should also sell for a good price.\"","By now, Mo Chuhan had completely recognized the reality that in the future he would have to work hard to make a living like an ordinary commoner. No matter how hard it was, as long as his family lived in prosperity, it would be fine.","Mo Jiuye took out several more dried fruits for his eighth brother, and the two walked while eating.","Finally, the brothers came to the rabbits.","\"Eighth brother, look. The foreigners said that these rabbits do not dig holes and are not prone to disease, making them very suitable for captive breeding.\"","Not to mention the Giant Angora and Mini Lop rabbits. Apart from their appearance, they also look very good.","Mo Chuhan laughed and said, \"Such rabbits given to Han Yue, she will definitely like them.\"","Not just Han Yue, even he as a grown man wanted to hug them when he saw them, they were so cute...","As for those rabbits prepared for profitability, they were not exactly the same as the wild rabbits hunted in the mountains. Wild rabbits have longer ears and don't have the larger size of these adult rabbits.","What’s more, these rabbits were as white as snow, encountering a white wild rabbit was very rare.","After taking a look around, Mo Chuhan asked, \"Ninth younger brother, there are at least two hundred rabbits large and small, right?\"","\"That's right, exactly two hundred.\" Mo Jiuye replied.","Mo Chuhan was at a loss.","\"Ninth younger brother, with so many rabbits, what will we use to feed them in the future?\"","In his perception, wild rabbits mostly lived on wild grass and wild fruits in the mountains.","While it would be fine in other seasons when they could go up the mountain to cut grass to feed them, what about in such cold weather?","\"Eighth brother, the foreigners said that in addition to grass, rabbits can also eat radishes and vegetables, and at worst feed them some coarse grains.\"","Hearing Mo Jiuye's explanation, Mo Chuhan felt relieved.","\"It turns out I really didn't know that rabbits can eat these things.\"","But seeing how fat the foreigners raised rabbits, there should be no mistake.","Just after the two brothers had checked the goods in the warehouse, they heard He Zhiran speaking at the door.","\"Husband, eighth brother, the ox carts hired by Liang Hao have arrived, let's move the goods.\"","The two brothers responded and walked towards the door together.","Liang Hao and the others had hired more than a dozen ox carts, orderly waiting outside the warehouse.","Mo Jiuye directed his family members, together with the carters, to successively load the goods onto the ox carts.","It had to be said that the things He Zhiran had prepared this time were still quite a lot. It was only when more than ten ox carts were fully loaded that a quarter of the goods in the warehouse were moved.","From this it could be seen that in order to move all these things completely, at least four trips would be needed, and it was estimated that the sky would be dark by then.","Both Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran were concerned about the matter of building a hay shed at home. So they handed over the freight work to their eighth brother and followed the freight ox carts back to Xi Ling Village.","As soon as the ox carts entered the village, they aroused the onlookers of the Zhao and Zhou families.","Having lived in Xi Ling Village for so long, this was still the first time they had seen someone buy so many things at once.","Even the once richest Cui Family had never been so extravagant.","For this reason, the clansmen of the two families unanimously believed that the Mo family would surely become Xi Ling Village’s richest family in the future...","Luckily there were still two vacant rooms at home. Storing the fluffy fabrics there for the time being was just right.","As for the plastic cloth, if left outside for too long it would be prone to weathering, so it might as well be stored in the vacant room along with the fluffy fabrics.","As for the glass and tiles, they were temporarily stacked on the empty ground in the yard.","After sending off the ox carts to continue transporting goods from the warehouse, Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran went to the backyard.","Mrs. Mo was truly a capable household manager. After her son and daughter-in-law went out, she went to find the Zhou clan chief, hoping to hire some clansmen to help build hay sheds at home.","Not only that, Mrs. Mo had also come up with a win-win idea.","Just like the modern package deal, she was responsible for the money and plan, while the other party was responsible for the materials and manpower.","What Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran saw when they arrived at the backyard was just such a scene.","Mrs. Mo and several daughters-in-law stood not far away watching, while the villagers kept bringing dried hay and coarse wooden poles from outside the courtyard wall, throwing them in. People on this side of the yard were responsible for building the woodshed.","From this it could be seen that not only was Mrs. Mo decisive, those villagers also had a very good skills at working.","The hay shed was built against the courtyard wall with the basic outline already in place. At this rate, it would surely be completed before nightfall.","At that time, they could move her little rabbits back and orderly put the cages in the hay shed. Then use a grass curtain to block the entrance and it would be all set."]},{"number":214,"title":"Chapter 214: Great Joy","paragraphs":["Just as He Zhiran and Mo Jiuye were about to go over and greet Old Lady Cui, Mo Jiuye, who had extremely good hearing, suddenly heard chaotic noises coming from afar.","These noises did not seem to foretell any danger. Rather, they sounded like the Cui Family members crying and wailing...","At the same time, there were also sounds of people from the Zhou Family running outside the courtyard walls.","\"I heard a group of government officials went to the Cui residence. Let's go take a look quickly!\"","\"Hurry up, or we won't get good spots!\"","\"With so much crying, the Cui Family is probably doomed...\"","He Zhiran and Mo Jiuye exchanged glances and headed out of the yard together.","It wasn't that they were gossipy or liked to watch other families' misfortunes. They mainly wanted to learn more about the Cui Family's situation as soon as possible, so they could buy the yard and land at the foot of the mountain earlier.","By the time the two of them arrived near the Cui residence, the area was already crowded with villagers who came to watch the commotion.","The crying and pleas for mercy from the Cui Family members were becoming more and more intense.","\"Your Honor, it was all Cui Wen who did it. I had nothing to do with it at all. You can't treat me like this!\"","\"Your Excellency, please just let me go this once. I still have an 80-year-old mother at home that I need to take care of.\"","\"Your Honor, I beg you, spare me this time...\"","The government officials were very impatient, constantly whipping the Cui Family members with rods in their hands.","\"All of you shut up! Now you know to plead for mercy, but at the time you committed those bad deeds, you didn't think about today!\"","The whips fell on the bodies of over a dozen Cui Family members, causing their screams to rise another notch.","For the Zhao and Zhou Family members, such a scene was extremely gratifying.","The villainous Cui Family was finally getting their retribution.","They thought only a few Cui Family members would be arrested, but unexpectedly, the officials went to find the Zhao and Zhou clan leaders afterwards.","The two clan leaders had no idea why they were being implicated in the Cui Family's offenses. In front of the officials, they looked very apprehensive.","\"Your Honor, we do not know why you have summoned us.\"","The official loudly proclaimed: \"The County prefect has ordered that any woman who was forced to marry into the Cui Family against her will can now get an annulment from her husband or a divorce if she is unwilling to continue the marriage.\"","Soon after the official finished speaking, three women came running from the direction of the Cui Family members.","The three women knelt down in front of the officials together: \"Your Honors, we ask to be granted divorces.\"","After speaking, they did not forget to glare fiercely back at the Cui Family members.","He Zhiran looked over these three women. Just by their patched-up clothes, it was obvious they did not match the status of the Cui Family.","It was clear how difficult their lives must have been after marrying into the Cui Family.","While He Zhiran was lost in thought, several people also came running from the direction of the Zhao and Zhou crowd.","They found their daughters and held them while crying bitterly.","\"Er Ni, it's all because your parents were incompetent that you suffered over two years of mistreatment in the Cui Family. But now, the County prefect has allowed you to get a divorce. Let's finalize it today!\"","\"Qiao Xing, those beasts in the Cui Family treated you like a servant. Today, we will help you divorce him!\"","\"Wonderful! My daughter finally doesn't have to suffer in the Cui Family anymore. Don't worry, once you're home, your parents and brothers will provide for you.\"","As they held their daughters and wept, amidst the women's shrieking cries from the Zhao and Zhou crowd, several sturdy men dragged a few unsightly women to the officials.","The men casually flung those women onto the ground.","\"Your Honor, we request annulments. Even if we can never remarry, we don't want Cui Family women for the rest of our lives!\"","\"That's right, we would rather die than take Cui Family women!\"","Seeing the men's determined attitude, the Cui Family women also stopped crying.","One woman who looked plump and young tried to grab one of the Zhao men's arms.","\"Zhao Yushan, marrying me was your blessing. Don't disgrace yourself like this!\"","Zhao Yushan abruptly jerked his body back. He no longer endured like before.","\"I, Zhao Yushan, do not need such blessings. You should go back to your Cui Family!\"","The Cui woman refused to accept this and moved to tear at Zhao Yushan again.","\"Don't you forget, I gave birth to two sons for you!\"","Zhao Yushan sneered coldly: \"So what if it's two sons? They still took your surname!\"","The other Cui Family women who had been dragged out also attempted to cling to their husbands. From their behavior, it was obvious this wasn't the first time they had thrown such tantrums.","Seeing the chaos, the official loudly admonished everyone before things finally quieted down slightly.","Afraid that something might change, the Zhao and Zhou clan leaders hurriedly ordered people to fetch paper and writing brushes on site. They publicly wrote annulment notes for the Cui women and hastily removed the women's names from their family trees.","Getting divorces for the women who married into the Cui Family was slightly more troublesome. Not only did the clan leaders have to help write the divorce papers, they needed to go to the county yamen to stamp the official seal for them to take effect.","For this reason, the families of the women decided on the spot to follow the officials to the county yamen, and finalize the divorces from the Cui men today no matter what.","The officials were also unambiguous. Regardless of whatever unlawful acts they once helped Cui Wen with, now that there was a new County prefect, they had to curry favor at all costs. This was the only way for them to redeem themselves.","Therefore, the officials worked very efficiently. After tying up those implicated Cui Family members, they hurried back to the county yamen.","Watching over a dozen clansmen taken away and so many abandoned wives and divorced husbands, the Cui Family completely deflated.","Some were still prone to habitually scolding the Zhao and Zhou families. But facing their vastly different demeanor now, they no longer dared.","For over ten years, the Zhao and Zhou families finally attained a sense of pride in Xi Ling Village.","They no longer needed to fear oppression and bullying from the Cui Family anymore. Life would certainly become better and better from now on.","Seeing that the officials had left with the prisoners, He Zhiran and Mo Jiuye returned home before the crowds dispersed to continue working on household matters, just as they had anticipated.","Sure enough, when it was nearing dusk, the horse carts continuously went back and forth, transporting all the goods from the warehouses.","Getting so many items in one day greatly astonished the Zhao and Zhou clansmen. They knew the Cui Family lived prosperous lives but had never imagined the Mo Family newly settling in to purchase this much.","Moreover, most of the items being unloaded seemed unfamiliar to them.","It was understandable. For someone who was once a high-ranking official in the capital city, even if he was exiled, he still had a substantial foundation.","Both families were glad that the Mo Family did not yield to Cui Wen. Otherwise, they would not have been assigned to Xi Ling Village. Their country bumpkin selves would not have the chance to broaden their horizons at home..."]},{"number":215,"title":"Chapter 215: Onigiri doesn't have any special abilities, does it","paragraphs":["<He Zhiran>He Zhiran</He Zhiran> did not know what those villagers were thinking. After the last batch of goods was transported back, he paid the carters their silver.","At the dock warehouse, <Rice Ball>Rice Ball</Rice Ball> also returned it to the landlord as instructed by <Mo Jiuye>Mo Jiuye</Mo Jiuye>.","After purchasing so many goods, every single item made the family members unable to take their eyes off them.","Especially those few Angolan giant rabbits and mini lop-eared rabbits. The women simply couldn't put them down. Even the rice balls they had been eyeing hungrily for days seemed less enticing next to these rabbits.","The rice balls were oblivious to having lost some popularity.","It went to the thatched shed on its own initiative, wanting to set some rules for those two hundred rabbits.","When everyone was about to go check on the rabbits, as soon as they walked into the thatched shed, they were dumbfounded by the scene before their eyes.","The <Rice Ball>Rice Ball</Rice Ball> was still sitting on the ground emitting sounds people simply couldn't understand, and its short, fat, little hands would knock on the ground from time to time.","Those rabbits seemed to have received some kind of order. Whether adult or young, they were all leaning against the cage walls with their legs on the ground and both front paws placed against their chests, their eyes fixed intently on the <Rice Ball>Rice Ball</Rice Ball>...","After a brief stunned moment, a wave of uproarious laughter rang out.","<Second Sister-in-law>Second Sister-in-law</Second Sister-in-law> pulled <He Zhiran>He Zhiran</He Zhiran> along, jokingly saying:","“Youngest sister-in-law, could <Rice Ball>Rice Ball</Rice Ball> have some kind of special ability? It actually managed to set rules for so many rabbits.”","<He Zhiran>He Zhiran</He Zhiran> couldn’t help but break into a cold sweat for <Rice Ball>Rice Ball</Rice Ball>.","It just had to cause such a big ruckus with this bit of ability...","Last night in the empty room, those wild rabbits had obediently lined up against the wall. And it could also manipulate the rabbits in the room to enter the cages.","Today’s performance was even more so. Those rabbits’ postures were all identical.","However, given <Rice Ball>Rice Ball</Rice Ball>’s capabilities, it could probably only make those animals weaker than itself listen to it.","Regarding <Rice Ball>Rice Ball</Rice Ball>’s special ability, <He Zhiran>He Zhiran</He Zhiran> really didn’t dare to underestimate it. Although <Second Sister-in-law>Second Sister-in-law</Second Sister-in-law> was just joking around, this was enough to show that <Rice Ball>Rice Ball</Rice Ball>’s extraordinariness could easily be seen through by others.","It was good that the little guy had supernatural powers, but this kind of thing was not suitable to publicize too ostentatiously.","After all, human hearts were unpredictable. No one knew what would happen in the future or what kind of people they would encounter. <Rice Ball>Rice Ball</Rice Ball>’s abilities absolutely could not be known by more people, otherwise it would definitely bring unnecessary trouble to the family.","“Second sister-in-law, I think it should be that these rabbits got scared after seeing an animal more powerful than themselves. It’s just their instinctive reaction.”","After entering the thatched shed, <Mo Jiuye>Mo Jiuye</Mo Jiuye> quickly noticed <Rice Ball>Rice Ball</Rice Ball>’s extraordinariness.","He and his wife held the same view—no matter whether <Rice Ball>Rice Ball</Rice Ball> really had some kind of supernatural power, it was not suitable to be wantonly publicized.","Therefore, after <He Zhiran>He Zhiran</He Zhiran> spoke, he also explained: “<Rice Ball>Rice Ball</Rice Ball> is silly all day long, doing nothing but eating and sleeping all day. How could it possibly have any special abilities?”","<Second Sister-in-law>Second Sister-in-law</Second Sister-in-law> had just casually said so for fun when she saw the hilarious scene before her. Seeing that both the ninth younger brother and the ninth younger sister-in-law were rebutting her words, she said with a smile: “I’m just saying, how could a silly bumpkin have that kind of ability?”","Seeing that <Second Sister-in-law>Second Sister-in-law</Second Sister-in-law> had already brushed the matter aside, <He Zhiran>He Zhiran</He Zhiran> didn’t want <Rice Ball>Rice Ball</Rice Ball> to keep putting on a performance here either. She walked over and hugged the round furball in her arms.","Feeling the familiar embrace, <Rice Ball>Rice Ball</Rice Ball> immediately turned into a soft and adorable little cutie, fawning over its owner.","Those rabbits also reacted very cooperatively. No longer holding their stances, they resumed whatever postures felt most comfortable.","<Fifth Sister-In-Law>Fifth Sister-In-Law</Fifth Sister-In-Law> and <Fifth Elder Brother>Fifth Elder Brother</Fifth Elder Brother> walked up to <Mo Jiuye>Mo Jiuye</Mo Jiuye> and <He Zhiran>He Zhiran</He Zhiran>.","“Ninth younger brother, ninth younger sister-in-law, your fifth elder brother said that he often goes hunting in the mountains. Sometimes when there is too much game, he would also raise them for a few days. So he should be no stranger to raising rabbits. Why don’t you leave these rabbits for us fifth elder brother and sister-in-law to take care of from now on?”","<Fifth Sister-In-Law>Fifth Sister-In-Law</Fifth Sister-In-Law> truly hoped that she could contribute more effort to the family. After wandering in exile for a few months, she didn’t have a penny on her. Not only did she have to spend <He Zhiran>He Zhiran</He Zhiran>’s money, but <He Zhiran>He Zhiran</He Zhiran> also had to worry about everything. She truly felt bad about it.","Now that there was finally something she could share the burden of, <Fifth Sister-In-Law>Fifth Sister-In-Law</Fifth Sister-In-Law> would absolutely take it on dutifully.","<Fifth Elder Brother>Fifth Elder Brother</Fifth Elder Brother> also said in a low voice, “I can take good care of them.”","<He Zhiran>He Zhiran</He Zhiran> looked at <Fifth Sister-In-Law>Fifth Sister-In-Law</Fifth Sister-In-Law> and <Fifth Elder Brother>Fifth Elder Brother</Fifth Elder Brother>, then looked towards <Mo Jiuye>Mo Jiuye</Mo Jiuye>, intending to ask for his opinion.","Raising these rabbits was no easy task.","There were two hundred rabbits now. Rabbits bred quickly so their numbers would grow faster and faster.","Just those droppings alone needed someone to carefully handle them. Also, when she placed these rabbits into cages in her space last night, she did not separate the males and females, only allocating them based on quantity.","The young rabbits were fine, but those adult rabbits were bought specifically for breeding purposes after all. The males and females had to be evenly distributed.","As for the excess male rabbits, there was no more value in continuing to raise them, so they had to be slaughtered in a timely manner to exchange for profit.","These things definitely required a meticulous person to busy themselves with.","<Fifth Sister-In-Law>Fifth Sister-In-Law</Fifth Sister-In-Law> was a meticulous person. <He Zhiran>He Zhiran</He Zhiran> believed that she would definitely be able to manage the rabbits well. In the future when the mother rabbits gave birth to young rabbits, she would also surely be able to take good care of them.","As a strong man, it was a suitable job for <Fifth Elder Brother>Fifth Elder Brother</Fifth Elder Brother> to do things that required effort like cleaning the rabbit shed and moving their food.","<Mo Jiuye>Mo Jiuye</Mo Jiuye> lightly nodded towards <He Zhiran>He Zhiran</He Zhiran>.","“Since that’s the case, we’ll leave them for fifth elder brother and fifth sister-in-law to manage for now. In the future when there are more rabbits, we can discuss it again.”","Seeing that her request was approved, <Fifth Sister-In-Law>Fifth Sister-In-Law</Fifth Sister-In-Law> happily asked: “Ninth younger brother, ninth younger sister-in-law, what do you think your fifth sister-in-law should do now?”","<He Zhiran>He Zhiran</He Zhiran> looked at the color of the sky outside. These rabbits had been placed in the storeroom since early morning and had gone the entire day without food. They must have been starving already.","“Fifth sister-in-law, it’s too late in the day now. Just feed these little guys their fill first. Then separate the adult rabbits by gender tomorrow. Other than cleaning the rabbit shed, your job from now on, along with fifth elder brother, is to observe whether these mother rabbits are pregnant or not.","Rabbits have a relatively short gestation period of just one month. For rabbits about to give birth, put them alone in a cage.","As this was her first time dealing with small animals, <Fifth Sister-In-Law>Fifth Sister-In-Law</Fifth Sister-In-Law> listened very attentively.","“Don’t worry ninth younger sister-in-law, your fifth sister-in-law will definitely take good care of these little guys. If there’s anything I don’t understand, I’ll ask you again.”","Seeing that <Fifth Sister-In-Law>Fifth Sister-In-Law</Fifth Sister-In-Law> had found something to do, the other sisters-in-law grew increasingly anxious in their hearts.","“Ninth younger sister-in-law, what can we do that would be suitable?” the <Eldest Sister-in-law>Eldest Sister-in-law</Eldest Sister-in-law> asked.","<He Zhiran>He Zhiran</He Zhiran> knew that the sisters-in-law all wanted to contribute to the family. She smiled and responded:","“Sisters-in-law, don’t be impatient. This time, I purchased a lot of plush fabrics from the foreigners. Making plush toys happens to be your forte!”","“Ninth younger sister-in-law, I felt those bags in the empty room. They were soft and fluffy. Could they be plush fabrics?” <Third Sister-in-law>Third Sister-in-law</Third Sister-in-law> asked in sudden realization.","“That’s right, those bags all contain plush fabrics, and I bought quite a lot of different colors this time too.”","Before <He Zhiran>He Zhiran</He Zhiran> could even finish speaking, her whole person was surrounded by the sisters-in-law, scaring <Rice Ball>Rice Ball</Rice Ball> in her arms into rapidly shrinking its neck.","“Ninth younger sister-in-law, quickly give us those fabrics! We can start making plush toys tonight.”","“That’s right, ninth younger sister-in-law. Even if we're idle, it’s better we earn some money for the family if we can.”"]},{"number":216,"title":"Chapter 216: The First Wife","paragraphs":["He Zhiran did not hurry to make dolls this time.","Over the past few days, she took a look around Yuncheng and found that although there were some wealthy people here, there were not as many as in other cities.","Although the cost of making dolls was not high, Tang Mingrui had previously sold them for the sky-high price of ten taels each.","Moreover, she did not know when she would have the chance to replenish these fabrics again after they were used up.","Additionally, there had been no news of Tang Mingrui at all since he entered Yuncheng with them.","She planned to contact Tang Mingrui first before making any plans.","Therefore, there was no rush at all to make the dolls, but that did not mean she could not do it at all.","Over the past few days, her sisters-in-law had worked very hard for family affairs, so there was no need to exhaust themselves staying up late for business that was not urgent.","\"Sisters-in-law, there is no rush to make the dolls. Since there are many colors of fabric this time, I want to research some more styles first.\"","When the sisters-in-law heard that the ninth younger sister wanted to research some more doll styles, they knew there was no need to hurry this matter. Thus, they gave up the idea of immediately making them.","Old Lady Mo stood behind the crowd. Seeing that everyone had almost finished speaking, she urged:","\"It's getting late. Everyone should go back and rest after eating. There will still be things to be busy with tomorrow.\"","The sisters-in-law had always listened to their mother-in-law's words and left the thatched shed one after another to prepare dinner.","There were still many fresh ingredients at home that had not been tasted by everyone. He Zhiran had worked hard today, so she gave up that idea.","After she and Mo Jiuye had dinner, they entered the space together with the rice balls.","Mo Jiuye knew his wife had worked hard today. After washing up, he took the initiative to massage her.","It had been quite a long time since He Zhiran had enjoyed such treatment.","When Mo Jiuye's big hands pressed on her slightly sore shoulders, He Zhiran let out a few muffled moans of comfort.","\"Hmm... right there...\"","That voice...","That soft touch...","To Mo Jiuye, it was simply heavenly torture.","His body had already unconsciously become restless.","However, the little woman enjoying her husband's super service still did not know that she was playing with fire!","Mo Jiuye felt unbearably hot and restless. The strength of his hands also gradually became imbalanced.","He Zhiran noticed something wrong with the strength and turned to ask:","\"Do you have something on your mind? Why are you so distracted?\"","Before her voice fell, her body was pulled into his embrace with force.","What followed was a domineering yet slightly clumsy kiss.","He Zhiran had just been immersed in the comfort brought by the massage when Mo Jiuye suddenly attacked her. Her instinct was to push him away.","After all, it was the first time in her two lifetimes that she had been so intimate with a man, and it made He Zhiran feel a little overwhelmed at first.","But she was no match for Mo Jiuye's strength. She tried pushing him several times to no avail as he remained steady as Mt. Tai. That domineering kiss only deepened.","As the kiss intensified, He Zhiran also gradually lost herself.","She wrapped her arms around Mo Jiuye's neck as her true feelings took over, responding passionately to him.","The two had now completely forgotten themselves. Mo Jiuye's hands grew bolder, continuously roaming her back, feeling that unique softness.","After an unknown amount of kissing, Mo Jiuye already felt his body nearing the brink of explosion. Just as he was about to pick He Zhiran up and carry her to the bed, Rice Ball trotted back on his little short legs after digging bamboo shoots in the bamboo forest.","Seeing that his owner seemed to be bullied, the little guy rushed to Mo Jiuye's side, hugging his leg tightly while taking a fierce bite.","Damn you, Silver, daring to bully my owner. I'm going to bite you to death...","Feeling the pain in his calf, Mo Jiuye instinctively loosened his arms around He Zhiran.","At the same time, most of his senses also returned.","He Zhiran also felt the strength holding her ease up a bit. She looked down panting at the position by her feet.","Rice Ball was firmly hugging Mo Jiuye’s leg, barking while still trying to continue biting.","Not bothering about the kiss that had made her entire body go limp and weak just now, He Zhiran gently scolded: \"Rice Ball, don't bite people.\"","Rice Ball did not understand why his owner would treat him this way when he was clearly helping her.","The heartbroken little guy reluctantly let go of Mo Jiuye's calf and looked at He Zhiran pitifully.","He Zhiran took the opportunity to pick Rice Ball up and retreated several steps back to mask her embarrassment.","Her first kiss in two lifetimes had come so suddenly without any mental preparation on her part.","It seemed to also be triggered by the massage...","Mo Jiuye's face was flushed with embarrassment, and he did not quite dare to look straight at He Zhiran.","He had heard from the veterans in the barracks that they were all quite clumsy the first time they were intimate with their wives, and they could accidentally bite their wife's lips until they bled, especially when kissing.","Thinking of this, Mo Jiuye felt a little guilty, wondering if his clumsy kiss just now had hurt his wife.","Also, that Rice Ball was definitely his number one nemesis.","According to what the veterans said, after the wife goes limp, she would let him have his way. He was already at that point, but that damned Rice Ball just had to ruin it.","Oh well, at least this put an end to things before they went too far. After all, he had promised Rangrang to give her a perfect wedding night with candles and flowers. If they had hastily done the deed today, it would really not have lived up to his promise to her.","Thinking of this, Mo Jiuye awkwardly said, \"I just lost control for a moment.\"","In fact, He Zhiran had already accepted Mo Jiuye wholeheartedly in her heart and was mentally prepared to become his true wife.","As for the so-called perfect wedding night with candles and flowers, whether or not it had that setting did not matter as long as she was with the man she loved.","If she had not been willing today, there would have been no way she could have cooperated in that manner.","She had thought it would happen naturally when Rice Ball interrupted them.","Thinking of this, He Zhiran found it somewhat amusing.","When she looked up again at Mo Jiuye's handsome yet unsatisfied face, she walked up to him and took the initiative to wrap her arms around his waist, pressing her head tightly against his chest.","\"I'm your wife. It doesn't matter if you lose control.\"","The intimate contact between their bodies rekindled the flames of desire in Mo Jiuye that had just died down a bit.","At this moment, he could no longer control his body and mind. If he endured any longer, he felt he would go crazy.","He wanted to possess her immediately and unite her body with his own...","Mo Jiuye no longer cared about any perfect wedding night. He leaned down to kiss her again.","To prevent Rice Ball from interfering, this kiss was even more aggressive than the previous one. Feeling his beloved wife go limp in his arms, he swiftly carried her to the bedroom, shutting that troublemaker outside the door.","As it was He Zhiran's first time becoming a wife, there would inevitably be physical discomfort, so Mo Jiuye tried his best to restrain himself lest she could not handle it.","However, a man in his prime with vigorous energy, no matter how much he tries to control himself, still made He Zhiran feel her body could not withstand it."]},{"number":217,"title":"Chapter 217: Nine brothers and sisters, you don't pretend","paragraphs":["That night, Mo Jiuye took He Zhiran in and out of the bathroom no less than seven times.","Lying back in bed, He Zhiran used her last bit of strength to bite his shoulder.","\"Mo Jiuye, you're just a lustful bastard.\"","Bitten, Mo Jiuye was not bothered at all.","He gently took her into his arms.","\"I'm sorry Zhiran, it was all my fault, I'll be more careful from now on.\"","After speaking, Mo Jiuye gently kissed her forehead: \"Sleep, don't get up so early tomorrow, I'll take care of things outside.\"","Drowsiness washed over He Zhiran, she just lightly hmm-ed, and after that she didn't know anything.","Mo Jiuye had the most accurate biological clock, he would wake up before daylight.","He had also learned to look at the big clock on the wall, it was five in the morning.","Mo Jiuye got up quietly and got dressed neatly, if he didn't have to leave the space, he simply couldn't bear to wake up his sleeping little wife.","\"Zhiran, send me out first, you can sleep a little longer.\"","Hearing Mo Jiuye's voice, He Zhiran squinted to see the time on the clock.","The willpower forged in the army in her previous life was really of no use to her this time.","But in order not to arouse other people's suspicion, He Zhiran still tried her best to invigorate herself for a few seconds, moved her thoughts, and appeared in the room in Xiling Village along with her clothes, Mo Jiuye and the rice balls.","He Zhiran lay back down on the kang to rest, and Mo Jiuye quietly left the room.","Rice ball was worried about its owner all night last night. Now that the bad guy who bullied its owner had finally left, the little guy struggled up onto the kang, sticking close to her side, trying to continue protecting its owner.","It wasn't until the sun was high in the sky that He Zhiran slowly got up.","She got dressed neatly and opened the door to walk out.","Just then, Eighth Sister-in-Law had just returned from the backyard and caught sight of her at first glance.","\"Sister-in-law, I heard Ninth Brother say you were not feeling well last night, are you better now?\"","\"Much better already, thanks for your concern, Eighth Sister-in-Law.\"","He Zhiran said and then scolded Mo Jiuye in her heart.","It was all this guy's fault. She now felt like her whole body had fallen apart and she had no strength at all.","Not only that, she didn't even dare to take big steps when walking...","\"That's good as long as you're fine now. I'll go heat up the breakfast I saved for you earlier.\" With that, Eighth Sister-in-Law had already walked into the kitchen.","He Zhiran had already gotten up late to begin with, how could she let Eighth Sister-in-Law go through the trouble of heating up food for her.","She hurried to catch up.","\"Eighth Sister-in-Law, please let me do it myself!\"","That's what she said, but her body was not cooperating, unable to take big steps, only clipping her legs forward, which made He Zhiran feel very annoyed.","Just as bad luck would have it, she had just taken a few steps out when she bumped into Eldest Sister-in-Law and Second Sister-in-Law.","Eldest Sister-in-Law was more attentive and noticed at a glance that He Zhiran was walking funny.","She revealed an ambiguous smile and came over to take He Zhiran's arm, and said gently: \"Sister-in-law, Ninth Brother said you were uncomfortable, I thought what had happened...\"","Although Second Sister-in-Law was usually rough, as someone who had gone through this before, after what Eldest Sister-in-Law had just said, she would have to be an idiot not to get it.","\"Ninth Brother is really... Sister-in-law is so delicate, how could he not know to cherish jade.\"","After a few words from the two sisters-in-law, He Zhiran's face instantly turned red.","The ancients were too amazing!","They could even tell from this?","If she was not thick-skinned enough, she would have to find a crack in the ground and drill into it...","\"Cough cough... Eldest Sister-in-Law, Second Sister-in-Law, what are you talking about? It's not what you think, I really am a little uncomfortable...\"","\"Tsk tsk... We're all women of experience, what can Second Sister-in-Law not see... Sister-in-law, stop pretending.\"","Eldest Sister-in-Law was even more excessive.","\"Sister-in-law, I wonder if we'll have another big fat boy in our family next year?\"","He Zhiran...","It seemed that her previous explanation had only made things worse?","The two sister-in-laws were getting more and more excited.","Just as He Zhiran was about to try to explain something, Old Lady Mo heard the movement in the yard and came out too.","Second Sister-in-Law was afraid that there would be any secrets in the family that she didn't know about, so she hurried over and said, \"Mother, Ninth Brother is really capable, just wait to hold your big fat grandson next year!\"","Hearing this, Old Lady Mo looked at He Zhiran with a smile.","And from time to time she would glance at her flat belly.","As if she really had a bun in the oven...","This was a situation He Zhiran had never imagined.","She kept psyching herself up in her heart:","He Zhiran, you are a modern soul, you just did a few nucleic acid tests with your husband, so what?","What's there to be shy about?","Every woman here has done this with her man.","After pumping herself up, He Zhiran finally bravely raised her head.","\"Mother, daughter-in-law got a little uncomfortable last night and woke up late.\" She wanted to divert the topic first, as long as everyone stopped thinking about it, she wouldn't feel embarrassed.","At the same time, she scolded that culprit Mo Jiuye again in her heart:","Damn Mo Jiuye, he did bad things and disappeared without a trace, leaving her alone to face all this.","At this moment, Mo Jiuye was driving a mule cart towards the yamen.","After breakfast, he went to find the two clan chiefs, Zhao and Zhou. The purchase of land and courtyard had been settled. It would be reassuring to have the ownership transferred to him early.","Unexpectedly, while he was chatting idly with the two chiefs, he suddenly sneezed twice...","He Zhiran silently scolded Mo Jiuye, and finally felt a little more balanced. She continued taking small steps towards the kitchen.","After eating breakfast simply, she was going to go see how the rabbits in the backyard were doing.","She had just walked to the door when she bumped right into Fifth Sister-In-Law.","\"Sister-in-law, I was just about to look for you. These rabbits have such a big appetite. I'm afraid the cabbage and carrots we have stored at home can only last two more days. What should we do when it runs out?\"","For Fifth Sister-In-Law, who had always lived a life of having clothes put onto her and food served to her, even on the road to exile, Sister-in-Law had arranged everything, she only needed to help out with some effort.","Now that she had taken the initiative to feed the rabbits, she was already stumped on the first day.","She had just finished speaking when Fifth Elder Brother also walked over from the backyard.","And from the steady pace of Fifth Elder Brother's walking, it could be seen that his body had recovered a lot.","\"Wife, don't worry about the rabbit food, I'll go to the village in a bit and ask around, buy some extra vegetables from whoever has them.\"","He Zhiran chimed in, \"What Fifth Elder Brother said makes sense. Most peasant families will store some cabbage and carrots. Let's go to the village and ask around later.\"","What He Zhiran wanted to do now was to go and take the opportunity while purchasing vegetables from the peasants to pad the numbers with some vegetables from her space.","Unexpectedly, as soon as she turned around, the pain in her body reminded her that she should not go out today...","Fifth Sister-in-Law reacted quickly as well. As soon as she heard what the two of them said, she immediately grabbed Fifth Elder Brother's arm.","\"Dear, let's go to the village right now and ask around.\""]},{"number":218,"title":"Chapter 218: Your husband was always a gentleman.","paragraphs":["When He Zhiran and Fifth Brother and Sister-in-law were about to leave, He Zhiran quickly stopped them, \"Fifth Brother, Sister-in-law, there is no rush for this matter. Wait for my husband to return and have him take care of it.\"","She could only cheat easily when she was with Mo Jiuye.","Fifth Brother and Sister-in-law thought that the vegetables and radishes at home were enough to last them for a while, so they readily accepted her proposal.","...","Shortly after noon, Mo Jiuye returned.","He threw the donkey cart aside and strode back to his own room.","He Zhiran was feeling uncomfortable and walked strangely, so she simply stayed in her room to avoid going out and being teased by her sisters-in-law.","Seeing his wife still lying on the kang, Mo Jiuye thought he had really hurt her.","\"Ranran, are you uncomfortable anywhere?\"","Seeing the disgraceful culprit, He Zhiran glared fiercely at him, then turned over with her head facing inward, not looking at him.","Mo Jiuye took the opportunity to take off his shoes and climbed onto the kang, taking his delicate little wife into his arms.","The foodie seemed to be used to the way the masters interacted and very tactfully climbed down to the floor to admire itself in the corner.","\"Ranran...\" Mo Jiuye gently called her name in a warm tone.","Feeling the familiar embrace, He Zhiran angrily flipped over and fiercely punched his chest with her little fists.","\"It's all your fault, making me get teased by my sisters-in-law early in the morning.\"","Mo Jiuye didn't dodge her punches but frowned deeply and asked earnestly.","\"Why did the sisters-in-law tease you?\"","Seeing that this obtuse man didn't understand her words at all, He Zhiran felt even more stifled.","How could she explain this kind of thing?","Forget it, it was impossible to communicate with such a slow-witted man.","She was not the kind of person who would nitpick over something anyway.","He Zhiran pushed him away and sat up straight.","\"Where did you go today?\"","Seeing that she was not really angry, Mo Jiuye breathed a sigh of relief and also sat up straight.","He took out a stack of land deeds from his arms and placed them in front of He Zhiran.","\"I went to the yamen and transferred the ownership of the land and houses.\"","When He Zhiran heard that he had gone to the yamen to transfer ownership, the first thing she thought of was having to pay silver to those villagers.","\"Where did you get the silver?\"","Mo Jiuye smiled awkwardly. \"I took some from the space this morning.\"","He Zhiran...","This guy was quite forward-thinking, knowing to take silver himself when he needed it. He had made progress and was much better than that penniless person he used to be.","Mo Jiuye had handled the matter very clearly. The amount of land and houses matched exactly with what they had agreed with the two clan chiefs the other day.","She stuffed the land deeds back into Mo Jiuye's hands.","\"Mother is the head of the household. Send these to the old lady first. If she doesn't intend to manage them, then take them back.\"","In fact, the couple knew very well that since being exiled, Grandma Mo had basically stopped managing anything. She had handed over all the big and small household affairs to He Zhiran to manage. It could be said that she had completely let go.","By doing this, He Zhiran was also showing respect to her elder.","Mo Jiuye smiled as he put away the land deeds, and was about to take He Zhiran to see his mother together.","But He Zhiran declined. The way she walked would still get her teased by her sisters-in-law if she went out. Even if they didn't tease her, their eyes alone were something she couldn't quite handle.","Mo Jiuye also guessed that her discomfort was probably due to him being too wild last night, injuring his wife's body, so he did not force her.","As He Zhiran had expected, Mo Jiuye soon returned with the land deeds intact.","It was just as well, keeping them in the space was safer than anything.","He Zhiran had completely given up for that day. Not only did she not leave the room, she lay on the kang thinking of nothing to do.","Finally, she endured until the evening. Mo Jiuye was eager to urge her into the space together.","Seeing his wolf-like eyes, He Zhiran's body shook involuntarily.","This man was too vigorous. Her petite body really could not withstand him.","\"Um... can we...?\"","Ceasefire tonight...","He Zhiran found the latter words somewhat hard to say.","Mo Jiuye naturally understood what she meant, and his face flushed red.","\"Ranran, I was wrong last night. I hurt you. Don't worry today. I guarantee...\"","\"Even going lightly is no good. I'm still sore!\" He Zhiran interrupted him.","Mo Jiuye quickly explained, \"What I mean is, I guarantee I'll sleep honestly tonight.\"","He Zhiran...","So what he was saying was \"I guarantee I'll sleep honestly tonight.\" She had just imagined too much extra.","Thinking of this, her old face turned a bit red.","\"A gentleman stands by his word. You have to keep your promise.\"","Looking at his awkward little wife, Mo Jiuye walked over and gently kissed her forehead.","\"Your husband has always been a gentleman.\"","A gentleman?","If she hadn't witnessed his ferocity last night, He Zhiran would have always thought so too.","Now... she really couldn't say.","At this time, the foodie seemed to be hungry too, whining incessantly at its owners.","He Zhiran felt bad that the little guy hadn't been able to roll around in the bamboo forest all day. So she took the big gray wolf and flashed into the space together.","It was indeed difficult for an aroused man to restrain his desires.","But Mo Jiuye was true to his word. Faced with his delicate wife, he would rather take a cold shower when consumed by fiery lust, fulfilling his gentleman's promise...","After a night of recuperation, He Zhiran was much better the next day. As usual, she took Mo Jiuye and the foodie out of the space early.","The land deeds were at hand. The whole family had not gone to check it out yet. It was a good time today with nothing special to do, so they could go take a look.","After breakfast, the family set off towards the foot of the mountain.","The two clan chiefs personally led the way, telling them about the location of those farmlands and houses.","It could be said purchasing the land and houses was rather rash of He Zhiran and Mo Jiuye. They only knew the approximate locations and had not even looked at the specifics before daring to buy.","In fact, this had a lot to do with He Zhiran's extravagance.","Besides, the seeds produced in her space were not picky about soil and climate anyway, so there was no need to care about those things. What they valued more was the location of the land.","The main thing was that it not be fragmented.","Those forty-six mu of land could only be said to barely gather together.","The reason for saying barely was that there was still some land belonging to the Cui family interspersed.","As such, they would have to buy those Cui family lands too.","Fortunately, those lands were similarly barren. The Cui family would surely be willing to sell too.","Of course, given the Cuis' character, even if they were willing to sell, the process would surely not go smoothly.","In any case, He Zhiran and Mo Jiuye were determined to obtain this piece of land.","After walking around all the land, He Zhiran and Mo Jiuye discovered that there was also a vast expanse of barren land to the north of these lands, the edges of which could not be seen with the naked eye.","The area of these barren lands was no less than, and even exceeded, that of these previously reclaimed lands.","Mo Jiuye asked Clan Chief Zhou, \"Elder, is that stretch all barren land?\""]},{"number":219,"title":"Chapter 219: Are you sure that Foreigner isn't lying to You","paragraphs":["Chief Zhou was familiar with everything here.","\"These are indeed uncultivated lands. Our clan members only cultivated up to this point,\" he explained.","Mo Jiuye asked further, \"To purchase these uncultivated lands, do we simply go to the government office to complete the procedures?\"","\"Yes, over the years, the government has been selling uncultivated lands for one or two silver coins per mu. Once you choose the desired location, you can apply at the government office. They will send an official to survey the land, and after paying the fee, they will issue a land deed,\" Chief Zhou replied.","Having understood the market situation for these lands, they planned to visit the town and apply at the government office on another day.","With Meng Huaining present, they believed everything would go smoothly.","After examining the land, the group arrived at the abandoned houses.","These houses were once owned by three different families and were not concentratedly purchased by the Zhao and Zhou families, just like the lands.","The houses were in a state of disrepair, necessitating demolition and reconstruction. Therefore, they only needed to assess the size of the area and make a plan.","They were not in a hurry to plan the area as the Cui family's courtyard had not been acquired yet.","Having spent several days in Xi Ling Village, He Zhiran took a careful walk for the first time.","While inspecting the houses, she noticed that there was at least a hundred meters of distance between the back of the houses and the foot of the mountain.","The land in this distance was not as flat as the uncultivated lands to the north; it had a slight slope.","Moreover, judging from the soil, it seemed to be darker than the soil in those uncultivated lands.","If her guess was correct, this area should have a similar soil quality to the mountain.","Behind these uncultivated lands was the West Mountain.","It was already deep winter, and the tall trees on the higher ground stood tall and bare.","In contrast, the lower ground was different. Perhaps due to the villagers cutting trees for firewood, there were hardly any robust trees left.","And even if there were, their numbers were scarce.","He Zhiran couldn't help but ask, \"Chiefs, were all the trees in the lower part of the West Mountain cut down for firewood?\"","Chief Zhao replied, \"Indeed, that's the case. Xi Ling Village is cold in winter, and we need a lot of firewood for heating. Most of the nearby trees have been cut down.\"","As expected.","At this moment, He Zhiran thought that this mountainous area, devoid of trees, would be convenient for her to plant some fruit trees.","Not only could it prevent sandstorms, but it could also bring in some profits.","\"Chief Zhao, is it possible to buy this mountain?\" she inquired.","Upon hearing about buying the mountain, Chief Zhao frowned.","\"Oh, young miss, if you buy this mountain, it would cut off the livelihood of everyone in the village.\"","He Zhiran was puzzled, \"Why would Chief Zhao say that?\"","Chief Zhao explained, \"The villagers of Xi Ling Village rely on the West Mountain for their firewood. During the spring, summer, and autumn seasons, people also go up the mountain to hunt or gather wild vegetables to sustain themselves. If you buy this mountain, it would mean that we, the villagers, would have no means of survival.\"","He Zhiran hadn't expected Chief Zhao to mention all these points.","Even if she had thought about it, she had a better solution to resolve the issue.","However, in order to acquire this mountain, she would have to be more selfless.","\"Chief Zhao, what if I only buy a part of the mountain and leave a portion for you all?\"","Furthermore, I acquired a special crop from a foreigner. This crop not only has a high yield, but after harvesting, the remaining parts can all be used as firewood.\"","She remembered in her past life when she followed the troops to the countryside to experience life there. The villagers would burn corn cobs and stalks during the winter.","The farmers there said that as long as they had enough corn planted, they wouldn't have to worry about firewood throughout the winter.","In other words, if these villagers could trust her, she could sell them the high-yielding corn seeds produced in her space and have everyone in the village plant this crop.","She believed that once they planted it, they would experience the benefits of this crop.","In He Zhiran's mind, although cornmeal wasn't as tasty as white flour, it had the advantage of high yield and was much better than the rough flour that scratched one's throat in this era.","On this journey, she also realized that there was a significant wealth disparity in the Da Shun Dynasty.","A small minority of people could be described as dripping with wealth, while the majority of the common people struggled to fill their stomachs.","Take the people of Xi Ling Village, for example. Before the Cui family arrived, they could be said to have trampled over the other two families in terms of clothing and food.","And when you looked at the Zhao and Zhou families, most of them wore patched-up clothes and, in terms of physique and complexion, were not as well-off as the Cui family.","It's easy to imagine how tight the lives of the Zhao and Zhou families were.","When the two clan chiefs listened to He Zhiran's words, they exchanged glances. Both of them knew that the Mo family had a deep heritage, but they had never heard of high-yielding crops despite a lifetime of farming.","Chief Zhao asked skeptically, \"Are you sure that foreigner didn't deceive you, Jiu Jia?\" It wasn't surprising for someone who had been farming their whole life to have such doubts.","At present, she was not yet twenty years old and had never been involved in agriculture. No matter how she explained it, she wouldn't be convincing.","Therefore, this matter needed to be substantiated with facts.","\"Both clan chiefs, next spring I will cultivate this high-yielding crop here. After the harvest, you can see if you're satisfied before making a decision.\"","The two clan chiefs didn't really take He Zhiran's so-called high-yielding crop seriously.","\"Alright, we'll wait and see the results of your cultivation next year.\"","Clearly, Chief Zhao's tone carried a sense of perfunctoriness.","As the saying goes, actions speak louder than words. He Zhiran didn't owe anyone anything, and if it weren't for her desire to buy this mountain, she wouldn't have voluntarily shared such excellent seeds with others.","In any case, she had made up her mind to buy this mountain. Even if it was only for the sake of those villagers, she would buy a part of it.","Glancing at the sky, it was already close to noon.","They had finished inspecting the purchased property, so everyone started heading back.","Just as they entered the village, they heard commotion coming from the Cui family's side.","Because of this, instead of going their separate ways, they followed the source of the noise.","To their surprise, Meng Huaining had come in person today.","He immediately spotted Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran walking over from the village and took the initiative to greet them.","\"Brother Jiuye, Sister-in-law Nine.\"","Mo Jiuye took a step forward. \"Brother Meng, why did you personally come here today? Is it because of the Cui Family's matter?\"","Meng Huaining nodded. \"These past few days, we have been working tirelessly to investigate the Cui Family's case, and now everything has been revealed.","Since there are many matters regarding compensation involved, the officials in the yamen are merely eating free meals and can't be of any help. So, I had to personally make a trip.\"","As soon as he finished speaking, Meng Huaining turned around and instructed the government officials to gather all the members of the Cui Family together.","The efficiency of the government officials these days was remarkable. In less than five minutes, all the members of the Cui Family had been summoned before Meng Huaining."]},{"number":220,"title":"Chapter 220: I should have known better Now.","paragraphs":["Meng Huaining looked over and then ordered: “Meng An, the Cui family members have all arrived, read it out!”","Meng An took out a thick stack of papers from his bosom, and stood in front of the Cui family to read aloud.","\"Cui Fugui, head of the Cui clan, holds an official position in Xiling village. He abused his power and used his nephew Cui Wen's connections to extort twenty-five acres of good land from the Zhao and Zhou clans. He exploited the Zhao and Zhou clans as forced labor, and allowed his clansmen to bully and plunder.","Now there is ironclad evidence. Considering his old age, the county magistrate has exempted him from fifty heavy beatings and sentenced him to ten years in jail starting today...\"","As soon as Meng An finished speaking, the Cui clan members began wailing.","\"Your Honor, we are wronged!\"","\"All of you shut up!\" Along with the crisp sounds of whips striking human bodies, the cries of the Cui clan were immediately silenced.","Seeing the surroundings had quieted down, Meng An continued reading:","\"Starting today, the Cui clan must compensate the Zhao and Zhou clans 280 taels of silver within three days.\"","There were also compensations for others which he didn't need to read out. In other words, the Cui clan had to compensate more people than just what they heard.","At this, the Cui clan was completely shocked again.","280 taels? Where could they get so much silver?","\"Your Honor, please show mercy. Our old man is now in jail, and my sons have not returned. There are only us old people, women and children left in the family. We cannot come up with so much silver...\"","Meng An sneered at the old woman who had shouted. Judging by her tone, she was probably Cui Fugui's mother-in-law.","\"Don't worry, there are also fines for your sons. I will tell you the full amount after I have finished reading everything.\"","Upon hearing this, the old woman was so shocked she fainted on the spot.","Several daughters-in-law quickly helped her up and knelt before Meng Huaining, tearfully begging for mercy.","But the Cui clan's crimes were too grave, and no matter how piteously they wept, they would not be forgiven.","Without needing Meng Huaining's orders, the yamen runners stepped forward to maintain order. When the women no longer dared to wail loudly, Meng An continued to announce the Cui clan's punishments.","Cui Fugui's sons had also committed many misdeeds. In addition to jail time, they also had to compensate the Zhao and Zhou clans 100 taels.","Not a single Cui clansman who had done wrong was spared. Those who deserved jail time were jailed, and those who owed compensation paid it.","This news was extremely gratifying for the Zhao and Zhou clan members.","Finally, they would no longer be oppressed by the Cui clan, and could even obtain due compensation.","The crowd knelt before Meng Huaining in unison, ceaselessly shouting, \"Blue Sky Magistrate!\"","Judging by their reaction, if shouting \"Long Live\" wasn't taboo, they would have shouted it several times.","Meng Huaining gestured for the commoners to stand.","\"I'm just doing my official duty, no need for such courtesy.\"","Then he turned towards the Cui clan and said loudly, \"If you cannot hand over the fines within three days, your houses and land will be confiscated as payment.\"","The Cui clan had thought that since they couldn't take out the silver, the county magistrate could do nothing to them.","They didn't expect the county magistrate to be so decisive as to confiscate their houses and land as compensation.","Now the Cui clan was truly dumbfounded. The silver they had extorted had been slowly frittered away. Where could they find so much silver for compensation now?","If they didn't pay compensation, their houses and land would be sold off. How would they survive after that?","Thinking of this, the Cui clan members knelt before Meng Huaining.","\"County Magistrate, have mercy on us. Please spare us...\"","Meng Huaining looked coldly at them.","\"You should have thought of today before doing those misdeeds. Wrongdoings must be punished accordingly.\"","After speaking, he flicked his robe sleeves and turned to find Mo Jiuye.","\"Brother Jiu, Sister-in-law, it's still early today. I hope I'm not intruding by visiting your home?\"","How could Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran possibly refuse such a thing?","\"You are most welcome.\"","Meng Huaining ordered the yamen runners to carry out their duties, while he went with Meng An to the Mo house.","After the county magistrate and yamen runners left, the Cui clan members returned home, faces full of grief, to think of ways to raise the silver fines. Seeing there was no more spectacle, the Zhao and Zhou clan members also returned home.","When Meng Huaining came visiting, the Mo family naturally had to treat him well.","Fortunately He Zhiran had recently gotten many new and exotic foods from the foreigners. Whipping up a table of proper dishes was no trouble at all.","He Zhiran went with the women to prepare food, while Mo Jiuye and Mo Chuhan accompanied Meng Huaining in the room to chat.","Meng Huaining looked around the Mo family's current lodgings. Though the house was a little shabby, at least it could keep out wind and rain.","\"Elder Brothers, is your family comfortably settled here?\"","\"It's great here. Other than the Cui clan, the other two clans are very amiable. Compared to the gossip and drama of the capital, this place is much more peaceful.\" Mo Jiuye said.","\"Elder Brother speaks true. I also aspire to such a life.\"","Meng Huaining was speaking his true thoughts. If not for his whole family's hopes resting on him, he would be too lazy to work for such an incompetent emperor.","He turned to Mo Chuhan and asked, \"When will Eldest Brother finish handling affairs back home? My yamen is short on manpower since I just arrived in Yuncheng.\"","Mo Chuhan had originally thought to stay home longer to help his younger brother and sister-in-law.","But he could see that his younger brother and sister-in-law were extremely capable in handling matters, and didn't really need his help at all.","Since that was the case, it would be better to report for duty at the yamen earlier. No matter how little, he could still earn some income for the family. Also, the position of Chief Constable was a supervisor role in the yamen and came with some status. Having such an identity would help the family in many ways.","\"If Brother Meng needs me, I can report for duty anytime.\"","Meng Huaining was overjoyed to hear this. \"In that case, Eldest Brother, come to the yamen tomorrow to report in. I'll have Meng An make all the arrangements.\"","\"Alright, I'll be there on time tomorrow morning.\"","After settling Mo Chuhan's employment, Mo Jiuye brought up the mountain and the wastelands up north.","\"Brother Meng, I have one more matter to trouble you with.\"","Meng Huaining politely replied, \"No trouble at all. Brother Jiu, just tell me anything I can help with. As long as it's within my ability, I will certainly assist you.\"","\"Let me be frank, my wife and I have our eyes on the mountain behind the village, as well as some of the wastelands. We wish to purchase them.\"","Meng Huaining knew the Mo family had already bought quite a bit of land from the villagers, as he had personally helped process the paperwork.","At the time, he wondered why the Mo family, with just over a dozen people, mostly women, were buying so much farmland. How could they work it all?","Not only that, the Mo family had also purchased many dilapidated compounds.","In Meng Huaining's opinion, even if they had money to spare, such spending was frivolous.","Later, he conjectured for himself that the Mo family was buying so much land in order to hire laborers to farm it, just like those wealthy households with their manors and estates. All were worked by hired hands rather than the owners themselves.","Therefore, the Mo family must have similar ideas for buying up so much land."]},{"number":221,"title":"Chapter 221: Nothing short of bottomless indulgence.","paragraphs":["Furthermore, regarding those abandoned courtyards, it's possible that they considered the fact that there are nine family members living in the house. Regardless of the size of the population, if the family decides to separate in the future, having more houses would be beneficial.","However, just when he finally understood the reason why Mo Jiuye bought so much land and courtyards, Mo Jiuge dropped another bombshell.","\"Jiuge, what's the use of buying that barren mountain? It can't be used for growing crops.\"","Mo Jiuye knew that as soon as he mentioned buying a mountain, the other party would have such thoughts.","Anyway, the things they would do in the future would have to come to light, and there was no need to keep it a secret.","\"My wife made an agreement with that foreigner. The next time he comes, he will bring some specialty fruit trees from their hometown. It is said that many of those fruit trees grow on the mountainside, so I plan to buy a piece of mountain to try cultivation.\"","As he explained, not only did Meng Huaining fail to understand, but even Mo Chuhan also disagreed.","\"Jiudi, I know that Jiumei's maternal family gave her a considerable amount of money before she was exiled. With that money, you should save some for future needs. Besides, even if those foreigner's fruit tree saplings do come, it's uncertain whether they can be successfully planted in the northwest's climate.\"","Mo Jiuye couldn't explain too much about this matter. Only he knew that the fruit tree seeds in his wife's space didn't care about climate or soil quality.","\"Baoge, if Ranan likes them, then let her have her way this time.\"","Speaking like this, his younger brother pampering his wife, what could he, as the older brother, say?","Mo Chuhan wisely kept his mouth shut.","Seeing that Mo Jiuye had already said so much, Meng Huaining, as an outsider, didn't feel the need to advise him any further.","\"The government has always had regulations that set the selling price of mountains the same as wasteland, which is one or two silver coins per mu. But Jiuge, you can rest assured, when my people come to survey, we'll add some water.\"","In any case, this was all he could do. Hopefully, your fruit can be successfully cultivated.\"","\"And also, when Meng Brothers send people to survey the barren land in the north, they can measure it as well,\" Mo Jiuye continued.","\"That's not a problem. I'll send people to survey it tomorrow.\"","After a pause, Meng Huaining couldn't help but ask.","\"Jiuge, with you buying so much barren land, it won't be productive for several years. Why not wait until the Cui family sells their fertile land before making a move?\"","Mo Jiuye understood that Meng Huaining's words were all for his own good.","If it were someone else buying so much unproductive barren land, he would also have such doubts.","Since today's conversation had reached this point, Mo Jiuye didn't intend to conceal anything.","\"My wife bought some high-yielding crop seeds from that foreigner. It is said that these seeds don't care about soil quality, so she wants to give them a try, and naturally, I support her.\"","It's Jiudi again...","Meng Huaining had already noticed it when they first met. Mo Jiuye dotes on his wife, but now it seems that it's not just doting anymore.","It's simply unbounded indulgence!","Looking at Mo Jiuye's resolute attitude, Meng Huaining instantly swallowed the words he wanted to advise.","\"Since Jiuge thinks it's suitable, then go ahead and plant them...\"","Mo Jiuye knew deep down that even though Meng Huaining said this, he still didn't agree with it.","No matter what others think, Ran Ran has always let the facts speak for themselves.","As for the dilapidated houses of the Cui family at the foot of the mountain, it won't be long before their relatives come knocking on their door, begging them to buy them.","After all, it's no secret that they purchased the houses of the Zhao and Zhou families.","It's believed that only he would spend money to buy such rundown houses.","The few of them chatted in the room for a while, and then the elder sister-in-law and the second sister-in-law came in with freshly brewed tea made by Ran Ran.","It was the first time they had brewed tea at home. The tea leaves came from Ran Ran's space, where she grew Biluochun tea on the mountains of her farm and processed it using the operation platform. The taste was incomparable to ordinary Biluochun tea.","Especially in this era, tea processing techniques were outdated, and there was no such tea as Biluochun.","When her Biluochun tea was brought out, it was definitely the finest of the finest.","They hadn't had the chance to buy furniture yet, so they all sat on the kang (a heated brick bed).","The elder sister-in-law and the second sister-in-law placed the tea by the edge of the kang.","The tea set looked quite new; it was a set of relatively inexpensive antique-style tea utensils that Ran Ran purchased on Taobao.","Mo Jiuye took the teapot and poured the tea. As soon as the tea started to flow, the room was filled with the fragrance.","Mo Chuhan and Meng Huaining both came from noble families, so they were no strangers to judging the quality of tea.","\"Great tea...\" Meng Huaining, whose lifelong hobby was tea tasting, couldn't help but praise when he smelled the tea's fragrance.","\"Ninth Brother, did you buy this tea from foreigners?\" He said this because during the Great Shun Dynasty, they hadn't come across such good tea.","The tea leaves in the water were tender green, obviously the most delicate part carefully selected.","One could imagine the preciousness of this tea.","Mo Chuhan was more direct; he naturally had to taste the finest tea first.","It was the first time Mo Jiuye had tasted tea produced from his wife's space. Seeing the impatience in both of them, he lifted the tea cup and made a gesture of invitation.","\"Eighth Brother and Brother Meng, why don't you give this tea a try?\"","As soon as he finished speaking, both of them took a sip.","\"It has a fragrant and elegant taste, smooth and refreshing, with a rich and mellow flavor that lingers and a sweet and aromatic aftertaste.\" Meng Huaining gave a series of evaluations.","Mo Chuhan nodded repeatedly. \"Indeed, it's excellent tea, refreshing and with an aftertaste.\"","The elder sister-in-law and the second sister-in-law had also tasted some when Ran Ran brewed the tea. They both felt that it was the best tea they had ever tasted in their lives.","Therefore, they didn't rush to leave after bringing the tea; they wanted to see the men's reactions.","Sure enough, their expectations were met. How could anyone not like such tea?","The second sister-in-law smiled and said, \"Ninth Sister-in-law is generous. If it were someone else, they wouldn't want to share such good tea.\"","The elder sister-in-law chimed in, \"Yes, according to Ninth Sister-in-law, she only has two packets of this tea, and once they're finished, there won't be any left.\"","Meng Huaining had originally planned to ask Ran Ran for some of this good tea before leaving, but when he heard what the two sisters-in-law said, he immediately felt discouraged.","Others only had two packets, and he really couldn't bring himself to ask for any.","Da Sao and Er Sao had no idea what Meng Huaining was thinking. Their intention in speaking like that was simply to ask for a favor for their ninth sister-in-law.","Now that their purpose had been achieved, the two of them had no intention of staying any longer. After exchanging greetings, they left.","The three of them had finished drinking an entire pot of tea but still felt unsatisfied.","Fortunately, at this moment, preparations for the meal were already underway.","As before, He Zhiran took charge of cooking, with the sisters-in-law assisting him. With the addition of so many special ingredients, it was impossible for the dishes not to be delicious.","Wu Ge, along with Liang Hao and others, went to borrow some tables and chairs from the villagers once again. Eight dishes and one soup were placed on the table, allowing everyone to once again be amazed."]},{"number":222,"title":"Chapter 222: Smallpox","paragraphs":["The brightly colored tomato scrambled eggs, tender garlic stir-fried pork, sour and spicy potato shreds, and a shredded sweet potato, spareribs with beans and corn all cooked together in one pot were all dishes that no one had seen before.","Seeing these unfamiliar dishes, not only Meng Huaining, but even the eighth and fifth brothers at home couldn't help smacking their lips.","He Zhiran also didn't intend to explain too much. She gave Mo Jiuye a look, and Mo Jiuye promptly got everyone started eating.","This first bite was no joke...Meng Huaining could no longer mind his image. He rolled up his sleeves with the Mo brothers and heartily wolfed it all down.","Only when he felt somewhat stuffed did Meng Huaining put down his chopsticks and ask, \"Ninth Brother, I haven't seen these ingredients either. They weren't also bought from the foreigners, right?\"","He knew himself that he was asking even though he knew, but he just couldn't help asking...","\"That's right, Brother Meng should eat more if he finds it delicious.\" Mo Jiuye vaguely replied.","At this moment, he had no heart to explain too much. As long as his wife's cooking tasted good, he had to eat more.","One pot of tea, one table of delicious food, and Meng Huaining even wanted to loaf around at the Mo's and not leave.","However, he still had to face reality.","After the meal, He Zhiran brewed another pot of tea for them. It wasn't until the evening that Meng Huaining reluctantly brought up taking his leave.","No matter what, Meng Huaining had helped the family a lot, so He Zhiran generously gave him a package of Bi Luo Chun tea.","For Meng Huaining, this gift was simply an unexpected favor.","He couldn't resist such good tea leaves and could only shamelessly accept them.","From now on, he would have to take special care of the Mo family to live up to this package of tea.","After sending off Meng Huaining, everyone tidied up and then returned to their rooms.","Early the next morning, Mo Chuhang got up early to go to the yamen to work.","Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran planned to buy some simple furniture for the house, so they hurried along with him in the mule cart.","Buying furniture was something He Zhiran really couldn't accomplish using the space's capabilities. After all, the style of the furniture bought in the space would seem out of place with this era if said to have been purchased.","Moreover, they would build a new house next spring, so He Zhiran planned to design the furniture herself at that time.","For now, the more simple the better for what they were using in the house, as long as it was usable.","So the two asked around for furniture shops in Yancheng and went directly there.","The style of furniture in this era was relatively simple. Apart from those wealthy families that would customize some high-end goods, what was placed in the shops were all practical and affordable pieces.","Therefore, Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran simply chose some tables, chairs, and cabinets that the house urgently needed.","With so many people in the house, even so, the two bought a huge pile.","It had been a long time since the shop owner had encountered such big customers, so he was overjoyed and even threw in a few extra small stools for them.","The shop owner was responsible for delivering the furniture to their door, they just had to clearly state the address.","After buying the furniture, there was still some time before noon, so the two wanted to stroll around town and look for news about Tang Mingrui.","They hadn't walked far when they saw the commoners in front of them all running in the opposite direction from them.","The commoners seemed to be shouting as they ran, \"Hurry, get away from that clinic!\"","Mo Jiuye didn't know what was happening. He grabbed a man running towards them and asked, \"Big brother, what happened up ahead?\"","The man glanced at Mo Jiuye and said, \"There's a smallpox patient in front of the clinic, hurry and run!\"","After speaking, the man forcefully struggled free from Mo Jiuye's grip and continued running away with the crowd.","Smallpox was no small matter in ancient times. Not only was it contagious, but it also killed many people.","Mo Jiuye solemnly said to He Zhiran, \"Ranran, you go into the space first. I had smallpox as a child and won't be infected. I'll go take a look first.\"","He Zhiran shook her head. \"Smallpox is spread through the air, droplets, and contact. I'll be fine if I'm careful.\"","Anyway, she had as much alcohol in her space as she needed and could carry out the most thorough disinfection.","As she spoke, He Zhiran had already pulled Mo Jiuye to an empty place, and the two entered the space together.","He Zhiran took out two masks, one for herself and Mo Jiuye to wear.","In addition, medical gloves were also necessary protective measures. As for protective clothing and such, it would be too ostentatious to wear out, so she temporarily gave up on that for now.","They could thoroughly disinfect with alcohol when they got home later.","Mo Jiuye understood clearly that if he didn't let Ranran participate in such matters, she would definitely not be willing.","So he could only indulge her.","After simply protecting themselves, the two flashed out of the space.","At this time, no one could be seen on the street. They had probably all run far away.","The two walked in the direction of the clinic.","They saw a young man sitting limply in front of the clinic door, holding a little girl in his arms who didn't look older than ten.","The two were not unfamiliar with this young man. It was none other than Tang Mingrui, whom they had intended to look for.","Tang Mingrui's face was full of decadence, and the light in his eyes was also gone.","Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran strode over.","\"Brother Tang, what on earth happened?\"","Although the two people coming towards him had strange things on their faces, Tang Mingrui recognized them with one glance.","\"Big Brother Mo, Big Sister Mo.\"","Tang Mingrui's voice carried sobs.","\"My sister broke out in red blisters on her body. I brought her here for treatment, but unexpectedly, she has smallpox...\"","He Zhiran didn't hurry to speak, but carefully observed the little girl Tang Mingrui held in his arms.","The little girl did have many red rashes on her face, but however you looked at them, they didn't seem like smallpox.","The lesions from smallpox were relatively deep, but the blisters on the little girl's face were very clearly floating above the outer layer of skin.","To further confirm her judgment, He Zhiran walked forward a few steps and squatted in front of the little girl.","She tentatively reached out to touch the blisters on the little girl's face.","Tang Mingrui and Mo Jiuye moved at the same time.","\"Ranran, you can't touch her!\" Mo Jiuye shouted loudly before rushing forward to grab her.","Tang Mingrui hugged his sister and scooted back, \"Sister Mo, it's dangerous!\"","He Zhiran first said to Mo Jiuye, \"I suspect she doesn't have smallpox.\"","Mo Jiuye was surprised. He had also just seen that the rash on the little girl was the same as when he had smallpox, so how could it not be smallpox?","\"Ranran, if it's not smallpox, what could it be?\"","\"I suspect she has chickenpox.\"","\"Chickenpox?\" Mo Jiuye and Tang Mingrui asked at the same time.","He Zhiran could only patiently explain, \"The symptoms of chickenpox are somewhat similar to smallpox, but it's not as severe. I guarantee I can cure her.\"","Mo Jiuye understood his wife would never say anything she wasn't confident about.","He Zhiran felt the grip on her relax. She struggled free and came before the little girl again. Her gloved fingers gently touched one of the more prominent blisters on her face.","He Zhiran's face immediately revealed a smile."]},{"number":223,"title":"Chapter 223: Hardly Life-threatening","paragraphs":["From her expression, Mo Jiuye and Tang Mingrui both guessed the good news.","Tang Mingrui eagerly asked, \"Sister-in-law Mo, my sister doesn't have smallpox, right?\"","He Zhiran nodded, \"Yes, she indeed doesn't have smallpox.\"","After a pause, she continued, \"However, this kind of illness is also contagious. With proper treatment, it basically won't endanger life.\"","Hearing her words, Tang Mingrui heaved a big sigh of relief.","Just as he was about to ask He Zhiran about the treatment, an old doctor walked over to the clinic entrance.","The old doctor looked rather knowledgeable. With a mask covering his face, he stopped about five to six meters away from them.","\"Young lady, aren't you tired of living? Let me advise you, stay away from them, lest you get yourself in trouble.\"","He Zhiran knew his words were for her own good.","\"Are you the doctor here?\" He Zhiran stood up and looked straight at the other party.","The old doctor nodded, \"I'm the doctor of this clinic. Young lady, listen to my advice and leave quickly!\"","He Zhiran had already confirmed that the girl's illness was not smallpox, so she naturally had to explain clearly to avoid causing panic in the city.","\"Doctor, she doesn't have smallpox. See, the blisters on her face are superficial and completely different from smallpox.\"","The old doctor didn't believe He Zhiran's words at all. Having practiced medicine for most of his life, how could he not recognize smallpox?","This young woman actually dared to say this wasn't smallpox in front of him, simply preposterous.","The old doctor didn't plan on explaining too much. Fortunately, he had only glanced at the girl and didn't have close contact.","Just now, he had already sent his apprentice out the back door to report the smallpox outbreak in the city to the county magistrate. Now he just had to close the shop and brew some herbal supplements to drink, and he would definitely get through this smallpox epidemic safely.","Seeing the old doctor close the clinic door, he must not have believed her words.","Whether others believed her or not didn't matter. In any case, she must save the Tang girl's life.","\"Young Master Tang, take your sister home first. I guarantee I can cure her illness.\"","Hearing this, Tang Mingrui was so emotional he almost cried.","There were only a few family members who had escaped, and if his sister died again, he would lose another loved one.","\"Thank you, Sister-in-law Mo. I'll take you to my home in Yun City right away.\"","Mo Jiuye led the mule cart over. Together with Tang Mingrui, they headed to his family home in Yun City.","Tang Mingrui had earned some silver from his puppet business with He Zhiran, and found the right opportunity to earn a little more money along the way.","By the time he arrived in Yun City, he already had over a thousand taels of silver.","Houses in Yun City weren't expensive. He spent 500 taels to buy a very large courtyard in the city center for his family to live in.","He had already inquired about the specific location of the Mo family manor at the yamen, intending to pay them a visit after getting his family settled in.","He didn't expect his sister to break out in rashes just as everything was properly arranged.","Fortunately he met He Zhiran today, otherwise if the old doctor had really diagnosed his sister with smallpox, he would surely have reported it to the government.","Once the government knew, they would definitely take his sister and the whole family away for isolation.","If they encountered good officials it would be fine, but if they met those kinds of officials who didn't care for commoners, they might even directly kill them...","Thinking of this, Tang Mingrui felt terrified in hindsight.","After about a quarter hour, the mule cart arrived at Tang Mingrui's home.","At this moment, neither Mo Jiuye nor He Zhiran were in the mood to admire the Tang family courtyard. They followed Tang Mingrui straight to the little girl's room in the back.","Seeing her son carrying her daughter back, Lady Tang came out to greet them with the whole family.","\"Mingrui, how is Mingxin?\"","Right now, Tang Mingrui couldn't be bothered to explain much to his mother.","\"Mother, my sister is fine. Sister-in-law Mo can treat her.\"","Speaking, Tang Mingrui had already carried Tang Mingxin into the room.","Lady Tang had met Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran on the way to the northwest, so they were not strangers to each other.","She knew saving her daughter was the priority now, and just politely nodded to them.","The best way to treat Tang Mingxin's chickenpox was western medicine combined with IV infusion.","IV infusion was out of the question in this era, so they could only choose western medicine.","She had plenty of western medicine in her space, and could buy more on Taobao if needed, so there was no need to worry about that.","He Zhiran carefully examined Tang Mingxin's condition, then got up.","\"There is medicine in the cart. I'll take it out now for the little girl to take.\"","The cart was parked in the front yard of the Tang residence. He Zhiran went straight into the carriage.","She entered her space with her mind, and prepared various drugs to treat Tang Mingxin's chickenpox.","She specifically prepared capsule drugs, peeled off the outer coating and repackaged them in oil paper so they wouldn't seem suspicious when taken out.","With the medicine prepared, He Zhiran returned to Tang Mingxin's room.","She handed Tang Mingrui several small paper packages.","\"These medicines are self-formulated, perfect for treating the little girl's illness.\"","Tang Mingrui gratefully accepted the medicine He Zhiran gave and fed it to his sister as she instructed.","He Zhiran observed Tang Mingxin for a while. Her fever had subsided by now.","She asked some questions, and Tang Mingxin said she felt fine except for lack of strength.","This showed Tang Mingxin's condition was under control as long as she took the medicine on time.","\"In the next few days, the little girl should stay in bed and rest, reduce activity as much as possible, and she will recover in about ten days.\"","Hearing her words, the Tang family unanimously breathed a sigh of relief.","To be safe, He Zhiran and Mo Jiuye did not leave the Tang residence immediately, intending to observe a while longer before leaving.","Lady Tang hurried to prepare lunch.","Since the two were rather hungry, they did not stand on ceremony.","Until near dusk, Tang Mingxin's condition remained very stable, and He Zhiran was finally at ease.","\"It's getting late, we won't disturb you further. We're currently staying in Xi Ling Village. When the little girl gets better, you're welcome to visit us at home.\"","Lady Tang and Tang Mingrui saw them to the door.","Just as they reached the entrance, they saw a group of officials with cloth covering their noses and mouths going door to door on the street.","At this moment, two of them happened to be walking towards the Tang residence.","One of the officials was not a stranger to Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran, it was Ma Junshan.","Ma Junshan's attitude was more polite than usual when he saw them.","\"Master Mo, Madam Mo, why are you still in the city?\"","With such a big incident in the city, the commoners from the surrounding villages had fled home early, afraid of being trapped if the city gates closed.","Seeing the officials going door to door, they had guessed the government already knew someone had smallpox and were looking for them everywhere.","\"Are you looking for those who have contracted smallpox?\"","\"That's right.\" Ma Junshan was anxious to finish his errand and go rest, so he simply replied and was about to search the Tang residence."]},{"number":224,"title":"Chapter 224: It Was an Own Mistake","paragraphs":["Mo Jiuye stopped him.","\"There's no need to go in. The person you are looking for is in this courtyard.\"","Ma Junshan was stunned for a moment, then asked somewhat puzzledly: \"Ninth... Ninth Lord, that's smallpox... How can you stay so boldly here?\"","He Zhiran explained: \"The little girl didn't get smallpox at all. The doctor at the clinic misdiagnosed her.\"","Ma Junshan was instantly dumbfounded, with his mouth wide open, not knowing what to say.","After a long time, he asked: \"Is what the Ninth Lady said true?\"","He Zhiran nodded: \"It's true.\"","Ma Junshan was so happy he almost jumped up.","\"I'll go back right away to give this good news to my master.\"","After he finished speaking, Ma Junshan pulled his companion, who was still dazed on the spot, and ran away like smoke.","Seeing Ma Junshan, Mo Chuhan must also be busy with this matter.","Mo Jiuye discussed with He Zhiran for a while. They would go to the yamen to see, and go home together with Eighth Brother.","The two of them headed towards the yamen on a mule cart.","Along the way, there were almost no people to be seen. Every household had their doors closed tightly, as if the end of the world was about to come.","The mule cart was faster than walking. When He Zhiran and Mo Jiuye arrived at the yamen, Ma Junshan hadn't arrived yet.","At the moment, Meng Huaining was a little frustrated. It wasn't that he lacked governing ability, but when faced with such epidemics, he really couldn't think of a perfect solution.","In order to prevent the spread of smallpox, he could only order the city to be sealed off, so as to prevent smallpox from spreading to more places.","Not only that, as soon as he received the news, he had ordered people to go to the prefectural yamen. With such a big thing happening, it must be reported upwards.","All the officials had been sent out to handle affairs, and only Meng Huaining was left in the yamen.","When Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran arrived here, they walked in directly without needing to announce themselves.","Seeing them, Meng Huaining hurriedly came up to greet them.","\"Ninth Brother Mo, Sister-in-law, why are you still in the city?\"","After receiving the news, he had sealed off the city. That was already in the morning.","Currently, no one was allowed to enter or leave Yun City, which meant that the two of them had entered the city early in the morning, but still hadn't left at this time.","The two of them knew that Meng Huaining was in an anxious state at the moment. He Zhiran quickly explained: \"Brother Meng, it is pure nonsense that someone in the city has contracted smallpox.\"","\"Nonsense? What does Sister-in-law mean?\" The news Meng Huaining received was from the clinic. It couldn't be wrong. How could Big Sister Mo say this?","\"The little girl who the doctor diagnosed with smallpox, I have examined her. She didn't get smallpox at all, but another disease called chickenpox.","Chickenpox looks very similar to smallpox. It's not surprising at all that the clinic doctor misdiagnosed it.\"","Upon hearing this, Meng Huaining didn't even bother asking if He Zhiran understood medicine. Just based on the medicine she gave him to treat the plague, it was enough to prove her skills.","\"Is what Sister-in-law said true?\"","He Zhiran solemnly nodded: \"Of course it's true. I've already given medicine to the little girl to treat her illness. I believe it won't be long before she recovers.\"","Mo Jiuye was worried that Meng Huaining didn't believe his wife's words, so he added: \"What my wife said is all true. She has been studying medicine since childhood and would definitely not misdiagnose this.\"","In fact, Meng Huaining had never doubted He Zhiran's words at all. In his heart, he had an inexplicable trust in the Mo family.","\"In that case, I will immediately order the blockade on Yun City to be lifted.\"","As they were talking, Ma Junshan also ran back panting, together with an official.","Seeing that Mo Jiuye and his wife were there, Ma Junshan figured the explanation didn't need to come from him.","Seeing someone return, Meng Huaining hurriedly ordered: \"Ma Junshan, go to the prefecture at top speed immediately and tell the Prefect that the smallpox in Yun City was a misdiagnosis.\"","Hopefully the Prefect hadn't submitted his memo yet. Otherwise they'd have to send people to chase it down on the road.","Not long after Ma Junshan had just left upon receiving the order, an official brought over several worried-looking doctors.","\"My Lord, the Prefect has sent over some doctors.\" The official reported.","Meng Huaining just glanced at those doctors and knew that they must have been forced to come.","When faced with smallpox, a highly contagious disease that was hard to cure, coming here was a dead end.","There were historical records of a severely smallpox-stricken county where even the commoners who were not sick were trapped alive inside.","Therefore, upon hearing about smallpox in Yun City, Meng Huaining had already prepared for the worst.","He didn't expect this to be a false alarm.","\"Doctors, thank you for the trouble. This official will have someone send you back soon.\"","The doctors were puzzled. They had already prepared themselves for death before coming to Yun City, and had even tied up loose ends.","But what did the county magistrate say?","He was going to send them back?","\"My Lord, are you really sending us back?\" A slightly younger doctor asked in disbelief.","Meng Huaining nodded: \"It has been verified now that there is no smallpox outbreak in Yun City.\"","After speaking, he ordered the officials: \"Send these doctors back now!\"","For a moment, the doctors felt as if they were hallucinating. Some even dug hard at their ears.","Eventually they confirmed that this was not a dream.","The officials were also somewhat puzzled, but the magistrate's words were indisputable. They beckoned to the doctors and went out.","At the same time, at the prefectural yamen in the prefectural city.","A man in brocade robes was pacing back and forth with his hands behind his back in the study.","Feng Prefect earnestly advised: \"Your Highness Rui Wang, Yun City is too dangerous. This insignificant official implores you to reconsider!\"","Nan Rui waved his hand: \"Feng Daren need not say more. This is my Great Shun's land. Even if I was in the capital right now and heard such news, I would still ask my Royal Father for permission to come and provide relief.","Now I am only a stone's throw away from Yun City. How can I just stand by and watch?\"","Feng Prefect was already sweating profusely.","He had just taken office here, and such a big incident happened. Fortunately, it just so happened that Prince Rui who had just arrived stumbled upon it.","If anything untoward happened to Prince Rui because of this, not to mention his own official position, even his own life would be lost.","However, seeing the Prince's resolute attitude, Feng Prefect knew that persuasion would be futile.","\"Your Highness, if that's the case, this insignificant official is willing to accompany you to Yun City.\"","\"No need. I will go alone.\"","The things he came here to do absolutely could not see the light of day. The fewer people around him the better, how could he possibly bring Feng Prefect along?","Upon hearing this, Feng Prefect instantly relaxed.","He knew how much courage it took for him to say that he would accompany Prince Rui. Now that the Prince didn't need him to accompany him, his life was temporarily still safe...","Nan Rui looked at the sky, and loudly ordered outside: \"Prepare a horse. Follow me to Yun City.\"","This trip to the northwest was not a public action to begin with. If not for Yun City being sealed off, and him not knowing what was going on, Nan Rui would not have shown up at the Prefectural Yamen at all."]},{"number":225,"title":"Chapter 225: It's not easy that I'm still alive.","paragraphs":["Before leaving, Nan Rui warned in a deep voice, \"Prefect Feng, this prince's trip is only for leisure. Please forget about seeing me today.\"","Prefect Feng nodded repeatedly, \"Your Highness, please rest assured.\"","Nan Rui glanced at Prefect Feng again, giving him a warning look, before departing with his entourage.","When he arrived at Yun City, the city gate had already been ordered to be opened by Meng Huaining, which puzzled Nan Rui.","Upon entering the city, Nan Rui went straight to the county office.","With such a significant incident happening in Yun City, even though it was just a misunderstanding, as the prince of Da Shun, he needed to carefully understand the situation.","\"Come with me to the county office first,\" Nan Rui instructed his subordinates.","\"Yes,\" the subordinates responded and dispersed around Nan Rui, providing protection.","Nan Rui walked along the streets and arrived at the county office.","At this moment, Mo Chuhan had just returned with a group of officials and was preparing to go out and inform the people that there was no smallpox. Unexpectedly, as soon as he reached the entrance, he encountered Nan Rui.","Mo Chuhan immediately became vigilant. Ninth Brother had speculated that he was once among the assassins sent by Nan Rui to kill Ninth Brother.","In other words, even if Nan Rui wasn't the one who gave him the puppetry gu, he was still involved.","Therefore, when Mo Chuhan saw Nan Rui, not only did his vigilance rise, but his anger surged.","Nan Rui recognized Mo Chuhan at a glance. He didn't expect to encounter him here by chance. However, he was unaware of Mo Chuhan's current situation, so he didn't act recklessly.","After a moment of hesitation, Mo Chuhan still saluted Nan Rui.","After all, before tearing each other's faces apart, when meeting the current prince, it was necessary to maintain a superficial courtesy.","\"Why has Prince Rui come here?\" Mo Chuhan asked.","Nan Rui furrowed his brow slightly. If the mother gu he held in his hand encountered the child gu, there would definitely be a reaction. However, being in such close contact with Mo Chuhan, there was no reaction at all.","While feeling puzzled, Nan Rui raised his hand towards Mo Chuhan and said, \"Mo... no need for formalities.\"","Nan Rui initially wanted to say \"General Mo, no need for formalities,\" but when he thought about the misfortune that had befallen the Mo family, he didn't know how to address Mo Chuhan.","Mo Chuhan quickly straightened up without saying anything, intending to let Nan Rui take the initiative in the conversation.","At the same time, the group of officials behind him were dumbfounded.","The fact that the Chief Constable Mo had just called the person in front of them Prince Rui left them unsure how to act. They even forgot the basic courtesy of kneeling and bowing.","Nan Rui once again observed Mo Chuhan and saw him dressed in the official uniform of the Chief Constable. Out of curiosity, Nan Rui asked, \"Are you working in the yamen now?\"","Mo Chuhan didn't dare to tell the truth for fear of implicating Meng Huaining.","\"The county magistrate doesn't know my identity. I just wanted to find a job to support my family,\" Mo Chuhan replied.","Regardless of whether Nan Rui believed him or not, he didn't pursue the matter further.","At present, what concerned him the most was why he couldn't control Mo Chuhan with his mother gu.","When he was talking to Mo Chuhan just now, Nan Rui attempted to manipulate the gu, but to his surprise, Mo Chuhan showed no reaction at all.","He couldn't figure out what went wrong. If it weren't for his intervention, Mo Chuhan's puppetry gu would be impossible to remove.","\"Your body?\" Nan Rui intended to ask Mo Chuhan something.","At this moment, Mo Chuhan was certain that there was a direct connection between the puppet gu curse he was afflicted with and Nan Rui.","With this in mind, Mo Chuhan no longer wanted to continue beating around the bush with Nan Rui. He thought that even if it meant going all out and risking everything, he didn't regard the dozen or so guards accompanying Nan Rui as a threat.","Considering this, Mo Chuhan sneered, \"Thanks to His Royal Highness Ruiwang's gift, it's truly not easy for me to stay alive.\"","Nan Rui's expression immediately changed upon hearing his words.","\"What do you know?\"","Mo Chuhan first glanced at the several government officials behind him. He surmised that Nan Rui's purpose in coming here was because of him.","Even though his Mo family had already been exiled, it wasn't appropriate to bring up such matters openly. However, Nan Rui had brazenly asked about it.","If he were also so careless and blurted it out in front of those government officials, their little conspiracy would be exposed in an instant.","\"Does Wangye really intend to discuss it here?\"","Reminded in this way, Nan Rui realized that there weren't just the guards he brought along, but also those government officials present. He had indeed been careless.","Nan Rui immediately turned around. \"Come with me.\"","Mo Chuhan dismissed the scared government officials and followed closely behind Nan Rui as they left.","The two of them went straight to a nearby restaurant and requested a private room.","Facing Nan Rui, Mo Chuhan showed no courtesy and seated himself directly.","Nan Rui wasn't offended either and sat across from him, lost in thought for a moment before speaking up.","\"I came to the northwest this time to find you.\"","Mo Chuhan wasn't surprised when he heard him say that.","\"I wonder what business Ruiwang has with me?\"","Nan Rui didn't intend to beat around the bush either and placed a small porcelain bottle he held in his hand on the table.","\"This bottle contains the mother gu of a puppet gu.\"","Mo Chuhan raised an eyebrow, knowingly asking, \"What does that have to do with me?\"","Nan Rui shook his head helplessly, wearing a bitter smile.","\"In fact, you know everything, so why does Wangye have to spell it out so clearly?\"","Mo Chuhan sneered and didn't plan to play dumb any longer.","\"As a man of the Mo family, I shed blood on the battlefield to protect the Da Shun territory. Now, we've been reduced to being exiled. Can we still pose a threat to anyone?\"","Nan Rui hurriedly explained upon hearing this, \"You've misunderstood. I didn't come here with any ill intentions toward the Mo family.\"","\"In that case, I'll take my leave now.\" Mo Chuhan stood up, intending to leave.","Since it wasn't harmful to the Mo family, regardless of Ruiwang's intentions, he didn't want to entertain him.","As for the matter of being cured by his ninth younger sister, he had no intention of explaining it to Nan Rui.","Nan Rui saw that Mo Chuhan really intended to leave and quickly stood up to stop him.","\"I'm also being coerced. Please sit down and let me finish speaking.\"","Mo Chuhan glanced at Nan Rui askew and sat back down reluctantly.","Nan Rui organized his thoughts and began, \"Although the mother gu is currently in my hands, the puppet gu on your body was not placed by me.\"","You should know that my mother, the consort, was not favored, so I have always felt insignificant in the palace since I was young. I am well aware that I lack the talent to be an emperor, so I have deliberately avoided getting involved in court disputes.","Despite that, someone has targeted me.\"","As he spoke, Nan Rui raised the porcelain bottle in his hand to show Mo Chuhan.","\"This is the former owner of this Gu poison. He used my mother as leverage to force me to do his bidding. Anything you have seen or heard related to me is not of my own volition.\"","Just as Nan Rui finished speaking, there was a knock on the door, and a guard entered to report, \"Prince, Lord Mo Jiuye and his wife have arrived.\"","Nan Rui didn't expect Mo Jiuye to come at this moment."]},{"number":226,"title":"Chapter 226: Didn't you give me the puppets","paragraphs":["Mo Jiuye learned from the officials that Eight Brother had left with Prince Rui, and immediately went after them with He Zhiran.","Prince Rui ordered the guards to invite them in.","Mo Jiuye's eyes were cold as he said solemnly, \"Greetings to Prince Rui.\" His words were polite, but his tone held no respect at all. He didn't even bother to bow.","He Zhiran had never cared much for the etiquette of this era to begin with. She stood beside Mo Jiuye without moving, not even opening her mouth.","Prince Rui glanced at the two of them, then made a welcoming gesture. \"Please sit.\"","Mo Jiuye pulled He Zhiran to sit unceremoniously next to Eight Brother.","His hearing was excellent. When he had asked the guard to announce them to Prince Rui outside the door earlier, he had already overheard snippets of the conversation inside the room.","When dealing with someone who was likely an enemy, Mo Jiuye held nothing back with his words. \"Based on what Prince Rui just said, the puppet worm in my Eight Brother was indeed your doing?\"","Faced with Mo Jiuye's question, Prince Rui was quite frank. \"I can only say I'm involved.\"","Mo Jiuye raised an eyebrow. \"So you didn't put the puppet worm in my Eight Brother?\"","Prince Rui shook his head and smiled wryly. \"I didn't, but now that the mother worm is in my hands, I'm implicated regardless.\"","Seeing that was Prince Rui's response, Mo Jiuye decided to hear his explanation before interrupting.","Prince Rui continued, \"Five years ago, I went on an outing to the suburbs with some staff. On the way, a mysterious man appeared and scattered some poisonous powder right in front of me. The people with me all fainted from the poison, but I was unaffected.\"","Mo Jiuye asked, \"Why?\"","Prince Rui gave a bitter laugh. \"I've had a unique constitution since childhood that makes me immune to worms and poisons, so I didn't fall victim.\"","\"What happened after?\" Mo Jiuye intended to hear the full story before commenting.","\"Afterwards, the mysterious man knocked me out and took me away. When I woke up, I was in a basement.","There were many skilled guards watching me, so I couldn't escape. It wasn't until a day later that the mysterious man appeared again.","He told me that he had used worms on my Imperial Mother. If I didn't do as he said, he would use the worms to torment her.","Knowing I didn't believe him, he sent me directly to the palace to visit my mother. Within three hours, my mother would suffer agonizing worm bites all over her body. If I wanted her to live, I had to go to Wangpo Pavilion twenty li south of the capital to find him after that happened.","I rushed back to the palace as fast as I could, and found that my mother was suffering exactly as the mysterious man had described, her whole body writhing as if from worm bites. It was a fate worse than death.","To save my mother, I didn't dare hesitate. I hurried to Wangpo Pavilion where the man was indeed waiting, just as he'd said.\"","As he spoke, the pain in Prince Rui's eyes grew clearer.","\"The man took out a white porcelain bottle again, and told me this contained the mother worm controlling my mother. Whether she lived or died was now in my hands.","I asked what he wanted me to do. The mysterious man said I had to obey his every order, or he would crush the mother worm and kill my mother.","To save my mother's life, I had no choice but to compromise for the time being, while I looked for a way to get the worm out of her.\"","Hearing this, the three listeners had countless questions arise in their minds.","Mo Jiuye asked, \"What did he make you do?\"","Speaking of this brought a look of shame to Prince Rui's face.","\"He told me to get close with people from the Ministry of War. I'm not skilled in forming factions and plotting privately. I found out that He Zhiyuan's concubine had borne him a daughter, so I set my sights there...\"","This completely confirmed what He Zhiyuan had told them. The one behind everything was indeed Prince Rui, just as they'd suspected.","\"So you were the one who had He Zhiyuan withhold supplies from the Border Pass soldiers?\"","Seeing that the Mo brothers were glaring at him like tigers eyeing prey, Prince Rui felt a chill down his spine.","But since he had chosen to come here, he was prepared for the consequences. He had no intention of shirking responsibility.","\"Yes, I told him to do that.\"","Mo Chuhan slammed the table and jumped to his feet.","\"Prince Rui, you are an imperial prince of the Da Shun Dynasty. How could you do something like this?\"","Prince Rui didn't call anyone in to restrain Mo Chuhan as expected. Instead, he explained,","\"I openly told He Zhiyuan to withhold supplies, while secretly tipping off Nan Qi. I knew if something happened, the Mo Family would never just stand by.\"","Mo Chuhan was hot-tempered by nature. Even with this explanation, he still didn't look pleased.","\"That doesn't erase your crimes.\"","\"I know I'm guilty. Once I find someone who can remove the worm from my mother, my wish will be fulfilled. When that time comes, I'll accept whatever you brothers decide to do with me.\" Prince Rui said sincerely.","Mo Chuhan gave a cold snort. \"Hmph! As mere commoners, what right do we have to deal with an imperial prince of Da Shun?\"","Mo Jiuye still had many questions. He pulled Eight Brother's sleeve to signal him to keep calm.","Seeing Eight Brother sit back down and fall silent, Mo Jiuye asked,","\"What about the puppet worm in my Eight Brother?\"","When it came to the puppet worm in Mo Chuhan, Prince Rui took the initiative to hand over the bottle to the brothers.","\"While searching for ways to remove the worm from my mother, I privately found many books related to worm techniques, so I gained some understanding in that area.","One day the mysterious man sent a messenger to bring me a message. The messenger wore black robes and a face covering, but his eyes were blank and dull. I could tell with one look that he was under the control of a puppet worm.","Perhaps because the will of the man in black was strong, after delivering the letter he was supposed to leave immediately but instead lingered in front of me, wandering back and forth.","Out of curiosity, I took the chance to pull down the black-robed man's face covering, and recognized him as Mo Chuhan with one glance.","I was completely shocked in that moment. As far as I knew, Mo Chuhan had died at the Border Pass, so how could he be this man's puppet?","At that time, only you, Mo Jiuye, remained of the Mo bloodline. I respect the Mo Family, so I decided to try to rescue Mo Chuhan.","Before Mo Chuhan could return to report, I hurriedly scribbled a note saying I didn't have many skilled fighters by my side and wanted Mo Chuhan to stay and help me.","I was just taking a chance with this. My mother's life was in his hands, so there was nothing I could do if he refused.","I had already given up hope and was thinking of other ways when, to my surprise, the man brought Mo Chuhan to me himself.","He said he was very satisfied with how I handled things, and I would need capable guards by my side when I ascended the Da Shun throne in the future. Therefore, he agreed to give me Mo Chuhan, and also handed over the mother worm controlling Mo Chuhan.\"","On this point, neither He Zhiran nor Mo Jiuye doubted him. When they read that book \"Compendium of Worms\", it mentioned that transferring control of a mother worm only required the worm master to make the new master drip a drop of blood."]},{"number":227,"title":"Chapter 227: I hope Mo Chu Han can follow me back to the Capital","paragraphs":["Mo Chuhan thinking that he could find this place is not surprising as he was sent to assassinate Mo Jiuye but went missing.","To confirm Nan Rui's words, He Zhiran's consciousness entered the space to check on the larval worm.","The bottle was transparent, and the situation of the larval worm inside was in full view.","That usually very quiet larval worm was strangely frantic at this moment, desperately struggling to get rid of the restraint.","Regarding this, He Zhiran was not worried at all. First, not to mention the safety level of the bottle, even if the larval worm really escaped, it would still be in her space and could not pose any threat to people outside.","It showed that the object in Nan Rui's hand was indeed the mother worm that could control the larval worm in Mo Chuhan.","He Zhiran had just withdrawn her consciousness from the space when she saw Mo Jiuye ask Nan Rui again, \"How can you make me believe your words?\"","Without thinking, Nan Rui answered, \"I don't know if anyone has sent you a message at the border, but it was me who had Mo Chuhan's grave dug up.\"","\"Why did you do that?\" Mo Jiuye asked.","\"Because I know there are many soldiers loyal to the Mo family at the border. Seeing Mo Chuhan's grave dug up, they would definitely try to inform you.\"","Regarding this, Mo Jiuye did not doubt it. After all, only Nan Rui knew that Elder Brother Hachi was alive. He could think of no other reason for doing this except to convey the news of Elder Brother Hachi being alive to him in another way.","However, Mo Jiuye was still puzzled about it.","\"Wouldn't it be more convenient to just send someone to tell me directly if you want me to know that Elder Brother Hachi is still alive?\"","Nan Rui shook his head: \"I did think of that, but with you Mo family men's temperament, in order to save your family member, you would surely rush back to the capital recklessly to rescue Mo Chuhan if I had sent a message telling you that Mo Chuhan was in my hands.","If that were the case, my previous efforts would have been in vain. Therefore, I chose to secretly dig up Mo Chuhan's grave and give you a little information before using maggots to manipulate Mo Chuhan to become a member of the assassins.","Mo Chuhan has superior martial arts. I was worried that you might not be his match. So I deliberately controlled him these days to not eat or drink to reduce his strength, just hoping that you could find something familiar in him during the fight...\"","Nan Rui's words could all be explained plausibly. Mo Jiuye continued to inquire about other things.","\"Since you put Elder Brother Hachi in the assassination team, why did you still come here looking for him?\"","This was the key.","This was indeed Nan Rui's main purpose in coming here.","\"None of the assassins in black I sent survived, which would naturally arouse that person's attention. At the same time, he also found out that Mo Chuhan was not with me.","Moreover, it could be seen from the mother worm's performance that the larval worm in Mo Chuhan was still alive and well, which meant that Mo Chuhan was still alive but just not under my control.","The previous few times, I had used sending Mo Chuhan to do things as an excuse to gloss over it, but I always felt that this was not a permanent solution. Rather than letting that person find here with the mother worm, it would be better for me to take action first.\"","\"But won't that person be suspicious of you when you come to the northwest?\" Mo Jiuye continued to ask.","\"His subordinate told me when he passed me a message that the person was busy with something important recently and would not show up for a few months. So I took the opportunity to rush to the northwest.\"","Speaking, Nan Rui began to look over Mo Chuhan again. No matter how he looked at him, he did not seem to be under the maggot's spell.","Especially just now, he had tried to control Mo Chuhan several times with the mother worm, but Mo Chuhan did not react at all.","This was also the thing that puzzled Nan Rui the most after seeing Mo Chuhan.","He wanted to ask Mo Chuhan, but considering that the latter still had great hostility towards him, even if he asked, the other party might not tell him. Therefore, Nan Rui decided to try another way.","He pointed to the porcelain bottle containing the mother worm and said, \"I can now remove Mo Chuhan's maggot, but I have a small condition.\"","Mo Chuhan knew that his Ninth Brother was better at negotiation than himself, so he did not speak.","Mo Jiuye had long seen through Nan Rui's intention. Since the puppet worm in Elder Brother Hachi had been removed, he had nothing to worry about.","\"I'd like to know your condition first.\"","Nan Rui said, \"I hope Mo Chuhan can come back to the capital with me and continue to pretend to be under the worm's spell, otherwise, if that person finds something wrong, I'm afraid I can't guarantee my mother's safety.\"","\"That's impossible,\" Mo Jiuye rejected very bluntly.","Nan Rui was a little anxious: \"Don't you want to remove Mo Chuhan's maggot?\"","Mo Jiuye sneered: \"Does my Elder Brother Hachi look like he is under the maggot's spell to you?\"","No, he did not, Nan Rui had noticed it early on.","Could it be that Mo Chuhan's maggot was removed?","In his understanding, the only way to remove the maggot was to find the breeder of the mother worm and have the breeder kill the mother worm, and then the larval worm on the other party would die as well.","But the mother worm was raised well in his hands. How was Mo Chuhan's maggot removed?","\"Do you know someone who can remove maggots?\"","Mo Jiuye did not answer but asked back, \"Who exactly is this mysterious person you mentioned?\"","Nan Rui shook his head: \"I have never seen the real face of that person. I only know that he has white hair and appears before me as a different woman every time.\"","White hair?","Woman's appearance?","This matched exactly with the appearance of Yun Li's master that she had described.","At this moment, both He Zhiran and Mo Jiuye could confirm that the person secretly controlling Nan Rui behind the scenes was the master with white hair and a young complexion mentioned by Yun Li.","\"Do you know where this person is?\" Mo Jiuye asked eagerly.","This mysterious person had harmed so many of his Mo family members. Now that there was finally some news about him, Mo Jiuye did not want to give up so easily.","Nan Rui spread his hands helplessly: \"I have only met that person three times. Every time he came and went without a trace. I really don't know where he is. And it was always him who took the initiative to send someone to contact me. If I want to find him, I can only wait for his people to come and pass on the message.\"","At this moment, Mo Jiuye no longer had any doubt about Nan Rui. If he really wanted to make trouble, there was no need for him to come to the northwest in person.","But in any case, Elder Brother Hachi could not go back to the capital with him.","Since Nan Rui could not provide any information about the mysterious person here, Mo Jiuye could only find other ways. Also, see if Third Brother could bring back good news when he returned home for the New Year.","Nan Rui did not know the whereabouts of the mysterious person, but Mo Jiuye would not give up this opportunity to obtain other information.","\"Do you know if there are any other men in my Mo family who have been controlled by that person besides my Eighth Brother?\"","Nan Rui shook his head: \"I don't know for sure, but I overheard that person say inadvertently that it would be the day he took revenge for his beloved if all the Mo men could become his puppets.\"","Nan Rui was just recounting it. As for how Mo Jiuye saw it, it had nothing to do with him.","What he cared most about now was the matter of Mo Chuhan's maggot removal.","\"Can you tell me which expert removed the maggot from Mo Chuhan?\""]},{"number":228,"title":"Chapter 228: Are You Messing with Me","paragraphs":["Mo Jiuye didn't tell Nan Rui that he couldn't afford to expose his precious wife to danger at this time.","Although Nan Rui's words were well-reasoned, he had done things that were detrimental to the Mo Family.","If he found out that Ran Ran could cure the curse, there was no guarantee that he wouldn't have ulterior motives.","\"The person who helped Eighth Brother cure the curse is an extraordinary hermit, and I don't know his whereabouts now.\"","Nan Rui became anxious upon hearing this. After finally finding someone who could cure the curse through alternative means, Mo Jiuye didn't know the person's whereabouts.","\"Can you provide me with some clues?\"","Mo Jiuye didn't want to completely shut down the possibility. If helping Nan Rui's mother resolve the curse would be beneficial to him, he would consider asking Ran Ran for help.","\"The person who helped Eighth Brother is quite eccentric, doesn't like to interact with strangers, and never reveals their true identity. If I recklessly disclose their whereabouts, it may bring trouble to the Mo Family.\"","Nan Rui sincerely promised, \"I swear, as long as you can help me find that master who can cure the curse, I will agree to whatever you ask of me.\"","Mo Jiuye didn't immediately make a decision. It was such a big matter that he had to discuss it with Ran Ran before giving a response.","\"If Prince Rui doesn't hurry to leave in the next few days, I will try to contact that extraordinary person. If there's any news, I will inform you immediately.\"","There was a reason why Mo Jiuye did this.","He wanted to find the mysterious person with graying hair and a youthful face through Nan Rui's connection. Only by finding that person could he learn about his eldest and second brother's whereabouts.","Nan Rui, seeing that Mo Jiuye was willing to help him find a solution, stood up in excitement, even forgetting his own identity as a prince.","He deeply bowed to Mo Jiuye.","\"As long as you can help my mother resolve the curse, I'm willing to do anything.\"","Many nobles in the capital knew about Nan Rui's filial devotion.","Nan Rui and his mother had not received favor in the palace since they were young, and they had relied on each other to survive until now. It was evident how strong Nan Rui's feelings were for his mother.","Mo Jiuye stood up directly. \"Three days later, at the same place, I will give Prince Rui the news.\"","\"Alright, I'll be waiting here for your good news.\"","Mo Jiuye no longer looked at Nan Rui and took Ran Ran's small hand as they stood up. \"Eighth Brother, let's go back.\"","Instead of immediately returning to Xiling Village, they went to the county government office.","At this time, Meng Huaining had already handled the aftermath of the \"Heavenly Black Dragon\" incident. When he saw them return, he arranged for a dinner.","As for Nan Rui, since he didn't come looking for him directly, Mo Jiuye simply ignored his presence.","However, Mo Jiuye politely declined. \"Thank you for your kind offer, Brother Meng, but we have been out all day, and my elderly mother must be worried. We won't disturb you here today.\"","Meng Huaining didn't insist. \"Since that's the case, let me see you off, brothers.\"","The three of them boarded a mule cart. Mo Jiuye and Mo Chuhan scanned their surroundings cautiously before directing the cart towards Xiling Village.","Nan Rui came, and although they mostly believed what he said, there was always a chance that things could go wrong.","They felt it was better to be cautious about it.","When they returned to Xiling Village, their family was indeed very worried. Old Lady Mo was accompanied by her fifth son and anxiously looked into the distance at the village entrance.","If they didn't return soon, the elderly were planning to send Mo Chongyuan to Yuncheng to search for them.","Mo Chongyuan was skilled in martial arts, so his hearing was naturally much stronger than that of an ordinary person.","When the donkey cart was still some distance from the village entrance, he heard a commotion and went forward with Old Lady Mo's support.","The donkey cart was moving quickly and soon appeared in Old Lady Mo's line of sight.","Mo Jiuye didn't have time to explain in detail. He first helped his mother into the carriage with He Zhiran, and Fifth Brother and Eighth Brother walked back home.","Inside the carriage, He Zhiran told Old Lady Mo about meeting Tang Mingrui today and the incident with the smallpox misunderstanding. After all, they came back so late, so there must be a reason.","As for Nan Rui coming to Yuncheng, He Zhiran didn't plan to tell Old Lady Mo, so as not to add to the old lady's worries.","Back at home, the furniture they bought in the city had already been delivered, and everything was properly arranged. The sisters-in-law had prepared the meals, and the whole family was waiting for their return to have dinner.","Rice Ball was originally playing with a few little rabbits in Mo Hanyue's room, but when it sensed its owner's presence, it quickly ran out, rolling and crawling.","However, when it saw He Zhiran, it didn't rush into her arms as it usually did. Instead, it came to her side and avoided looking at her.","He Zhiran couldn't help but laugh and picked up the cute little creature.","\"Rice Ball, are you angry with me?\"","Rice Ball turned its head away again, refusing to look at its owner.","He Zhiran was amused by the little creature's behavior.","\"Okay, okay, don't be angry. Can I give you something delicious later?\"","Something delicious?","Rice Ball couldn't resist the temptation of food after all. It slowly turned its round body and rubbed against its owner's arms.","After soothing the sulking cutie, He Zhiran had dinner and then entered the space with Mo Jiuye and Rice Ball.","She took out carrots, apples, and pumpkins from the warehouse for Rice Ball to eat, and then with a single thought, she sent the little creature to its exclusive bamboo forest.","Seeing that his wife had some free time, Mo Jiuye asked, \"What do you think about helping Nan Rui's mother concubine break the curse?\"","The reason he didn't immediately agree to Nan Rui was that he wanted to privately seek his wife's opinion.","If his wife didn't agree, no matter how beneficial it was for the Mo Family, he wouldn't force it.","He Zhiran could guess some of Mo Jiuye's thoughts.","\"You plan to use Nan Rui's relationship to find that person, right?\"","Mo Jiuye nodded, \"That's exactly what I have in mind.\"","\"It's fine if you think that way. If Nan Rui's mother concubine can really break the curse, he won't be under that person's control anymore, and it'll be more convenient for him to do things.","Also, if Nan Rui places his hopes on helping his mother concubine break the curse, I believe that he won't spread the Mo Family's affairs after he goes back. It can temporarily silence him.\"","\"Do you really trust Nan Rui that much?\" This was the real question that He Zhiran had in mind.","After all, she and the original host didn't know enough about Nan Rui's character. To determine whether he was a friend or foe, Mo Jiuye needed to assess it herself.","\"I carefully pondered over what Nan Rui said, and the inconsistencies in his statements don't exist. Therefore, I can conclude that what he said is true.","But this doesn't rule out the possibility that Nan Rui is intentionally using a feigned retreat as an advance. Regardless of his intentions for coming to the northwest, I only want to achieve my goals using this opportunity.","As for what happens later, we can only adapt and respond accordingly.\"","He Zhiran completely agreed with what Mo Jiuye said.","Based on Nan Rui's description of that mysterious person, it could be deduced that this person's actions were extremely peculiar, and they didn't reveal their true identity. Finding this person wouldn't be easy.","Therefore, there might not be any gains from Third Brother's journey. Since they had a clue to finding the mysterious person, they couldn't let this lead go cold, no matter what."]},{"number":229,"title":"Chapter 229: How dare I say it","paragraphs":["He Zhiran thought for a moment and said, \"Even if I am willing to help Nan Rui's Empress Dowager dispel the gu poison, I cannot reveal my true identity.\"","Mo Jiuye agreed, \"That's right.\"","It was simple for He Zhiran to not reveal her true identity. She only needed to buy some props and put on some makeup. No one would be able to recognize her.","\"How about I pretend to be an old person and try not to speak as much as possible?\"","Mo Jiuye nodded, \"Okay, it's decided. I will notify Nan Rui in three days and tell him the gu poisoning expert has been found.\"","After settling the matter, the lovers lingered together before falling into a deep sleep.","The next morning, some officials arrived.","Because there had been a smallpox scare in Yuncheng the previous day, the original plan to have the officials come and survey the wasteland and mountainside had not happened.","Today, Meng Huaining was quite concerned about this matter and had sent people over early.","Mo Jiuye led the officials to survey the land. The wasteland was not much different from their estimated quantity, a total of 51 mu.","However, the estimate for the mountainside was way off. The officials only surveyed around the foot of the mountain and then casually decided to sell the entirety of the mountainside upwards to the Mo family. The area was extremely arbitrary, stated as just 100 mu.","For such a large mountainside, there was no way it was only 100 mu. Mo Jiuye estimated it was at least 300 mu. It was clear Meng Huaining had given instructions to the officials before they came.","In any case, the Mo family's relationship with Meng Huaining would not end like this. There would be plenty of chances to repay this favor in the future.","While Mo Jiuye was busy leading the officials in the survey, He Zhiran was not idle either.","The Zhou clan chief specifically sent someone to tell her the Cui family could no longer endure and planned to sell not only their fertile fields but also the house they lived in.","After thanking the Zhou clan messenger, He Zhiran decided to go take a look at the Cui family's situation.","Old Lady Mo was worried the Cui family would hold a grudge against them, so she had Liang Hao accompany He Zhiran, a weak woman with no martial arts skills, so she would be safe.","When He Zhiran and Liang Hao arrived at the Cui family's land, it was already surrounded by people.","Perhaps because the Cui family had spread the news about selling their fields and houses early, there were many unfamiliar faces among the onlookers.","They were likely outsiders who wanted to buy property and land here.","People from the Xie and Fang families had also come. They crowded around He Zhiran when they saw her.","After greeting them, He Zhiran maintained an observational stance.","She wanted to see if the Cui family could still play any tricks at this point.","Just then, an elderly Cui clansman loudly declared, \"Heaven is unfair. It does not allow my Cui family to survive. We have no choice but to sell the houses and land in our hands.\"","The elder called over a young man and had him lead the outsiders to see the Cui family's fields for sale.","As the Cui youth guided the outsiders to the fields, He Zhiran and the Xie and Fang families followed along.","He Zhiran did not plan on buying the Cui fields. After all, the wasteland she had purchased was already enough. The only thing she was interested in was the abandoned fields and dilapidated houses at the foot of the Cui's mountainside.","She was just tagging along out of curiosity.","Indeed, it was just as He Zhiran expected. The Cui family was in a hurry to raise money for the fine, yet they still tried to rip people off.","As the Cui youth pointed to his clansmen's fields, he declared, \"Look, this is it. These are all my Cui family's fertile fields. We have carefully cultivated these fields, so they yield much more than ordinary fields.\"","Upon hearing his words, He Zhiran almost laughed out loud.","She wondered how he could say such things. The people coming to look at the fields were basically all farmers. They could tell the quality of the fields at a glance.","Higher yield indeed! This was pure exaggeration...","Someone had already grown impatient with his inflated claims and urged, \"Stop with the useless chatter. Just tell us the price per mu!\"","The Cui youth had been coached by his clansmen, so he naturally knew how to quote prices.","\"You probably can't find such good fields anywhere in Yuncheng. Our Cui family is in urgent need of money, so we are selling them at the low price of 12 taels of silver per mu.\"","As soon as the youth finished speaking, sighs of dissatisfaction arose from the crowd.","\"It seems your Cui family is not in urgent need of money but wants to take advantage to make a huge profit.\"","\"That's right. Do you think we are all fools? 12 taels per mu, how preposterous!\"","\"Forget it. I can't afford such expensive fields. I'm leaving...\"","Amid waves of complaints, the potential buyers gradually dispersed until only He Zhiran and the Fang and Xie families remained.","However, they did not speak up but simply wanted to see how the Cui family would resolve this predicament of no one willing to pay their asking price when they desperately needed money to pay the fine.","Seeing the buyers leave, the Cui youth was no longer composed.","He knew very well that even 8 taels per mu would be fair for this land, yet they insisted on an inflated price. Of course people would walk away.","But so many clansmen felt their fields were good and only reluctantly put them up for sale. They all wanted to sell at a high price.","Now what? The deadline to pay the fine was tomorrow, but how could they come up with so much silver?","The Cui youth glanced anxiously at He Zhiran's group before dejectedly returning to his clansmen.","Seeing the buyers leave, the Cui clansmen were frantic with anxiety.","Especially the Cui elder, who hurriedly asked the returning youth, \"What happened? Why did they all leave?\"","The Cui youth grimaced. \"As soon as I mentioned the price, they turned and walked away.\"","The Cui elder angrily rapped the youth on the head. \"You fool, didn't I tell you? 12 taels was just the asking price, still negotiable. Why didn't you tell them that?\"","The other Cui clansmen also scolded him. \"That's right, 12 taels was just the asking price. Why didn't you say so?\"","The youth was bewildered. \"I got nervous and forgot...\"","The Cui clan nearly wanted to give him a beating, but collecting money was most urgent now. They didn't have time for violence.","After discussing amongst themselves, the Cui family elders focused their hopes on He Zhiran's group.","Although they had not gone out much recently, they had heard the Mo family bought up all the abandoned fields at the foot of the mountain from the Zhao and Zhou families.","The reason the Mo family would buy such fields was because they could not find suitable fertile land to buy in the village.","Therefore, their last hope now rested with the Mo family.","They did not dare let that incompetent youth negotiate again.","This time it was the Cui elder who took the initiative to step forward.","To successfully sell their family's fields, the Cui elder lowered his stance as much as possible.","\"Excuse me, is the Mo family head here?\""]},{"number":230,"title":"Chapter 230: Let them know what it's like to be screwed.","paragraphs":["He Zhiran smiled ambiguously and said: \"I'm here.\"","When the Cui Family Elder saw that the person speaking to him was a young woman, he suddenly felt like he was being toyed with.","\"I know you are from the Mo Family, but for such a big matter of buying land, can you make the decision?\"","Amused that she was being doubted, He Zhiran didn't have the patience to haggle with the Cui family here.","\"I'm not interested in your family's farmland.\"","Seeing that He Zhiran was so young yet spoke bluntly, the smile on the Cui Family Elder's face instantly disappeared.","\"Humph, old man, you don't seem like someone with much say either. I won't discuss this with you.\"","Then he looked towards Xie Tianhai and Fang Chuanzhou: \"Do your two families want to purchase farmland and houses?\"","Xie Tianhai said: \"That depends on your price for the farmland. If it's twelve taels of silver per mu, we're not interested.\"","He had already inquired earlier that prime farmland in Xi Ling Village was only eight taels of silver per mu.","As for houses, they weren't needed either. They had already purchased the courtyard they were renting a few days ago.","Now they just needed to acquire a few more mu of farmland. When the men were free during the off-season, they could go out to find odd jobs to make ends meet. Their family's food and shelter shouldn't be a problem.","Seeing that the other party was interested in buying farmland, the Cui Family Elder was afraid they would also be scared off by the price of twelve taels and quickly explained: \"The price is negotiable.\"","Those outsiders had already been frightened away by the price of twelve taels per mu. The elder had finally encountered two people who wanted to buy land, he couldn't be careless.","\"What's negotiable mean? How many taels of silver per mu?\" Xie Tianhai asked.","The elder glanced at his clansmen first, then said: \"Nine taels, it's already very cheap.\"","Seeing the Cui Family Elder haggling endlessly here, Fang Chuanzhou couldn't wait and said: \"Six taels of silver per mu, and I'll buy it. Otherwise, no deal.\"","The elder stared at Fang Chuanzhou as if he had misheard: \"Are you joking? Such good farmland for only six taels?\"","Fang Chuanzhou dismissively said: \"I think your farmland is only worth that much.\"","The Cui Family elder knew his clansman urgently needed money, but selling farmland for six taels per mu would cause them huge losses.","Seeing his attitude was so firm, for a moment, the elder was at a loss.","\"Hold on, let me discuss this.\"","Fang Chuanzhou didn't reply, tacitly approving his actions.","Soon, the elder returned with several Cui family members.","The Cui family members tried to persuade Fang Chuanzhou to add some silver, but Fang Chuanzhou refused to budge.","In the end, the Cui family gritted their teeth and decided to sell the farmland for six taels per mu.","Now, Fang Chuanzhou and Xie Tianhai were quite satisfied. The farmland that was worth eight taels of silver per mu could be bought for six taels, so they had gained a small advantage.","Even He Zhiran, who had no interest in the farmland, was a little moved, but she still didn't show any desire to purchase it.","The Fang and Xie families discussed and decided to buy ten mu each.","The Cui family had originally planned to sell one hundred mu of farmland, so they wouldn't have to consider selling their houses.","But the Fang and Xie families only bought twenty mu in total, which was a drop in the bucket for the Cui family's fine they needed to pay.","Suddenly at a loss, the Cui family members became worried frowns.","Sensing the timing was right, He Zhiran finally spoke up: \"The Mo Family can buy the rest of your farmland.\"","Hearing this, the Cui family members looked towards He Zhiran in pleasant surprise.","At this moment, the Cui Family elder no longer pondered whether this young woman could represent the Mo Family or not.","\"Young lady, do you really mean it?\"","He Zhiran didn't want to waste words with the Cui family either.","\"I can buy the farmland, but I have one condition.\"","\"What condition?\" the Cui Family elder asked.","He Zhiran pointed in the direction at the foot of the mountain: \"Sell me the dilapidated courtyard and neglected farmland down there as a package deal.\"","Sell it to you as a package deal?","Of course that was good.","That farmland and courtyard were ones they didn't want anyway. Now someone was offering to buy them, this was terrific.","How was this a condition? It was clearly helping their Cui family.","But He Zhiran's next words burst their pleasant surprise.","\"For that neglected farmland and courtyard you don't want anyhow, I'll offer twenty taels of silver. What do you think?\"","\"What? So much farmland and a courtyard, and you're only offering twenty taels? That's too little.\" Immediately some Cui family members objected.","He Zhiran shrugged. \"Since you won't accept my condition, I won't buy the farmland either.\"","Your Cui family has cheated so many people over the years, now it was time for He Zhiran to let them taste being cheated.","The Cui family members were now completely at a loss.","The farmland and courtyard at the foot of the mountain belonged to their clansmen, they couldn't make decisions for them here.","But they had finally gotten an opportunity to sell all the farmland, they didn't want to give up like this either.","The Cui family members discussed among themselves and decided to go back and consult those clansmen.","He Zhiran was in no hurry either, and just waited there.","It took the Cui family members quite a while to discuss this time, almost half an hour before they returned.","Undoubtedly, the Cui family had no other way to get silver at the moment. And the deadline for paying the fines to the government was approaching. They could only take the loss.","In the end, He Zhiran used five hundred taels of silver to purchase eighty mu of Cui family's good farmland, plus over twenty mu of neglected farmland at the foot of the mountain, and five abandoned houses.","To prevent going back on their word, He Zhiran immediately asked the Cui family to send someone with her to the county government office to process the paperwork.","It just so happened that Mo Jiuye had also finished surveying the mountainous area and was back. Handling the paperwork at the government office was left to him.","He Zhiran brought Mo Jiuye several hundred taels worth of silver notes. When the land deeds were under the Mo Family's name, the silver would be given to the Cui Family.","Rather than saying given to the Cui Family, it was more like directly handed to the county government. That silver was just barely enough for the Cui family members to pay their fines.","Fang Chuanzhou and Xie Tianhai also took the opportunity to go into town with Mo Jiuye to process their land deeds.","By evening, Mo Jiuye had brought back the land deeds for the wasteland and mountainous area purchased today.","For now, the Mo Family members' acquisition of land in Xi Ling Village was temporarily settled.","He Zhiran pondered over other matters.","The good farmland purchased from the Cui Family goes without saying. Come spring, they just needed to plow it simply and it could be planted.","As for the land neglected by several families, it just had some weeds growing on it. They just needed to remove the weeds.","However, it was different for the uncultivated wasteland. Not only was the wasteland overgrown with weeds, there were also many large and small rocks inside.","He Zhiran planned to get a head start on clearing it, in case they couldn't hire workers during the busy farming season in spring.","So on the second day, she asked the two clan leaders Zhao and Zhou over, asking them to inquire whether their clansmen were willing to help clear the wasteland.","The price for clearing the wasteland would be based on local rates, one tael of silver per mu."]},{"number":231,"title":"Chapter 231: I am here to wait for King Rui and Princess Deoki.","paragraphs":["At this time, although it was winter, the weather in the northwest was cold, but the ground had not frozen enough to make reclaiming wasteland difficult.","When they heard there was money to be earned, the clansmen of the Zhao and Zhou families were willing to come and earn this money as long as they were not lazy.","Anyway, the wages were not calculated by days. The more they did, the more they earned. As soon as the two families got the news, they brought their tools and rushed to work on the wasteland.","This matter of reclaiming wasteland was arranged, and the problem of feed for the rabbits raised at home also had to be solved.","It was just the day when Mo Jiuye had agreed to meet with Nan Rui, so Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran went to Yuncheng early in the morning.","The two first went to the Tang house to see Tang Mingxin's situation. The little girl's rash on her body had not subsided except for the other symptoms that had improved. He Zhiran left some scar removal ointment for her before leaving with Mo Jiuye.","After wandering around the city, the two found an abandoned house.","He Zhiran took out the carrots and cabbage produced by the space and piled them up there, while Mo Jiuye went to hire an ox cart to transport them back to Xiling Village.","When it was about time, the two went to meet with Nan Rui as agreed.","Nan Rui was more attentive about this matter and had been waiting here an hour ago. When he saw Mo Jiuye, he eagerly asked, \"How is it? Can you contact that expert?\"","Mo Jiuye did not answer immediately, but pulled He Zhiran straight into the private room and sat down before slowly opening his mouth.","\"Luckily, I did contact the expert, but the expert is going to retreat soon, supposedly for three months. If you want him to help lift the Gu poison, you can only wait until after three months.\"","This was the time Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran had agreed on.","On the one hand, the New Year was coming soon. At that time, Third Elder Brother who had gone out to investigate would come back, and they didn't know if he would have any next moves. Therefore, they left themselves enough time to deal with things.","In addition, the capital was far from the northwest, not a short distance. If they traveled on foot as exiles, even if they could walk every day, it would take at least three months.","For Nan Rui to bring his mother here to lift the poison, he would have to return to the capital to arrange everything before he could smoothly bring people out.","Round trip, even if only going by horse carriage, would take at least three months.","So the three months they talked about was just right.","Nan Rui didn't expect that he could help lift his mother's Gu poison in three months.","Although the time was a little tight, just being able to contact that expert was extremely fortunate, and he could not be tangled over the time issue.","Nan Rui stood up and cupped his fists towards Mo Jiuye: \"I will leave for the capital immediately.\"","Mo Jiuye raised his eyebrows, seemingly smiling, \"Aren't you afraid that the expert will notice something wrong if you don't take my Eighth Elder Brother back with you?\"","\"This...\" Nan Rui hesitated a little, but still spoke his mind: \"If you had told me today that you couldn't contact that expert, I would have asked Mo Chuhang to come back to the capital with me.","Now that we've contacted the expert, no matter what I can endure three months.\"","As long as his mother's Gu poison was lifted, he would never be controlled by others again. Even if he had to live in hiding with his mother in the future, he would no longer participate in the deceitful struggles in the court.","These later thoughts were just in Nan Rui's mind. This was his biggest goal now, but to achieve this goal, he would still have to make great efforts.","Since Nan Rui had given a reasonable explanation, Mo Jiuye also temporarily dismissed his doubts for the time being.","\"Then in three months, I will be here waiting for Prince Rui and Imperial Concubine Mother.\"","With that said, Mo Jiuye took He Zhiran and left the restaurant.","Leaving the restaurant didn't mean they went far.","They had to watch Nan Rui and everyone he brought leave the city before they could rest assured.","Nan Rui did not disappoint them. Soon after Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran had just left, he summoned all his men to leave Yuncheng.","Only when they saw Nan Rui's group disappear from sight did Mo Jiuye hurry back home on the mule cart.","The tricky matter was finally over, and life in the Mo family finally got back on track.","Eighth Elder Brother got up early every day to go to work at the yamen. Fifth Elder Brother and Fifth Sister-In-Law were busy raising rabbits.","By now, the couple had completely gotten the hang of raising rabbits, busily enjoying themselves every day.","They had even discovered several pregnant mother rabbits and kept them separately in a cage for special care.","Besides pestering her owner for affection, Baozi would occasionally go for a run in the mountains, but most of the time she was in the rabbit shed laying down rules for the little ones.","With Baozi's participation, it was very convenient for Fifth Elder Brother and his wife whenever they went to clean the hutches. They didn't have to worry about the rabbits running out at all.","Because with one order from Baozi, all the little rabbits would line up against the walls of the cage and not move.","Tang Mingrui also gave accurate news that he planned to sell a batch of dolls in other cities before the New Year.","Other than preparing three meals a day, the sisters-in-law had already started making plush dolls.","He Zhiran did not leave out the Fang and Xie families when it came to making dolls. After all, everyone had supported each other along the way. She had thought of making dolls in the first place because she wanted to help them out a bit.","The Xie and Fang families were even more grateful to He Zhiran. They had never imagined that after arriving in the northwest, He Zhiran would still be willing to earn money with them.","Fortunately when they were dividing up the village, they didn't hesitate at all to choose to stick with the Mo family through thick and thin.","Now they could earn so much silver just sitting at home. If not for He Zhiran giving them this, they might never find such a livelihood in their lifetime.","For this batch of dolls, He Zhiran drew several new styles again based on the books.","With more doll styles, everyone didn't feel bored at all making them.","While the women were busy here, Fifth Sister-In-Law came over to ask He Zhiran,","\"Ninth Younger Sister, I found that half of our adult rabbits are male. Ten or eight are enough as studs. Keeping the rest is a waste of food.\"","That was true. Excess male rabbits couldn't reproduce like females, and they were already adults without room to grow. Continuing to feed them would only increase costs.","He Zhiran had thought of this when she planned to raise rabbits, but recently she had been busy with other things at home and had neglected this matter.","\"Fifth Sister-In-Law, have Fifth Elder Brother slaughter ten male rabbits first, be sure to peel off the fur completely intact.\"","Fifth Sister-In-Law didn't know why Ninth Younger Sister only agreed to slaughter ten male rabbits, but she was used to listening to everything Ninth Younger Sister said. She responded and hurried to the backyard.","More than an hour later, Fifth Sister-In-Law came to call He Zhiran again.","\"Ninth Younger Sister, your Fifth Elder Brother has slaughtered the male rabbits.\""]},{"number":232,"title":"Chapter 232: Hot and Good","paragraphs":["He Zhiran was playing with Rice Ball when she heard a voice and quickly walked out of the house, following Fifth Sister-In-Law to the backyard.","On the neatly arranged stone slabs were ten rabbits that had already been skinned, and the snow-white and intact rabbit skins were hung on bamboo poles by Fifth Elder Brother.","This step was correct, as she knew a method for handling rabbit skins.","The method involved drying the freshly peeled rabbit skins, then using a blunt shovel to scrape off the oil film and residual meat on the skin, soaking it in clean water for one to two days. This would restore the rabbit skins to a fresh state, and finally, they would be dried again, making the rabbit skins very soft.","At present, the rabbit skins had been hung on bamboo poles by Fifth Elder Brother, and what He Zhiran needed to do was to process the rabbit meat.","Raising so many rabbits was undoubtedly to earn some silver coins.","If she simply sent these rabbits to the restaurants in the city for sale, there would still be profits, but it would be much less than He Zhiran's plan.","Just as He Zhiran was about to take two rabbits to the kitchen, Fifth Elder Brother spoke up.","\"Junior Sister Nine, I used to send the rabbits I caught while hunting to the restaurants in the city. Skinned rabbits like these can be sold for 130 wen each.\"","130 wen?","The rabbits produced in her space were not only large in size but also had a lot of meat. Each rabbit weighed at least six or seven jin, and they were only sold for 130 wen. Such a small amount of money did not do justice to the words \"produced in the space.\"","However, if she wanted to earn more money, she had to consider the purchasing power of this era. The method she thought of could sell for one or two silver coins, or even less, but at least several times more than 100 wen.","\"Fifth Elder Brother, I want to try making these rabbits into ready-to-eat dishes and send them to the restaurants. If it succeeds, I estimate that we can earn more silver coins,\" she said.","Upon hearing that she could earn more silver coins, Fifth Elder Brother wholeheartedly agreed.","If it weren't for the fact that his body hadn't fully recovered, he would have gone into the mountains to hunt for silver coins long ago.","Now that he had taken on the task of raising rabbits, he could only obediently stay at home and do the work.","\"In that case, Junior Sister Nine, give it a try. If there's anything I can do, just let me know,\" Fifth Elder Brother said.","He Zhiran responded and then carried two rabbits to the stove.","The sisters-in-law, Old Lady Mo, and Mo Hanyue were all busy making dolls, and it was not yet time to cook dinner. Therefore, no one disturbed her as she worked in the kitchen, making it convenient for her to take out some seasonings from her space.","Following the method from her past life, He Zhiran made these two rabbits into cold rabbit dishes.","The spicy and fragrant aroma quickly wafted out of the kitchen. Fortunately, the sisters-in-law were all in their rooms; otherwise, they would have gathered around to take a look.","He Zhiran put the prepared rabbit meat into containers and waited for it to cool down to become authentic cold rabbit dishes.","She had just bought an electronic scale from Taobao, so she measured the weight. The two skinned rabbits together weighed thirteen jin and eight liang.","After making them into cold rabbit dishes, she measured again, and there was less than seven jin left.","In other words, if she sold the cold rabbit dishes by weight, she would need to charge at least 300 wen per jin to achieve her desired selling price.","By this calculation, the price sounded a bit high, so it would be better to sell it by portion.","A batch of cold rabbit meat was carefully wrapped in oiled paper, divided into twenty packages. Each package was priced at one hundred wen, which is a reasonable price.","Of course, these were made today for the family to taste. Even if there were plans to sell them, the final decision would depend on the family's evaluation and unanimous approval.","After making the cold rabbit meat in the kitchen, He Zhiran, still feeling the numbing and spicy aroma all over her body, took advantage of the busy atmosphere and decided to enter her space for a quick wash.","After drying her hair, He Zhiran spent some time playing with Rice Ball in the space. It was already evening.","Considering the cold weather at this time, her cold rabbit meat should have cooled down by now.","When He Zhiran arrived at the kitchen to check, she was stunned by the scene before her eyes.","Each sister-in-law held a piece of rabbit meat, their faces filled with an intoxicated expression.","Even those who couldn't handle spicy food sighed from time to time, their faces flushed but still eagerly devouring the meat.","As everyone noticed He Zhiran's presence, they all stopped their actions.","Second Sister-in-law smiled and said, \"Ninth Sister, this delicious meat must be your creation, right? We came here to prepare dinner and immediately noticed this, so everyone wanted to taste it.\"","They said \"taste,\" but it seemed like each of them had already eaten several pieces.","Fortunately, He Zhiran had made plenty; otherwise, the sister-in-laws would have already eaten it all...","What she cared about most right now was not the quantity of the cold rabbit meat but everyone's evaluation of this dish.","\"Sister-in-laws, do you think this cold rabbit meat is delicious?\"","Everyone nodded, \"Mmm, it's delicious, incredibly delicious.\"","\"It's spicy and satisfying.\"","\"After eating one piece, you crave another.\"","Hearing the sister-in-laws' praise and looking at their expressions, He Zhiran knew that her cold rabbit meat venture was already half successful.","Tonight, she would make the remaining eight rabbits and try selling them in the city tomorrow morning.","Not only did the cold rabbit meat receive high praise from a few sister-in-laws, but even Fifth Elder Brother, who usually said very little, kept praising how tasty it was.","He Zhiran had only tried making cold rabbit meat here once, just to see how it would turn out, but she didn't expect it to be a success on the first try.","The two rabbits' worth of cold rabbit meat disappeared in an instant as the family devoured it.","The sister-in-laws knew that Ninth Sister would be making cold rabbit meat again tonight, so after dinner, they didn't return to their rooms to continue making dolls but followed her to the kitchen.","He Zhiran knew that the sister-in-laws would come and help in the evening, so she had already prepared all the ingredients and didn't need to retrieve them from the space. She wasn't worried about being discovered since that scapegoat foreigner had always been useful.","Fortunately, these ingredients didn't take up much space. Last time, there was a big bag of things labeled as seasonings in the storage room.","There weren't many rabbits that could be slaughtered at home now, so occasionally, she secretly added some seasonings to the bag. It would be enough until they could grow these seasonings themselves.","He Zhiran didn't hold back in teaching the sister-in-laws the method of making cold rabbit meat. After all, this was just a small venture, and she planned to develop other profitable businesses in the future. She couldn't always rely on this one thing.","The sisters-in-law were all very devoted to their studies, repeating each step in their minds several times, afraid of forgetting them when they woke up after a nap.","After working for more than an hour, the eight rabbits were finally transformed into delicious cold rabbit dishes once again.","Eldest Sister-in-law took a piece while it was still hot and found that it tasted the same as the one made by Ninth Younger Sister.","Following He Zhiran's instructions, all the cold rabbit dishes were arranged in containers and would be divided and packaged the next morning.","When He Zhiran returned to the room, Mo Jiuye was already waiting there, looking bored.","Upon seeing his wife, he pulled her into his arms.","He Zhiran struggled to break free, saying, \"I smell strongly of cooking fumes.\"","\"I don't mind. I love all the scents my wife has,\" Mo Jiuye replied.","He Zhiran...","Nowadays, Mo Jiuye would say such things almost without thinking, without needing to prepare in advance."]},{"number":233,"title":"Chapter 233: Sister-in-law Try Whatever you Want","paragraphs":["He Zhiran nodded: \"Yes, since pendants are meant to be hung on clothes or backpacks, they naturally can't be too big.\"","After listening to He Zhiran's explanation, Sixth Sister-in-Law picked up the blueprint and studied it carefully.","The other sisters-in-law also craned their necks to look together.","After a few minutes, Sixth Sister-in-Law put down the blueprint.","\"Ninth younger sister, let me make a finished product first to try it out.\"","\"Great. With so much rabbit fur, sisters feel free to try it out,\" He Zhiran generously pushed all the rabbit fur in front of the sisters-in-law.","By dusk, Sixth Sister-in-Law had made a rosy red long-eared rabbit pendant.","The eyes of the long-eared rabbit were ready-made products that He Zhiran had bought from Taobao Mall, and the four claws at the ends of the long-eared rabbit were all white, making it look very cute.","He Zhiran picked it up and examined it carefully, constantly praising Sixth Sister-in-Law's dexterity.","\"Sixth Sister-in-Law, this is how it should be. Just make them according to this standard in the future.\"","It was truly perfect. It was identical to, if not better than, those sold at Taobao Mall.","The only thing missing was that the long-eared rabbit pendants sold at Taobao Mall had a metal hook, and she had to think of a suitable item to replace it.","Just as He Zhiran was thinking about what to replace the hook with, Eldest Sister-in-Law spoke up.","\"Ninth younger sister, looking at the design of your blueprint, there should be something like a rope on the pendant, right? I learned how to tie knots from my mother when I was young. Let me try.\"","After speaking, Eldest Sister-in-Law found a coil of red thread, separated it into strands to thicken the thread, and then started braiding in front of everyone.","Soon, a red monkey's fist knot was made.","When He Zhiran saw the red monkey's fist knot in Eldest Sister-in-Law's hand, her eyes lit up at once.","\"Eldest Sister-in-Law, this will work. We'll use this monkey's fist knot as decoration on the finished long-eared rabbit pendants.\"","Having gotten the approval of her ninth younger sister-in-law, Eldest Sister-in-Law said with a smile, \"Sounds good. We'll use this monkey's fist knot on the pendants we make.\"","Now, a finished pendant was completely done. He Zhiran didn't need to worry about the sisters-in-law's craftsmanship either. So she could let go of making the pendants again.","The family could no longer provide cold rabbit meat dishes, and Tang Mingrui had taken away a lot of plush toys to sell last time, so he probably wouldn't come again for a while.","But thanks to the sisters-in-law's efforts, the family had produced one hundred pendants in various colors in just three days.","Now the time was nearing the twelfth lunar month, and there was one month left until New Year's. He Zhiran thought that the time before New Year's was when people were most willing to spend money. So she took the initiative to look for Tang Mingrui.","Her timing happened to be perfect. Tang Mingrui had just returned last night from going out to sell plush toys these past few days. If they hadn't caught him, their trip could very likely have been in vain.","When Tang Mingrui saw these pendants made with real rabbit fur, even a grown man like him couldn't help but fiddle with them lovingly in his hands.","He couldn't hide the surprise and delight on his face at all: \"Ninth Sister-in-Law, these are pendants?\"","\"Yes, does Brother Tang think these will sell well?\" He Zhiran asked knowingly.","Let alone getting them into Tang Mingrui's hands, even she, someone who didn't understand business, knew that pendants like these appearing on the market would definitely be very popular.","\"Of course, Ninth Sister-in-Law, don't worry. Brother will definitely sell these great pendants for a good price.\"","He Zhiran didn't ask for more. Although the pendants were made with real rabbit fur, they didn't cost much for her. What made them special was the variety of colors and the sisters-in-laws' fine craftsmanship.","Also, the pendants were much smaller than the plush toys. It would be pretty high already if they could sell for a few taels of silver each.","Tang Mingrui didn't estimate the price of the pendants in advance this time. For such exquisite little things, he planned to try selling them at a high price.","When He Zhiran and Mo Jiuye came over, they brought all one hundred pendants made at home and handed them over to Tang Mingrui before leaving.","They thought Tang Mingrui wouldn't come for a few days, but who knew, he came early the next morning.","He took those one hundred pendants to sell at the prefectural city. Unexpectedly, the young ladies and daughters-in-law of those wealthy families in the city adored these delicate and petite pendants.","With word spreading from one to ten to a hundred, the one hundred pendants he brought were far from enough to sell.","Not only that, many people wanted to place preorders with him.","Also, the price Tang Mingrui sold the pendants for was higher than for the plush toys, fetching as much as twelve taels each. He Zhiran thus got a higher commission as well.","He Zhiran didn't know that the reason Tang Mingrui could sell the pendants at such a high price had to do with the gemstone-like rabbit eyes inset on them.","Although he couldn't tell what material they were, each one was shiny, round, and plump - clearly no ordinary object. Hence, after Tang Mingrui made up some words about the rabbit eyes, the buyers all felt they got their money's worth.","The pendants were popular, which could have been taken advantage of to make a lot of money, but unfortunately, the rabbit fur at home was limited. To produce them in large quantities, they'd have to wait until after New Year's when they slaughtered another batch of male rabbits.","Luckily Tang Mingrui didn't accept those preorder orders, otherwise he would have lost credibility with customers.","Of course, He Zhiran wouldn't get involved in how Tang Mingrui did business. Right now the fur fabric and rabbit fur at home were used up. What she needed to do was prepare for the first New Year's she'd spend since arriving in this different world.","On the twenty-third day of the twelfth lunar month, it was the day people made offerings to the Kitchen God, also marking the start of the entire Spring Festival.","Old Lady Mo placed great importance on these solar terms, and didn't neglect the spring cleaning and Kitchen God offerings.","The family started busy preparations early in the morning. Old Lady Mo found Mo Chongyuan and asked him to try painting an image of the Kitchen God.","She had raised nine sons; Mo Chongyuan's martial arts were weaker than his eight brothers, but he was slightly better at working with ink.","If he hadn't been born in a family of military generals, it was very likely Mo Chongyuan would have chosen a scholarly path instead.","However, life played with people, not only making him suffer so much at such a young age, but ultimately ending up losing his memory.","Actually, the reason Old Lady Mo arranged for Mo Chongyuan to paint the Kitchen God image was also hoping it could evoke some of his memories.","In previous years when the family worshipped the Kitchen God during the New Year, the images were always painted by Mo Chongyuan. She hoped he could still paint them despite his amnesia.","Mo Chongyuan was still a bit dazed when called over from the rabbit shed.","\"Mother, you called me?\"","Old Lady Mo put the paper and brush on the table in front of her.","\"In the past, the Kitchen God images in our family were always painted by you. This time I hope you'll paint them again.\"","Upon hearing his mother mention that he had painted Kitchen God images for the family before, Mo Chongyuan reflexively tried to recall it.","He didn't know why, but recently whenever anyone mentioned anything about the past to him, as long as he tried hard to remember it, he would get a splitting headache.","And the harder he tried to remember, the more severe this feeling became.","When this happened, Fifth Sister-in-Law would run to find He Zhiran.","With Fifth Elder Brother conscious now, He Zhiran could only check his pulse for him.","After checking, He Zhiran didn't find anything wrong with Fifth Elder Brother. Adding her experience as a doctor in her previous life, she figured that Fifth Elder Brother's condition was probably not a bad thing. It was likely the blood clots in his brain slowly being absorbed, a sign that his memories were being triggered.","Still, He Zhiran instructed that Fifth Elder Brother should keep a peaceful state of mind and not force anything. His memories would return sooner or later."]},{"number":234,"title":"Chapter 234: Simple to understand yet Elegant","paragraphs":["He Zhiran was afraid that any noise would lead to embarrassment if overheard by her family the next morning, since the houses were built so close together and the ancient houses were not soundproof. She quickly pulled Mo Jiuye into the space with her.","Thinking of the smell of oil smoke on her body, He Zhiran went into the bathroom again to wash up.","Mo Jiuye was particularly clingy today. Wherever his wife went, he would follow her wherever she went. He even claimed that his wife had worked hard today and that he was willing to wait on her to bathe...","In front of Mo Jiuye, He Zhiran's strength was like a little white rabbit encountering a big gray wolf. She was caught off guard for a moment and Mo Jiuye hugged her tightly. The sudden kiss made her somewhat unprepared.","Accompanied by the sound of water in the bathroom, her mind instantly went blank amidst the entanglement of lips and tongues, and her whole body was completely under Mo Jiuye's control.","Soon, she became very cooperative, tilting her slender, fair neck to take the initiative to cater to his wild kiss.","After a long time, Mo Jiuye finally let her go. He Zhiran felt that she was almost suffocated.","Just as she was gasping for breath, Mo Jiuye had already grabbed the bath towel hanging on the side and wrapped He Zhiran's whole body in it, then carried her straight to the bedroom...","After a night of passion, it resulted in He Zhiran getting up late again the next day.","The sisters-in-law seemed to have become accustomed to this situation. Every time she walked out of the room in broad daylight, everyone's eyes would unconsciously fall on her lower abdomen.","He Zhiran coughed awkwardly twice without explaining like the first time.","Because she knew in her heart that the more she explained this kind of thing, the worse it would get.","She coughed lightly twice, \"Sisters-in-law, please help divide the cold rabbit meat into small portions and wrap it in oiled paper.\"","The sisters-in-law knew that the ninth younger sister had thin skin and tacitly did not tease her.","After eating breakfast, Mo Jiuye prepared to take He Zhiran into the city by mule cart to promote and sell to a restaurant.","Unexpectedly, as soon as the two drove the mule cart to the gate, they saw a carriage coming.","The carriage headed straight for the Mo family and stopped about ten meters away from the gate.","Tang Mingrui jumped down from the car.","\"Ninth brother Mo and ninth sister-in-law, are you going out?\"","At this moment, He Zhiran was sitting in the carriage. Hearing the familiar voice, she also got out.","\"I'm thinking of selling some food I made in the city.\"","In He Zhiran's mind, although Tang Mingrui was down and out now, he was still a big businessman and would not be interested in this kind of snack.","So she didn't think about cooperating with him.","Unexpectedly, Tang Mingrui showed great interest.","\"I don't know what kind of delicacies the ninth sister-in-law has made. May I take a look?\"","Let alone take a look, you can even have a taste.","He Zhiran took out a package of cold rabbit directly from the carriage and handed it to Tang Mingrui.","\"This is made from rabbit meat raised by my own family. Brother Tang, please try it first.\"","Tang Mingrui opened the oil paper package and put a piece of rabbit meat in his mouth.","His reaction was the same as the Mo family's last night. His mouth was numb from the spiciness, but he still wanted to keep eating.","After eating three consecutive pieces, Tang Mingrui finally stopped. He knew that the ninth sister-in-law of the Mo family had the final say, so he ignored Mo Jiuye directly.","\"Ninth sister-in-law, this meat is too delicious. Why don't you cooperate with me?\"","He Zhiran didn't expect Tang Mingrui to be interested in this kind of snack.","Anyway, it would be more convenient to have a future business tycoon cooperate than for her to go to the city to promote it herself.","\"Brother Tang, please come in. We can discuss the details of cooperation.\"","Only then did Tang Mingrui realize that he had been rude, stopping people at their door to taste delicacies.","His face flushed slightly as he said, \"Okay.\"","Mo Jiuye led the mule cart back to the yard and took Tang Mingrui to his room.","With him there, there was no need to worry about issues of other men or not, especially these days, he had discovered that the villagers here paid little attention to such things. He might as well be a person who follows local customs.","After everyone was seated, Tang Mingrui couldn't wait to ask, \"Ninth sister-in-law, does this food have a name?\"","\"This rabbit tastes better when eaten cold, so I called it Cold Rabbit.\" He Zhiran explained.","\"Cold rabbit... Good name, simple, easy to understand and elegant.\" Tang Mingrui couldn't stop praising the name.","Then he asked about the price.","He Zhiran would not lower the price of cold rabbit just because she was cooperating with an acquaintance. At most she just wouldn't make too much profit.","\"I wrapped all the cold rabbit in oil paper. What Brother Tang took just now was a portion. The selling price per portion is 100 wen.\"","If Tang Mingrui felt it was expensive, she would go to the city herself to find buyers. Anyway, a package of cold rabbit must not be less than this price.","Tang Mingrui looked subconsciously at the package of food in his hand.","It looked like it could fill a plate.","He thought of the prosperous cities he had been to, where a signature dish in a restaurant could sell for several taels of silver.","If a plate of cold rabbit was served, the minimum selling price would probably be more than one or two taels of silver.","This was a good deal.","Although the Tang family declined, they still knew many big businessmen who owned restaurants, such as the largest restaurant in the nearest prefecture from Yuncheng, whose boss was acquainted with his father.","Such good food, which was probably the only one in the world, if he gave it to them, it would probably sell like hot cakes.","\"Okay, according to what Sister Mo said, 100 wen per portion. I want as many as you have here.\"","He Zhiran did not know Tang Mingrui's sales channels, nor did she care about these things.","Her intention to have Mo Jiuye lend a hand to save the latter was for future business cooperation.","\"We prepared 80 portions of cold rabbit today. Brother Tang has tasted one package, we'll take that one.\"","Although it was only 100 wen, for the hardworking He Zhiran, it was still necessary to make it clear.","Tang Mingrui did not stand on ceremony either. He would never put profits first when dealing with a benefactor's business.","He would still pay according to the profit sharing ratio later. He believed he could definitely help the Mo family a bit.","Since the cold rabbit had not yet been delivered to the restaurant, Tang Mingrui could not determine the final selling price either. Therefore, unlike before with the dolls, he did not mention sharing profits with the ninth sister-in-law in advance.","After settling the sales of cold rabbit, Tang Mingrui brought up something else.","His purpose in coming today was to see how the doll production was going.","He Zhiran hadn't paid much attention to the number of dolls these past few days, it was the sisters-in-law who were in charge.","So she went out to ask her eldest sister-in-law about the number of dolls.","The eldest sister-in-law told her that in the past few days, together with the women of the Xie and Fang families, they had made a total of 150 dolls.","He Zhiran relayed the numbers to Tang Mingrui.","Hearing that there were so many dolls, and eager to go to the prefecture to sell cold rabbit, Tang Mingrui left West Ridge Village with the dolls and cold rabbit together, at the fastest possible speed."]},{"number":235,"title":"Chapter 235: Ten times what she had planned to sell for.","paragraphs":["In terms of payment, a tacit understanding had formed between them - settlement would come after goods were sold. He Zhiran had also grown used to this and did not hurry to collect money.","He Zhiran believed that once the Cold Rabbit Meat reached the restaurant, it would definitely become a hot-selling dish. If nothing unexpected happened, Tang Mingrui would come to her door tomorrow to ask for goods.","Upon thinking of this, He Zhiran immediately notified Fifth Brother to slaughter another ten male rabbits.","Without He Zhiran even needing to instruct, the sisters-in-law took the initiative to enter the kitchen to start making preparations.","Sure enough, as He Zhiran had expected, Tang Mingrui came early the next day.","Once the Cold Rabbit Meat was delivered to the prefecture, he observed for a while there and found that it was deeply welcomed by the diners.","Not only that, but the restaurant even sold a plate of Cold Rabbit Meat for the sky-high price of four taels of silver!","Of course, the restaurant selling the Cold Rabbit Meat at such a high price had a lot to do with Tang Mingrui.","He sold each serving of Cold Rabbit Meat for two taels of silver. Restaurants were places that split profits at least fifty-fifty. If they didn’t sell each plate for four taels of silver, it would seem they weren’t making any profit.","Regardless, Tang Mingrui’s promotional efforts for Cold Rabbit Meat were wildly successful. His restaurant owner boss also expressed that for such delicacies, however much Tang Mingrui brought, he wanted that much.","Therefore, Tang Mingrui hurried back to Yancheng overnight without even going home, heading straight for the Mo family residence.","Upon arrival at the Mo family residence, he directly gave He Zhiran eighty taels of silver, ten times what she had originally planned to sell for!","Looking at so much shiny silver before her, He Zhiran was surprised and asked, “Brother Tang, what is the meaning of this?”","Tang Mingrui smiled and said, “I’m selling Cold Rabbit Meat for two taels of silver a serving. From now on, for any business cooperation with Ninth Sister-in-Law, as far as I’m able, I’ll try my best to split profits with you evenly, fifty-fifty.”","At this moment, Tang Mingrui still did not know that his grateful words today would reduce his profits by who knew how much in the future.","However, for Tang Mingrui, this was not a big deal at all. After all, his businesses in the future would be all over the country, and the cooperation with the Mo family was only a portion.","Upon seeing Tang Mingrui voluntarily propose this kind of profit sharing method, He Zhiran did not show any sign of refusal.","Although her space had endless silver that could not be used up in several lifetimes, who would refuse more silver for being too cumbersome?","After putting away the eighty taels of silver, Tang Mingrui also handed over some profits from selling the stuffed animals. With the large quantity of stuffed animals and also wanting more profit for himself, naturally he would not have the blazing sales speed like with the Cold Rabbit Meat.","Therefore, today’s share given to He Zhiran was only a portion of the stuffed animals’ split profits.","Even so, for He Zhiran, this was still a huge income.","Tang Mingrui was in a hurry to rush to the prefecture to deliver Cold Rabbit Meat, so he bid farewell and hurriedly left after exchanging pleasantries.","After sending Tang Mingrui off, He Zhiran continued directing the sisters-in-law in making Cold Rabbit Meat.","The domestic affairs at home were all handled by He Zhiran. Mo Jiuye took Liang Hao and the other men, together with those villagers, to clear rocks in the wasteland.","Being busy for five straight days, not only was the wasteland taken care of properly, those kind villagers also voluntarily helped pull out the weeds.","This wasteland, after plowing it once come spring next year, would be ready for planting.","After finishing up matters with the wasteland, Mo Jiuye still did not rest.","He employed villagers with a pay of twenty coins per day to completely tear down all the dilapidated houses at the foot of the mountain, as well as clear away all the rubble till smooth and clean.","At the same time, he also made arrangements to purchase various building materials.","At this time, all the male rabbits at home that could be slaughtered were used up. To continue the Cold Rabbit Meat business, they would have to wait until after New Year’s, when the young rabbits grew into adults.","Meanwhile, the first batch of rabbit fur was also processed and completed.","He Zhiran purchased dye in the Taobao online store and dyed the rabbit fur into beautiful colors. The rabbit fur, after being dyed vivid colors, felt soft and supple to the touch, completely unlike the conventional hard and stiff feeling that people would imagine.","Before even talking about what could be made with this beautiful rabbit fur, just looking at the colors, they were surely a rare find even within the capital of Great Shun Dynasty.","In her previous life, many young girls would buy long eared rabbit pendants made with rabbit fur. The silly and cute appearance of the long eared rabbits was extremely endearing, plus the wide variety of bright colors, it gave buyers a large amount options in selection, and this was one of the biggest draws of the rabbit fur long ear rabbit pendants.","Therefore, she planned to use the rabbit fur to make stuffed rabbit pendants. The rabbit fur did not need to worry about photosensitivity issues. As the scale of rabbit husbandry at home expanded in future, there would be more and more rabbit fur, believing that it would not lead to the situation of business dictated by intermittent supply like the plush stuffed animals.","He Zhiran drew up the blueprints in her space, then brought the colored rabbit fur to find the sisters-in-law. She could come up with ideas and designs, but her hands-on ability was somewhat lacking. With such good rabbit fur, she did not dare carelessly handle it herself, for fear that she would ruin the materials and what a waste that would be.","The sisters-in-law were all gathered together making stuffed animals. When they saw the youngest sister-in-law carry in piles of multi-colored fluffy stuff, at first glance they did not recognize that it was rabbit fur.","Second Sister-in-Law stepped forward to greet her and receive the items from her hands, while inquiring at the same time, “Youngest Sister-in-Law, this is......” Before her words were finished, she reacted quickly, “Youngest Sister-in-Law, this is rabbit fur right?”","He Zhiran smiled with a nod, “Yes, I used the dyes purchased from the Westerners to dye these rabbit furs, and the colors are quite nice. I got inspiration for a new style of plush toy and wanted the sisters-in-law to try making them.”","Hearing that the colored rabbit fur was also being used to make plush toys, the other sisters-in-law surrounded them one after another, grabbing and picking up a piece to look over.","“Youngest Sister-in-Law, with such beautiful colors, making them into leather clothes would definitely look very nice too,” Eldest Sister-in-Law could not help commenting. In her mind, she had already quickly envisaged what rabbit fur clothing would look like after being made.","Seventh Sister-in-Law chimed in, “With such lovely colors, anything made from them would look really good.”","Of course He Zhiran knew that leather clothing made from rabbit fur looked extremely gorgeous. However, it was not the kind of rabbit fur before their eyes. If she remembered correctly, the rabbit fur clothing that people wore in her previous life were made using fur from ermines.","Since the sisters-in-law were enthusiastic about making leather outfits, after the houses at home were rebuilt, she could consider increasing ermine rabbits in the breeding stock. Right now, the home did not yet have the capacity to expand the breeding grounds; they should be content with making some rabbit fur stuffed toys first.","Although there was endless silver that could not be spent in her space across several lifetimes, He Zhiran felt that there were many women dependents in the household. According to ancient and present views, the more women in a place, the easier it would be for malicious undercurrents and intricate schemes. On the other hand, if everyone had their own matters to keep busy, there would be no time to overthink unnecessary things, which would be helpful for harmony.","Not only that, she also hoped for the sisters-in-law to each have their own skills for the future, so that even as widows, they would be able to support and conduct themselves independently.","Bringing back her wandering thoughts, He Zhiran took out the picture diagrams that she had drawn.","“Sisters-in-Law, take a look. This is the rabbit fur pendant that I designed. Let’s try making them first. No need to worry about wasting materials since the rabbit fur are all from our family’s own production.”","Sixth Sister-in-Law who was more attentive immediately noticed the uniqueness of the diagram upon one glance.","“Youngest Sister-in-Law, based on your design, the size of this plush toy pendant should be just palm sized only right?”"]},{"number":236,"title":"Chapter 236: I'm going to invite my nine brothers and sisters over.","paragraphs":["{I'm sorry everyone, sent by mistake. Chapter 235 is before Chapter 233. Please jump over when reading. Sorry!}","As she said, Fifth Brother Mo Chongyuan tried his best to restrain himself from recalling anything when he felt uncomfortable.","However, today's situation was completely different from the past. Mo Chongyuan just instinctively recalled the past about painting the Kitchen God image, and his head started hurting again.","Unlike previous headaches, as soon as the image of the Kitchen God flashed in his mind, his head hurt as if it was about to split open.","This sudden intense pain caught Mo Chongyuan off guard. His handsome and robust features were tightly knitted together.","Seeing her son like this, Old Lady Mo immediately asked with concern, \"Chongyuan, is your head hurting again?\"","His sisters-in-law also looked at him in shock, because Mo Chongyuan's current state was quite frightening.","His forehead veins were bulging, but still, in order not to worry his mother and the women of the house, Mo Chongyuan said with difficulty, \"I'm fine.\"","Mo Chongyuan was already trying hard not to recall anything about the Kitchen God image, but his head still hurt so badly that he felt like losing control.","Seeing this, Second Sister-in-law panickly ran outside, \"I'm going to call Ninth Sister-in-law over!\"","When He Zhiran was pulled over by Second Sister-in-law, she saw Mo Chongyuan hugging his head with both hands, his body already convulsing in pain.","Without further ado, He Zhiran quickly took out silver needles from her clothes and inserted them at several of Mo Chongyuan's acupoints.","Before long, Mo Chongyuan quieted down and then passed out.","Old Lady Mo was still worried after seeing her son's condition just now. She asked anxiously,","\"He Shi, what exactly is going on with your Fifth Brother?\"","Judging solely from taking his pulse, it would be hard to determine Mo Chongyuan's condition at the moment.","\"Mother, I need to do further checks on Fifth Brother's condition. I'm going to call my husband over to help.\"","Of course, her main purpose in asking Mo Jiuye to come over was to provide cover for her to bring Mo Chongyuan into her personal dimension.","Mo Jiuye was receiving building materials delivered at the foot of the mountain. Seeing his wife coming over, he put down what he was doing and went to greet her.","\"Ranran, something wrong?\"","He Zhiran pulled Mo Jiuye along, \"Come back home with me first. Fifth Brother is not doing well. I plan to bring him into my dimension to do some checks.\"","Nothing more needed to be said. Mo Jiuye understood why his wife called him back.","With so many eyes around the village, Mo Jiuye could not openly use his lightness skill. The couple quickly ran back home hand in hand.","Back in the room, no matter how others wondered about the reason they were not allowed to stay, Mo Jiuye decisively sent everyone out.","After closing the door, he nodded slightly at He Zhiran.","He Zhiran brought Mo Chongyuan into her dimension space. After a quick examination, she reappeared in the room with a delighted expression.","Seeing her expression, Mo Jiuye was stunned for a moment, then asked, \"Ranran, is Fifth Brother going to regain his memories?\"","He Zhiran smiled and said, \"I just helped Fifth Brother do a checkup. I discovered that the blood clots in his head have been almost completely absorbed. If nothing goes wrong, his memories should be able to recover.\"","Hearing this, Mo Jiuye was overjoyed. He immediately ran out to tell the family the good news.","Soon, Old Lady Mo came back to the room with the women.","Old Lady Mo grabbed He Zhiran's hand excitedly, \"Is it true that your Fifth Brother is going to regain his memories?\"","He Zhiran held Old Lady Mo's hand in return, \"Mother, if nothing goes wrong, Fifth Brother will remember everything when he wakes up.\"","Standing next to Old Lady Mo, Fifth Sister-In-Law burst into tears when she heard about her husband's condition.","\"My husband is finally getting better. Doesn't this mean that he won't feel like a stranger to me anymore in the future?\"","Thinking of this, Fifth Sister-In-Law felt extremely aggrieved.","Although her husband was still alive, the two of them had always interacted formally as if they were mere acquaintances. This was completely different from how affectionate he used to be.","Facing the same face as before but without the previous closeness, Fifth Sister-In-Law felt empty inside.","If she didn't know that her husband was so cold because he lost his memories, Fifth Sister-In-Law would have wondered if he had a change of heart.","Now, Ninth Sister-in-law said that after her husband woke up, he would regain his memories. Finally, she could be intimate with her husband again. From now on, they would try their best to have a child or two, and this life would be enough.","Although the examination showed that the blood clots in Fifth Brother's head had been completely absorbed, He Zhiran still did not dare to relax too much.","She kept a close eye on the unconscious man in bed, hoping that everything would go as she had envisioned after Fifth Brother woke up.","After about half a hour, Mo Chongyuan finally opened his eyes.","However, instead of the joyful surprise everyone was waiting for, what greeted them was Mo Chongyuan's extremely pained expression.","Not understanding what was going on, Old Lady Mo went up and gently asked, \"Chongyuan, where are you feeling uncomfortable?\"","At this moment, Mo Chongyuan's gaze was distant. He did not respond to his mother at all. His consciousness was completely immersed in the pain of the past.","He remembered back then, when he led his men to pursue the remnants of the southern border army, they had accidentally entered a hidden valley.","He watched helplessly as his men were killed by the rain of arrows. Then the warhorse he was riding suddenly went out of control...","Thinking of these, Mo Chongyuan hugged his head again, unwilling to recall that disgraceful past.","However, the more he tried to escape it, the more these scenes appeared, forcing him to face it.","\"Ranran, what exactly is going on with Fifth Brother?\" Mo Jiuye anxiously asked his wife.","Facing Fifth Brother's state, He Zhiran was also at a loss.","According to her, the results of the advanced equipment's examination in her space couldn't be wrong. Why did Fifth Brother behave like this after waking up?","He Zhiran went up to take Fifth Brother's pulse, but he stubbornly held his head with both hands, completely uncooperative.","Mo Jiuye forcefully grabbed one of his arms and pried it away from his head.","Taking the chance, He Zhiran placed her fingers on Fifth Brother's pulse.","\"Fifth Brother's pulse is completely normal.\"","Not only was it normal, it was also very healthy.","\"But judging from Fifth Brother's appearance, it seems like his head is still hurting?\" Mo Jiuye asked in puzzlement.","After thinking for a while, He Zhiran speculated: \"I suspect that Fifth Brother has recalled some disgraceful memories, which is why he would behave like this.\"","Disgraceful memories?","In the Mo family's understanding, Mo Chongyuan had an optimistic personality. Also, he didn't encounter anything disgraceful before his \"death\" in battle.","Could it be the scene when he \"died\" in battle?","Or maybe after being captured, he suffered some inhuman torture?","These were all just guesses in everyone's minds. Only Mo Chongyuan himself knew the real answers.","Facing this Fifth Brother, even He Zhiran was at a bit of a loss.","Obviously the person was very healthy. She couldn't keep sedating him with needles. That would be completely useless.","Things that have happened in the past cannot be erased by anyone. Overcoming this mental demon could only rely on oneself.","Additionally, there was another method, which was to awaken him through his loved ones.","By loved ones, it naturally referred to the person he considered most important in his life."]},{"number":237,"title":"Chapter 237: You remember Me, don't you","paragraphs":["He Zhiran looked towards Old Lady Mo and Fifth Sister-In-Law.","\"Mother, Fifth Sister-In-Law, try telling Fifth Elder Brother some happy things from the past, and see if you can get him to come out of his pain.\"","Hearing Ninth Younger Sister-in-Law's words, Fifth Sister-In-Law no longer cared about keeping up appearances. She took off her shoes and climbed onto the kang beside the fireplace, while Old Lady Mo sat on the other side.","Mother-in-law and daughter-in-law embraced Fifth Elder Brother's arms from both left and right.","\"Chongyuan, do you still remember when you were sixteen? Mother had taken a liking to the eldest daughter of the Chen Family, and wanted to find someone to help arrange your marriage alliance, but you refused no matter what.","Later, under Mother's repeated questioning, you said you liked a girl... \"","Hearing this, Fifth Elder Brother's pained expression relaxed a lot. He said softly, \"It's Jiajia. I liked Jiajia, so I didn't want to marry the Chen Family's eldest daughter.\"","When Fifth Sister-In-Law heard her husband say her name, tears rolled down her face again like a broken strand of pearls.","She hugged Mo Chongyuan's arm tightly and sobbed, \"Husband, look at me, I'm Jiajia...\"","Mo Chongyuan seemed to have heard a familiar voice and instinctively looked at his tearful wife.","When their eyes met, Fifth Elder Brother immediately took her into his arms.","\"Jiajia, my Jiajia.\"","Fifth Sister-In-Law was now sobbing uncontrollably.","\"Hus...husband...you remember me, don't you?\"","At this moment, with his beloved wife in his arms, Mo Chongyuan could no longer avoid the truth.","\"Yes, I remember. You're my wife, my Jiajia...\"","Seeing this scene, the women of the family began to wipe their tears.","Eighth Sister-in-law was still doing better. Mo Chuhan had not lost his memory, so he treated her the same as before, and the couple was even more affectionate now. The only regret was that they didn't have children yet.","Although Third Sister-in-law knew her husband was still alive, it had not yet been made public in the family. Also, after meeting her briefly, her husband had left, and she didn't know where he was now, so her heart was anxious every day.","Seeing Fifth Elder Brother and Fifth Sister-In-Law, Third Sister-In-Law missed her own husband even more.","The other sisters-in-law had completely different feelings. They dreamed that their own husbands could also return from the dead. Seeing Mo Chongyuan and his wife reunited, they were extremely envious.","Mo Hanyue pulled Old Lady Mo's arm and sobbed, \"Mother, Fifth Elder Brother really remembers now...\"","Old Lady Mo nodded with tears: \"Yes, he remembers.\"","After a long time, everyone finally calmed down a little.","Considering Fifth Elder Brother's emotional outburst when he first woke up, everyone tacitly avoided asking him about his past.","Mo Chongyuan also seemed to realize his condition earlier. But after communicating with his wife and mother, his emotions had gradually stabilized. Recalling that humiliating past now, he seemed able to bear it.","He looked at everyone in the room and said, \"Back then, I was reckless and fell into their trap because of the sinister scheme of the Southerners, and suffered all kinds of torments.\"","Everyone's gaze fell on Mo Chongyuan as he spoke. They knew he was going to recount that experience.","Fifth Elder Brother went on, \"That year I led a group of men to pursue the retreating Southerners, but accidentally fell into their ambush.","Many of the men I brought were shot dead by their chaotic arrows. I wanted to go rescue them, but my lone horse was frightened and completely beyond my control. In its panic, it brought me deep into the valley.","Just as I realized the danger and was about to abandon the horse to escape, a white smoke suddenly appeared and I immediately lost consciousness.","When I woke up again, I was chained in a prison cell. At that time, I could feel that my mind was sometimes clear and sometimes very blurred.\"","Upon hearing this, Mo Jiuye's eyes had turned red. He knew that at this point, Fifth Elder Brother had been poisoned.","\"Fifth Brother, do you know who poisoned you?\"","\"I couldn't see that person's appearance clearly, but I still have a vivid memory of a lock of white hair that was exposed from under his hat. \"","Hearing about the lock of white hair, both Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran immediately thought of the same person - the mysterious man who was Cloud Li's master, as Nan Rui had said.","Now the disappearance of several surviving elder brothers in the family was related to that man, they just didn't know why the mysterious man had been so obsessed with the Mo family.","Mo Jiuye knew clearly that now was not the time to investigate the reasons. What he wanted to know more was what happened to Fifth Elder Brother afterward.","\"What happened then?\"","\"Later, that man took out a white porcelain bottle in front of me. The moment he removed the stopper, a bug flew out from inside. I knew the Southerners were not lacking in gu raisers, so I determined it must be a gu worm.","I saw with my own eyes as that bug pierced my skin and drilled into my body. And I felt a voice in my brain constantly calling to me, telling me to do things I didn't want to do.","I was very resistant to this and struggled hard against that voice. I don't know how long passed, but I guess my willpower eventually defeated the voice controlling me, and the gu worm drilled back out through a hole in my arm by itself.","Not long after, that man came before me again. He was very angry that the gu didn't succeed in controlling me.","He ordered his men that since they couldn't manipulate me, they shouldn't let me keep my life.","While struggling against the gu worm, I was also trying to break free of my restraints. Before those people could lay a hand on me, I had already desperately broken free of one side of the chains and escaped with all the internal energy in my body.","They chased me relentlessly until I reached a cliff. I had used up all my internal energy breaking the chains, so in order not to become their puppet again, I chose to jump off the cliff.","When I woke up, I found myself lying in the house of a farming family, and at the same time I had lost my former memories.","It just so happened to be nearing dusk then. Without my memories, I didn't know that was when the toxins in my body acted up. Fortunately, I had injured my leg in the fall. My benefactor was quick on his feet, so I didn't hurt him.","It was like this for two consecutive days. Worried that I might accidentally hurt my life-saving benefactor, I asked him to help bring me to the mountains.","I barely survived in the mountains for over a month until my leg injury healed before I thought about leaving.","But I didn't know who I was or where to go, so I wanted to find a more remote place away from crowds.","Later I discovered Xi Ling Village at the foot of the mountains. It didn't have many people, and there was a house that could shelter from wind and rain, so I temporarily settled there until your arrival...\"","Hearing Mo Chongyuan recount his experiences, the Mo family felt both hatred and heartache—hatred for the mysterious man who had treated Fifth Elder Brother so badly, and heartache for the humiliating ordeal Fifth Elder Brother suffered.","If they hadn't been exiled here and if He Zhiran hadn't helped with the treatment, Mo Chongyuan might never have been able to reunite with his family again in this lifetime.","Thinking of this, Old Lady Mo was still apprehensive.","Her sons, all stalwart and devoted to protecting their family and country, had ended up in such circumstances..."]},{"number":238,"title":"Chapter 238: The One who really has something good is Shunwu Emperor","paragraphs":["Mo Chongyuan finished telling about his experiences, feeling much more relaxed in body and mind, and the pained expression had left his face.","Old Lady Mo wiped away the tears at the corners of her eyes and said, \"As the saying goes, what doesn't kill you makes you stronger. Chongyuan has already suffered through this life's tribulations, and things will only get better for him from now on.","Your mother is getting old now, I only hope that our whole family can live in peace and safety from now on.\"","\"Mother, we will, I and younger brother number eight and nine will take good care of you from now on,\" said Mo Chongyuan.","As he spoke, Mo Chongyuan had already risen from the kang and solemnly knelt in front of his aged mother.","\"I was unfilial before and made you worry,\" he said.","Seeing her son like this brought fresh tears to Old Lady Mo's eyes, and soon the other daughters-in-law were also dabbing at their eyes.","He Zhiran was also a woman, and although she was a bit tougher mentally than her sisters-in-law and Mo Hanyue, she had to admit she was made of water.","She couldn't stand scenes like this, and seeing everyone crying loudly, she figured it wouldn't end anytime soon and might bring up more painful memories.","So she dabbed at her somewhat reddened eyes and said, \"Mother, sisters, it's good that fifth brother has regained his memories. Wasn't mother wanting fifth brother to paint the kitchen god? It's almost noon already, what are we waiting for?\"","Old Lady Mo also knew her daughter-in-law's intention, and led the way in wiping her tears and urged Mo Chongyuan to go paint the image of the kitchen god.","Sure enough, Mo Chongyuan had incredible literary talent, and the image of the kitchen god he painted was absolutely magnificent.","He Zhiran even thought of having him paint some other things to put in her online shop to try selling.","Speaking of her online shop, she hadn't managed it for a long time, just casually checking if revenue had increased.","Also, Little Collector hadn't been around to buy things recently, seemingly having disappeared.","He Zhiran didn't know much about the customs around the New Year, and she and Mo Jiuye had already taken care of getting all the necessary food when they went out the day before.","Now all of their meat came from her personal dimension, and they had also bought a lot of seafood from the fishing village, along with preparing several kinds of vegetables that made sense.","Now all of the food at home was prepared, her sisters-in-law didn't need He Zhiran to manage things, she just needed to cook any special dishes.","Just happening to have some free time, He Zhiran returned to her room and flashed into her dimension.","There were still a lot of items taken from Deputy Magistrate Cui in the storage room that, although not as valuable as the things in the imperial treasury, were still antiques worth hanging in her shop.","To keep these things from taking up space in the storage room, He Zhiran took photos of everything and uploaded it all to her shop to sell.","Just as she finished organizing these things, the personal icon below her phone screen shook.","This personal icon was not unfamiliar to He Zhiran, it was none other than Little Collector, who had been missing for a long time.","Little Collector: [Boss, you're really amazing, new inventory in your shop again.]","He Zhiran: [They're just some worthless stuff.]","Little Collector: [Boss is too modest, anything that's an antique can't be called worthless stuff.]","He Zhiran: [It's all relative.]","This was no lie, when she uploaded the photos just now, like those few jade ornaments for example, they were priced at less than half of what was in the imperial treasury.","This showed that Deputy Magistrate Cui was just a country squire, the one with truly good stuff was still Emperor Shunwu.","Little Collector: [Boss, the antiques sold in your shop are real and good value. If I could get my funds to turn around now, I would definitely buy up everything in your shop.]","He Zhiran: [Did something happen?]","She was just casually caring about a regular customer. She didn't expect Little Collector to answer very sincerely:","[My family has always dealt in the antique business and never had money issues before. It was just that I partnered with a friend sometime ago to buy a 10 centimeter wide South Sea pearl that was stolen when I was arranging for it to be exhibited.","That pearl was very valuable, taking up over half of my net worth. Since the pearl was lost under my watch, I have to pay my friend for their portion of course.]","South Sea pearls were not unfamiliar to He Zhiran, and their value also varied greatly.","She was very curious now what kind of quality was the pearl that Little Collector had lost:","[What was that South Sea pearl you mentioned like?]","Little Collector: [That South Sea pearl was very special, 10 centimeters in diameter, jet black throughout without a single flaw. Many experts appraised it and determined it was produced during the Da Shun Dynasty, an extremely rare antique grade piece.]","He Zhiran had seen South Sea pearls before, but had never seen a black 10 centimeter wide one.","The clam that produced that kind of pearl must have become a spirit...","Because Little Collector mentioned the South Sea pearl originating from the Da Shun Dynasty, it greatly piqued He Zhiran's interest:","[You said this South Sea pearl came from the Da Shun Dynasty?]","Little Collector: [That's right, experts determined this pearl originated from the Da Shun Dynasty. It's said there's also some backstory to this pearl.]","He Zhiran became even more interested: [What backstory?]","Little Collector: [It's said this pearl came from the Southern Frontier, and the emperor there lost a battle at the time. Emperor Shunwu proposed he use that pearl as part of his war indemnity, but the Southern Frontier Emperor stubbornly refused.","That's because the pearl was Empress of Southern Frontier Yun Li's favorite possession, and the Southern Frontier Emperor doted on his wife, so he'd rather cede a city than hand over that pearl.]","Regarding this bit of history, He Zhiran actually didn't know much about it at all.","After all, later generations learned central plains culture, with only some history experts deeply researching those ancient small periphery states.","So there was no record of this in the history books she bought either.","Speaking of Yun Li, this bit of history must have been changed by her too.","If she didn't traverse here, Mo Jiuye's chances of surviving likely weren't high, let alone capturing Yun Li and Nan Heng at the salt lake and killing them.","But thinking about the South Sea pearl that Little Collector mentioned, now there was a high possibility that it was still being kept in the Southern Frontier's treasury or imperial palace.","What He Zhiran was thinking now was, if she went to the Southern Frontier and helped Little Collector look for that black South Sea pearl from this era while she was there, then sold it to him in her shop, wouldn't that be a mutually beneficial action for both parties?","Thinking this, she tentatively asked: [If I can find that pearl, would you want it?]","After waiting about a minute and not seeing Little Collector reply, He Zhiran figured he had gone offline or wasn't looking at his phone right then.","Since it was just an passing idea anyhow, she was about to put her phone aside to go take care of something else.","But before her fingers even touched the screen, Little Collector replied.","[That precious of a pearl, I used all my power and even got the police involved but still couldn't find it. Could the theft of the pearl have something to do with you?]","He asked very directly, because aside from those involved in the theft, it was impossible for anyone else to know the pearl's whereabouts."]},{"number":239,"title":"Chapter 239: Sell Me Fuel.","paragraphs":["He Zhiran had already anticipated that saying such words would elicit skepticism from the other party.","Anyway, she was now in ancient times. Even if she revealed the truth, modern experts who wanted to catch her for scientific research wouldn't be able to find her.","For now, it all depended on the receptiveness of the Little Collector - whether he could believe that she was a time traveler.","【I'm currently in the Da Shun Dynasty. Regarding the south pearl you lost, I can go to the south border to help you find it.】","These words truly shocked the Little Collector speechless.","If it wasn't for the fact that he had bought so many genuine antiques from He Zhiran's shop, he might even suspect that she had lost her mind to say such things.","Was she just boasting?","Previously, he had also wondered why there would be so many antiques from the Da Shun era being sold in this shop. For this, he had made some inquiries with others in the same industry, but no one knew of the existence of such an influential antique dealer.","Could the boss of this shop really be a time traveler?","【You're not deceiving me?】","He Zhiran laughed at being asked this.","【You've seen the goods in my shop. Let me ask, even industry leaders among antique dealers wouldn't possibly have as much inventory as I do, right?","Moreover, the prices are the lowest. I believe you've made quite some profit reselling the antiques you bought from me, no?】","The Little Collector found these words completely reasonable. Although he still felt it was impossible for time travel to actually exist, somehow, he was starting to believe.","【If you really can help me find that black south pearl, and the sale price is reasonable, my losses can definitely be reduced greatly.】","Although he would still have to spend money here, he had patronized this shop many times already. The prices of the antiques were much lower than market price.","If that was the case, it would be much more cost-effective for him to buy them at a low price here than to compensate his friend for half the losses.","When the south pearl was exhibited again in the future and auctioned off at a high price, at worst he wouldn't make any profit from this deal.","Right now there were no other options - either compensate his friend for the losses, or take a gamble here with the shop owner.","【Since that's the case, I'll have to trouble you to help search for that south pearl.】","He Zhiran did not bother guessing at the Little Collector's thoughts. Anyway, she wasn't lying. As for whether or not she could find that south pearl, that would just depend on luck.","Moreover, she had chosen to reveal her identity as a time traveler not just for the money from the south pearl. She had so many antiques hanging in her shop for sale, even without that south pearl, she could still earn a lot.","He Zhiran's main goal was that in the future, she might need some modern items that could not be bought on Taobao Mall. If the Little Collector could help her, their cooperation would be mutually beneficial.","【I'm very far from the south border right now, and the new year is almost here. Even if I rush there, it would probably take over a month. Will that be in time?】","Little Collector: 【My friend gave me three months to raise money. It would be best to get it within three months.】","He Zhiran: 【Three months is enough time. Whether I can find the south pearl or not, I will notify you here.】","Little Collector: 【Good, I'll await your good news.】","He Zhiran: 【However, I might need your help.】","Little Collector: 【What do you need me to do?】 He really couldn't figure out how he, someone living in modern times, could help her.","He Zhiran: 【The road to the south border is long and arduous. It would be great if there was a helicopter or off-road vehicle.】","She had thought that the distance from the northwest to the south border was about the same as the distance from here to the capital city. Even rushing day and night on fast horses, it would still take over twenty days. Wasting so much time on the road truly was a pity.","She had assumed she could just buy a helicopter or off-road vehicle on Taobao Mall, but fuel had become a major issue.","In her past life browsing various shopping sites, she certainly hadn't seen anyone selling gasoline or diesel fuel.","This request was not a big problem for the Little Collector at all.","Although he was currently facing difficulties with capital turnover, he still had two helicopters and over a dozen luxury cars in his possession.","【I have both helicopters and cars, but how do I get them to you?】","He Zhiran thought for a moment before answering: 【In the past when I bought items on Taobao, the shops directly shipped them. I can buy the helicopter and off-road vehicle myself. The only thing lacking is fuel.","If possible, I hope you can open a shop on Taobao to sell me fuel.】","Getting some fuel would be even simpler for the Little Collector.","【No problem, I'll immediately apply to open a shop. Tell me whenever you need it. I'll turn on notifications from today onward to guarantee I can reply to your messages immediately.】","He Zhiran: 【Good, it's settled then. I'll contact you before I set off for the south border.】","With the Little Collector supplying her fuel, He Zhiran no longer worried that the journey to the south border would be delayed, instantly putting her in a much better mood.","Their chat was put on hold for the moment. He Zhiran left the space.","At this time, Mo Jiuye was in the room.","\"Husband, were you waiting for me?\"","Under normal circumstances, Mo Jiuye would be busy with things outside at this time if there was no special matter. He wouldn't return to the room.","Mo Jiuye pulled her to sit down together.","\"I've been thinking, since Fifth Elder Brother could resist the puppet poison's control by that mysterious figure, it's possible Eldest Brother and Second Brother who are still missing could do the same.\"","He Zhiran had not yet carefully considered this point. Now that Mo Jiuye had brought it up, she fell deep into thought.","After a long while, she guessed:","\"I remember the Compendium of witch insect Techniques mentioned that puppet poison is very difficult to raise. Many people might not successfully raise it even if they try. So the raiser's talent and capabilities are greatly tested.","Fifth Elder Brother was the first of the Mo family members to get into trouble. It's very likely the mysterious figure's puppet poison was not yet fully mature.","Eldest Brother and Second Brother's incidents happened somewhat later. If they really are alive, the possibility they are still under the puppet poison's control is quite big. Otherwise, how could there be so many cases of sudden amnesia happening in this world?\"","Listening to his wife's analysis, Mo Jiuye kept nodding. Other than what she said, he truly could not think of any other reasonable explanation.","\"No matter what, I hope Eldest Brother and Second Brother really are alive.\"","He Zhiran could see that Mo Jiuye was very anxious to rescue Eldest Brother and Second Brother. Third Older Brother had already secretly gone out to gather information. They could only hope Third Older Brother brought back some useful news when he returned.","They had analyzed the situation as far as they could. The future was still uncertain and they would just have to take it one step at a time.","He Zhiran sighed. \"Let's go. Mother has probably finished preparing to worship the Kitchen God. Let's go over to take a look.\""]},{"number":240,"title":"Chapter 240: Offering Sacrifices to the God of the Kitchen Stove","paragraphs":["Old Lady Mo and her husband went to the main hall. As expected, Old Lady Mo had already set up the offering table for the Kitchen God, and the portrait of the Kitchen God painted by Fifth Elder was also hung on the wall.","At this time, the sisters-in-law also came to call He Zhiran. They had already prepared the ingredients and were just waiting for her to start cooking.","Although they had always lived together as a big family, for the Mo Family, celebrating a festival so formally was still He Zhiran’s first time since crossing over.","She was not very familiar with some of the customs here, but she also had an attitude of following local customs and tried her best to integrate into the family.","Today's ingredients were still purchased by He Zhiran, not only that, but also the game caught by Liang Hao and the others from the mountains.","There were too many dishes that needed to be cooked. Even though the sisters-in-law had prepared all the ingredients in advance, He Zhiran was still busy for about an hour.","When all the food was cooked, the sisters-in-law very tacitly took some of it and went to offer it to the portrait of the Kitchen God.","At the same time, Mo Jiuye also took the repackaged Maotai liquor poured by his wife and placed a cup in front of the portrait of Kitchen God.","Everything was ready. Led by Old Lady Mo, the family members began to sincerely burn incense, hoping that the Kitchen God would bless the Mo Family to be safe and sound in the future.","Just as the Kitchen God worship had just ended, it was already evening.","Everyone thought that after Mo Chuhan, who worked in the yamen, came back, they would start dinner.","Soon, Mo Chuhan returned, but unexpectedly, Meng Huaining was with him.","Meng Huaining did not come alone, he also brought a lot of yamen runners.","After many days of sorting out, the Cui Wen case had been settled.","Cui Wen was extremely evil and was directly sentenced to immediate decapitation. His family members and clansmen involved in the case also received due punishment.","The reason why the case took so long to process was mainly because Cui Wen and his clansmen committed too many crimes. Just sorting out the dossier took almost ten days.","Meng Huaining’s main purpose in coming to Xi Ling Village today was to join the Mo Family for the festivities and celebrate the New Year's Eve with them. In addition, it was to distribute the fines confiscated from the Cui Family to the victims of the Zhao and Zhou families in proportion.","Not only that, the land that the Cui Family had fraudulently obtained from the Zhao and Zhou families over the years had to be returned in full.","This move once again caused the Cui Family to wail.","They had sold farmland and barely paid the fines. Now they had to compensate a large amount of farmland to the Zhao and Zhou families.","This would instantly turn them into penniless people, and they would even have no livelihood for the future.","However, the law would not sympathize with those who had done evil before. If you did something wrong, you had to pay the proper price.","The Zhao and Zhou families did not expect that they could still get compensation.","They thought that with the backing of the powerful Cui Family gone, it would be good enough if they no longer had to suffer oppression from the Cui Family. Unexpectedly, the honorable county magistrate was so wise and brave that he even claimed compensation for them.","After receiving the compensation, the members of the Zhao and Zhou families kept kowtowing to Meng Huaining outside the Mo Family's yard.","Meng Huaining immediately ordered Meng An to appease these people. He had already smelled the aroma of the food and did not want to deal with the commoners at this time.","Meng Huaining was invited into the main hall by the three Mo brothers. After taking his seat, the women brought out the dishes one after another.","Undoubtedly, with such good ingredients and He Zhiran's cooking skills, this meal made everyone extremely satisfied.","The mellow Maotai liquor was even more delicious to Meng Huaining. If he could eat such food and drink every day, even an immortal would not change places with him.","The Mo Family women did not know that Meng Huaining would come today. It would be fine if he came alone, but he also brought so many yamen runners.","The food and wine prepared at home was simply not enough for so many people. Fortunately, the sisters-in-law had prepared dumplings in advance to entertain those yamen runners.","No matter what happened before, they were all Mo Chuhan’s subordinates now, not to mention that today was New Year's Eve. It would be inappropriate to let them leave with empty stomachs after arriving at the Mo Family home.","Now Mo Chuhan was the head of these yamen runners. With the county magistrate present at the Mo Family today, even if the Mo Family did not entertain them, they would not dare to say anything.","Unexpectedly, they could even enjoy a delicious dumpling meal here.","Moreover, the taste of the Mo Family dumplings was simply better than even the famous restaurants in the city.","The yamen runners ate their fill and were also filled with complex emotions, especially those who had previously tried to play tricks on the Mo Family to help Cui Wen. They felt particularly apologetic.","No matter what, things had happened, and now regret was useless. They could only make up for their past mistakes by being loyal to Chief Constable Mo in the future.","It was not until the hour of the dog watch that the New Year's Eve banquet began to clear the table. It was so late that Meng Huaining was expected to bid farewell.","Unexpectedly, he was attracted by a sentence from Mo Hanyue.","The surprise in Mo Hanyue's voice could not be concealed at all.","\"Ninth Sister-in-Law, come and see quickly, my long-eared rabbit has given birth...\"","He Zhiran was cleaning up bowls and chopsticks with the sisters-in-law in the kitchen. Hearing the voice of the young aunt, she immediately ran out.","\"Hanyue, I'm coming.\"","Hearing that the long-eared rabbit had given birth, the other sisters-in-law also threw down what they were doing and ran after He Zhiran to see.","The long-eared rabbit was much larger than an ordinary rabbit, and its appearance was very lovely. If Mo Hanyue was not reluctant to part with it, they would have wanted to ask her for one to raise long ago.","Now that the long-eared rabbit had finally given birth, it meant that they could also have their own little pets.","Meng Huaining was not the kind of person who liked to join in the fun, but today he was a little abnormal.","He had been inexplicably attracted by Mo Hanyue at first sight. This young girl looked bright and lively, and her temperament was not pretentious like the young ladies of wealthy families.","The elders at home had asked him before about what kind of wife he wanted in the future.","At that time, he had answered very simply that he wanted to find one that he felt was suitable and did not put on the airs of a young lady.","Although his requirements were not high, it was not easy to find someone who could meet both conditions.","Although the Meng Family had declined a lot since the death of their grandfather, they were still a prestigious scholarly family. There were still some thresholds when it came to choosing a wife.","Even if Meng Huaining was willing, girls from commoner families might not be able to pass the elders at home.","Mo Hanyue was different. Although the Mo Family was exiled by the court, Mo Hanyue grew up in a prominent family since childhood and received an education that was incomparable to that of commoners.","Especially the old lady of the Mo Family. She herself came from a prestigious family, and the daughters she personally taught could not fail to be outstanding.","Moreover, these Mo Family women all seemed knowledgeable and reasonable. Even when faced with the tragic circumstances of their husband's death in battle and the family's exile, they still maintained an optimistic and positive attitude.","How could girls who grew up in this environment not be optimistic and positive?"]},{"number":241,"title":"Chapter 241: Am I not back","paragraphs":["Most importantly, when Meng Huaining first saw Mo Hanyue, he felt his heart race.","He was not the kind of absent-minded bookworm who had never experienced love between men and women, but he knew clearly that this was the feeling you get when you fall for someone.","Therefore, when he heard Mo Hanyue's voice, no matter what had happened there, he hoped he would have a chance to participate.","With this thought, Meng Huaining stood up and said to Mo Jiuye, \"Brother Jiu, I have never seen a rabbit give birth before. May I come along to broaden my horizon?\"","Mo Jiuye did not think too much of it and assumed Meng Huaining was just curiously.","\"Sure, I'll take you to see now.\"","At this moment, the pregnant lop-eared rabbit had already been carried by Mo Hanyue to an empty room.","To make the room warmer, Mo Hanyue lit the kang stove herself.","The lop-eared rabbit in labor was alone in a cage.","When Meng Huaining and Mo Jiuye arrived, the lop-eared rabbit had already given birth to six baby bunnies.","\"Sisters-in-law, I hope she can give birth to nine babies at once. Then I will give each of you one.\" Mo Hanyue said excitedly.","\"Hanyue, you are finally willing to give me a lop-eared rabbit. That's not easy.\" the Second Sister-in-law joked.","\"Sister-in-law, are you saying I'm stingy?\" Mo Hanyue complained.","The Second Sister-in-law continued joking, \"You still say you are not stingy. For the rabbits given to you by Sister-in-law Jiu, if we want to hug them a little, you can't bear to let us.\"","Mo Hanyue really couldn't bear to part with them. She hoped that through her own efforts, these rabbits could give birth to more babies and earn some money for the family.","Back in the capital city, she was a young lady from a prominent family and knew what those girls liked.","Mo Hanyue was certain that these cute and beautiful lop-eared rabbits would be loved by those young ladies.","Therefore, she took very good care of every rabbit, especially after discovering pregnant does. She took extra care of them for fear that something unexpected might happen to the rabbits under her care.","When these rabbits gave birth, she believed they would fetch a good price.","As they talked, the sisters-in-law noticed Mo Jiuye and Meng Huaining walking in.","As a guest, Meng Huaining must have come because of the rabbits. Thus, the sisters-in-law tacitly gave him a good spot to observe.","On the surface, Meng Huaining was watching the little bunnies, but he would sneak glances at Mo Hanyue when others were not paying attention.","Mo Hanyue was carefully observing the doe rabbit when she inexplicably sensed a gaze fixed on her.","She instinctively looked in the direction of the gaze and met Meng Huaining's deep eyes.","Meng Huaining was engrossed in staring at her and did not expect her to look back at him.","In panic, he averted his eyes, his heartbeat racing to the extreme unknowingly.","Mo Hanyue felt the same. Although she did not have any improper thoughts about Meng Huaining, as an innocent girl, she could hardly resist such a fiery gaze.","Moreover, it seemed that she did not dislike Meng Huaining's gaze...","Everyone's attention was on the rabbit in labor and no one noticed the expressions of the two.","After about half a quarter of an hour, the lop-eared rabbit had given birth to 12 kits. Feeling that she was not moving anymore, Mo Hanyue carefully moved the cage aside.","At this point, Meng Huaining could not find a suitable reason to stay longer. He secretly glanced at Mo Hanyue again before bidding farewell to the Mo family.","The Mo family was also busy for a day. After tidying up, they each went back to rest.","The next day, there was good news in the family again. The rabbits raised by the Fifth Brother and Sister-in-law had reproduced several litters.","By evening, the number of offspring reached more than 200, and the new baby bunnies made the whole family joyful.","Time flew by, and New Year’s Eve arrived in the blink of an eye.","It should have been a happy day, but the Mo family was worried because Third Brother Mo Yunfeng had not returned as scheduled.","Old Madam Mo knew her sons best. He had been taught by her since childhood to be true to his word.","If Mo Yunfeng had not run into some thorny issues, he would not still be away as the New Year approached.","Ever since early morning, the anxious Third Sister-in-law had been restless. The whole family was busy preparing ingredients for the New Year's Eve dinner while she kept making mistakes when doing chores.","For example, when beating eggs, she put the eggs into the trash can and left the shells on the plate.","Fortunately, most of the women in the family did not know that Mo Yunfeng was still alive. Otherwise, the whole family would have become gloomy.","The Third Sister-in-law knew that her mind was not there, afraid of ruining more things in the house. So she went back to her room on the excuse of feeling unwell.","Because of this, Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran lost their enthusiasm for setting off firecrackers they bought from town.","Until night fell, Old Madam Mo thought that the New Year should not be ruined just because someone was missing. So she urged everyone to sit down for dinner.","Including Liang Hao and others, they sat at two tables.","Just as everyone had just sat down, several masters with martial arts skills suddenly stood up.","Mo Chuhan said, \"There are footsteps outside. I'll go take a look.\"","With that said, he strode out, and Mo Jiuye and Mo Chongyuan looked at each other before following him out.","The Third Sister-in-law had been desperately waiting for her husband's return. Hearing that there were footsteps, she subconsciously went outside with everyone.","Soon, Mo Chuhan's slightly excited voice came, \"Third Brother, you finally came back. If you didn't come back, Jiuye and I were going to go looking for you tomorrow morning.\"","Mo Yunfeng was apparently somewhat tired but still looked spirited as ever.","\"I ran into some things on the way that delayed me, otherwise I could have been back earlier.\"","The women left in the room were confused, except for Old Madam Mo and He Zhiran.","Who did Mo Chuhan just call?","Third brother?","To verify that their ears were not mistaken, the sisters-in-law, including Mo Hanyue, all came out.","He Zhiran also helped the trembling old lady who was excited. They walked at the end.","The moment everyone saw Mo Yunfeng, their expressions varied.","Except for those few who knew, disbelief filled the eyes of the women.","The reaction of the Second Sister-in-law was even more dramatic. She fiercely pinched the Fourth Sister-in-law next to her.","\"Did it hurt, Sister-in-law Si?\"","The dumbfounded Fourth Sister-in-law nodded, \"Yeah, it hurt a lot.\"","\"Then it means I'm not seeing things...\" the Second Sister-in-law murmured.","At this time, the Third Sister-in-law had already recklessly thrown herself into Mo Yunfeng's arms.","\"Husband, you finally came back. I thought I was going to lose you again...wuwuwu...\"","Mo Yunfeng raised his arm around his wife and gently soothed, \"Don't cry, didn't I come back?\"","The Third Sister-in-law still wept bitterly. The other women surrounded Old Madam Mo and asked when the resurrected Third Brother had come back to life.","Old Madam Mo was also a little overwhelmed being surrounded by so many daughters-in-law.","\"Alright, it's cold outside. Let's go back in and talk inside.\""]},{"number":242,"title":"Chapter 242: Seems to have a certain calmness about him.","paragraphs":["The elders had spoken, so everyone naturally had to listen.","The crowd escorted Mo Yunfeng into the main house and sat down around the dining table.","The few brothers gathered together, feeling like they had a bellyful of questions to ask.","But seeing that the dishes on the table were about to get cold, and moreover, seeing Mo Yunfeng's travel-worn appearance, the few brothers tactfully did not ask immediately.","Old Lady Mo also felt the same way. Her son had rushed back with difficulty, even if there were earth-shattering events, it could not delay the family from having a nice reunion dinner.","After sweeping her eyes around, Old Lady Mo spoke.","\"Let's eat first, if there's anything you want to ask, there's plenty of time to chat during the New Year's Eve, it can help pass the time.\"","Mo Yunfeng also thought that those matters were not tricky, and it would be fine to talk about them later.","\"Let's all listen to Mother and eat first.\"","At this moment in the Mo family, apart from Old Lady Mo this elder, Mo Yunfeng was the oldest among the brothers, so he had more say at the dinner table.","Mo Jiuye saw the tense atmosphere in the family relax, and went out to the courtyard to light firecrackers.","Accompanied by the sound of firecrackers popping, the Mo family in the northwest finally started their first reunion dinner on New Year's Eve.","The dishes on the table were all carefully prepared by the women.","Especially for the ingredients and menu, thanks to He Zhiran's arrangements, it was definitely at the level of an imperial feast.","Steamed bass, spicy crab, garlic stir-fried lobster, spicy stir-fried mantis shrimp, shrimp and vermicelli soup, braised swimming crabs, stir-fried cuttlefish, stewed sea cucumber.","Living by the seaside was good. Just the seafood dishes on the Mo family's New Year's Eve dinner totaled eight.","Apart from that, there were another eight meat dishes, plus cold dishes and some vegetable dishes. The number of dishes on the Mo family's New Year's Eve dinner was actually over twenty.","Fortunately, the dining table Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran bought back was big enough, otherwise there would not be enough room to place all the dishes.","Even so, the dishes were stacked up, very compact.","Moreover, most of these dishes were personally prepared by He Zhiran, so the taste must be extraordinary.","In order to let the family eat well, He Zhiran also made orange juice in her space. For the men who liked to drink alcohol there was Wuliangye liquor, while she and the other women had orange juice.","Ever since they were exiled, the family had seen many rare items, they were too lazy to even ask where this sweet and refreshing orange juice came from.","With Ninth Brother and Ninth Brother's wife around, they could get all kinds of good stuff...","At this moment, everyone temporarily ignored their concern for Mo Yunfeng and was completely immersed in the delicious food.","Since the news came out that Mo Yunfeng had died, it had been almost four years. Reunited with his family again, he did not expect the dishes at home to have become so delicious.","During this period of time he was looking for the whereabouts of Eldest and Second Brother outside, eating simple meals day after day. He simply hadn't had a decent meal.","Especially today, in order to reunite with his family earlier, he had used his lightness skill since daybreak to rush back.","He hadn't had a grain of rice or a drop of water for a whole day, over consuming his energy. At this moment he was starving.","He could no longer chat with his brothers and Liang Hao, and kept his head lowered to keep putting food into his mouth.","It could be said he was originally a young master from a prestigious family, and must have no lack of proper manners, and they would have been ingrained.","But faced with so many delicacies, Mo Yunfeng directly discarded all the aloofness that he should have to the back of his mind.","He thought he would be very embarrassed, but when he looked up after having eaten fifty percent of his meal, he saw his brothers in the same state. Even Liang Hao and the rest who were usually more restrained in front of them were the same.","Seeing this scene, Mo Yunfeng understood.","It wasn't that he lacked manners, but that everyone was the same as him.","Therefore, Mo Yunfeng no longer had any reservations in his heart and continued to eat heartily with his brothers.","Not only Mo Yunfeng had doubts about this issue. Mo Chongyuan, Mo Chuhan and Mo Jiuye had also questioned themselves similarly before.","Later, the few brothers finally found the reason why they would not be courteous when eating now - the dishes at home now were so delicious that it completely defeated the so-called aloofness in their hearts.","The women were much more elegant, their eating movements not as fast as the men. Even so, by the end of the New Year's Eve dinner, there was almost nothing left on the table.","The women took the initiative to stand up and clear the bowls and chopsticks. Only then did Old Lady Mo look at Mo Yunfeng.","Mo Yunfeng's dark short jacket was already dirty beyond recognition. Although his hair was not as messy as when Old Lady Mo first saw him at the salt lake, there was still a layer of dust on it.","The stubble on his face was particularly conspicuous, evidently he had not grooming himself for a long time.","Thinking that her son who had previously loved being clean had now become so slovenly, Old Lady Mo couldn't help but feel a pain in her heart.","\"Yunfeng must have suffered a lot along the way?\"","When facing his mother, Mo Yunfeng appeared very respectful.","\"Mother worries too much, your son is fine.\"","The mother and son had just spoken a few words when Third Sister-in-law came over.","\"Husband, look how dirty you are. I just boiled some hot water, go take a wash first.\"","It wasn't that Third Sister-in-law wanted to snatch him from Mother-in-law, but she knew her husband's habit of loving cleanliness better.","If they hadn't rushed to eat the New Year's Eve dinner just now, her husband would probably have gone to wash up first.","Old Lady Mo also had this intention in mind, gently saying, \"Yunfeng, go freshen up first, then we'll talk.\"","Mo Yunfeng had already felt very uncomfortable all over, so he got up and left with his wife.","During her free time, Third Sister-in-law had made him quite a lot of changes of clothes, including underwear, outerwear and padded clothes, and even shoes were prepared in several pairs.","In less than an hour, Mo Yunfeng returned, washed up and tidy.","When He Zhiran opened the door, she was actually stunned for a few seconds.","Who was this messy person just now?","He looked exactly like a tall, rich and handsome guy...","The Mo brothers were almost all over 180 cm tall with well-proportioned figures.","Needless to say about their looks, any one that He Zhiran had seen were dignified.","Now in his prime years, Mo Yunfeng naturally exuded a sense of stability.","And when Third Sister-in-law looked at her husband, her eyes were full of love.","Old Lady Mo pointed to the place beside her.","\"Yunfeng, come, sit by Mother.\"","Seeing Third Brother sit down, Mo Hanyue quickly went forward to pour him a cup of tea.","Mo Yunfeng knew everyone had a bellyful of questions to ask, he took a sip of tea before taking the initiative to speak.","\"After I left the salt lake, I went straight to the Southern Border.","Only after entering the Southern Border region did I realize many people there raised Gu, and the Gu Masters there kept a very low profile, their daily coming and going was no different from ordinary people, you couldn't tell who was a Gu Master at all.","Later, after my extensive inquiries, I learned that there was a Gu rearing sacred land in Southern Border called Si Meng Mountain Villa. They didn't know the real name of the founder, everyone called him Mr. Si Meng.\"","Hearing the two characters \"Si Meng\", Old Lady Mo frowned slightly.","The abnormal reaction from Mother-in-law did not escape He Zhiran's eyes."]},{"number":243,"title":"Chapter 243: What's so special about that name","paragraphs":["\"Daughter, is there anything special about this name?\" Old Lady Mo hesitated for a moment and told a story from the past.","\"I'm just a little sensitive to the word 'Meng', that's all. Back then, when your father and I had just married, the border wars were intense, and His Majesty immediately appointed your father as Marshal to lead the troops to provide support.","When I was young, I was impatient and didn't want to be separated from your father, so I disguised myself as a man and followed the army.","Your father won a great victory when he went out on the expedition, and it only took him two months to drive the bandits in the South Border out of our Da Shun's territory, while capturing the top general of the South Border.","It was only when he was being interrogated that it was discovered that the top general of the South Border turned out to be their Crown Princess Yuan Meng.","At that time, I was standing next to your father in the uniform of an ordinary soldier. It was obvious that she was infatuated with your father and even claimed that as long as your father agreed to marry her, she would immediately return to the South Border to persuade her father the Emperor to completely surrender to Da Shun.","Her request was rejected outright by your father on the spot. Later, that Yuan Meng was unwilling to accept it. After she was exchanged back by the Emperor of the South Border with a large amount of wealth, she still tried every means to get close to your father.","Until we returned triumphantly to the capital, when I had already given birth to your eldest brother, Yuan Meng was still infatuated with your father.","For this reason, the Emperor of the South Border specially sent envoys to request that His Late Majesty arrange a marriage between Yuan Meng and your father.","His Late Majesty knew about the Mo Family rules and understood your father’s temperament even better, so he directly rejected the request of the South Border envoys.","Even so, Yuan Meng still didn’t give up. Not long after the South Border envoys returned, she personally came to the capital city of our Da Shun and pestered your father relentlessly.","In the face of such a person, your father and I both felt extremely angry. As a last resort, your father asked His Late Majesty for permission to voluntarily guard the western border.","As he became the border garrison commander, he could naturally bring his family along, so I had always been by his side.","Unexpectedly, Yuan Meng still didn’t give up. She madly used her own blood to raise Gu.","Unfortunately, Yuan Meng was too impatient. When she was casting the Gu, your father saw through it in one glance. In a fit of anger, he beheaded Yuan Meng on the spot.","This incident caused a sensation between the South Border and Da Shun that year. Shao Xin, a young master from the South Border who was in love with Yuan Meng, personally volunteered to attack Da Shun in order to avenge Yuan Meng and behead your father with his own hands.","Unfortunately, whether it was martial arts or military tactics, Shao Xin was no match for your father. When the army of the South Border was defeated and retreated, Shao Xin swore in front of both armies that his only wish in this life was to avenge Yuan Meng and curse the Mo Family to have no descendants left. \"","After listening to this story, Mo Jiuye asked solemnly, \"Mother, do you mean that this Sir Si Meng is very likely to be that Shao Xin who was in love with Yuan Meng back then?\"","Old Lady Mo said lightly, \"I've said so much, it's just speculation. Your brothers have all been poisoned by Gu, and the Gu technique originates from the South Border. This makes me inevitably think of this person.","Especially your father's death, which has a lot of similarities with what happened to your brothers.\"","Mo Jiuye was still young when Lord Mo died in battle. He also only heard the specifics from his elders and older brothers.","He only knew that his father had also been poisoned by the villain from the South Border, and was later captured and had his severed head hung on the city wall.","Now, when he thought about what happened to his brothers carefully, wasn't it exactly the same as what happened to his father?","The Mo brothers couldn't help but clench their fists at the same time.","Mo Chuhan tried his best to suppress the anger in his heart and asked, \"Third Brother, were you able to find out the true identity of Sir Si Meng on your trip?\"","This was the key question that everyone wanted to know. Mo Yunfeng said solemnly,","\"I probed in the South Border for months before finally finding the Si Meng Mountain Villa. It was completely different from what I had imagined. Not only was it not magnificent, it looked a little shabby instead.\"","\"Shabby?\" Mo Jiuye couldn't help but ask. Indeed, this was not only unexpected to Third Brother, but he also felt a little incredulous.","It was known that those gu raisers from the South Border were very rich. How could they even describe the place where they live as shabby?","Mo Yunfeng nodded, \"That's right. It was indeed very shabby, and I searched there for three days but didn't see anyone.","Just when I was about to leave, I suddenly found someone coming out of the mountain villa. I guessed that there must be some kind of secret passage in the mountain villa, otherwise why didn't I find anyone after lingering there for so long?","So I carefully followed that person. He should have gone out to buy supplies. He went to the market to buy some rice and then went back.","I followed him back into the mountain villa again. Perhaps that person had long discovered my existence. When he reached the mountain villa, he deliberately took a roundabout route and finally stopped in a corner.","That person used Gu as soon as he made a move. Fortunately, I dodged it quickly and didn't get hit. Then that person threw several Gu worms at me but I dodged them all. Perhaps realizing that he was no match for me, he scattered a handful of poison powder and fled the scene.","Having suffered such losses before, I instinctively covered my nose and mouth when I saw the poison powder. Taking advantage of this opportunity, that person fled quickly.","I chased him for three full days until I caught him within the territory of Da Shun.","Only through interrogation did I learn that Sir Si Meng had not returned there for six years. Those who had previously sought protection under Sir Si Meng had also gradually left, and now there were only a few gu raisers guarding the mountain villa.\"","\"So the Si Meng Mountain Villa does have secret chambers and the like.\" Mo Chongyuan said solemnly.","\"That's right. I learned from that person that the entrance to the secret chamber of Si Meng Mountain Villa is under a dried-up well. That place is very hidden, no wonder I didn't find anything after searching for so long.","If it wasn't for the thought that my family would worry if I didn't rush back home for the New Year, I would have definitely gone back to check it out.\" Mo Yunfeng said lightly, \"Now my family knows I'm safe. I plan to go back and investigate after the New Year.\"","Among the brothers, Mo Chuhan had the most impulsive temperament. He stood up and slammed his fist heavily on the table.","\"I'll set off for the South Border now and turn the Si Meng Mountain Villa upside down.\" After speaking, Mo Chuhan had already turned to leave but was stopped solemnly by Old Lady Mo.","\"Chuhan, sit down. Things haven't been figured out yet. What are you going to do if you go?","Besides, the people in Si Meng Mountain Villa are all good at gu techniques. Can you be sure you won't get hit again if you go?","When that happens, not only will you not find out anything about your eldest and second brother, but the family will have to try to save you too.\"","Hearing his mother's words, Mo Chuhan suddenly lost his momentum and reluctantly sat back down.","\"Mother, then what should we do? It's hard to finally find a clue. Can we just give up like this?\"","Old Lady Mo's eyes swept around and finally settled on He Zhiran.","She had noticed long ago that the brains of her ninth daughter-in-law were much better than those of her sons. At times like this, it was necessary to listen to her opinion.","\"Lady He, what do you think about this matter?\"","After listening to Third Brother's account, He Zhiran had also been pondering."]},{"number":244,"title":"Chapter 244: Nine Ye has a point.","paragraphs":["When Grandma Mo asked, she did not hurry to express her opinion, but continued to inquire Mo Yunfeng.","\"Third Brother, have you asked the people you caught about the real situation of those who stayed at the mountain villa? Also, does he know about Mr. Si Meng's whereabouts?\"","\"I've asked all these questions. Including him, there were a total of six people staying at the mountain villa. As for Mr. Si Meng's whereabouts, he said that people at his level basically have no access to that information.","He also heard from others that Mr. Si Meng would go to the west border of Da Shun every July, but what exactly he was doing there was unknown.\" Mo Yunfeng told them the information he had found out.","When He Zhiran heard this, she asked Old Lady Mo again: \"Mother, what month was it when Father accidentally killed Yuan Meng?\"","Old Lady Mo didn't even need to think and answered directly: \"It was July.\"","Mo Jiuye stood up abruptly: \"In that case, it is very likely that Mr. Si Meng is that young master from a prestigious family who was in love with Yuan Meng.\"","Old Lady Mo nodded: \"I think so too, otherwise why would that puppet master be so against our Mo family?\"","He Zhiran fell silent for a moment before speaking: \"No matter whether this Mr. Si Meng is that person or not, this is a very useful clue. This person's whereabouts are currently unknown, and trying to find him would be like looking for a needle in the ocean.","Instead of going to the west border in July to take a look, we can't let our guard down in the south either, although there are many puppet masters there, so we still need to make some preparations in advance.\"","Whether the trip to the south was to look for new clues or not, she had to go there anyway.","The black south pearl she promised the little collector, and the molting skin antidote her sisters-in-law needed were all in the south.","\"But the later we find out about Eldest and Second Brother's whereabouts, the more dangerous it will be for them.\" Mo Chuhan still felt somewhat uneasy.","Mo Jiuye understood his eighth brother's eagerness to save people, but currently whether Eldest Brother and Second Brother were even still alive was unknown, moreover, it had been several months since he and his wife had killed Yun Li. If that Mr. Si Meng really was Yun Li's master, he must have guessed by now that Yun Li was already dead.","Since he knew of Yun Li's death, if the news of Third Brother still being alive was not deliberately concealed, it wouldn't take long for it to spread.","Even if Mr. Si Meng was brainless, he could figure out that Yun Li was dead while the Mo Yunfeng he was controlling with his puppet worm was still alive. This would definitely put him on high alert.","There was also Nan Rui's side to consider, whether he would be able to conceal the truth of Eighth Brother's already having dispelled the puppet worm.","In order to find Eldest Brother and Second Brother's whereabouts now, they really had to act low-key to avoid attracting that person's attention.","Not to mention, to go out looking for Eldest and Second Brother, they would have to bring Zhiran with them. With so many secrets about his wife, it would be very inconvenient with other people tagging along.","\"Eighth Brother, you still have to go to the government office to work. I'll take care of the trip to the south.\"","As soon as Mo Jiuye's voice fell, Mo Yunfeng and Mo Chongyuan stood up at the same time.","\"Count me in too. I'm quite familiar with the south from my previous trip. Locating Si Meng Mountain Villa will be no problem.\"","\"I want to go too. More people means more power.\"","Liang Hao and others, who had been silent all this time, also expressed their desire to accompany Mo Jiuye to the south.","Mo Jiuye understood the logic of there being more power in numbers, but his wife had too many secrets on her. It would be inconvenient with other people around.","\"The main purpose of this trip south is to gather information. The family's safety here is also very important. Zhiran can dispel puppet worms. I've decided it'll just be the two of us going.\"","\"No!\" Third Brother objected first.","\"No!\" Fifth Brother didn't agree either.","\"Ninth Master, it's dangerous in the south. Please take us with you!\" Liang Hao pleaded anxiously.","Mo Jiuye waved his hand. His mind was set. Even if they insisted on following along, he could still think of other ways to act separately with Zhiran.","\"We'll change our outfits. No one will recognize us there. A large group would only attract unwanted attention instead.\"","Seeing the group of bickering children, Old Lady Mo finally spoke up.","\"What Jiuye said makes sense. Let the couple go take a look first. No matter what, they have to go early and come back early. If they encounter any difficulties, don't overdo it and just come back so we can think of solutions together.\"","Although Old Lady Mo didn't actually say it out loud, she knew best in her heart that being able to successfully rescue her sons was all thanks to her ninth daughter-in-law's capabilities.","Without her, even if they found out her sons were still alive, with the puppet worms in them they still wouldn't be able to bring them back safely.","Therefore, when it came to making decisions, Old Lady Mo would of course listen to Mo Jiuye.","With Old Lady Mo having made the final call, even if the others were unhappy, they could only obey.","\"There's no rush for this matter. Have Jiuye and the young Miss He set off after New Year's,\" Old Lady Mo said again.","With that, the matter was completely settled. Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran would prepare and set off for the south after the new year, while the official inspections could be left to Mo Chuhan and Meng Huaining. No doubt they would have it under control.","Not to mention, Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran would definitely disguise themselves before leaving, so no one would be able to recognize the Mo family members leaving the city.","Seeing his mother help settle the matter, Mo Jiuye also relaxed.","Even though he had already thought of ways around it, if everyone went together, they would inevitably have to come up with excuses to split off midway. This way was better, with just him and Zhiran. If they encountered danger, they could still hide in her space—that was safer.","The festival was originally meant to be joyous, but the news Mo Yunfeng brought back plunged everyone's mood into gloom for a while.","Especially Eldest Sister-in-Law and Second Sister-in-Law. Hearing that their husbands might still be alive stirred up complex emotions.","In order not to ruin the festive atmosphere for the family, they endured the tears welling up in their eyes.","They also realized that the other women didn't know about this matter, only a few uncles and the Ninth Sister-in-Law, as well as Mother.","It would have been awkward to ask the uncles. After the decision to go south was made, the two pulled He Zhiran aside to ask.","Since the matter was already being openly discussed, He Zhiran told the two sisters-in-law everything she knew.","As for the possibilities she and Mo Jiuye had privately analyzed, she didn't mention those. It wasn't right to give the sisters-in-law too much hope over uncertain matters. If Eldest Brother and Second Brother really weren't around anymore, wouldn't that just lead to empty joy for the two sisters-in-law?","Learning more, Eldest and Second Sister-in-Law completely lost control of their tears. They hugged each other tightly and wept bitterly, then after crying it out, they knelt on the ground and prayed for their husbands to still be alive...","Faced with this situation, He Zhiran also didn't know how to comfort them. Perhaps crying it all out was the best way to vent their feelings.","She quietly exited her sisters-in-law's room and returned to her own quarters.","Today was New Year's festival, yet her precious little bun was still alone in her space. Taking advantage of everyone being in the main house to keep vigil for the new year, she entered her space to accompany her little bun.","The moment she walked into the farm, He Zhiran was stunned by the sight before her eyes.","In the distance, she could clearly see Rice Ball sitting upright at the edge of the pasture, his two plump little paws waving back and forth.","The hundred-plus sheep raised inside the space were lined up neatly in two columns facing the little guy.","Sensing his master's aura, Rice Ball clumsily glanced back. Unlike usual times, he didn't run over looking for affection. Instead he continued waving his paws at the sheep."]},{"number":245,"title":"Chapter 245: Big G","paragraphs":["He Zhiran did not disturb it and stood there quietly watching.","I saw that after hearing Rice Ball's order, the first row of sheep started running to the left, while the row behind went in the opposite direction.","Soon, the flock of sheep had surrounded themselves into a large circle.","Looking again, Rice Ball's round little body was already standing upright, waving its little paws again, while still making a sound similar to a sheep's cry coming from its mouth.","After hearing Rice Ball's cry, the flock of sheep gradually gathered inward, then gathered densely together.","Only then did Rice Ball stop its actions, stepping with its little short legs to run to its owner as if to show off its achievement, while also making a chirping sound of excitement.","When the little guy ran over, He Zhiran grabbed it and hugged it, helping it tidy up the grass blades and dirt on its body.","\"Rice Ball, I didn't expect you to be more capable than the sheepdog, training those sheep to be obedient.\"","\"Hmm -\"","Rice Ball seemed to be able to fully understand its owner's words. After calling out, it strenuously drilled its furry little head into her arms.","Seeing such an adorable little dumpling, He Zhiran's heart was melting.","She quickly made a bowl of milk with her thoughts to reward Rice Ball.","At the same time, she was also thinking about Rice Ball's placement issues after she went to the South.","This guy usually likes to stick to her the most, and also really likes life in the space.","Especially its various foods, which are currently all produced in the space. If the little guy is left at home, in addition to not being used to it, its diet would also be difficult to resolve.","After thinking it over, He Zhiran decided to take Rice Ball with her to the South.","Anyway, this guy has been lying in her space recently. When others asked about it, she always said that Rice Ball went into the mountains.","One thing led to another, as long as others didn't see Rice Ball, they would think it went into the mountains. After all, it was a wild little animal, so there was nothing strange about it going into the mountains.","She could just conceal it with this excuse at that time...","His wife finally reunited with her husband who had returned home, and her whole person looked much more spirited than before.","She had tidied up the room over and over again. Her husband was a clean freak. In the past, it was the servants in the house who handled these things. Now she took the initiative to do it herself, afraid that her husband would find it unsatisfactory after seeing her work. After cleaning up, she carefully checked it again.","Seeing that there were no hygiene blind spots left, she folded back to the main room.","When she got there, the family was still discussing going to the South. She couldn't get a word in edgewise and could only sit there silently watching.","Finally, after midnight, the family ate dumplings and Mother Mo arranged for everyone to go back and rest.","Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran entered the space together. Neither of them were sleepy at the moment, so they planned things for their trip to the South.","Since it was just the two of them going this time, He Zhiran was going to make use of modern means of transportation.","To get from here to the South, it would take ten days at full gallop.","She didn't want to waste time on the road. It would be great if she could use those modern means of transportation. As long as they traveled at night when everyone was resting, and then rested during the day, they would probably save a lot of time with this method.","Thinking of this, He Zhiran sent a message to Little Collector.","[Hello, is your shop open now?]","Little Collector responded very quickly.","[The shop is already open, the fuel has all arrived, just waiting for whenever you need it. I also have off-road vehicles that can be provided. Or a helicopter if it comes down to it.]","It was evident that Little Collector really was a competent person. He Zhiran hurriedly responded gratefully.","[You don't need to provide the vehicles, as long as there is fuel.]","In her previous life, many private cars had a phrase painted on them - Never lend your wife or your car.","And that was indeed the rationale. A car was like the existence of a wife. Those who were car enthusiasts didn't like lending their cars out. Although she didn't know if Little Collector had this sort of thinking, in any case, she herself didn't want to break this unwritten rule.","Besides, she had earned so much money selling antiques, and had been worrying about not having anywhere to spend it all along. Now there was finally an opportunity to put it to good use. She must buy a car she liked.","Even if she couldn't use it often in ancient times, it didn't matter. She could keep it in her space just to feast her eyes on.","Earlier, He Zhiran had been checking out cars for sale on Taobao. After all, it was online shopping, so the selection wasn't very comprehensive. After browsing for a while, she decided to buy the most expensive G-Wagen on the Taobao Mall.","The performance of this car was pretty good. Most importantly, it had very powerful horsepower, so bumpy ancient roads wouldn't be a problem. Thus, the G-Wagen became her first choice.","Little Collector: [Let me know what kind of fuel you need, I can list it for sale at any time.]","He Zhiran: [95 octane gasoline would be good.]","Soon, a new message popped up in the chat box.","[Little Collector's shop has new listings, welcome customers to browse!]","He Zhiran followed the link and entered. She knew this was the gasoline specially prepared for her by Little Collector.","Glancing at the price, it was actually only listed for 1 yuan, in order to prevent others from taking advantage of a good deal. He Zhiran immediately placed an order.","After this wave of operations, ten huge iron buckets suddenly appeared on the empty ground in front of her.","And the model and weight of the gasoline were marked on each iron bucket.","Counting them up, there was a total of 2,000 liters of gasoline, completely enough for a round trip to the South for her, and there would definitely still be some left over.","[I'm so grateful to you. I will definitely try my best to help you get your thing done. Even if I can't, I will think of a way to find other precious items to compensate you.]","He Zhiran didn't dare make any promises, because she didn't even know where that black nanzhu was, let alone finding it. If she really couldn't locate it, she would also have to find a treasure of equivalent value for Little Collector.","[It's just a little gasoline, thanks for your trouble.]","After closing the chat box with Little Collector, He Zhiran searched for the link to the Mercedes-Benz G-Wagen.","Mo Jiuye was astonished when he saw so many big iron buckets appear in front of him. And just as he was in disbelief, another iron box with four wheels appeared before his eyes.","This time, he was completely dumbfounded.","\"Ranran, what is this?\"","He Zhiran really felt bad about this matter. She had this idea but forgot to tell Mo Jiuye about it all along, resulting in Mo Jiuye not recognizing a car at all.","Seeing Mo Jiuye's stunned look, He Zhiran hurriedly pulled his arm to explain: \"This is called a car. I also saw it while browsing Taobao.\"","\"Car?\" Mo Jiuye could tell this big guy was some kind of vehicle, but the term \"car\" was too unfamiliar to him.","He Zhiran could only patiently explain: \"I read the description that said this car can be operated by a person to run very fast without needing animals to pull it. And sitting inside is also very comfortable.\"","She couldn't say too much more. There were too many things she wouldn't be able to explain if she did.","For example, the secret that she was a transmigrator..."]},{"number":246,"title":"Chapter 246: What man doesn't like Cars","paragraphs":["When comparing the identity and space of a time traveler, it is too inconceivable.","To put it bluntly, she is just a wisp of soul from another world, and He Zhiran is not sure if she can be accepted by the people of this era.","Therefore, she intends to keep this secret buried in her heart forever.","Mo Jiuye was shocked for a moment, but soon adjusted his mood. His wife's space is so against the sky, especially that Taobao treasure that can buy things. Although he has not checked it carefully, which of the things bought from there does not overturn his cognition?","Thinking of these, he soon accepted the big iron box in front of him.","With such a weird thing in front of him, how could Mo Jiuye not take a look?","He came to the big G, first touched the window lightly with his hand, and then asked, \"Ranran, is this glass?\"","He Zhiran nodded: \"Yes, it's glass.\"","Mo Jiuye has seen the glass purchased from Henry, so she doesn't need to explain too much.","Seeing Mo Jiuye fumbling around there, she walked up and carefully explained the operation here.","Mo Jiuye was a little suspicious in his heart. Although his wife has such a magical space, he has never seen her study cars. How does she know so much about cars?","Although he was suspicious, he was used to not asking questions. After all, there were big secrets on his wife's body!","At the moment, he couldn't wait to get on the car and drive it.","He Zhiran could see Mo Jiuye's eager appearance. Which man would not like cars in the previous life?","In order not to make herself appear too familiar with cars, He Zhiran deliberately tried every move.","Mo Jiuye sat in the passenger seat and watched carefully, and remembered every step firmly in his heart.","After deliberately dragging on for a while, He Zhiran finally started the car.","She drove the car around the open space of the space and ran two laps before being replaced by the eager Mo Jiuye in the passenger seat.","It has to be said that Mo Jiuye really has a talent for driving. After only one lap, he can already operate skillfully and very steadily.","Such skills are definitely not suitable for modern roads full of traffic, but this is ancient times.","The roads they will take in the future are also some roads outside the city. At night, you can basically see no pedestrians.","Although the roads are bumpy, she bought a Great Wall SUV. Forget about bumpy roads, even if you take a rugged mountain road, there is no problem.","Mo Jiuye has completely fallen in love with the feeling of driving. This is much more relaxing and comfortable than driving a mule cart.","Moreover, the seat under him is soft and comfortable, and he doesn't feel tired at all.","At the moment, the gloom that was still in Mo Jiuye's heart just now has been completely replaced by the excitement at the moment.","He kept driving the car until the self-contained gasoline was completely exhausted before reluctantly stopping.","If he didn't know how hard it was to get that gasoline, Mo Jiuye would definitely drive a few more laps.","The transportation to the South Xinjiang has been in place, and He Zhiran also prepared some realgar.","She had seen in the \"Gu Book\" that most Gu worms were afraid of realgar and raging flames.","Compared with using a flamethrower, He Zhiran felt that realgar was more convenient. When they arrived in southern Xinjiang, they could sprinkle realgar on their clothes so that they didn't have to worry about those Gu worms getting close.","If necessary, the flamethrower can also be used to kill them completely.","As for the road trip supplies and dry food, He Zhiran only prepared some to cover up. After all, she has everything she wants in her space, and she is not worried at all about eating poorly on the road.","Everything is ready, just wait to discuss the departure time with the family.","For He Zhiran, going to southern Xinjiang was not urgent.","In her cognition, although southern Xinjiang belonged to the Fanbang small country, it was the same as Dashun. Every household celebrated the lunar new year.","With the speed of their Great Wall SUV, even if the road was bad, she believed it would take three to five days to arrive.","Going to southern Xinjiang at this time, the common people were all nestled at home celebrating the New Year, and there were few people on the road to inquire useful information.","After breakfast on New Year's Day, the family got together and discussed the result that everyone hoped they would go after the Lantern Festival.","He Zhiran was very satisfied with this time. It just so happened that the young rabbits she bought earlier had grown up, and the female rabbits had become pregnant one after another. Those male rabbits could be slaughtered to make cold rabbit meat and pendants.","Before the New Year, Tang Mingrui often came to ask when there would be new stock. It was a good time to take this opportunity during the New Year to make another batch to earn money.","After Mo Yunfeng came back, he had already explained all the information he had explored about going to southern Xinjiang. The family no longer asked him questions, and everyone was busy with their own affairs.","Now He Zhiran was supervising the slaughter of male rabbits, and all the men in the family were put to use.","There were 100 male rabbits this time. It took the men a whole morning just to carefully skin the rabbits.","Not until noon did the first guest of the new year arrive at the house.","Meng Huaining came alone, holding several oil paper bags in his hand, his face full of joy.","The reason was simple. After he realized that he had fallen in love with the girl from the Mo family, he immediately wrote a letter home to inform them.","He wanted to get his family’s consent before finding an opportunity to come to the Mo’s family to propose.","Just two days ago, he received a letter from home.","When the family members heard that he had fallen in love with the girl from the former Duke Mo's family, they all expressed their support.","Although the Mo family declined now, they all knew what was going on. They also expressed deep sympathy for the Mo family's experience.","The Mo family were all upright people, and they believed the daughter they raised must be good too.","If it wasn't for the consideration that it was New Year's Eve yesterday, he would have wanted to come earlier.","However, Meng Huaining did not intend to propose immediately. After all, he did not know Mo Hengyue's thoughts, let alone the Mo family's intentions. He was afraid that rashly mentioning this matter would have the opposite effect.","Therefore, Meng Huaining decided to come to the Mo's house more often, and take the opportunity to get in touch with Mo Hengyue.","When Meng Huaining came, the Mo brothers temporarily handed over the rabbit skinning work to Liang Hao and others, and the brothers all came to the main house to entertain him.","Meng Huaining was very surprised. He didn't expect that not only the fifth and eighth brothers of the Mo family were alive, but today he also saw a living third brother.","This made him have to think twice.","What was going on with the Mo family? The dead men came back to life one after another, which was too inconceivable.","It even made Meng Huaining have the idea that the Mo brothers might all be alive.","As for how the Mo brothers died and came back to life, this question was sensitive, and Meng Huaining was still very sensible not to ask.","But he was really happy for the Mo family from the bottom of his heart.","After chatting for a while, Meng Huaining took out the gifts he brought."]},{"number":247,"title":"Chapter 247: What a mistake this gift is.","paragraphs":["It had to be said, Meng Huaining really did everything meticulously.","What he gave to the only elder of the Mo Family, Old Lady Mo, was a stalk of aged wild ginseng to nourish her body.","What he prepared for his sisters-in-law were osmanthus cakes from the famous dessert shop in Yuncheng, and for the Mo brothers it was the tea leaves sent by his family before the new year.","Finally, Meng Huaining took out an exquisite little cloth bag, inside was actually a long-eared rabbit pendant...","In order to pick out a meaningful gift for Mo Hanyue, Meng Huaining went through a lot of trouble.","He specifically sent Meng An out to gather information on what items young ladies liked these days.","What Meng An found out was that recently, whether in Yuncheng or the surrounding counties, young ladies from wealthy families all took pride in being able to buy one of these pendants.","However, Tang Mingrui currently did not have any in stock. Meng Huaining managed to barely obtain this one by leveraging his position as the county magistrate.","Not only that, he even spent a premium price for it. People were buying them at 12 taels each, but he ended up paying 24 taels to get his hands on one.","Upon seeing this long-eared rabbit pendant, the Mo Family people had varied reactions.","The Mo brothers all looked at each other, wanting to laugh but not daring to.","The sisters-in-law were the same, and when they heard Meng Huaining spent 24 taels to buy this pendant, they all covered their mouths trying not to laugh.","Meng Huaining observed their reactions and realized something was off. Somewhat at a loss, he asked:","\"Brothers and sisters, where did I do wrong?\"","Seeing that Meng Huaining spent money wrongly buying this pendant for her, Mo Hanyue's face turned red as she explained embarrassingly.","\"Master Meng, this long-eared rabbit pendant was made by me and my sisters-in-law.\"","Hearing this, disbelief was written all over Meng Huaining's face. But looking into Mo Hanyue's pure, innocent eyes, he tried his best to gently ask:","\"Miss Mo means these pendants were made by you?\"","Mo Hanyue nodded vigorously: \"Yes, our family raises rabbits. This was made using the tanned rabbit hides.\"","Meng Huaining knew the Mo Family raised rabbits, he just thought it was to earn money selling rabbit meat.","He didn't expect they would utilize the fur so aptly.","As the youngest daughter of the family, Mo Hanyue was doted on by everyone. Seeing the pendants they made delighted the little miss, each sister-in-law had kept one of every color for her.","Mo Hanyue went back to her room for a bit, and soon brought back seven long-eared rabbit pendants in various colors.","She displayed them in front of Meng Huaining.","\"Please see, Master Meng, I have seven pendants in different colors.\"","Meng Huaining was stunned...","He had painstakingly picked out a special gift for Mo Hanyue, but in the end what he chose turned out to be something made by the Mo Family themselves.","On top of that, he had paid more than double the price to purchase it.","Thinking of this, a faint embarrassed blush crept up Meng Huaining's originally fair face.","This gift had really backfired. He blamed Meng An for not inquiring clearly when buying it, causing him to end up in such an awkward situation.","Seeing Meng Huaining's discomfort, Mo Jiuye realized his sister had poured oil on the fire by bringing out the seven colored pendants.","Even if he wanted to ease the atmosphere, he didn't know what to do.","Ultimately it was Old Lady Mo who spoke first, breaking the brief silence.","\"Although these long-eared rabbit pendants originated from our Mo Family, the quantity has always been limited. Many who failed to buy one offered high prices for them. For Master Meng to choose such a gift for Hanyue, he really gave it much thought.\"","The eldest sister-in-law also played along, \"That's right, you can tell Master Meng put great care into selecting this gift. This item is especially popular among the young ladies in the city right now.\"","The corner of Meng Huaining's mouth twitched as he followed the lead they gave him and said,","\"When this official was selecting a gift, I did think so at the time. Since this pendant came from the Mo Family, it doesn't count as a gift. This official will look for an even better item to give Miss Mo as compensation.\"","Mo Hanyue quickly waved her hands, somewhat embarrassedly saying, \"Master Meng needn't go through the trouble. I really like this gift.\"","As she spoke, she placed the pendant Meng Huaining brought together with her original seven.","\"This way it's even better, I have an additional lovely pendant.\"","As the little girl was speaking, she bashfully lowered her head.","In Northwest China, in the capital city, rich families followed strict customs. Young ladies would not appear before male guests from outside the home.","Meng Huaining was also the first outsider Mo Hanyue had interacted with at such a close distance since she was little.","Especially since Meng Huaining had extraordinary bearing himself, causing Mo Hanyue's heart to race at the sight of him.","Sitting at the head, it seemed Old Lady Mo also noticed something.","She got up and called to Mo Hanyue, \"Hanyue, accompany Mother to the rear courtyard.\"","Mo Hanyue obediently followed her mother outside.","Once outside, Old Lady Mo's expression immediately became stern.","She looked at Mo Hanyue. This girl had reached marriageable age. If it wasn't for the Mo Family's fall from grace, she would have already planned to find a suitable match from a good family for her in the capital city.","Now in Northwest China, the Mo Family's once prestigious status was gone. They were now just commoners.","Mo Hanyue's marriage had truly become a difficult matter weighing on Old Lady Mo's mind.","Although she didn't place as much importance on social status, especially since the Mo Family had already declined, as a mother she still sincerely didn't want her daughter to marry a peasant.","After all, Mo Hanyue had been well-educated since she was little, even proficient in musical instruments, chess, calligraphy and painting.","Forget about status for now. Two children raised in completely different environments living together would surely have many issues accepting each other, and in that kind of life, Hanyue likely wouldn't find happiness.","Just now, Old Lady Mo had inadvertently captured Meng Huaining's barely hidden gentle glow when looking at Mo Hanyue.","With her experience, she judged that Meng Huaining had feelings for her daughter.","It seemed her daughter did not dislike Meng Huaining either.","Although the Mo Family had fallen on hard times now, the Meng Family situation wasn't much better. Meng Huaining was only a magistrate of the seventh rank. His family had also declined.","Therefore, Old Lady Mo didn't feel that Mo Hanyue marrying Meng Huaining would be reaching too high above her station. On the contrary, it was a good match.","Thinking this, she was willing to fulfill the wish of these two young people.","However in these kinds of matters, the man's side should make the overtures first. Even if she intended to matchmake her daughter with Meng Huaining, she could not indicate so in front of others.","But before that, Old Lady Mo still wanted to understand her daughter's thoughts.","Mo Hanyue's heart and mind were simple. She didn't think about why her mother would bring her out.","Mother and daughter returned to the room. Mo Hanyue carefully placed those pendants back in their original spots, then prepared to go help out at the rear courtyard.","Seeing her about to leave, Old Lady Mo quickly stopped her.","\"Hanyue, talk to Mother.\""]},{"number":248,"title":"Chapter 248: Where is the reason for a girl not to marry","paragraphs":["Mo Hanyue heard what was said and sat back down next to her mother.","\"What does Mother want to say to Hanyue?\"","Seeing her daughter growing more graceful by the day, Old Lady Mo reached out and stroked her smooth hair.","\"My Hanyue is becoming more and more beautiful.\"","Flattered by her mother's praise, Mo Hanyue coyly said, \"Mother gave birth to me, so of course I would be beautiful.\"","Old Lady Mo lovingly put her arm around her daughter and gently said, \"Mother remembers back in the capital, suitors from prominent families would come knocking down the Mo family's door to propose to Hanyue. Back then, Mother always wanted to carefully help you choose, but who would have thought our Mo family would suffer such an unforeseen calamity, which has delayed your marriage.\"","When her mother brought up her marriage, Mo Hanyue's face immediately turned red. At the same time, the image of a person flashed through her mind.","That person had an elegant demeanor and stately bearing, possessing an innate sense of justice beyond compare with the young masters of the capital.","Mo Hanyue did not know why Meng Huaining would appear in her thoughts, nor why her heart was pounding rapidly.","To conceal her embarrassment, Mo Hanyue deliberately rested her head on her mother's shoulder so that she could not see her expression.","\"Mother, Hanyue is not getting married. I will stay home and serve you for the rest of my life.\"","Old Lady Mo laughed. \"Silly girl, it wouldn't be proper for an young lady not to marry.\"","Mo Hanyue pouted. \"But Mother, Hanyue wants to always be with you.\"","Old Lady Mo patted Mo Hanyue on the back and her tone became a little more serious.","\"Mother thinks very highly of Master Meng. What do you think?\"","Upon hearing his name, Mo Hanyue's racing heart stirred again.","She buried her head deeply in Old Lady Mo's embrace. \"Mother... how can you ask a young lady like me such a thing?\"","Hearing her daughter's response, Old Lady Mo understood completely. Her innocent daughter also looked favorably upon Master Meng.","Now that she knew her daughter's feelings, Old Lady Mo was in no hurry. Still, it would have to depend on the man taking the initiative. As for the final outcome, that would be up to the fate between them.","The men were chatting in the room while He Zhiran took the women to the kitchen to make cold rabbit meat dishes. Fresh rabbit meat at this time of year made the best cold dishes.","The main reason Meng Huaining came to the Mo family was that he wanted to see more of Mo Hanyue. But whether intentionally or not, she had not shown her face all day.","In fact, Mo Hanyue was not the lazy type. Usually when her sisters-in-law were busy, she would lend a hand. But with Meng Huaining here today, she felt too embarrassed to come out and had been holed up in her room all afternoon reading the book on medicinal herbs that her ninth sister-in-law had given her.","It was not until dinner time that Mo Hanyue finally put down her book and left her room.","Given the Mo family's current situation, meals were taken together by men and women in the main house, albeit not at the same table.","Mo Hanyue had thought to deliberately sit far from the men's table to avoid awkwardness. But her gregarious second sister-in-law happened to pull her to sit beside her, which was the closest to the men's table.","Mo Hanyue wanted to decline, but her sisters-in-law were too quick. With all the other seats already taken, she had no choice but to reluctantly sit there.","It goes without saying that the dishes for dinner were all carefully prepared by He Zhiran, most important of which was the long-awaited cold rabbit meat dishes.","Usually Meng Huaining loved eating at the Mo family the most, but today with Mo Hanyue occupying his thoughts, he was somewhat distracted during the meal.","While others were unaware of why, the perceptive Old Lady Mo had a good guess.","After dinner while drinking tea, Old Lady Mo deliberately stayed behind and casually asked some questions.","\"If I remember correctly, Master Meng should have two elder brothers in your family?\"","Old Lady Mo was fairly knowledgeable about the Meng family situation, as Meng Huaining's father's generation were her peers. They were also acquainted from their time as officials in the capital years ago.","Asked so directly, even the usually candid Meng Huaining became a little nervous, as if meeting his future mother-in-law.","\"Old Lady, please just call me Huaining. No need to stand on ceremony. Yes, I do have two elder brothers who are currently back home looking after our parents.\"","Old Lady Mo was blunt. She had looked at Meng Huaining like he was of the younger generation, and only addressed him formally out of etiquette.","\"In that case, I will call you by your name from now on.\"","After a pause, Old Lady Mo continued asking, \"Your elder brothers have long been married, no?\"","Meng Huaining respectfully answered, \"My two elder brothers were married early on under my parents' arrangement. They are fathers already.\"","Old Lady Mo sighed. \"Time and tide wait for no one. Back when I was in the capital, I saw your elder brothers who were still boys. And now they are already fathers.\"","When Old Lady Mo mentioned his brothers, Meng Huaining hoped that she would ask about him too, so that he could have a chance to express his position.","But after waiting for half a day, Old Lady Mo did not ask further.","If it were any other matter, Meng Huaining was not one to beat around the bush. He would have directly spoken his mind. But when it came to his most important personal affair, he became timid.","What a pity. When there was finally an opportunity to communicate with the Mo family elder, he did not say a single important word...","Old Lady Mo also saw that when it came to his own marriage, the young man was still somewhat reserved. She had already taken the initiative to bring up the subject, yet he did not say anything.","Since this was the case, his prospects with Mo Hanyue could only depend on fate now.","After all, he was a guest. With the hour growing late, Meng Huaining naturally had no reason to continue staying. After drinking a cup of tea, he reluctantly bade them farewell.","The women had worked late into the night before finally turning all one hundred rabbits into cold dishes. Early next morning after packaging them up, Mo Jiuye was about to deliver them directly to Tang Mingrui's place.","As luck would have it, every time right after the cold rabbit dishes had just been loaded onto the mule cart, Tang Mingrui would show up at their door with gifts.","Accompanying him this time was Tang Mingxin.","The little girl's face showed no trace of scars from the chickenpox thanks to the ointment from He Zhiran. She still had her previous spirited and cute appearance.","Seeing Tang Mingrui, Mo Jiuye knew he did not have to make the trip anymore.","He first led Tang Mingrui into the main house, then told him about preparing a huge quantity of cold rabbit dishes overnight.","Tang Mingrui had come purely to pay a New Year visit and did not expect to receive such a nice surprise this time.","To a budding young merchant, nothing was more important than business. He immediately abandoned his sister and went to check out those cold rabbit dishes, eager to bring them into the city soon for major profits.","Seeing the little female guest, Mo Hanyue took the initiative to bring her to her room to play."]},{"number":249,"title":"Chapter 249: She Must hold Her hands up.","paragraphs":["Tang Mingrui had originally planned to stay at the Mo Family for one day. At this time, people were at home celebrating the New Year. He didn't have much business to attend to, so it was a rare leisure time most suitable for visiting friends and relatives.","However, after taking stock of those cold rabbit dishes, he couldn't sit still. He wanted to transport those cold rabbit dishes into the city before noon to sell more silver during the New Year.","He called Tang Mingxin to leave together. Unexpectedly, when Tang Mingxin came out from Mo Hanyue, she was actually hugging a furry thing that looked bigger than a puppy.","The fur on the furry thing was long. Its ears were also drooping on both sides of its head because they were too long. If the rabbit had not moved, Tang Mingrui would have thought it was a new kind of doll made by the Mo Family again.","Tang Mingxin hugged the Angora lop rabbit with a smile that made her eyes curve.","\"Big brother, look, Sister Hanyue gave me a big treasure.\"","Tang Mingrui had long been attracted by the fluffy furry thing in his sister's arms. He went over to take a look and asked, \"Is this a rabbit?\"","Tang Mingxin nodded vigorously, \"Yes, it's Sister Hanyue's darling. She generously gave me one.\"","Tang Mingrui knew that the Mo Family raised rabbits. He had also followed to the backyard rabbit shed to take a look before, but those were just more good-looking than common wild rabbits, and had no comparability with this one at all.","If it was said that this rabbit was also used to eat meat, Tang Mingrui would definitely not believe it.","He knew that the rabbits raised by the Mo Family were all taken care of by Auntie Jiu, so he asked He Zhiran:","\"Auntie Jiu, did you raise this rabbit too?\"","He Zhiran had originally planned to talk about the Angora lop rabbit business after the New Year. After all, those newborn baby rabbits were still very small, and they would have to be weaned for at least some time.","What she didn't expect was that the Angora lop rabbit that Mo Hanyue had always treasured, she would so generously give someone one today.","Since Tang Mingrui had already seen it, she simply explained,","\"This is called an Angora lop rabbit. The prototype of the ornaments we make is this breed of rabbit. This kind of rabbit has a cute appearance and is very friendly. It is more suitable as a pet.\"","After listening to He Zhiran's explanation, Tang Mingrui carefully took the Angora lop bunny from his sister's hands and examined it carefully.","Not to mention the peculiar figure of the Angora lop rabbit. Just based on this silly cute appearance, even he, a grown man, liked it very much.","If such rabbits were sold on the market, the proceeds would surely be considerable.","Of course, such business would still have to find wealthy buyers.","\"Sister-in-law Mo, do you sell such rabbits?\"","\"Sell, of course they will be sold.\" He Zhiran answered very directly.","Hearing such an answer, it seemed that Tang Mingrui could already see countless banknotes flying towards him.","He remembered that when he was young and went to Jiangnan for business with his father, a wealthy family had raised one or two white long-haired cats with different colored eyes. It was said that because the cat had a special appearance and was extremely rare, the wealthy man had spent thousands of gold to buy it.","Although this was just a rabbit, its appearance was absolutely comparable to that cat.","If he could meet a buyer who really valued it, he didn't dare to guarantee that he could sell it at the sky-high price of thousands of gold, but thousands of silver should not be a problem.","Of course, such business would still have to find wealthy buyers.","\"Auntie Jiu, can you give me one or two of these rabbits to bring with me? After the fifth day of the new year, I plan to go to the prefecture to find wealthy buyers.\"","Hearing Tang Mingrui mention wealthy buyers, He Zhiran had already guessed that he intended to sell the rabbit at an astronomical price.","In this regard, she had to support it wholeheartedly.","However, He Zhiran agreed with the idea in her heart that Angora lop rabbits were going to be sold as pets.","Keeping pets is different from buying other goods. Many people like to raise them from a young age so that the feelings between humans and pets can become increasingly profound.","Not to mention that Mo Hanyue had always raised these Angora lop rabbits as treasures, so she must have deep feelings for them. If those adult rabbits raised for a few months were taken out to exchange for money, the little girl would surely feel bad.","With this thought in mind, He Zhiran explained, \"There are not many such rabbits in our family at the moment, and many have already given birth. It is estimated that in another twenty days, those baby rabbits can survive independently. Brother Tang, why don't you consider selling the baby rabbits directly at that time? I feel that would be more acceptable to people.\"","When she mentioned the baby rabbits, Tang Mingxin suddenly became all smiles. She had just witnessed how cute they were at Sister Hanyue’s place earlier.","Then she gave her elder brother a vivid description of how cute those baby rabbits were.","\"Brother, you didn't see that those baby rabbits were all white, each one like a little meatball. If Sister Hanyue wasn't worried that those rabbits were too small and I wouldn't be able to raise them, she would have definitely given me a baby rabbit.\"","After listening to his sister's description, Tang Mingrui was even more tempted.","\"Auntie Jiu, can I see those little rabbits?\"","No matter what, he had to see what these little rabbits looked like clearly. Even if he couldn't do the business immediately, at least when he met rich people in the future, he could describe it.","It seemed that Mo Hanyue must have heard the movement outside. As soon as Tang Mingrui finished speaking, she walked out holding a baby rabbit.","\"Brother Tang, please take a look. This is an Angora lop baby rabbit.\"","Such a ball of white cuteness made Tang Mingrui’s heart melt.","\"This little guy is really cute.\"","When it came to her rabbits being cute, Mo Hanyue’s pretty tail was about to curl up to the sky.","\"Of course, I take good care of them.\"","Seeing the girl's naughty appearance, Tang Mingrui suddenly felt that she was cuter than the little rabbit.","Unconsciously, he was somewhat stunned.","He Zhiran noticed Tang Mingrui's abnormality at a glance. She coughed lightly to remind, \"Brother Tang, these rabbits can be sold in twenty days after giving birth.\"","Tang Mingrui also regained his inappropriate thoughts and said solemnly, \"Okay, twenty days later, I’ll come to pick up the Angora lop rabbits.\"","The miniature lop rabbits bred a batch as well, just that the time period was shorter, and the little rabbits still couldn't handle the wind, so she let Mo Hanyue hold an adult one for Tang Mingrui to see.","The lovely appearance of these two kinds of rabbits completely subverted Tang Mingrui's cognition.","The big ones looked like puppies, and the small ones were only a little bigger than a palm. This was simply too cute.","\"Auntie Jiu, I will definitely sell these rabbits at a price that satisfies you.\"","Even without Tang Mingrui saying this, He Zhiran was very clear in her heart. After all, it was not the first time the two had worked together on business.","Especially for He Zhiran, who didn't understand business operations, she thought very highly of Tang Mingrui's business talent.","\"Alright, just sell them according to your plan when the time comes. I'm responsible for providing the rabbits.\"","Of course, the male Angora lop rabbits and male miniature lop rabbits she decided to sell could only be sold. The females could not be sold, and care had to be taken to prevent them from leaking out.","This was the only way to avoid others taking them to breed and compete with her business."]},{"number":250,"title":"Chapter 250: Arriving in Southern Xinjiang","paragraphs":["The cold rabbit meat business was indeed booming for Tang Mingrui during the New Year. He came to collect goods from the Mo Family three times in a row, and all the goods were sold out.","Life went on as usual for the Mo Family, and soon after the Lantern Festival, Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran prepared to head for the Southern Borderlands on the sixteenth day of the first lunar month.","Mo Chuhan, considering their long journey ahead, specially helped them borrow a horse from the yamen.","Meng Huaining guessed that Mo Jiuye and his wife might leave the city, and turned a blind eye to it.","The plan was to go to the Southern Borderlands with Rice Ball. When He Zhiran went out, she was holding the little guy.","Mo Jiuye got on the horse first, then pulled his wife up. Rice Ball sat obediently in front of his master. At first glance, it looked somewhat like a family of three going on a trip.","After some exhortations from Old Madam Mo, the couple set off for the Southern Borderlands with Rice Ball.","To avoid Rice Ball attracting too much attention, He Zhiran sent the little guy into the space after leaving the sight of the family.","The two set off in the morning. They had to wait until the dead of night to open the G-Wagon, so they had to conserve their energy during the day.","Therefore, after leaving Yun City, they found a place with sparse population on the official road and entered the space to rest.","Not until the big clock in the space showed 8 pm did they bring out the G-Wagon, fully fueled, onto the official road.","In ancient times, it was already deep into the night at this time, and the official road on both sides was pitch dark without a ghost in sight.","Therefore, they were not worried that someone might see the car. The road was smooth at night. The G-Wagon drove steadily through the night. Although the road was not very easy to travel, it was much faster than riding a horse.","Mo Jiuye, a novice driver, was just getting addicted to driving - he resented that dawn came too soon.","He Zhiran was really impressed by his endurance - driving all night long, yet looking no tired at all, without the slightest sign of fatigue all over his body.","As soon as He Zhiran entered the space, she was caught by this energetic man...","After a passionate and fulfilling battle, He Zhiran finally fell asleep.","Rice Ball was very sensible now. He no longer participated in the fights between his two masters, instead, he would run as far as possible into the deepest part of the bamboo forest to hide.","After living like this for four consecutive days, Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran finally arrived safely in the south, which was the border between Da Shun and the Southern Borderlands. Their current location was still within the Da Shun territory.","Mo Jiuye was so familiar with this place. Which Mo Family man had not guarded here before?","Coming here made Mo Jiuye feel sad. Back then, he and his Mo Family brothers shed blood on the frontier, but what did they get in the end?","Suppressed and exiled by the emperor...","He Zhiran noticed the sadness in the man at first glance. She took the initiative to put her arm around his.","\"It's all in the past. Trust me, the future will definitely get better and better.\"","Mo Jiuye pulled her into his arms and planted a deep kiss on her forehead.","\"I'm already open-minded about it. Having you and so many family members living a peaceful life together, I'm very content.\"","Of course, it would be even better if he could find Eldest and Second Brother smoothly.","At this moment, it was already dawn. The couple did not rush to enter the territory of the Southern Borderlands. Mo Jiuye took He Zhiran to visit the place where his father and brothers were buried to pay respect.","The Mo Family tombs were deep in the mountains. The climate in the south was slightly warmer, and the trees on the mountain could still be seen as green.","Due to long-term war, there were no commoners living around here. Therefore, the two did not encounter anyone on their way up the mountain.","After climbing a slope, Mo Jiuye pointed to the densely forested direction ahead and said,","\"It's just past there.\"","He Zhiran could see that Mo Jiuye was in a very heavy mood at this moment. She lightly hmm-ed and at the same time squeezed his slightly rough big hand to comfort him.","The couple arrived at a mountain depression with heavy hearts. What came into view were nine tombs overgrown with weeds.","The tombstones in front of the tombs were engraved with the names of the Mo Family men.","At the very top was the tomb of the old Duke Mo Qing. After years of sun and rain exposure, and recent neglect, the characters on the stone tablet had become somewhat blurred.","Below Mo Qing's tomb, there were eight tombs of varying newness and oldness, engraved with the names of the Mo brothers respectively.","At this moment, Mo Jiuye's eyes seemed to be filled with blood, and the sadness in them could not be concealed at all.","He knelt down heavily in front of the tombs.","\"Father, brothers, Jiuye has come to see you.\"","After speaking, he solemnly kowtowed three loud times.","Although He Zhiran was not acquainted with these dead Mo Family men, thinking of their family's dedication to Da Shun, she could not help but feel distressed.","She knelt down in front of the tombs with Mo Jiuye, and at the same time, her consciousness entered the space to purchase some offerings, which she neatly placed in front of the tombs, along with incense and spirit money for worship.","Mo Jiuye looked at her gratefully and lit three incense sticks on his father and brothers' tombs.","He Zhiran murmured softly, \"Heaven is unfair, letting such good people die one after another, while bad people live so luxuriously.\"","Mo Jiuye stood up with a mocking smile, \"We Mo Family men shed our blood and laid down our lives for Da Shun, now when I think about it, it really wasn't worth it.\"","At this moment, He Zhiran was in no mood to persuade Mo Jiuye to restrain his grief. After all, her own mood was also very heavy.","Perhaps grief was the driving force for them. They were about to enter the Southern Borderlands soon. As long as their motivation was strong enough, she believed they would definitely accomplish something on this trip.","After worshipping, the two did not leave immediately. Eighth Brother's tomb had been dug up by Nan Rui's people. He Zhiran wanted to check it out, hoping to find some useful clues here.","The two went to Mo Chuhan's tomb very tacitly and examined it carefully.","Lan Hao had already said that after they found Mo Chuhan's tomb dug up, they tidied it up again.","Therefore, this tomb now looked newer than the others, and the soil on the tomb was also a little loose.","They both knew there was no corpse of Mo Chuhan left here, so after examining the exterior, they did not investigate further.","There was not even a corpse inside, it was probably just an empty coffin.","As for Third and Fifth Brother's tombs, they remained intact with no visible anomalies on the outside.","He Zhiran was more interested in the other brothers' tombs.","Especially Eldest and Second Brother - the possibility of them still being alive was very high, so she wanted to dig them open and take a look.","However, this had to be agreed by Mo Jiuye. After all, the respect ancient people had for the deceased was not something a modern person like her could understand.","The so-called \"rest in peace\" - disturbing the dead in their peaceful rest was a great disrespect."]},{"number":251,"title":"Chapter 251: Digging Graves","paragraphs":["If she did not do this, He Zhiran would not be able to make further favorable judgments.","After thinking for a while, she spoke up, \"I want to take a look at Eldest and Second Brother's corpses.\"","Sure enough, as soon as she said this, Mo Jiuye did not agree immediately. His eyebrows were locked in a frown for a long time before he asked, \"Can any clues be found from the corpses?\"","He Zhiran knew her request would be questioned. She expressed her thoughts.","\"There is an instrument in the medical room of my space that can detect familial relationships between people. I was thinking that if Eldest and Second Brother were still alive, the people lying in the graves would not be Mo Family members. As long as we examine it, we will know the result.\"","Mo Jiuye had not expected there to be such an operation in her space.","This was indeed a good method. If the people in the graves were not Mo Family members, they could completely determine that Eldest and Second Brother were still alive.","On the other hand, if the people lying here were indeed Eldest and Second Brother, they would have no need to continue searching.","After analyzing the pros and cons, Mo Jiuye solemnly came to the graves of his two elder brothers and bowed deeply.","\"Eldest Brother, Second Brother, please forgive your younger brother for being impolite. In order to ascertain whether you are still alive, this is the only method.\"","Having said that, he looked at He Zhiran with a serious expression.","\"Ranran, take the tools out from your space. I will dig open the graves now.\"","He Zhiran thought Mo Jiuye would use iron shovels, the most primitive method for grave digging. She felt it would be somewhat time consuming.","Because she had not told Mo Jiuye that after examining Eldest and Second Brother's graves, she also wanted to dig open the other graves and take a look.","At this rate, even if they dug all day, they probably would not be able to dig up so many graves.","Therefore, she did not immediately purchase iron shovels and tools of that nature. Instead, she decided to look for a small, time-saving and labor-saving mechanical device on Taobao.","After searching for a while, He Zhiran found a suitable mini excavator.","Unlike the large excavators people were used to seeing, this mini excavator was only about a square meter in size and very convenient to operate, perfect for this kind of \"grave robbing\" task.","The mini excavator required diesel fuel. He Zhiran immediately contacted Little Collector and asked him to get her some diesel fuel.","Little Collector was especially attentive to He Zhiran's messages now. Seeing her message, he would reply at the first opportunity.","Fortunately, when he had been preparing gasoline recently, he had also brought along a few barrels of diesel fuel. Upon learning of He Zhiran's need, he immediately listed them for 1 yuan each.","He Zhiran did not have time to check exactly how many barrels of diesel fuel had been added to her space. After fueling up the mini excavator, she took it out.","Mo Jiuye had thought his wife would be gone for a while to buy iron shovels. He did not expect her to bring out such a strange contraption.","At the moment, both of them were rather serious. Neither felt like joking about the mini excavator.","He Zhiran knew Mo Jiuye would not know how to operate this equipment, so she took the initiative to lift the excavator and start it up.","A deafening mechanical sound echoed through the open valley, startling the birds roosting in the trees into frantically flapping their wings and fleeing in all directions.","Fortunately, there were absolutely no people around here, allowing He Zhiran to use the mini excavator without any reservations.","Before long, all of the soil on top of Eldest Brother's grave was dug away, exposing the coffin lid.","He Zhiran's consciousness entered her space again and she purchased some tools from Taobao.","Mo Jiuye stepped forward to pick up a curved iron hammer. With a slight exertion of force, the thick coffin cover was pried open.","Inside the coffin was a headless skeleton.","Mo Jiuye thought He Zhiran would be frightened seeing this. After opening the coffin, he went to her side and gripped her little hand tightly.","At the moment, He Zhiran was staring fixedly at the skeleton. Seeing this, Mo Jiuye thought she was scared.","\"Ranran, I'm here. Don't be afraid.\"","He Zhiran currently had no mind to explain that she was not afraid, because she noticed the bones of the skeleton had a vaguely bluish-black tinge.","\"This person died from poisoning.\"","\"Poisoning?\" Mo Jiuye was somewhat puzzled.","Eldest and Second Brother had been killed on the spot by enemy troops, and then had their heads cut off and displayed at the city gates. How could they have been poisoned?","At this time, He Zhiran had already broken free of Mo Jiuye's grip on her hand. She slowly walked to the coffin.","She took out a stainless steel scraper from her space and scraped some powder from the skeleton. Then she pulled Mo Jiuye along to quickly enter her space.","In her haste to find answers, she directly ignored the steamed buns who had come over looking for hugs.","She looked seriously at Mo Jiuye, \"I need a little of your blood for testing.\"","Mo Jiuye did not hesitate at all to hold out his arm, because he had seen his wife take blood samples from others several times by pricking their arms with a needle.","He Zhiran's actions were very smooth. She drew some blood from the artery in Mo Jiuye's arm, then immediately buried herself in the laboratory.","After about an hour, the DNA test results came out. As expected, the corpse had no blood relation to Mo Jiuye.","Since there was no blood relation, she also had no need to continue investigating what poison the person had died from, much less analyze the cause of death of a substitute corpse.","When Mo Jiuye learned that the corpse was not Eldest Brother, he felt a burst of elation in his heart.","This very likely meant that Eldest Brother was still alive.","The two had the same idea without discussing it and decided to dig open the graves of the other brothers as well to test their DNA against Mo Jiuye's.","The mini excavator worked continuously for less than an hour and opened up the graves of Fourth, Sixth, and Seventh Brothers.","Mo Jiuye had already learned how to collect cells from the bones. Without waiting for He Zhiran to act, he finished up.","Just as He Zhiran was about to bring Mo Jiuye into her space to run the tests, Mo Jiuye suddenly halted his actions.","He gestured for He Zhiran to keep silent. He Zhiran reacted very quickly. She guessed that Mo Jiuye was alerting her to some abnormality in their surroundings. She promptly stored the mini excavator and tools into her space.","Mo Jiuye swiftly picked her up by the waist and leapt onto a thick tree.","The two looked down and saw several people dressed in Da Shun Army uniforms walking in their direction."]},{"number":252,"title":"Chapter 252: Of Course You Can't Go Wrong","paragraphs":["Mo Jiuye fixed his eyes and took a look. He recognized several people.","They were all his former subordinates.","As they walked, they said, \"We haven't come to pay respects to the Mo Family's generals for a long time.\"","\"Alas... we can't blame ourselves. They keep such a close eye on us that if they find out we've come to pay respects to the Mo Family's generals, they will definitely use it against us.\"","\"If I didn't have a shred of passion left for defending my country, I really wouldn't want to stay here any longer.\"","As they spoke, all of them were stunned into silence.","After a long while, one soldier forcibly swallowed a mouthful of saliva before pointing to the grave in front of him and saying, \"What...what exactly is going on here?\"","\"That's right. The Mo Family has been loyal and righteous for generations. Why desecrate their graves even after their deaths?\"","\"I heard Old Duke Mo's family was exiled to the northwest. I'm thinking of finding an opportunity to go over and join them.\"","\"We don't know the situation with the ninth master's family right now. If we go, won't we cause them trouble?\"","\"What trouble could we cause them? If we go, we can find work and help the ninth master out a bit. He has to provide for such a huge family on his own. I doubt he can manage it alone.\"","\"......\"","The unconcealable grief and indignation on the soldiers' faces was evident as they slowly stepped forward and filled in the soil of the graves with their bare hands.","Seeing these people, Mo Jiuye felt an urge to reveal himself to them.","But he couldn't show himself for the time being. After all, he was secretly traveling, and the fewer people who knew about it the better.","If those former subordinates really went to the northwest to find him as they intended, that would be perfect.","Right now, the entire national treasury's silver was with him and He Zhiran. Supporting a few brothers who had lived and died alongside him should be no problem.","Besides, with his current status, he felt that he couldn't be of any help to these soldiers, so revealing himself would be meaningless.","After watching for a while and seeing that the soldiers kept filling in the soil, He Zhiran glanced at him as if asking for his opinion. The two then slipped into the space.","The first thing He Zhiran wanted to do was run a DNA test.","The conclusion shocked both of them to some extent.","The DNA comparisons showed that none of the three sets were biologically related to Mo Jiuye.","What did this mean?","It meant that it was very likely his three brothers were also still alive...","Mo Jiuye was instantly petrified. He couldn't understand why his brothers had disappeared one after another. What kind of conspiracy was behind all this?","If that mysterious man was really the one Mother had spoken of who had liked Yuan Meng, then his treatment of the Mo Family made sense. He was getting revenge for Yuan Meng in a completely twisted way. It showed how dark that man's heart was.","In any case, it was good news that his brothers hadn't died on the battlefield. It meant there was a high chance they were still alive.","Mo Jiuye now deeply felt that he had an arduous task ahead of him. Not only did he have to find his eldest and second brothers, he also had to make every effort to track down clues about his other brothers.","Ultimately, the only shortcut was to find that mysterious man.","However, He Zhiran had no intention of stopping there.","\"Since we're here already, why not check your father's remains as well?\"","Mo Jiuye had thought of this too. Now that it was proven these graves didn't contain the Mo Family members, even if he was condemned for filial impiety, he still wanted to examine them.","\"Alright, let's see if those people have left first.\"","They had entered the space from the tree, and Mo Jiuye was worried He Zhiran would exit in the wrong spot. He immediately put his arm around her waist, the same way as when they had entered the space.","The two reappeared in the tree, just in time to see the soldiers' retreating backs.","After the people had walked far away, the couple came to Old Duke Mo's grave.","Mo Jiuye knelt down and kowtowed again.","\"Father, your unfilial son must commit this offense to verify whether you are still alive. Please forgive me.\"","After speaking, Mo Jiuye stood up. Through his earlier observations, he had already learned to operate the miniature excavator. So without He Zhiran lifting a finger, he took the initiative and started digging.","An hour later in the space—","\"Zhiran, you didn't get the test wrong, did you? This isn't father's corpse?\"","He Zhiran's tone was indisputable. \"Of course not. I can definitively tell you the corpse in the grave is not biologically related to you at all.\"","Mo Jiuye was instantly petrified again. Though his brothers' bizarre disappearances could still be reasoned out somehow, his father had already passed away for so long. Where could he be?","He Zhiran now felt that what had happened to the Mo Family was just too convoluted. Although they still hadn't been able to find out everything, based on what they knew about those few brothers, it seemed they were all still alive.","Even someone as steady and calm as Mo Jiuye normally would have a blank mind when encountering something like this.","He Zhiran could understand his feelings. It was good news that his family was alive, but they currently had no idea of their whereabouts or even a lead to start searching.","She went up and took Mo Jiuye's arm, and gently said, \"Since we're already in the South Borderlands, let's start looking for clues here first.\"","Mo Jiuye nodded. \"Alright, this is all we can do for now.\"","In fact, He Zhiran didn't know that at this moment, his heart was bleeding. He couldn't imagine what kind of circumstances his father and brothers were in right now. The wretched state of his third, fifth and eighth brothers was still vivid in his mind.","His fists were clenched tight now. No matter what, he had to find his missing father and brothers.","He Zhiran looked at the large wall clock. It was already 4 p.m.","They would definitely need to take some action after nightfall when entering the South Borderlands. She went to the kitchen to simply stir-fry two small dishes, and the couple had a simple meal.","Before leaving the space, the two changed disguises again. Mo Jiuye once again became that ugly man with sideburns.","Seeing Mo Jiuye like this now, He Zhiran couldn't laugh at all even though she was usually in a heavier mood.","She quickly changed into men's clothing and left the space hand-in-hand with Mo Jiuye.","To cover their tracks, Mo Jiuye first filled in the opened grave. Only then did the couple walk down the mountain hand in hand.","Night had just fallen when the husband and wife arrived at the entrance to the South Borderlands.","Perhaps because of the frequent battles recently, security was extremely tight at the entrance to the South Borderlands, and there were hardly any travelers coming and going.","Mo Jiuye pulled He Zhiran up onto a thick tree and softly explained,","\"The South Borderland people are very cautious. During times of war, to prevent spies from sneaking in, they station heavy troops to guard the entrance.\"","He Zhiran took a telescope out of the space and peered towards the entrance to the South Borderlands.","Sure enough, just as Mo Jiuye had said, they could clearly see with the naked eye several patrols grasping weapons while patrolling back and forth outside the entrance.","And this was just what was visible to the naked eye. Looking further away, there were nearly a thousand soldiers. Not only that, there was also a group of about fifty people, each leading a dog.","The dogs' build looked somewhat like greyhounds from the previous world, not seeming very big yet extremely fierce.","With such strict security, passing smoothly into the South Borderlands would really take some effort.","No wonder Mo Jiuye had suggested sneaking in under the cover of night early on."]},{"number":253,"title":"Chapter 253: Rice Ball Show Your Skills","paragraphs":["In the southern border of China, the defenses were so strict that it seemed almost impossible to infiltrate during broad daylight. Even someone as skilled as Mo Jiuye would find it difficult to do so.","Especially with those well-trained military dogs around.","These dogs had extremely sensitive senses and could detect even the slightest sound.","If He Zhiran and Mo Jiuye tried to enter the city as living beings, even with their light-footed techniques, they couldn't guarantee absolute silence.","Just like Mo Jiuye, He Zhiran was also worried about the dogs at the entrance. Neither of them dared to suggest infiltrating the southern border and instead focused on brainstorming strategies.","Feeling somewhat helpless, He Zhiran thought of using more grenades from her space. She planned to throw them towards the entrance of the southern border, causing chaos and allowing them to slip in unnoticed, regardless of the casualties.","However, just as she arrived at the medical room to retrieve the grenades, she was surprised by Rice Ball's unexpected actions.","Seemingly bored, the little fellow had somehow wandered into her medical room.","Not only that, but it also held a small bowl, the same one used for drinking milk, and was rummaging around the medical room.","He Zhiran guessed that Rice Ball probably wanted some milk. She usually prepared milk for it in the medical room, so it must have thought it could find some there.","However, He Zhiran's focus at the moment wasn't on Rice Ball's cleverness but rather on its abilities.","Back at home, Rice Ball could control rabbits and even establish rules for herds of cows and sheep in her space.","The question was whether those specially trained military dogs would listen to Rice Ball's commands.","Regardless, if Rice Ball could control those dogs, it would be much safer than using grenades to bomb the entrance.","With this idea in mind, He Zhiran brought Rice Ball out of her space.","The little fellow seemed a bit scared in this new environment, but its injured little heart was quickly comforted by the familiar scent.","He Zhiran gently stroked its head and said softly, \"Don't be afraid, Rice Ball. It's me.\"","Rice Ball tightly embraced its owner's neck with its chubby little arms and made a soft humming sound, looking incredibly adorable.","He Zhiran smoothed its fur and didn't care whether Rice Ball understood her words or not. She pointed in the direction of the military dogs and said, \"Rice Ball, there are many doggies blocking our way over there. Can you command them?\"","Rice Ball, with its dark, big eyes, stared earnestly at its owner and replied, \"Mm...\"","He Zhiran was certain that Rice Ball had understood her words, and she was ecstatic.","\"Husband, let's find a way to get closer to the entrance of the southern border,\" she said.","Mo Jiuye witnessed the interaction between He Zhiran and Rice Ball. If he hadn't personally witnessed Rice Ball's abilities, he would have thought He Zhiran had gone crazy.","But the truth was different. This black and white little ball was indeed quite extraordinary.","\"Alright, I'll take you there,\" Mo Jiuye said.","As he spoke, Mo Jiuye gently leaped down from the tree, carrying He Zhiran and Rice Ball in his arms.","He held the chubby Rice Ball in one hand and held his wife's hand with the other as they quietly approached the entrance to Southern Xinjiang along the roadside bushes.","When they were about five hundred meters away from the group of guards, he stopped.","\"Rice Ball, you try now,\" he said.","He Zhiran added, \"Rice Ball, sweetheart, make those dogs bark.\"","Rice Ball raised its little head high and barked in the direction pointed by its owner.","\"Ah...\"","The sound was completely different from the usual barking of Rice Ball, somewhat resembling a wolf's howl...","Whatever kind of howl it was, Rice Ball's voice had clearly alarmed the military dogs at the entrance.","Mo Jiuye surveyed the scene and jumped onto a high slope with He Zhiran and Rice Ball.","He Zhiran took out binoculars and looked towards the entrance of Southern Xinjiang.","She saw the military dogs struggling desperately, some of them breaking free from the soldiers' leashes and running around.","The soldiers were in a panic, trying to control the military dogs, while someone shouted, \"There's an enemy, be on guard...\"","After the commotion caused by the military dogs, the soldiers guarding the entrance were already in chaos, chasing after the dogs.","Looking at the guards at the entrance, although it hadn't reached a situation where none were left, the estimated number of people was not many.","Seeing that Mo Jiuye was already eager to act, He Zhiran gently patted Rice Ball's head a few times, then sent it into the space and quickly rewarded the little guy with a bowl of milk and a small apple using mental manipulation.","Just as her consciousness left the space, Mo Jiuye was already in action.","She saw him holding He Zhiran's waist, using his inner energy to leap into the air and sprint directly towards the position of the entrance to Southern Xinjiang.","As a precaution, He Zhiran tied a sleeve arrow to her arm and held a hand grenade. If there were any unforeseen circumstances, she would decisively take action.","After a few leaps, Mo Jiuye arrived at the entrance to Southern Xinjiang with He Zhiran in his arms.","Although he had been very careful, he still alerted the guards there.","Seeing the leader about to shout, He Zhiran aimed her sleeve arrow at the person's forehead and shot.","The other guards noticed someone falling down and provided Mo Jiuye with an opportunity to enter.","The two of them smoothly crossed the high wall at the entrance and entered the territory of Southern Xinjiang.","At this moment, some guards had already discovered their tracks and pointed in their direction, shouting, \"Quick, chase them, they're over there.\"","A group of guards with weapons chased after them in their direction.","Mo Jiuye displayed his lightness skill and increased his speed to the extreme, quickly distancing themselves from those people.","He Zhiran thought that they didn't have a clear route at the moment, so instead of running around like this, it would be better to temporarily hide in the space and recover.","Therefore, when Mo Jiuye turned into a hidden corner, she had a thought and the two of them entered the space.","Ever since Mo Jiuye discovered that the bodies of his father and brothers were all fake, his desire to save people became extremely urgent.","He originally planned to travel overnight and head to the next city in Southern Xinjiang. Who would have thought that he would be brought into the space by his wife?","\"He Zhiran, why did you hide in the space when those guards couldn't catch up to me?\" He thought that He Zhiran was worried about him being caught by those guards and did it to avoid danger.","He Zhiran explained, \"The pursuers outside will only increase in number. I'm not worried about your speed, but rather, how can we search for clues while hiding and moving forward like this?\"","Knowing He Zhiran well, Mo Jiuye was sure that his wife must have thought of a better solution.","\"He Zhiran, what should we do?\"","Just now, while they were on the run, they occasionally saw a few people from the southern region. He Zhiran deliberately observed their attire.","The dressing of the people from the southern region was somewhat similar to the traditional attire of Xinjiang in the previous life, especially the distinctive characteristic of the men's beards.","The young men's beards wouldn't be very long, located on the upper lip, black, dense, and the tips curled upward."]},{"number":254,"title":"Chapter 254: Something's Weird in Here.","paragraphs":["He Zhiran was dressed more simply, with her long hair braided into countless little braids and wearing a special floral hat.","After thinking for a moment, He Zhiran purchased two sets of clothing based on the characteristics of South Xinjiang attire from the Taobao Mall.","She and Mo Jiuye each put on the newly purchased outfits. This time He Zhiran did not continue to dress as a man, but made herself up as a South Xinjiang woman instead.","After Mo Jiuye had finished dressing up, he also did not look like his original self, and was a typical South Xinjiang man from head to toe.","The two checked each other and made sure there were no flaws before leaving the space.","Now they did not have to evade anyone, but could swagger down the street.","Indeed, as He Zhiran had expected, there were South Xinjiang soldiers everywhere on the street.","The military dogs that had been commanded around by the steamed bun were also gradually being called back.","The soldiers were in squads of ten or so, each walking a military dog, searching everywhere on the big streets.","In order not to attract the attention of the soldiers, Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran deliberately kept their heads low and walked as if very afraid.","Even so, the soldiers did not let them off. A soldier leading a military dog blocked their way.","\"Have you seen two Da Shun people?\"","Mo Jiuye held He Zhiran’s hand tightly, answering nervously, \"No...didn’t see them.”","He often dealt with South Xinjiang people and could respond completely in their dialect.","The dissatisfied soldier glared at them angrily before letting them leave.","Mo Jiuye pulled He Zhiran straight towards the next city in South Xinjiang.","On the way, they passed the place where their barracks were located, which was already on high alert.","They were not worried about this. Now that they were dressed as South Xinjiang people, they would be questioned at most, just like earlier.","As expected, when they reached the checkpoint, someone intercepted them.","\"What do you do?\"","Mo Jiuye quickly stepped forward and explained, \"We came to see an old friend on the border, and now we plan to return to Lian City.\"","Lian City was the city closest to the South Xinjiang border. As long as they passed through here, it was a two hour walk.","In addition, Mo Jiuye knew that South Xinjiang's management was not as meticulous as Da Shun's, and the city gates would not be closed at night except during wartime.","Therefore, saying they were going to Lian City now would not seem too abrupt.","The soldiers checked them and let them leave.","From time to time Mo Jiuye used some qinggong with He Zhiran to hurry on their way. In less than an hour they entered Lian City.","Lian City was not their final destination. Brother San had heard that the Si Meng Mountain Villa was in the suburbs of the South Xinjiang capital, which was still more than 200 li from Lian City.","In order to arrive at their destination sooner, the couple took out the G-Wagen outside Lian City's official road.","There were not many people here, and it was dark and windy, perfect for driving down the road.","Mo Jiuye had been very silent all the way because he had discovered that his elders were still alive.","He Zhiran did not bother him either, sitting in the passenger seat and thinking about the next step of the plan.","After thinking for a long time, she spoke up.","\"Where do you plan to go first?\"","Although Mo Jiuye had not spoken, he had been weighing this problem in his heart all along. Seeing his wife ask, he told her his thoughts.","\"I plan to go to Si Meng Mountain Villa first.\"","This proposal was consistent with He Zhiran's ideas.","At the beginning, although neither of them said the order in which to go, they had both tacitly agreed to go to the palace first.","Not only was there dendrobium that could help the sisters-in-law detoxify, but also the black South Pearl that she had promised little Xiaoxiao she would collect.","However, after digging up those tombs, their ideas had changed.","At this moment, nothing was more important to Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran than the news of the elders. Moreover, if they were really still alive, they didn’t know what kind of torment they were suffering now. Naturally, the sooner they were rescued, the better.","Therefore, Si Meng Mountain Villa was where the most important clue was at the moment.","He Zhiran said solemnly, \"Well, we should go there first. In case we make too much noise at the palace first and attract the attention of people with ulterior motives, that would not be good.\"","Mr. Si Meng's whereabouts were so bizarre that he was obviously a very meticulous person. Once there was any wind or grass that aroused his alarm, it was very likely that the only clue to Si Meng Mountain Villa would be cut off.","The couple agreed, and Mo Jiuye arrived in the suburbs of the capital before dawn driving the G-Wagen.","The two were dressed as villagers from the nearby area, each with a basket on their back. Following the route described by Brother San, they walked up the mountain trail.","Brother San said that there was an inconspicuous cave in the valley. As long as they entered from that cave entrance and walked to the end, they could see a valley where Si Meng Mountain Villa was located.","The couple went through a lot of trouble before finally finding the so-called inconspicuous cave.","It was truly fitting to call it inconspicuous. The cave entrance was very small to begin with, only allowing one person to stoop and walk in. Not only that, the weeds in front of the cave grew very tall. If it hadn’t been for Brother San’s description of the general appearance here, it would not have been easy for them to find it.","The two entered the cave one after the other, with Mo Jiuye in front, one hand holding a flashlight to illuminate the way and the other hand pulling He Zhiran.","After walking about a few hundred meters, light finally appeared ahead, and at the same time, Mo Jiuye turned off his flashlight and slowed down his pace.","He Zhiran suddenly felt cold all around her. She whispered to Mo Jiuye, \"It's a bit strange here.\"","\"Do you feel a little cold?\" Mo Jiuye had the same feeling.","As they spoke, the two walked out another ten steps or so. This feeling of cold grew stronger and stronger.","He Zhiran held Mo Jiuye's hand tightly. If there was danger ahead, she would take Mo Jiuye into the space as soon as possible.","The two tiptoed forward hand in hand cautiously when Mo Jiuye suddenly stopped walking. He pricked up his ears to listen carefully to the sounds ahead.","He Zhiran also tried her best to capture the source of the sound.","She only felt a rustling sound ahead.","The two looked at each other and moved forward even more carefully.","After walking another ten meters or so, Mo Jiuye stopped again.","The sound became clearer and clearer, and He Zhiran felt a slight hissing sound like groups of snakes tangled together.","Mo Jiuye whispered, \"There are probably snakes ahead, and a lot of them.\"","It was indisputable that there were many snakes, insects, rats and ants in South Xinjiang. However, the sound they heard was by no means that simple.","Except for someone deliberately breeding them, it was impossible for such a large group of snakes to appear at once.","\"Let's go into the space to think of a way, and rest for a while at the same time.\"","After traveling overnight and climbing the mountain for so long after dawn, He Zhiran’s body was somewhat taxed.","With that said, the two immediately appeared inside the space.","What He Zhiran said about entering the space to think of a way was undoubtedly about using realgar.","According to her understanding, as long as realgar was sprinkled on the body, snakes would avoid it as soon as they smelled it."]},{"number":255,"title":"Chapter 255: Into the Jungle","paragraphs":["In addition, there was her darling Rice Ball. The little guy could control the rabbits and sheep in her space, and even command those military dogs. She wondered whether it could also make these venomous snakes bow their heads in submission.","At this moment, Rice Ball also discovered its owner. It came running over on its little short legs, swaying from side to side.","Without a doubt, the first thing Rice Ball wanted when it saw its owner was a hug.","He Zhiran also had the innate desire to kiss, hug and toss in the air such an adorable little guy.","That was exactly what she did, indulging in sweet affection with the cute little fellow before preparing a bowl of milk for it.","Once Rice Ball was full, He Zhiran said to it, “Rice Ball has eaten its fill. Can it do me a favor now?”","“Mm...”","“There are many snakes outside. Can you make them listen to you?”","“Mm...”","“Alright then, I’ll rest for a while before taking you out.”","“Mm...”","Rice Ball kept emitting little “mm” sounds, amusing He Zhiran into softly laughing, while hugging and rubbing it in her arms again.","After awhile, she let Rice Ball go off on its own to play in the bamboo grove, and had a simple meal with Mo Jiuye, intending to take a nap before going outside again.","Although she said it was just a nap, by the time she woke up it was already afternoon.","The couple tidied themselves up, then held Rice Ball and emerged together within the mountain cave.","The sounds of the snakes were still audible. He Zhiran softly said to Rice Ball, “Sweetheart, do you hear the snakes?”","“Mm...”","Apparently Rice Ball’s call disturbed the snakes. The two humans stood still as they felt the sounds approaching them little by little.","He Zhiran intended for Rice Ball to control these snakes, so before leaving her space she had not dusted herself and Mo Jiuye with realgar powder.","She remained vigilant at all times. If Rice Ball was unable to successfully control the snakes, she could only return to her space again.","Just as the snake group was getting closer and closer, Rice Ball let out another burst of howls. The snakes immediately halted their advance.","At the same time, the two also saw the number of snakes. There were visibly over a thousand, densely packed together. Fortunately He Zhiran’s psychological resilience was strong, otherwise she would surely have been disgusted by the sight of the endless sea of snakes before her.","The scene was simply indescribable in words, but could be summed up in two words: “Disgusting”.","With so many snakes gathered together, there was no need to think about it. They must have increased the vigilance of the people at the Simeng Mountain Villa due to Third Master's previous intrusion.","In order to prevent anyone else from sneaking in, they had deliberately released so many snakes here.","While He Zhiran was lost in thought, Rice Ball let out another roar towards the snake group. The snakes then began to move in an orderly fashion, raising their heads and constantly flicking out their tongues...","He Zhiran and Mo Jiuye looked at each other. They both knew that Rice Ball had succeeded in controlling the snakes.","“Good boy, Rice Ball,” He Zhiran praised, unable to resist planting a loud kiss on its forehead.","Delighted, Rice Ball frolicked and hugged its owner’s neck affectionately.","He Zhiran had suddenly kissed Rice Ball on impulse. Right now she still had something for the little guy to do, and could not keep showering it with affection.","“Be good, sweetie. Get them to follow us and disperse once we’re safely out of the cave.”","“Mm...”","Rice Ball proceeded to bare its teeth and pull funny faces at the snake group, letting out a few different calls. The snakes then moved to stand in orderly rows along both sides, clearing a path.","Mo Jiuye cradled the proud Rice Ball in one arm and held He Zhiran’s hand with the other as they walked out along the channel created by the snakes.","Outside the cave was a primeval forest, tall trees and humid air. On the surface it looked like an uninhabited area, yet neither of them dared let down their guard.","Encountering the snake group could be considered a wake-up call. Since someone had already interfered and entered Simeng Mountain Villa, the road ahead would surely be fraught with danger.","As He Zhiran pondered this, she had already placed Rice Ball back into her space and taken out the prepared realgar powder to dust on herself and Mo Jiuye.","According to Third Master, after exiting the cave they would have to pass through the lush forest ahead to reach Simeng Mountain Villa.","Now that even the snakes had emerged, there was no telling what else might be lurking in the woods.","Speaking of which, in such a place there would be nothing more than other poisonous bugs and creatures. The realgar powder wouldn’t completely neutralize their venom, but could at least buy them a bit of time to react.","Once preparations were complete, the husband and wife set off together into the depths of the forest.","It was fine at the beginning. The path was covered in slippery green moss but didn't seem dangerous.","When they went deeper into the woods, they came to a sea of flowers that was a feast for the eyes.","Girls were born to love all things beautiful, and He Zhiran was no exception.","Yet right now she had no mood to appreciate the scenic view, because hovering above the flowers was a dense swarm of wasps.","The birds in the forest must have spotted the wasps and gradually flew in their direction to prey on them.","He Zhiran had originally considered purchasing some insecticide from Taobao Treasure to deal with the wasps.","But upon seeing the birds hunting them, she changed her mind.","The soundly sleeping Rice Ball was once again taken out of space by its owner. Woken up suddenly and finding itself in a different environment, the little fellow immediately started to fuss.","He Zhiran gently patted its back, coaxing softly, “Be good, Rice Ball. I need your help.”","On hearing that it was needed, the little guy immediately became serious. It seemed to know that by helping its owner it would get more bowls of milk.","“Mm mm mm...” Rice Ball seemed to be saying, Master, hurry and give me a task!","He Zhiran pointed towards the sea of flowers and said, “There’s a swarm of wasps over there. Can you call all the birds here to prey on them?”","She said this just to try it out. After all, controlling the entire forest’s population of birds was no small feat. She had no idea if the little guy could accomplish it.","But this was the most convenient method so she had to give it a shot.","Rice Ball blinked its pitch black eyes a few times then lifted its virtually invisible little neck and howled towards the sky.","In the blink of an eye flocks of birds came flying in from all directions.","Rice Ball demonstrated its prowess once more, calling out to the birds several times. All the birds that had flown over then headed straight for the sea of flowers, instantly covering up the wasps.","About five minutes later, the air above the flowers finally calmed down. Not only had the dense swarm of wasps disappeared without a trace, even the birds had flown away on their own."]},{"number":256,"title":"Chapter 256: Through the gift of the Great God.","paragraphs":["Rice Ball hugged its owner's neck, expecting a reward.","As expected, He Zhiran didn't disappoint the little guy. After giving it a kiss on its little head, he sent it back to the space.","At the same time, all the necessary food, like milk, tender bamboo shoots, small apples, and carrots, were not missing.","Watching Rice Ball excitedly running towards the food, He Zhiran regained his consciousness.","What followed was Mo Jiuye's sigh.","\"I didn't expect Rice Ball to have such great abilities.\"","\"Yeah, this little guy is clever.\" He Zhiran felt that Rice Ball's abilities were like a gift from a divine being who had sent her across time and space. Otherwise, how could one explain Rice Ball's extraordinary talents?","The two of them smoothly passed through the floral sea, thinking that there might be some difficult obstacles ahead. But to their surprise, they encountered no trouble until they saw the shadow of a house.","Si Meng Mountain Villa was right in front of them, and Mo Jiuye's heart became heavy.","If Mr. Si Meng was truly responsible for the demise of his Mo family, then his missing parents and siblings might have been here at some point.","It was still early in the day, and they couldn't determine the specific situation inside the villa. To avoid alerting anyone, they decided to sneak in after nightfall.","Even after nightfall, they remained cautious.","He Zhiran took out a drone and controlled it to hover around the villa to get a sense of the terrain.","As the drone observed, it was just as Third Brother had described. The place seemed like an abandoned manor on the surface, with nothing particularly noteworthy and no signs of human presence.","In other words, their first task was to investigate the specific situation inside the dry well based on the information obtained from Third Brother's interrogation.","He Zhiran stored the drone in the space.","Although the drone was advanced, it couldn't detect someone intentionally hiding. Therefore, they didn't take entering the villa lightly.","Mo Jiuye had formidable martial arts skills, and his senses of sight and hearing were beyond ordinary. He remained vigilant, carefully observing any movement around them.","And so, the two of them arrived at the edge of the dry well.","He Zhiran took out a flashlight from the space, intending to observe the bottom of the well. But Mo Jiuye immediately hugged her and swiftly rotated.","\"Be careful.\"","As he spoke, several arrows shot out from the well, but thanks to their quick reflexes, the arrows missed.","\"I didn't expect there to be traps in this dry well.\" He Zhiran's voice still trembled slightly. Thankfully, Mo Jiuye was quick-witted; otherwise, it wouldn't have been easy for her to evade those arrows with their speed.","Mo Jiuye's expression turned serious. \"Where did you touch just now?\"","According to the information obtained from Third Brother's interrogation, this was the entrance to the hidden chamber. It wouldn't be easy to enter the chamber without knowing how to avoid these traps.","He Zhiran tried hard to recall where she might have touched just now.","\"I didn't touch the well's opening. If there's a trap, it must be under our feet.\"","When she mentioned that the trap might be under their feet, Mo Jiuye quickly pulled her behind him and cautiously approached to examine.","Mo Jiuye crouched not far from where He Zhiran had just stood, cautiously probing the ground with his fingers, gradually increasing the pressure.","After a while, his movements suddenly stopped.","He Zhiran asked, \"Have you found something?\"","Mo Jiuye whispered, \"I feel like something's not right here.\"","He Zhiran carefully crouched down beside Mo Jiuye and reached out to gently touch the spot he mentioned.","Sure enough, the soil there was slightly softer than elsewhere.","Mo Jiuye gently scraped away the dirt and revealed an iron mechanism underneath.","He Zhiran didn't understand ancient mechanisms very well.","\"What do you think? Can you disable it?\"","If this mechanism only controlled the arrows, then they would be fine as long as they didn't step on it. He Zhiran was worried that the mechanism might have other purposes, so she thought it would be best to disable it before figuring out a way to enter the bottom of the well.","Mo Jiuye frowned and pondered for a moment before continuing to dig, trying to expose the entire control mechanism.","He was extremely cautious, every move made with great care.","After about ten minutes or so, Mo Jiuye finally managed to completely uncover the mechanism.","\"This is indeed a control device. When I led my troops into the Southern Frontier Palace, their treasury was equipped with a similar mechanism.\"","\"Is there a way to dismantle it?\" He Zhiran was clearly anxious, not knowing if her touching the mechanism earlier would alert the people below the well.","Mo Jiuye didn't answer but asked her to use a flashlight to illuminate the area.","He opened the cover of the controller and examined it for a long time.","\"Ranran, I need a pair of sharper scissors.\"","He Zhiran saw it too. Inside the controller, there were many copper wires extending in various directions, and in addition, there were several spring-like objects.","It was estimated that the principle of this mechanism was that the copper wires pulled a certain switch, while the springs were used to trigger contact reactions.","Although this mechanism was somewhat rudimentary in design, the wisdom of the ancients was truly admirable.","Without much thought, He Zhiran's consciousness entered the space and quickly purchased a pair of specialized iron-cutting scissors from Taobao, handing them to Mo Jiuye.","Mo Jiuye took the scissors and cut all the copper wires inside.","As a result, a sound of metal collision came from the bottom of the well, and under the light of the flashlight, several unidentified insects could be seen flying out from the well.","Mo Jiuye swiftly held He Zhiran and quickly retreated, reminding her, \"Be careful.\"","He Zhiran also reacted quickly, suspecting that these flying insects might be poisonous, so she immediately took out a bottle of insecticide from the space and held it in her hand.","Once Mo Jiuye's body steadied, she also raised the insecticide and sprayed it towards the insects.","The insects struggled for a moment in front of the two before falling to the ground.","After observing for a while and seeing no more insects flying out of the well, Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran returned to their original position.","Now that the mechanism was disabled, the two could finally examine the bottom of the well openly and boldly.","He Zhiran held a flashlight and shone it into the bottom of the well. Judging by sight, the well was at least five meters deep, with several protruding stones embedded on the walls on both sides.","At the bottom of the well, there were dozens of arrows and several sharp daggers.","These should be all the hidden weapons controlled by the mechanism.","In addition to that, there were a few disgusting-looking toads.","He Zhiran could only judge them as toads based on their appearance because these creatures were larger than the bullfrogs she had seen in her previous life, and their bodies were adorned with patterns of various colors.","\"Do you recognize this thing?\"","Mo Jiuye furrowed his brows tightly and said in a deep voice, \"This should be the Seven-Colored Toad. It is said to be highly poisonous, and many poisons used by people in the Southern Region come from the blood of the Seven-Colored Toad.\""]},{"number":257,"title":"Chapter 257: Colorful Frog","paragraphs":["Upon hearing the name of the rainbow frog, He Zhiran suddenly felt it was not so unfamiliar.","She discovered that after her sisters-in-law were poisoned, in the book on ancient and modern poisons that she had casually browsed through when purchasing it, it was recorded that mixing the blood of the rainbow frog with other medicinal ingredients could make sleeping potions, as well as high quality love potions.","The rainbow frog liked damp, gloomy environments, and its food had to be poisonous animals, such as poisonous snakes and scorpions.","One could imagine that the aggressiveness of the rainbow frog was also very strong, since it could eat poisonous snakes and scorpions.","It seemed that these rainbow frogs really were treasures.","He Zhiran suddenly had the urge to take possession of these rainbow frogs. She didn't care if she could raise them, as long as they were in her hands, she could take the time to extract their blood - it might come in useful one day.","With this thought in mind, her consciousness entered her storage space, where she bought an iron cage, intending to take all of the rainbow frogs away.","Her current position was at the well opening, still quite a distance from the rainbow frogs, so using her thoughts to get them into the cage was impossible.","Considering these creatures were full of poison everywhere, she didn't dare rashly go down into the well either.","It seemed that in order to get all of the rainbow frogs here into the cage, she would need the help of her precious little steamed bun.","Sure enough, as soon as her little darling came out, it immediately took care of the rainbow frogs.","She saw it roar at the rainbow frogs a few times, and the rainbow frogs quickly climbed up the walls of the well, before obediently jumping out of the well mouth and into the cage.","The little steamed bun was about to struggle free from its mistress' embrace to go take a look at its spoils of war, but He Zhiran heartlessly sent it into her storage space. These rainbow frogs were different from the others, being full of deadly poison. If her little steamed bun accidentally touched one, it would be a huge loss.","To be safe, He Zhiran also bought a box in her storage space that could contain the iron cage, and after placing the cage inside, locked it up before finally feeling reassured enough to send her little steamed bun into storage space.","He Zhiran knew that the little steamed bun would be unhappy at being forcefully put into storage space, and was just getting ready to enter her space consciousness to comfort it a bit, when at this moment, there was movement from the well below.","\"Senior brother, our rainbow frogs have all disappeared, and the mechanisms have been destroyed by someone too.\"","He Zhiran and Mo Jiuye could only hear someone speaking from below the well, but did not know the other side's martial arts skills. To be safe, the two of them hurriedly retreated to a nearby big tree.","\"It was probably the little steamed bun's cries that brought people out.\" He Zhiran guessed.","\"Mm, this is not bad too, at least it lets us know there are definitely people down in that well.\"","As they talked, Mo Jiuye could already sense someone coming up from the well.","He quietly reminded her, \"Someone's coming up.\"","He Zhiran did not reply, only fixed her eyes tightly on the direction of the well opening.","Soon afterwards, two middle aged men, one tall and one short, climbed up from the well opening.","The two first checked the mechanism control device that Mo Jiuye had just destroyed.","The tall one said, \"Not good, my rainbow frogs have all disappeared.\"","Although the short one did not speak, his eyes began to look all around, while one hand reached into his clothes and took out several small porcelain bottles.","He removed the stopper from one of the bottles and let out the poisonous gu insect inside.","\"Darling, go and find the scent of the living.\"","Just after his words fell, the gu insect, about the size of a honeybee, flew towards the direction of Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran.","Realgar could restrain gu insects, as He Zhiran had read in books.","She had never personally experienced whether it really worked, so she did not dare take it lightly.","To err on the safe side, she took out a flamethrower from her storage space and placed it in Mo Jiuye's hands - if necessary, they would rather expose themselves than let the gu burn to death.","They saw the gu flying straight towards them, just about to get close to the big tree concealing them, when it suddenly stopped.","Then it started flying about chaotically like a headless fly.","Seeing the gu insect's reaction, He Zhiran could confirm the realgar was effective, and finally let out a breath.","Although she and Mo Jiuye were unafraid of those two people, it was still best not to expose themselves before finding out anything.","Watching as the gu insect flew away, the short man was dumbfounded.","\"Senior brother, why is my gu so abnormal today?\"","The tall one was also somewhat at a loss. In all their years raising gus, they had never encountered such a situation before.","\"It was in front of that big tree that your gu started acting strange - there must be something fishy there.\"","As they spoke, both of their gazes fell upon the direction of the big tree.","\"Senior brother, let's go over and take a look.\"","\"Alright.\"","The two walked over, checking carefully the whole time, and were very cautious.","Mo Jiuye was also prepared to take action.","He Zhiran took out a sleeping potion made from green bamboo snakes from her storage space - as soon as these two people approached, she would first make them fall unconscious.","The two were careful, one hand grasping a weapon, the other holding a gu-breeding porcelain bottle, maintaining their readiness to take action at all times.","Just as Mo Jiuye was about to make his move, He Zhiran pulled him back with a grab.","She shook her head at Mo Jiuye, then quickly circled around him and scattered a handful of sleeping powder at the two men.","In merely an instant, the two had no chance to react before collapsing.","He Zhiran waved her little hand, instantly storing the two men away in her space.","Now that they had people to question for information, she and Mo Jiuye were in no rush to go down the well and investigate. The two entered the space together.","Mo Jiuye first searched the two men, and astonishingly found 5 small porcelain bottles for keeping gus on their bodies.","It seemed these two were no ordinary gu raisers - for the average gu keeper, they were outstanding if they could breed two gus in a lifetime, yet these two had a total of six gus, including the one they had just released outside.","That meant each of them had raised three gus.","Mo Jiuye most hated these gu insects. Of the three brothers he had found at home, two had been poisoned by gu, so he knew their harmfulness was not shallow.","Without He Zhiran needing to speak, he directly took out the flamethrower and completely destroyed the five gu insects.","But he was careless, and had not expected that out of the five gus, one was the tall man's cherished gu. With the death of the gu insect, the unconscious tall man vomited blood and went to meet the King of Hell...","Mo Jiuye...","He had only hated these gu insects, and hadn't thought that this man had actually bred a cherished gu.","The person who should have been questioned had died before they even had a chance to ask.","He Zhiran was also somewhat speechless for a time. She had long seen Mo Jiuye's actions and did not stop him.","Because she also hadn't expected that the tall man would be so impressive as to breed a cherished gu.","Now there was only one person left alive, they absolutely could not have any more accidents.","To be safe, Mo Jiuye tightly bound the short man up before letting He Zhiran wake him.","The short man opened his eyes, and was shocked stiff by the verdant scenery in front of him. His first instinct was to stand up, before he discovered his body had been tied up like a rice dumpling.","Turning his head, he saw the smiling yet not smiling faces of two people, and then lowering his head was his senior brother's corpse..."]},{"number":258,"title":"Chapter 258: What the hell are You Going to Do","paragraphs":["“Who exactly are you?”","The short man was quite bold. Having fallen into someone else's hands, he was completely unafraid.","If one did not know better, it would seem he still held some trump card that could save his life.","Mo Jiuye let out a cold snort before viciously kicking the short man, intent on reminding him of his current predicament.","The kick was unrelenting in its force. The short man wailed in pain while a nameless fear rose in his heart simultaneously.","He was about to ask his captors again why they had taken him when he suddenly felt something heavy collide violently with his body.","Both He Zhiran and Mo Jiuye could see clearly that it was the rice ball creature.","Seeing its master angry enough to kick that man, it also wanted to help.","What was originally a very serious scene was nearly ruined by the little creature's interference, almost making He Zhiran break out laughing.","Now was not the time for the rice ball to make mischief. He Zhiran held back her laughter and sent it off to the bamboo grove to play by itself.","The short man had also regained his senses. To think that he, a famous sorcerer from the Southern Borderlands, had been mocked by a black and white ball.","An urge to curse welled up in him, but when he saw the icy, piercing look in Mo Jiuye's eyes, he instantly lost his nerve.","\"Y-You... Just who are you? I've neither hatred nor grievance with you, why must you treat me thus?\"","\"Who I am is none of your concern. Answer what I want to know and I'll let you die quickly.\"","To show he was not joking, as soon as he finished speaking Mo Jiuye placed the dagger over another one of the man's fingers.","That posture clearly told the short man that if he dared refuse, this finger would be forfeit as well.","On her end, He Zhiran had also prepared a hypnotic pocket watch. If Mo Jiuye could not interrogate anything useful from the man, she would try using hypnosis.","Moreover, she could tell that the short man actually feared Mo Jiuye's threats but stubbornly refused to talk.","In situations like these, it was often because they had some handle being used to control them that prevented them from speaking out.","And indeed, even after Mo Jiuye cut off three more of his fingers, the result remained the same.","He Zhiran went over and tugged at Mo Jiuye's sleeve.","\"Let me try.\"","Then, she squatted in front of the short man.","\"Since you're unwilling to speak, we won't force you. But I wonder if you recognize this item I have here.\"","As she spoke, He Zhiran was already waving the pocket watch in front of the short man.","At first, he still tried hard to discern the oscillating object. Yet for some reason, after staring at it briefly, he felt an urge to doze off.","Soon, his eyes grew dull and listless.","To test whether the hypnosis had succeeded, He Zhiran first asked some simple questions.","\"What's your name?\"","Short Man: \"I'm called Huang Xu.\"","He Zhiran: \"Where are you from?\"","Huang Xu: \"I'm from the imperial capital in the Southern Borderlands.\"","He Zhiran: \"Where do you live?\"","Huang Xu: \"I live at Si Meng Mountain Villa.\"","After asking these few questions while taking note of Huang Xu's dazed expression, He Zhiran could completely determine that he had entered a hypnotized state.","She glanced at Mo Jiuye to signal him to come over and ask questions.","Mo Jiuye squatted beside his wife and asked in a deep voice, \"Who is Mr. Si Meng?\"","Huang Xu struggled briefly before answering, \"Mr. Si Meng is my master.\"","Mo Jiuye: \"Where is he now?\"","Huang Xu: \"I don't know. I haven't seen my master for three years already.\"","Hearing that he didn't know, Mo Jiuye instantly frowned.","He Zhiran waved the pocket watch and continued asking, \"How can we find your master?\"","Huang Xu: \"My master comes and goes like a spirit. If he has business with me, he will naturally appear.\"","He Zhiran: \"What if there's an urgent matter you need to report to your master?\"","Huang Xu: \"Even for urgent matters I can only send a message to the Western Territory of Dashun before July each year. My master will go there once every July.\"","He Zhiran: \"Where in the Western Territory can your group find your master every July?\"","Huang Xu: \"I don't know. I've never gone to the Western Territory to look for my master.\"","He Zhiran kept asking, \"Has no one else from your group gone to the Western Territory to find your master?\"","Huang Xu: \"No one has looked for him before.\"","He Zhiran knew that it was impossible for Huang Xu to lie while hypnotized. This could only mean he truly had no idea where Mr. Si Meng was.","Since he didn't know, there was no need to keep interrogating fruitlessly.","\"What's your master's full name?\"","Huang Xu: \"My master has never revealed his name. I only heard from my senior apprentice brother that his surname is Shao.\"","Indeed it was Shao, the same as the young lord surnamed Shao who was infatuated with Yuan Meng according to Lady Mo's account of the past. And this Mr. Si Meng also had the same surname, undoubtedly the same person.","He Zhiran continued asking, \"What does your master look like?\"","Huang Xu: \"My master has a full head of white hair. Whenever he comes to see us, he changes his appearance each time, so I don't know what he really looks like.\"","Mentioning a head of white hair, the first thought that came to He Zhiran's mind was Yun Li's description of ever-youthful white hair.","She pressed on, \"Does your master appear with ever-youthful white hair?\"","Huang Xu: \"He has only shown up once with ever-youthful white hair. The other two times he took on the form of a woman and an elderly person respectively.\"","He Zhiran: \"You don't even know his real looks. How do you confirm his identity then?\"","Huang Xu: \"My master has a token. We recognize him by the token.\"","After asking so much, it seemed there were hardly any useful clues, only confirmation that Mr. Si Meng was the person Lady Mo spoke about.","He Zhiran observed Huang Xu's hypnotized state, which currently showed no signs of fading. Since this was the case, she simply asked some other questions as well.","\"The snake pits blocking the path to the mountain villa, did your group put them there?\"","\"It was us who placed them there.\" Huang Xu answered very readily.","\"Why?\" He Zhiran asked.","Huang Xu: \"Before the new year, one of my junior apprentice brothers went out to buy supplies but never returned. Worried about the safety of the mountain villa, we put the snake pits there.\"","He Zhiran: \"Who was controlling the snakes?\"","Huang Xu: \"It was my eldest senior apprentice brother.\"","He Zhiran: \"Who is your eldest senior apprentice brother?\"","Huang Xu: \"It's the person who was with me.\"","He Zhiran: \"What about the colorful frogs at the bottom of the well then?\"","Huang Xu: \"Those were all my eldest senior apprentice brother's precious pets.\"","He Zhiran: \"So the well opening leads to your secret chamber?\"","Huang Xu: \"Yes.\"","He Zhiran: \"How many other people are still inside the secret chamber now?\"","Huang Xu: \"Aside from one person being held captive, there are three more of my junior apprentice brothers there.\""]},{"number":259,"title":"Chapter 259: Down Well","paragraphs":["Seeing that Huang Xu's tone of voice was somewhat dull, He Zhiran knew that her hypnosis was about to wear off.","Mo Jiuye also noticed something was wrong, and anxiously came forward to ask, \"Who are you guys guarding?\"","Huang Xu: \"I... I don't know. It's someone Master brought here for us to guard.\"","As his voice fell, he sobered up completely.","He Zhiran put away her pocket watch and stood up, looking towards Mo Jiuye, \"Do you have anything else you want to ask?\"","Mo Jiuye shook his head, \"No more.\"","After he finished speaking, he ended Huang Xu with a slash of his blade.","As for the two corpses, there was no need to hide them at all. Since they had already come to Si Meng Mountain Villa, they would definitely investigate this place clearly. Even without these two corpses, it would still attract the attention of interested people.","With a thought, He Zhiran made herself, Mo Jiuye and the two corpses appear outside.","The two corpses were thrown there directly, and the two returned to the edge of the dried-up well.","Now knowing there was no danger inside the dried-up well, Mo Jiuye swept He Zhiran by the waist and jumped down.","Standing firmly at the bottom of the well, there was indeed an iron door recessing inward, as Mo Jiuye had expected. He reached out and pushed the door open.","What came into view was a narrow passageway that could only accommodate one person walking at a time. The passage was lined with a few dim oil lamps on both sides.","Mo Jiuye walked in front, with He Zhiran following closely behind. After walking out for about fifty meters, the light ahead became brighter and brighter.","At the same time, they could vaguely hear people talking.","\"Eldest Senior Brother has been out checking for so long and still hasn't come back. Could something have happened?\"","\"It shouldn't be. Eldest Senior Brother has cultivated his life-protecting Gu, he can protect himself if necessary.\"","\"But they've been out for so long...\"","Before the voice could fall, the speakers heard the sound of the door.","\"Why were you guys out for so long, Eldest Senior Brother?\"","\"Your Eldest Senior Brother has gone to see the King of Hell.\" Mo Jiuye answered jokingly.","The voice was unfamiliar to those inside the secret room. Several people looked towards the entrance at the same time.","They saw a man and a woman standing there with their arms crossed, staring at them.","The few simultaneously reached into their clothes and took out their own Gu worms, assuming a vigilant posture.","At the same time, one who looked older spoke up and asked, \"Just who exactly are you?\"","Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran walked unhurriedly towards the man without answering.","Seeing this, the man quickly opened a porcelain bottle in his hand and released a Gu worm.","Before the Gu worm could get close to the two, it began to scurry around in panic.","Seeing this, the others immediately became vigilant and released their own Gu worms as well.","Mo Jiuye raised his flamethrower gun, aimed at the Gu worms and sprayed fire, burning the three Gu worms into ashes in the blink of an eye.","Seeing this, the three were shocked and turned pale. This was the first time they had encountered such a situation while using Gu worms.","Especially since they had raised these Gu worms for a long time, the Gu worms had reached a state of spiritual communication with their masters. As long as the masters conscientiously manipulated them, they would never easily die.","But what had they just witnessed?","Their Gu worms had actually been burned to death by that kind of fierce fire they had never seen before...","The few exchanged glances with each other, then prepared to release the rest of the Gu worms. They were even ready to take action personally.","He Zhiran would not give them a chance to release the Gu worms. She raised her hand and threw out a packet of sedative powder, rendering them all unconscious.","As their masters lost consciousness, the little porcelain bottles in their hands also fell to the ground, making a series of clinking sounds.","Mo Jiuye quickly came forward to collect those little porcelain bottles and used his flamethrower gun to kill all the Gu worms.","Then he searched the bodies of the few as well, but did not find any other Gu worms except for some silver tickets.","The men had been drugged by a sedative personally concocted by He Zhiran. Without external interference, they would be asleep for at least two hours. She and Mo Jiuye tacitly did not hurry to interrogate them, but began searching the secret room instead.","The secret room was quite spacious, visibly consisting of more than ten rooms.","Not only were there studies, cultivation rooms, even kitchens and toilets.","In addition, there should be the bedrooms where Mr. Simeng's disciples lived.","First, the two searched those bedrooms. Other than some men’s clothing, the amount of silver money was also considerable.","It goes without saying that these people must be engaged in some shady businesses, using Gu worms to do things for employers. It can be imagined that their income must be substantial.","He Zhiran wasn’t interested in those men’s clothes. She directly collected the silver tickets into her space.","After searching all the bedrooms, the two went to the cultivation room.","The cultivation room was also nothing special, just some meditation cushions and some small porcelain bottles for keeping Gu worms.","Lastly, they arrived at the study.","The secret room’s study was almost no different from an ordinary family’s study. Bookshelves lined against the three walls, containing books related to Gu techniques, as well as some about poison-making.","He Zhiran didn’t know if she would need these books in the future. Anyway, it’s best that such harmful things don’t circulate too widely, lest they bring harm to more people.","Therefore, she waved her little hand, collecting the books along with the bookshelves into her space all at once.","She had expected that as usual, the objects in front of her would vanish without a trace.","But that didn’t happen...","The books on the top shelf directly facing the door all disappeared, but the bookshelf didn’t budge one bit.","Mo Jiuye instantly noticed something was wrong. Based on his wife’s consistent style, it was impossible for her to deliberately leave only this one bookshelf behind.","There must be some special reason why she couldn’t put it into her space.","\"There's something wrong with this bookshelf. My spiritual sense doesn't work on it,\" He Zhiran said.","By now, Mo Jiuye had already come forward to touch the bookshelf tentatively.","On the surface, there didn't seem anything special about this bookshelf. It was just that no matter how hard he tried, he couldn't make it budge one bit.","\"There is indeed something strange about this bookshelf,\" Mo Jiuye frowned and said, \"If I'm not mistaken, this should be some kind of entrance to a secret passage.\"","He Zhiran had the same guess.","\"Huang Xu said there was still someone Mr. Simeng brought for them to guard. They must be inside the secret room.\"","The two gave up trying to move the bookshelf and started searching inside the study instead.","Other than the books and the other two bookshelves which He Zhiran had taken into her space, the rest of the items remained untouched in their original places.","After sweeping his gaze around, Mo Jiuye eventually arrived in front of the room’s only desk.","He first tapped around on the desktop and, finding nothing unusual, tentatively reached under the desk to feel around.","Seeing his body suddenly freeze, He Zhiran asked, \"What is it? Did you discover something?\"","Mo Jiuye solemnly said, \"The switch should be here.\"","However, when he tried pushing it a few times, there wasn’t the slightest sound.","He Zhiran took a flashlight from her space. The two of them squeezed under the desk to observe carefully.","The switch Mo Jiuye referred to looked like an extremely ordinary piece of scrap iron on the outside. If they hadn’t guessed that bookshelf might be the entrance to some kind of secret passage, it would have been difficult for them to think this piece of scrap iron was actually a switch."]},{"number":260,"title":"Chapter 260: Mo Xiuyan","paragraphs":["Mo Jiuye got up and tapped the spot on the tabletop that corresponded to the position of the iron lump below.","He Zhiran could see clearly from under the table that after just a few taps, faint cracks began to appear where the iron lump met the tabletop.","\"Tap it a few more times,\" she said.","Mo Jiuye responded and struck the tabletop again.","\"How about now?\"","\"It hasn't moved yet. Try tapping different spots,\" He Zhiran reminded him.","Mo Jiuye continued tapping the tabletop, not too quickly, asking after every three taps.","He Zhiran kept her eyes glued on the iron lump.","\"Don't move, it should be right here. Keep tapping this spot,\" she said.","She saw with her own eyes that the gap between the iron lump and the table grew a little wider.","Mo Jiuye tapped that spot again, three times, then three times more...","The iron lump slowly detached from the tabletop, extending into an iron rod as thick as a wrist.","There was a button on the rod. He Zhiran tentatively pressed it.","A muffled sound rang out in the silent room, and the motionless bookshelf slowly slid open on both sides.","As the bookshelf moved, a pungent, foul odor instantly filled the air...","Mo Jiuye took the flashlight from He Zhiran and walked into the opening first.","It was a very small room with little furnishing. In the corner was a bed.","Lying flat on the bed was a person who could easily be mistaken for dead if not for the visible rise and fall of his chest.","Mo Jiuye asked in a low voice, \"Who are you?\"","Mo Xiuyan thought it was those people coming again to humiliate him. Hearing the sounds, he closed his eyes.","He was now a crippled man, with even begging for death a luxury.","In this lightless room, he had already lost track of how long he had been locked up. Whenever those people came in, other than shoving him some food and water, all they did was insult him.","Mo Xiuyan was used to this by now. He only hoped that when those people tormented him, they would be a bit heavier handed so he could be freed from this misery sooner.","Hearing this voice, he felt an inexplicable sense of familiarity.","But he could never have imagined it would be his ninth younger brother. He thought it must be that he missed his family so much that he was hallucinating.","His rationality quickly defeated the longing in his heart. This must be someone new, only finding the voice unfamiliar on first hearing.","Therefore, Mo Xiuyan did not respond. He continued lying there with closed eyes, waiting for the next round of possible torture.","However, the expected did not come even after waiting for a long time.","Mo Jiuye had already walked over to his bedside, pulling He Zhiran along.","The bright flashlight beam forced Mo Xiuyan to open his eyes.","Having not seen light for years, Mo Xiuyan could only squint under the glaring flashlight.","The years of torment had stripped Mo Xiuyan of his former appearance. In Mo Jiuye's eyes, the man before him had disheveled hair covered in unknown grime.","His eye sockets were sunken, cheekbones protruding. If not for the breath still in him, he was the spitting image of a desiccated corpse.","Despite this, Mo Jiuye still made out the general features of his face.","He tentatively asked, \"Fourth brother, is that you?\"","As he spoke, he realized fourth brother could not open his eyes fully due to the bright light and redirected the flashlight beam elsewhere.","If Mo Xiuyan had thought the voice was a hallucination earlier, now that Mo Jiuye had called out \"fourth brother\", there was no way he could still think it unreal.","\"Ninth younger brother, is it really you?\"","Mo Jiuye had called out like that to test as well, since Mo Xiuyan looked so different from his impression.","He was clearly only around thirty, yet looked as old as a dying elder.","He Zhiran could feel Mo Jiuye's body trembling.","She saw him squat by the bed, hands shaking as he reached out to touch Mo Xiuyan.","Mo Xiuyan instinctively wanted to shy away but lacked the strength.","\"Don't...don't touch me, I'm filthy,\" he said.","Indeed, Mo Xiuyan's clothes were tattered beyond recognition, glowing with accumulated grime and stains from unknown filth.","Mo Jiuye would not be deterred at all. He continued what he was doing.","The moment he made contact with Mo Xiuyan's body, it was like his heart was bleeding.","\"Fourth brother, how did you become so emaciated?\"","Just the sight of Mo Xiuyan's skeletal form was hard to accept. The real feeling of touching him was simply too much for Mo Jiuye.","Mo Xiuyan squeezed out a pained smile. \"That I still draw breath today is already heaven's mercy.\"","Now was not the time to ask Mo Xiuyan for details of his ordeal. He Zhiran reminded, \"Husband, let me examine fourth brother's condition first.\"","Hearing that \"husband\", Mo Xiuyan knew without thinking that the woman speaking was his sister-in-law.","In his current filthy state, how could he possibly let his ninth brother's wife help examine him?","Mo Xiuyan quickly said, \"Sister-in-law, let me tell you...\"","He paused, then continued weakly, \"My legs are broken, my arm tendons severed, but otherwise I'm fine.\"","Fine?","How could such an emaciated body be described as \"fine\"?","Having been here for over six months, He Zhiran fully understood the thinking of ancient people.","Especially between elder brother and sister-in-law, an almost evasive relationship existed.","Mo Xiuyan's current condition was clearly not as simple as he claimed. To help examine him further required the advanced medical equipment from the System.","Therefore, He Zhiran did not insist on examining Mo Xiuyan right away.","She planned to let the two brothers chat for a bit first, then inject Mo Xiuyan with a tranquilizer to knock him unconscious before bringing him into the System.","Whether it was examining his condition or getting him out of here, Mo Xiuyan needed to enter the System.","Seeing his sister-in-law make no further moves, Mo Xiuyan finally relaxed his taut nerves a little.","He gave a self-deprecating laugh, then said, \"As a crippled man now, being able to see family again while still alive brings me much comfort.","As for my body, even the great healer Bian Que alive today could surely not cure it.\"","In the flashlight beam, He Zhiran could see the deep disappointment in Mo Xiuyan's eyes.","Anyone would feel heartache over his situation, locked away in this lightless room, probably thinking of nothing besides waiting for death each day.","\"Fourth brother, trust me. I will find a way to cure you,\" Mo Jiuye said resolutely.","Hearing his wife say this, he couldn't help asking, \"Ranran, can you really heal fourth brother's condition?\"","He knew his wife's medical skills were superb, but fourth brother's situation was no ordinary illness.","While broken legs did have a chance of being reattached, this was still only a probability.","Fourth brother had been missing for years, so his leg injury was surely quite old. Putting aside how serious it was, he had never heard of anyone in this day and age able to cure it.","As for fourth brother's severed arm tendons, this was also incurable by Mo Jiuye's knowledge."]},{"number":261,"title":"Chapter 261: I'll find a way to cure Brother Four.","paragraphs":["He didn't distrust his wife's medical skills, but Fourth Brother's condition was very special. Now that he was still alive after being found, it was already a blessing.","Mo Jiuye had even thought ahead that as long as he could bring Fourth Brother back home, he would be willing to support him for life as long as he was alive.","It was no surprise that He Zhiran was questioned. If she didn't master advanced medical technology from the future, and have those advanced medical equipment in her space, she would never dare to say such things.","\"Trust me, I will find a way to cure Fourth Brother.\"","The conversation between the two was heard clearly by Mo Xiuyan. In order not to make the young couple feel bad, he did not refute.","After all, they were in someone else's territory. To be safe, Mo Jiuye did not dare to stay here any longer.","He Zhiran had the same idea, so she took out silver needles from her space.","\"Fourth Brother, let me first apply acupuncture to make you feel more comfortable.\"","As soon as she finished speaking, without waiting for Mo Xiuyan to respond, He Zhiran had already quickly inserted silver needles at several acupoints on his head.","Soon, Mo Xiuyan lost consciousness.","He Zhiran also injected him with a small amount of tranquilizers before settling the man on the operating table bed in the space.","After examining the room once more and making sure nothing was amiss, the two returned to the entrance of the secret chamber.","Coming to Simeng Mountain Villa and finding Mo Xiuyan was already the biggest gain for them.","Moreover, from the interrogation of Huang Xu's situation, these people may not necessarily know more than him.","In order to leave here sooner to treat Mo Xiuyan, Mo Jiuye directly beheaded those three men and leapt out of the well with He Zhiran.","It was already midnight now. With poor visibility going down the mountain, He Zhiran decided to enter the space on the spot to first check on Mo Xiuyan's condition.","Back in the space, they saw Dough trying hard to climb onto the operating table.","It was understandable that the little guy was curious about the strangers.","Seeing this, He Zhiran hurriedly took the little guy to the side and coaxed him with a small apple to go play by himself.","Mo Xiuyan was still in a deep sleep.","Mo Jiuye first fetched a basin of clear water and simply cleaned Fourth Brother's body, then changed him into clothes that He Zhiran had temporarily purchased for him in Taobao Mall.","With everything settled, He Zhiran came to the operating room.","She first touched Mo Xiuyan's legs, and instantly frowned.","Seeing her expression, Mo Jiuye nervously asked, \"Ranran, how are Fourth Brother's legs?\"","\"The condition of Fourth Brother's legs is not very optimistic. This is not just a simple bone fracture.\"","He Zhiran thought for a while and told her initial judgment.","\"All the bones in Fourth Brother's lower legs are shattered. Compared to that, helping Fourth Brother reconnect the crushed bones is a small problem. The most important thing is that the muscles in his legs have all died, and those dead muscles must be removed and regenerated. Only then will Fourth Brother have a chance to stand up again in the future.\"","This was only He Zhiran's initial judgment. As for the condition of other parts of Fourth Brother's body, further examination was still needed to make a diagnosis.","After simply explaining to Mo Jiuye, He Zhiran then used her consciousness to control various examinations of Fourth Brother.","The results of the examination were not very optimistic.","Seeing his wife's solemn expression, Mo Jiuye felt uneasy in his heart again.","\"Ranran, how is Fourth Brother's body?\"","\"Fourth Brother has a serious deficiency of qi and blood.\"","In other words, he was malnourished. In order for Mo Jiuye to understand, she chose to express it in the language of traditional Chinese medicine.","\"And many of Fourth Brother's internal organs are damaged, especially the test indicators of his heart, which currently do not meet the conditions for surgery.\" He Zhiran tried to explain to Mo Jiuye in words he could understand.","Hearing this, Mo Jiuye became even more anxious.","Now that they had finally found Fourth Brother, he could not have anything happen to him.","\"Ranran, is there any good way for Fourth Brother's condition?\"","He Zhiran also felt that Fourth Brother's condition was tricky.","In her previous life, even if her patients had very poor physical condition, none of them had as many problems as Fourth Brother.","\"The injuries to Fourth Brother's legs and hands can be treated a little later. The most important thing now is to adjust his body to a state that can undergo surgery.\"","Mo Jiuye didn't understand medicine, but he believed his wife could surely cure Fourth Brother.","\"Alright, I'll leave it to you, Ranran.\"","There was no time to lose. Currently Fourth Brother's condition was very poor. If it weren't for him and He Zhiran rescuing him today, I'm afraid if they found him a few days later, it would be Fourth Brother's corpse.","This kind of treatment would take at least half a month to show results. Fourth Brother was only in a temporary coma and could not stay in the space for a long time.","But for now, He Zhiran was still confident. The amount of drugs Fourth Brother used would make him sleep soundly until noon tomorrow.","So He Zhiran hung plasma bags on both of Fourth Brother's hands, one was a bag of dark red plasma, and the other was a nutritional solution to help him quickly regain his strength.","After getting busy with these, the two did not rest at all and immediately left the space.","By now, it was almost dawn outside. Mo Jiuye hugged He Zhiran using qinggong (lightness skill) to swiftly rush down the mountain.","Inside the city, they found a local dental clinic and rented a yard to temporarily house Fourth Brother for recuperation. After all, they still didn’t know how long they would stay in the South. Living in a private house was much more convenient than an inn.","In addition to renting the yard, the two also bought a sixteen or seventeen year old boy from the dental clinic. According to the tooth dealer, his name was Shun Zi and he was born deaf and mute. Such a person would be most suitable to take care of Fourth Brother. This way, they would not have to worry about Fourth Brother having no one to look after him when they went out to do things.","First Mo Jiuye sent Shun Zi out to buy some household items. He and He Zhiran rushed to the rented yard first.","It was almost noon. After Mo Jiuye simply tidied up the bedding in the room, He Zhiran moved Fourth Brother onto the bed with a thought.","Fourth Brother was still not awake, but after some treatment, his complexion looked a little better than last night.","He Zhiran entered the space again and prepared some warming food for Fourth Brother. She had just finished when Fourth Brother woke up.","Seeing Fourth Brother awake, Mo Jiuye was in no hurry to ask about his ordeal. Instead, he brought over sea cucumber rice porridge and some small dishes that He Zhiran had prepared.","\"Fourth Brother, you're awake. Eat something first to fill your stomach.\"","With Fourth Brother unable to move his limbs, Mo Jiuye had to personally feed him, while also clearly seeing the appearances of the two people before him.","Originally in the dark secret chamber, he couldn't see very clearly and could only determine by voice that this person was Ninth Junior Brother.","Now in a room with decent light, he got a thorough look at both people. The voice was clearly Ninth Junior Brother's, but why did his appearance become like this?","Mo Xiuyan asked in puzzlement, \"Ninth Junior Brother, how did you become like this?\"","Only then did Mo Jiuye realize that he was still in disguise.","He tore off the fake beard and hat covering his whole forehead with his hand, \"Fourth Brother, in order to move around easily in the South, I simply disguised myself.\"","Now Mo Xiuyan finally found a trace of familiarity. No matter the makeup, Ninth Junior Brother's brows and eyes still had their original shadow."]},{"number":262,"title":"Chapter 262: The Past Events of Mo Xiuyan","paragraphs":["Mo Xiuyan only took a sip of the sweet rice porridge Mo Jiuye fed him. The warm rice porridge entered his belly, and the usually strong man actually shed tears.","This was the first time Mo Jiuye saw his eldest brother shed tears. His heart seemed to bleed along with it.","\"Fourth brother, everything will get better. If Mother and Fourth Sister-in-law know you are still alive, they will definitely be very happy.\"","Mo Xiuyan showed a bitter smile: \"Now I'm a cripple. Going back will only become a burden on my family. It's better if I die early.\"","\"Fourth brother, don't think like that. Believe in He Zhiran, she will definitely cure you.\" Mo Jiuye would not allow his fourth brother to have such self-abandoning thoughts.","Knowing that the ninth brother was distressed seeing him like this, Mo Xiuyan tried his best to squeeze out a smile: \"Okay, I'll listen to ninth brother.\"","No matter what, even if it was just to see his family again before he died, it would be good.","Unfortunately, he would be unable to serve his mother on her deathbed in this lifetime, and could no longer accompany his young wife.","These were just Mo Xiuye's inner thoughts. He could not let his dispirited thoughts affect his ninth brother's mood.","Mo Jiuye forcibly held back his tears and fed Mo Xiuye bowl by bowl of rice porridge.","At this time, Shun Zi who had gone to buy supplies also returned.","This guy was quite sensible. In addition to a large iron pot, he also bought some grain and vegetables.","Anyway, he was just looking for an excuse to send Shun Zi away, so it didn't matter what he brought back.","Shun Zi put everything in place, then came to Mo Xiuye's room, gesturing to indicate that he would take care of him.","Mo Jiuye didn't plan on leaving yet as he hadn't asked his fourth brother about his experiences, so he sent Shun Zi away.","Shun Zi obediently left, and Mo Jiuye sat down on the edge of Mo Xiuye's bed.","\"Fourth brother, what have you experienced all these years?\"","Recalling the experiences of recent years, Mo Xiuye's eyes were filled with sorrow.","At this time, he still didn't know that the Mo Family had already been ordered by Emperor Shunwu to have their property confiscated and exiled. He thought Mo Jiuye was here on some border mission and coincidentally discovered him.","\"With such a prince, the kingdom is in danger...\"","Seeing his fourth brother like this but still concerned about the kingdom, Mo Jiuye had mixed feelings.","\"Fourth brother, I'll tell you about it slowly later. Our family is now living very well in the northwest, and Mother is very healthy.\"","\"I want to know now what you've experienced all these years?\"","Mo Xiuye tried his best to digest the recent situation at home before slowly speaking.","\"Back then, Nan Heng followed me to guard the southern border. After a great victory in one battle, he insisted on chasing the southern border soldiers against advice. I saw he wouldn't listen to dissuasion and was worried he'd be in danger, so I led a team to support him.","By then, Nan Heng had already entered the trap set by the southerners. My soldiers and I fought desperately to save him and escape. Later as I desperately fled the scene, already heavily injured, I accidentally ran to the edge of a cliff.","With so many enemies, and me already crippled, I had no chance against them. To avoid becoming a prisoner, I chose to jump off the cliff.","I broke both legs from the fall and couldn't leave there. I could only hope Nan Heng would quickly send people to find me. But before Da Shun's search party arrived, I was found by the southern soldiers who captured me back.","At that time, I knew I couldn't escape death.","Unexpectedly, I had just been carried up from the ravine before being drugged unconscious again. When I woke up, I found myself lying in a cave.\"","Hearing this, Mo Jiuye couldn't help but ask: \"Were they going to curse you?\"","Mo Xiuye nodded: \"I did accidentally overhear their conversation.","They said my legs were now crippled beyond healing, so cursing me would be of no use. They might as well send me to be held in the manor, where I may come in handy if needed.","Not long after, they severed my arm tendons, covered my head in black cloth, and brought me to where you found me.","That place never saw daylight, I don't know how long I lay there.\"","After listening to his fourth brother's account, Mo Jiuye fiercely smashed the room's only wooden table with his fist.","The wooden table disintegrated on impact, fragments shooting in all directions.","This showed how furious he was to use such force.","\"Fourth brother, I, Mo Jiuye, swear I will find the people who persecuted our Mo men, and tear them into eight pieces, quarter them...\"","He Zhiran went up and stroked his chest: \"Finding Fourth Brother is a good thing, don't ruin your health being angry over those villains.\"","Mo Jiuye's body still trembled slightly. He grasped He Zhiran's small hand and solemnly said, \"I know.\"","Having said so much, Mo Xiuye felt somewhat exhausted and had already fallen deeply asleep.","Mo Jiuye looked at the sky, there was still some time before dark. He called Shun Zi to take care of Fourth Brother, while he and He Zhiran rested in the space for a while.","Counting it, they had barely closed their eyes for two days. He was strong and could take it, but was worried it would be too taxing on his wife's body.","He Zhiran was indeed a little tired. If it wasn't for everything going on keeping her conscious alert, she would have been visiting Mr. Sandman long ago.","Finally able to relax for a bit, she had to replenish her energy to avoid dozing off during their night action.","Ever since finding Mo Xiuye, Mo Jiuye had been in a tense state. Relaxing now, he still had no sleepiness at all.","But he knew there was no telling what would happen tonight, so he had to force himself to conserve his energy.","He held He Zhiran as they lay on the comfortable big bed, resting with eyes closed.","Until the sky outside had darkened, Mo Jiuye had no choice but to wake his sleeping beauty.","He Zhiran groggily yawned and murmured, \"What time is it?\"","Mo Jiuye gently replied, \"It's almost the hour of Xu.\"","\"Ah? It's this late already. Why didn't you wake me sooner? Fourth brother still needs to take medicine, and can't eat just anything.\"","Speaking, He Zhiran had already nimbly jumped off the bed. She first cooked some porridge in the kitchen. After a simple meal with Mo Jiuye, they left the space together.","Mo Xiuye was awake now. Knowing these past few days must have been tiring for his ninth brother and sister-in-law, he didn't have Shun Zi disturb them."]},{"number":263,"title":"Chapter 263: Enter the Prince's Palace","paragraphs":["Shun Zi had also prepared food for him, but Shun Zi's cooking skills were not very good, and the food he made could only barely fill one's stomach.","Mo Xiuyan's body was weak and he didn't have much appetite to begin with, so he only ate a few bites before stopping.","Just then, Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran came, bringing sea cucumber rice porridge and side dishes.","Mo Jiuye fed his fourth brother a little more, and only after did He Zhiran hand over several medicines suitable for Mo Xiuyan to take to Shun Zi, telling Shun Zi to give them to him on time.","After taking the medicine, Mo Xiuyan saw that the two were still in disguise and asked, \"Ninth younger brother, are you still planning to go out?\"","Today, Mo Xiuyan was extremely weak. Mo Jiuye had only told him about the exile at home. He didn't know the details. He also didn't know Mo Jiuye's true purpose for coming to the Southern Borderlands.","If the fourth brother was healthy, Mo Jiuye would choose to tell him these things, but given his current condition, he probably couldn't take any more blows. Therefore, Mo Jiuye planned to hide these things for the time being.","Of course, as a Mo family man, he had the right to know these things. Mo Jiuye would choose to tell him after the fourth brother's health improved a little.","\"Fourth brother, I and Ranran came here to find something. When we find it, we'll go back to the Northwest together.\"","Mo Xiuyan didn't know what Mo Jiuye was looking for that made him travel thousands of miles to the Southern Borderlands. He didn't ask any further questions, only nodded lightly, \"You two must be extra careful when going out.\"","\"Don't worry, fourth brother!\" Mo Jiuye said and then instructed Shun Zi to take good care of Mo Xiuyan before leaving with He Zhiran.","The two's target today was the residence of the Crown Prince of the Southern Borderlands, to complete the second goal of their trip to the Southern Borderlands.","Because the fourth princess of Da Shun came here to marry the Crown Prince of the Southern Borderlands, the greatest possibility of finding dan pi was in the Crown Prince's residence.","Mo Jiuye had led troops to attack the Southern Borderlands capital city before, so he was no stranger to the terrain here.","The two galloped all the way and soon arrived outside the gate of the Crown Prince’s residence.","It had to be said that the defenses of the Crown Prince’s residence were extremely tight. Just by the naked eye, there were two teams of soldiers patrolling back and forth in front of the gate, not to mention how many were hidden.","Even if they wanted to sneak in by climbing over the wall, they had to beware of the hidden eyes, which showed how extremely difficult it was.","Even so, it did not diminish Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran's determination to enter the Crown Prince’s residence to investigate.","The two circled the wall of the Crown Prince’s residence and walked to the back garden, pretending to pass by.","The defenses there were slightly more relaxed than the front courtyard, but there were still several guards patrolling back and forth.","Mo Jiuye seized the opportunity, hugged He Zhiran and leaped over the wall.","At this moment, a team of guards happened to patrol by. He quickly pulled He Zhiran to hide in the corner until those guards were far away before carefully walking out.","In order to be able to move freely in the Crown Prince's residence with such tight security, Mo Jiuye came up with a plan.","Soon, two night watchmen walked by not far away. He and He Zhiran looked at each other, then they went behind the night watchmen at the same time, and each knocked out one with a swift hand blade. They then quickly changed into their clothes and casually picked up the tools they used to beat the night watch.","To prevent the fainted night watchmen from waking up, He Zhiran gave each a shot to ensure nothing went wrong.","It wasn’t because they were soft-hearted, especially He Zhiran. In her previous life, she was a military doctor and would never play with human lives, of course, except for those extremely evil people.","These two night watchmen were obviously servants and slaves bought by the Crown Prince’s residence. They only exchanged their labor for food. There was no need to kill them all.","After dealing with everything here, He Zhiran picked up a lantern and Mo Jiuye picked up the bamboo stick used to beat the night watch. The two wandered around the Crown Prince’s residence.","Mo Jiuye was familiar with the terrain of the Southern Borderlands capital city but wasn’t very clear about the structure inside the Crown Prince’s residence.","They could only rely on experience to search, figuring that as the Crown Da Shun princess married the Crown Prince as the official wife, her courtyard should be slightly bigger. Therefore, the two specifically looked for bigger courtyards.","Unconsciously, the two arrived outside a huge courtyard.","This courtyard was very different from the others. From the outside, lights shone and melodious music could be heard coming from inside.","In addition, Mo Jiuye, who had extremely good hearing, could hear bursts of women's laughter.","Just as he was about to observe further, two black-clothed guards suddenly appeared in front of them.","The dark guards growled for them to leave, \"You two leave quickly. Is the Crown Prince's place somewhere you can peek at?\"","Mo Jiuye pulled He Zhiran and nodded at the two dark guards, \"Yes, yes, we're leaving now.\"","Although they were driven away for peeping by the dark guards, it wasn’t without some gains. At least they now knew the Crown Prince of the Southern Borderlands was inside.","It seemed that this Crown Prince liked enjoyment. This was good too, it didn’t hinder them from finding the whereabouts of the fourth princess.","Not long after leaving the Crown Prince’s location, they saw a woman dressed as a maid rushing anxiously toward the direction of the Crown Prince’s bedroom.","Perhaps the maid was too anxious. When she ran to a place not far from them, she didn’t know what she had stepped on and took a tumble.","He Zhiran took the opportunity to help prop the woman up, deliberately lowering her voice, \"Sister, be careful.\"","The maid grabbed He Zhiran's arm tightly and struggled to stand up. As a result, her ankle seemed to be sprained. She almost fell again when taking the first step.","Now the maid was even more anxious.","\"Brother, please go to the Crown Prince and help report that the Crown Princess has fainted. Please ask him to invite a witch doctor to come and take a look.\"","He Zhiran knew that the Southern Borderland people sought witch doctors. She just didn’t understand why the Crown Princess of a country needed to go through the Crown Prince to invite a witch doctor.","Also, she could hear the maid spoke in the Da Shun accent. She should be an accompanying palace maid of the fourth princess.","Mo Jiuye saw this too. To prevent the maid from noticing He Zhiran's accent was wrong, he quickly stepped forward and said, \"That's not a place people like us can enter at all.\"","\"Then what should we do? The Crown Princess is so seriously ill. If we don't ask a witch doctor to come and see, I'm afraid she may die.\" The maid was almost crying, which showed how helpless she felt.","Seeing this, He Zhiran hurriedly signaled Mo Jiuye with her eyes.","Mo Jiuye understood instantly and said, \"This little brother's ancestors were witch doctors. He also knows some medical skills. Why don't you let him go and take a look at the Crown Princess first while you go find someone to ask the Crown Prince?”","The maid knew that given her current situation, going to ask the Crown Prince again would likely delay a lot of time. Here was close to the Crown Princess's bedroom. She decided to take them back first while letting others go find the Crown Prince."]},{"number":264,"title":"Chapter 264: In the Face of the Daesun Dynasty","paragraphs":["The maid was determined and said, \"Since this is the case, there is no other choice.\"","Seeing the maid agree, He Zhiran took the initiative to support her, and walked to the Crown Princess Consort's palace step by step.","Contrary to their imagination, the Crown Princess Consort's palace was not the largest in the inner palace, but it looked shabby and remote instead of the largest.","Based on He Zhiran's experience of watching TV shows in his previous life, the fact that the Crown Princess Consort lived in such a place showed that she was not favored by the Crown Prince.","Not to mention the Prince's Mansion, even ordinary families would not let the official wife live in such a place.","With a belly full of doubts, the two followed the maid into the palace.","In fact, they didn't know that this was not a bedroom at all, but a cold palace in the Prince's Mansion.","The maid thought they were all people from the Prince's Mansion and knew all these things, so she didn't explain anything.","The outside looked like a small bedroom, but after walking in, He Zhiran and Mo Jiuye were shocked.","The two also realized that this was most likely the cold palace.","He Zhiran inevitably complained in his heart: Emperor Shunwu was really conservative. Back then, the Mo Family men guarded the borders and made the southern border fall like flowers and water.","For such a small defeated country, why did he need to send his own daughter here for a political marriage to suffer?","The Southern Border was obviously not taking the Da Shun Dynasty seriously, otherwise how dare they treat the princess who came to be married so rudely?","This was clearly slapping the Da Shun Dynasty in the face...","Of course, their purpose this time was to see the Fourth Princess. They wouldn’t care about things that Emperor Shunwu should worry about.","The Southern Border was not as regular as Da Shun, and the folk customs were more open than Da Shun’s, and there was no rule that men from outside could not enter the harem.","Therefore, no one questioned them all the way to the cold palace with the maid.","The maid limped and took the two directly to the Fourth Princess's room, and asked another maid to ask the Crown Prince to invite the witch doctor.","Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran took a simple look. In the room, only a dim oil lamp was burning, and with no furnishings in the room, it looked bleak.","Lying on a broken wooden bed opposite the door was a disheveled woman.","He Zhiran and Mo Jiuye walked over quickly.","Mo Jiuye had often entered the palace since he was a child. He was also escorting the Fourth Princess’ marriage, so he was no stranger to the appearance of the woman before him.","After confirming the identity of the Fourth Princess, Mo Jiuye nodded slightly to He Zhiran.","Only then did He Zhiran reach out and touch the Fourth Princess's wrist pulse.","After about two minutes, He Zhiran raised her hand.","The anxious maid asked, \"How is the Crown Princess Consort?\"","He Zhiran shook her head: \"She has reached the point of exhaustion. Now she only has one breath left. You might as well get ready!\"","What she didn't say was that when she took her pulse, she felt that her pulse was somewhat similar to that of the few Mo Family brothers who were poisoned, but not exactly the same.","He Zhiran guessed that it was very likely that the Fourth Princess was poisoned, but it was different from the puppet Gu that the Mo Family brothers had.","Without completely confirming it, He Zhiran did not say it.","\"No... Don't talk nonsense. The Crown Princess Consort is a precious daughter of a thousand gold. It’s impossible for her to just die like this. You simply don't understand medical skills, so you say that.\"","In fact, the maid knew very well that the Crown Princess Consort was indeed dying, but she just didn't want to believe this fact.","She had entered the palace to serve the Fourth Princess since she was a child. The Fourth Princess treated her extremely well, and often helped her family.","She had long determined that she would be the Fourth Princess's person for the rest of her life. Even after following her to the Southern Border for marriage and the princess became the unloved Crown Princess Consort, she never thought of leaving, and even thought that even if the Fourth Princess really died, she would definitely follow her so that the princess would not be lonely.","He Zhiran was also very helpless about this. She was a doctor, not a god.","At this time, the Fourth Princess's condition was much more serious than that of Mo Xiuyan when they had saved him, and it was beyond medicine and treatment.","And she could see from the Fourth Princess's pulse that the number of the Fourth Princess’ miscarriages was no less than three times, which had completely injured her vitality. Coupled with her grieving heart, I'm afraid she wouldn't make it through the night.","She looked at the grief-stricken maid and shook her hands helplessly: \"The Crown Princess Consort’s condition is before you. If you don't believe my words, there is nothing I can do.\"","Although she said that, He Zhiran had no intention of leaving.","Because she guessed that since the Crown Prince could bring the Fourth Princess to such a place, he would most likely abandon the marriage with the Da Shun Dynasty and would not care about her life or death.","The maid who had just gone out to find the Crown Prince was probably going to come back with no result. At that time, they would still have to place their last hope on her.","Sure enough, after about half an hour, the maid who had gone to find the Crown Prince came back.","\"Sister Lan, the Crown Prince’s people simply wouldn’t let me in, and said that if I disturbed the Crown Prince’s elegance, they would punish me.\"","At this point, Lan Er was completely petrified.","After a long time, she trembled and said, \"Could it be that the princess is going to die in the Southern Border like this?\"","As her voice fell, the two maids cried at the same time, and even tried to shake the Fourth Princess awake at the bedside.","Seeing this, He Zhiran hurriedly stopped the behavior of the two.","\"She was barely holding on just now. Do you want her to die faster by doing this?\"","At this moment, Lan Er could no longer attend to the disrespect in He Zhiran's tone. She knelt in front of her crying and said,","\"Please save our princess. As long as you can save the princess alive, I am willing to be an ox or a horse to repay you.\"","Although He Zhiran didn't have a good impression of the Fourth Princess, these two maids were absolutely loyal.","Facing such people, she couldn’t bear to be cruel at all.","It was a pity that she was also powerless in the face of the Fourth Princess’s current situation.","She gently helped Lan Er up and sighed, \"I have a way to make your princess regain consciousness. At this time she can convey some things to you, but I don't have the ability to let her live on.\"","Seeing her tone was firm and she was not lying, and looking at the Fourth Princess on the bed with her eyes closed without the slightest vitality, Lan Er had already prepared herself for the burial.","However, before that, she still wanted to serve the Fourth Princess again.","Lan Er wiped her tears and said, \"Please wake up the princess.\"","He Zhiran did not hesitate either, took out the needle pack from the space, and also brought a cardiotonic.","The two measures combined would definitely wake up the Fourth Princess.","She first pricked several acupoints on the Fourth Princess with silver needles, then took the opportunity when the two maids were not paying attention to inject a shot of cardiotonic into the Fourth Princess.","After about five minutes, the Fourth Princess woke up leisurely.","Seeing the moment she opened her eyes, Lan Er and the other maid rushed to the bedside.","\"Princess, you finally woke up.\"","The Fourth Princess looked at the two maids who had grown up with her with little energy, then shifted her gaze to Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran.","\"Who...who are they?\"","At this point, Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran felt that there was no need to conceal their identities.","Especially He Zhiran, who was clearest in her heart that the way she had awakened the Fourth Princess now could not prolong her time, but would accelerate her death rate instead."]},{"number":265,"title":"Chapter 265: I am the true Mo Jiuye","paragraphs":["\"He... who are they?\"","By this time, Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran felt there was no need to conceal their identities anymore.","Especially He Zhiran. She knew very clearly that by using this method to wake up the Fourth Princess, not only could she not extend the Fourth Princess's time, but it would accelerate her death instead.","As for the two maidservants, they were loyal to the Fourth Princess. And judging by the Fourth Princess’s current condition, she and the Prince of Southern Border were not of one mind. Even if the Fourth Princess died, presumably those two maidservants would not turn to the Prince of Southern Border.","They could not go back to Great Shun either, so there was no need to worry that today’s events would be divulged.","Thinking of this, Mo Jiuye stepped forward and said, \"Princess, I am Mo Jiuye.\"","Hearing this voice, the Fourth Princess struggled to open her eyes wide to look at him, trying to find a trace of familiarity in his face.","Mo Jiuye had altered his appearance by now and looked nothing like his original self. He knew it was normal that the Fourth Princess could not recognize him.","To prove his identity, Mo Jiuye spoke again, \"Princess, do you still remember? When I escorted you to the border between Great Shun and Southern Border, you asked me to secretly take you to worship my late father and brothers. You even said that if you were not allowed to burn incense at the Mo family men’s graves, you would die in front of me and absolutely refuse to go to Southern Border for the marriage alliance.\"","\"Cough cough...Are you really Mo Jiuye?\" Only Mo Jiuye alone knew about this matter at the time. And it was Mo Jiuye who accompanied her up the mountain to worship. There could be no mistake. And this voice was indeed the same as Mo Jiuye's.","\"I only changed my appearance to make things easier when acting in Southern Border. I am the genuine Mo Jiuye.\"","Now the Fourth Princess could confirm Mo Jiuye’s identity.","She exerted her arms, attempting to prop herself up to sit.","He Zhiran came over and said, \"It's better if you lie down to conserve your strength.\"","Judging by the Fourth Princess’s current condition, exerting even a little effort would drain the last of her life.","The Fourth Princess should also be clear about her own condition. Although she still did not know He Zhiran’s identity, since she was with Mo Jiuye, she must be his person. Thus, she was very obedient and did not move again.","He Zhiran asked, \"Princess, were you cursed by someone?\"","\"You...How do you know?\" The Fourth Princess was clearly somewhat surprised.","The curse in her body was wilfully cast by someone. Even the witch doctor did not detect it.","It seemed this frail-looking man should not be underestimated.","He Zhiran crossed her arms over her chest, \"Don't ask how I figured it out. Just tell me if it's true or false.\"","The Fourth Princess’s eyes dodged around, clearly unwilling to answer.","\"You don’t need to know about this.\"","Although the Fourth Princess spoke thus, He Zhiran had already confirmed her own judgment.","It was just, why would the Fourth Princess be cursed?","Did the Gu worms in her body have anything to do with Teacher Si Meng whom they were looking for?","This thought made He Zhiran feel an urge to inquire further.","She first looked at Lan Er and the other maidservant. Both maidservants kept their heads lowered, not daring to meet her gaze directly. This showed that these two maidservants also knew the inside story.","If she really could not get anything out from the Fourth Princess, she would target these two maidservants to find the answer.","Just as He Zhiran was pondering this, Lan Er suddenly knelt in front of the Fourth Princess's bed.","\"Princess, now that it has come to this, what more is there left to conceal? Moreover, the Mo family people are right in front of you. You've done so much for the Mo family. How could you still not speak at this time?\"","\"Cough cough cough... Cough cough...\"","Seeing her maidservant kneel down and say these things, the Fourth Princess instinctively wanted to stop her. But as soon as she opened her mouth, it triggered a violent coughing fit, rendering her unable to speak.","Mo Jiuye did not understand why Lan Er would say that.","\"What does she mean when she says you've done a lot for my Mo family?\"","He Zhiran also stared closely at the mistress and servant, wanting to know the answer.","Like Mo Jiuye, she could not think of any reason why the princess who was born to the Empress would do anything good for the Mo family, let alone do a lot.","The Fourth Princess was still coughing heavily. Although so, her eyes were fixed on Lan Er, carrying an obvious warning.","Lan Er no longer cared about much at this moment. As she helped her mistress breathe, she still said, \"Princess, it has come to this point. If even your life is going to be lost, what more can't be said?\"","Although the Fourth Princess knew her remaining time was numbered, she did not realize it was so dire.","She stared at He Zhiran and asked, \"How much longer can I live?\"","Telling the grim truth would be very cruel to the Fourth Princess, but He Zhiran still chose to be blunt.","\"If nothing unexpected happens, only about another hour.\"","\"What? Only an hour left?\" Lan Er widened her eyes in disbelief. In her impression, the princess had never been so spirited before. How could there only be an hour left?","Apparently the Fourth Princess was also very surprised. But after thinking about her ruined body, and realizing that if not for a persisting willpower supporting her, she would have long passed away, she accepted the outcome quite quickly.","\"Since I have come to my dying moments, I will not continue concealing things.\" She looked at Mo Jiuye and went on, \"But you must promise me that even after knowing this news, do not try to save him.\"","Mo Jiuye was left mystified by her words. He did not know who she meant by \"him\".","\"What is the Princess trying to say?\"","The Fourth Princess looked very solemn. \"Promise me first.\"","Mo Jiuye was also stubborn by nature. Without knowing what matter it concerned, even when facing a dying person, he would not compromise.","Especially after Lan Er mentioned that the Fourth Princess had done a lot for the Mo family.","Just who was this \"him\" she spoke of?","\"My Mo family people have always prioritized the greater cause. If it benefits the Mo family, I will naturally listen to the Princess's words. As for other matters, I'm afraid I cannot promise.\"","Seeing Mo Jiuye's firm stance, the Fourth Princess hesitated for a moment.","Unable to bear it, Lan Er urged, \"Princess, it has come to this point. Even your life is going to be lost. What else is there left to consider?\"","The other maidservant also knelt on the ground, sobbing, \"Yes Princess, you should just say it!\"","As He Zhiran and Mo Jiuye grew more confused, they even had a faint guess—could this \"him\" the Fourth Princess mentioned be the missing Mo family son?"]},{"number":266,"title":"Chapter 266: Where is my seventh Brother","paragraphs":["Just as Mo Jiuye was anxious to urge the Fourth Princess to speak up, a trace of reluctance and conflict appeared in her eyes, and she took the initiative to speak.","\"I want to talk about the whereabouts of Mo Yuance, the seventh young master of the Mo family.\"","Upon hearing this, both Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran expressed astonishment.","They had considered that it might be related to the male members of the Mo family, speculating it could be the eldest or second brother, but they never expected it to be the seventh brother.","Regardless, the whereabouts of any brother was equally important to Mo Jiuye.","\"Fourth Princess, where is my seventh brother?\"","At the thought of Mo Yuance, the Fourth Princess's heart bled.","When she was fourteen years old, Mo Yuance served as the commander of the imperial guards in the palace. She happened to see him once and was attracted by his resolute and handsome appearance.","The Fourth Princess knew that she would have to embark on the path of a political marriage in the future, so she never dared to have any extravagant hopes for Mo Yuance.","Unexpectedly, she encountered Mo Yuance again by chance.","The reason was that her pet parrot, which she had raised for many years, suddenly got frightened and flew away. She chased after it with the palace servants, but the parrot flew too high, and they could only see its silhouette without being able to catch it.","At that moment, a robust figure leaped high like lightning and effortlessly caught the flying parrot.","Mo Yuance calmly returned the parrot to her and then left with a bow.","The Fourth Princess already had an extremely favorable impression of Mo Yuance, and after the incident with the parrot, she couldn't forget about him.","She secretly mentioned this matter to her mother, but her mother dismissed it because of Mo Jiuye acting as a tutor for Nanqi, thinking that the Mo family was aligned with the third prince, and she directly crushed her hopes.","Moreover, as the legitimate princess of Da Shun, she was destined to enter into a political marriage. Even if her mother agreed, her father would not allow it.","Since then, she could only keep Mo Yuance silently in her heart and not dare to have any improper thoughts.","Later, when Mo Yuance got married, she cried for several days and lost a significant amount of weight.","And then, she heard the news of Mo Yuance's death in battle, and her heart was buried in the yellow earth along with Mo Yuance.","Thinking of the pitiful state in which she saw Mo Yuance, she felt indescribable pain.","She had always kept her feelings for Mo Yuance in her heart, not even her two most trusted maids knew about them.","Now she wanted to honestly tell Mo Jiuye about Mo Yuance's whereabouts, but she didn't intend to reveal these feelings.","\"I arrived in Nanchuan not long ago, and a Gu Master came to the Crown Prince's Residence. One person with him looks remarkably similar to Mo Yuance.","At the time, the Crown Prince treated me fairly well, so I asked him to help inquire about the person's identity. The Gu Master, knowing that the Crown Prince and the Mo family were at odds, did not conceal Mo Yuance's identity. He removed half of his mask, and I was completely convinced that this person is indeed Mo Yuance.\"","Upon hearing that the Fourth Princess had encountered her seventh brother, Mo Jiuye's nerves tensed instantly, and he anxiously asked, \"Princess, do you know the whereabouts of my seventh brother?\"","The Fourth Princess had just spoken so much, clearly out of breath.","Lan Er knew that there was still a lot more the princess wanted to say, and she was worried about the princess's physical condition. She spoke up, \"Princess, let me explain instead!\"","Understanding her own situation, the Fourth Princess knew there were indeed many things she needed to explain. Worried about her stamina, she nodded slightly at Lan Er, determined to gather the last of her strength to address some crucial matters.","With the princess's permission, Lan Er turned to Mo Jiuye and said, \"The princess secretly approached Seventh Master Mo to talk, but he showed no reaction. It was later revealed that he had been afflicted by a puppetry gu, which robbed him of his own will. He became completely controlled by the person who cast the gu, just like a puppet.\"","The princess didn't want to see brave men loyal to Da Shun being controlled by the people of Southern Frontier. So, she pleaded with the Crown Prince and the gu master to keep Seventh Master Mo in the Crown Prince's residence. This way, she could take care of him privately.\"","Pausing for a moment, Lan Er further explained, \"The princess was desperate to save Seventh Master Mo but forgot the extent of Southern Frontier's hatred towards the Mo family. When the Crown Prince saw the princess's plea, he immediately slapped her and ordered her to be confined to her chambers.\"","It was only later when the princess discovered she was pregnant that she was granted freedom after informing the Crown Prince. Even so, she didn't give up on the idea of saving Seventh Master Mo, but this time she didn't dare to use the real reason to convince the Crown Prince.","The princess claimed that the Mo family supported Prince Qi of Da Shun, who was opposed to her own brother, Prince Heng. She hoped to have leverage over a member of the Mo family to threaten them into siding with Prince Heng in the future.","Seeing the princess present a logical and well-founded argument, the Crown Prince dispelled his previous doubts.","A few days later, the gu master visited again and brought up a condition.","The gu master was cautious and couldn't fully trust a Fourth Princess of Da Shun. If he were to hand over Seventh Master Mo to the princess, she had to agree to one condition.\"","\"What condition?\" Mo Jiuye asked eagerly.","The gu master said that the princess must willingly accept his gu. If she were to do anything that went against his wishes, the gu inside her would torment her.","In order to keep Seventh Master Mo close to her and take care of him, the princess readily agreed to the gu master's condition.","Later on, as promised, the gu master delivered Seventh Master Mo to the princess's side, becoming her personal guard.","Unexpectedly, this incident aroused suspicions from the Crown Prince. He couldn't believe that the princess, who harbored such hatred towards the Mo family, would willingly accept someone placing a gu on her.","Not only that, the princess lost the child in her womb because of the gu, and when these two incidents were combined, the Crown Prince believed that Seventh Master Mo held a higher position in the princess's heart than himself. As a result, he constantly sought to torment the princess, leading to her current fate of being exiled to the Palace of Exile.\"","Listening to Lan Er's explanation, Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran roughly understood the situation of Seventh Brother. At this moment, they couldn't spare the time to carefully consider the princess's true motives but were eager to know the whereabouts of Mo Yuance.","According to Lan Er's words, Seventh Master Mo has become the personal guard of Fourth Princess. He must be nearby.","However, when they just arrived here, apart from two maids, there was no sign of any guards at all.","\"Where is Seventh Master Mo now?\"","Lan Er truly didn't know about the whereabouts of Mo Jiuye. All she knew was that ever since the princess was brought here, Seventh Master Mo was taken away by the Crown Prince's men.","Lan Er couldn't answer this question, so she could only look at Fourth Princess lying on the bed.","Since they had come this far discussing the matter, Fourth Princess had nothing to hide.","\"He is in the dungeon of the Residence of the Crown Prince.\"","Upon hearing this, Mo Jiuye intended to go to the dungeon to find Seventh Master Mo. He had just pulled He Zhiran to turn around when he was stopped by Fourth Princess.","\"Wait, you can't go and save him.\"","Mo Jiuye didn't understand. \"Why?\""]},{"number":267,"title":"Chapter 267: I Want the Santa Hide from the Princess's dowry.","paragraphs":["The Fourth Princess tried her best to raise her voice.","\"He was stung by the puppet gu, and the mother gu is with the Crown Prince. Once the Crown Prince finds out that he has been rescued, the Crown Prince will urge the mother gu to kill the child gu in his body. Once the child gu dies, Mo Yuance will not be able to survive either.\"","There was no need for the Fourth Princess to say this. Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran were already well aware that if the rescue of Seventh Master Mo was discovered and the Crown Prince crushed the mother gu, then Seventh Master Mo's life would be lost.","What they needed to do first was to get the mother gu from the Crown Prince's hands. Only by doing so could they ensure absolute safety in rescuing Seventh Master Mo and removing the gu from him.","Mo Jiuye did not want to explain too much to the Fourth Princess about his wife's ability to remove gu.","\"Princess, don't worry. Since I'm going to rescue my seventh brother, I will certainly consider all angles.\"","The Fourth Princess would never doubt Mo Jiuye's abilities. It was possible for him to successfully rescue Mo Yuance, but he would not be able to remove the gu from Mo Yuance.","\"You can't rashly go to the dungeons. The Crown Prince's men are guarding there. Once they discover that Mo Yuance has been rescued, the Crown Prince will crush the mother gu and his life will be lost.\"","After the Fourth Princess said so much in one breath, she suddenly became breathless.","Lan Er was so frightened that she quickly pulled He Zhiran, \"Master, please take another look at our princess. Lan Er begs you to save our princess. She is a good person.\"","What Lan Er wanted to say was that the princess had never done anything to wrong the Mo family. If it hadn't been for the princess' efforts to keep Seventh Master Mo there, Seventh Master Mo would have been sent out as a suicide soldier long ago. No one even knew now whether he was still alive.","Although unspoken, He Zhiran and Mo Jiuye could understand the implication behind her words. There is always someone to blame. It was the Empress who had poisoned the Mo family's women, and it was Nan Heng who had plotted against the Mo family. The Fourth Princess was unrelated.","However, even with He Zhiran's excellent medical skills, there was no way to reverse the Fourth Princess' current condition.","When she first took the Fourth Princess' pulse, she wondered how such a young woman in her early twenties could have such a deteriorating body.","Now she knew. The Crown Prince's abuse was a possibility, but the gu worms in her body also played a major role.","Thinking of this, He Zhiran suddenly realized a problem.","Their main purpose in looking for the Fourth Princess was to get the placenta skin. Mo Jiuye had lost some sanity when he learned about his seventh brother's situation. She must not follow him in confusion.","So she nudged Mo Jiuye with her elbow and softly reminded: \"Placenta skin.\"","With her reminder, Mo Jiuye remembered the real purpose for them to find the Fourth Princess.","\"Princess, I came to the Crown Prince's mansion this time specifically to ask you for something.\"","The Fourth Princess slightly raised her increasingly heavy eyelids, \"What else can you ask from me in this state of mine?\"","Mo Jiuye hesitated for a moment before speaking, \"I want the placenta skin from the princess' dowry.\"","\"What do you want that useless thing for?\"","Hearing the Fourth Princess ask this, Mo Jiuye could confirm that she did not know about the Empress poisoning the Mo family's women.","\"Someone needs the placenta skin for medical treatment. I know that the princess has it in her dowry, so I came here to ask for the medicine.\"","Upon hearing this, the Fourth Princess did not think much more. Placenta skin was an extremely rare item to begin with. Moreover, Mo Jiuye had escorted her to Nanjiang for her marriage back then, so it was not strange at all that he knew she had this item.","It was just that at the moment, she had no way of helping Mo Jiuye at all.","\"The placenta skin is indeed still around, but unfortunately my dowry is no longer in my hands now.\"","Mo Jiuye frowned. Even in an ordinary family, they seldom touch a woman's dowry, let alone the Crown Prince's mansion of grand Nanjiang. How was it possible that they needed to supplement the Crown Prince's treasury with the Crown Prince Consort's dowry?","Seeing her mistress gasping for breath again, Lan Er explained, \"Ninth Master doesn't know that my princess' dowry is now in Concubine Xiao's hands.\"","Mo Jiuye frowned and asked, \"Where is Concubine Xiao?\"","When it came to Concubine Xiao, it was obvious that Lan Er deeply loathed her.","\"Concubine Xiao is greatly favored, so of course she lives closest to His Highness the Crown Prince.\"","They had judged the location of the Crown Prince's courtyard based on the singing and dancing sounds. Naturally, they had also carefully observed the surrounding environment.","Not far behind the Crown Prince's courtyard was an extremely luxurious place. That must be Concubine Xiao's residence.","Through this brief exchange, Mo Jiuye's earlier impulse was gone.","He asked solemnly, \"Please, Princess, what does the gu raiser who brought my seventh brother here look like?\"","The Fourth Princess recalled and said, \"He was wearing a hood so I didn't see his appearance. I only know he is a man with a somewhat thin figure.\"","Mo Jiuye knew that the Fourth Princess did not intend to conceal anything. Since she said she did not see his face, then she definitely did not.","He Zhiran looked at the pitiful woman on the bed. If she had a way, she would also try to save her. After all, she was just over twenty years old and had not done anything detrimental against the Mo family.","Unfortunately, she was already at her last gasp. He Zhiran hoped she could be reborn into a good family in her next life and become an ordinary yet happy woman.","At that moment, the Fourth Princess suddenly felt choked. She could neither swallow nor cough it out, yet He Zhiran could see that she still had something to say.","So she hurriedly needled a few of her acupoints with silver needles.","\"Princess, you have at most another fifteen minutes. Quickly say what you need to say.\"","The needles did have a significant effect. The Fourth Princess' breathing stabilized noticeably.","Lan Er and the other maid immediately knelt by the bedside, crying as they held her hands, \"Princess, rest assured and move on. Yu Er and I will accompany you so you won't be lonely on the way.\"","The Fourth Princess forcefully held both maids' hands in return.","\"No, I won't allow you to do that.\"","With effort, she looked towards Mo Jiuye, \"Mo Jiuye, may This Palace ask you to help with something?\"","With one glance, He Zhiran could see the Fourth Princess' intention. If not for the solemn occasion, she would definitely have said, the Ninth Master is attracting peach blossoms...","Mo Jiuye still did not understand the Fourth Princess' true intention. At this time, he really thought the Fourth Princess would entrust him with some important matter.","Such as letting the Emperor Shunwu know about her real cause of death.","Seeing that Mo Jiuye did not refute her words, the Fourth Princess slowly spoke, \"My two maids, one named Yu Er and one named Lan Er, have served me since they were young. Although we are mistress and servant, we are as close as sisters. I don't want them to die meaninglessly in this foreign land like me.\"","\"No... Princess, we want to follow you wherever you go.\"","The two maids were already prepared to die.","Mo Jiuye still could not see through the Fourth Princess' true intention.","\"If it is within my ability, I can bring these two ladies back to Da Shun.\"","Of course he could bring them back to Da Shun, but he could not bring them to the capital city, otherwise his recent activities might be exposed."]},{"number":268,"title":"Chapter 268: I, Mo Jiuye, love her only in this life.","paragraphs":["The Fourth Princess shook her head.","\"No, even if they return to Great Shun, they will have no home to go back to. I want them to follow you.\"","At this point, even the dull-witted Mo Jiuye understood.","\"There is an ancestral precept in my Mo family that men do not take concubines. What's more, I only love my wife in this lifetime. The Princess's request is too difficult, I'm afraid I cannot agree.\"","Not only did Mo Jiuye not agree to this condition, but the two maidservants were also strongly against it in their hearts.","\"Princess, you absolutely can't do this. No matter life or death, we will stay by your side.\"","He Zhiran knew that Mo Jiuye was not the kind of man to go back on his word, but when it came to things like this, she couldn't help feeling sour in her heart.","She looked coldly at the few people there, unable to conceal the displeasure in her eyes at all.","Mo Jiuye's palms were already sweating. He was angry that the princess was randomly giving him her women, and even more worried that his wife would vent her anger on him because of this.","In order to get the Fourth Princess to give up this idea, he deliberately pulled He Zhiran in front of the bed.","\"This is my wife, the daughter of the prestigious He Family, the current Minister of Works. I, Mo Jiuye, only love her in this lifetime.\"","At this moment, the Fourth Princess' spirit had begun to waver indistinctly, but her brain was still working.","She also knew that the Mo family men did not take concubines. If she wasn't at death's door, she wouldn't have thought of such a way to settle her two loyal maidservants.","The Fourth Princess struggled to keep herself conscious, then looked towards He Zhiran.","\"I beg you......take them with you and help them find a good family in the future. Then I......I can......rest in peace......\"","As her voice fell, she slowly closed her eyes.","Lan Er and Yu Er broke down in loud crying.","\"Princess......Princess, wait for me. I will come to accompany you......\"","As Lan Er's voice faded, she charged towards a pillar in the room.","Seeing this, Yu Er did the same, following Lan Er's footsteps running towards the pillar.","He Zhiran and Mo Jiuye acted swiftly, coming up behind each of them and hitting them unconscious with a hand chop to stop them.","Then He Zhiran took out silver needles and inserted them into the fainting points on both of them before throwing them into her space.","She didn't want to play saint, but just letting her watch two living people die like this was something she, a modern soul, couldn't remain indifferent to.","Of course, if they were extremely evil people, even if they didn't commit suicide, she would still personally send them off.","Having obtained so much information from the Fourth Princess, the two dared not linger here any longer. There were still many things waiting for them to do.","Compared to the Seventh Elder Brother, everything else was less important. After the two came out of the Inner Palace, they saw guards patrolling and He Zhiran pulled Mo Jiuye to a stop first.","She then shouted at those guards, \"The Imperial Concubine has passed away...the Imperial Concubine has passed away...\"","While the guards were looking around trying to locate the source of the sound, He Zhiran pulled Mo Jiuye with her to flash into her space.","She intended to wait until these guards left before coming out again so as not to expose themselves before everything was done.","The two maidservants lay in the grassland of the farm in the space. Rice Ball was circling around them, looking them up and down from time to time and even reaching out to touch them with his chubby hands.","He Zhiran walked over first and picked up the little one to kiss him.","Previously, whenever his wife entered the space, she would also go to hug Rice Ball first. However, today Mo Jiuye felt like something was not quite right.","But he couldn't say exactly what was not right.","He Zhiran just didn't want to pay attention to him because of what had happened earlier. She still had a little bit of jealousy.","But she also knew clearly that this was not the time to be petty with her husband. She just didn't want to talk to him.","Feeling that enough time had probably passed, the news of the Imperial Concubine's death should have reached the Crown Prince by now.","If the Crown Prince was still out seeking pleasure at this time, it would really be inexcusable.","Even if just for appearance's sake, he should personally arrange the Imperial Concubine's funeral.","And the Crown Prince's residence would be more chaotic at this time. They could take the opportunity to do what they needed to do.","He Zhiran was worried that the two maidservants might wake up prematurely, so after injecting each of them with a tranquilizer, she took Mo Jiuye, who had a bewildered look on his face, out of the space.","Sure enough, things happened as expected. The guards had already left their original positions. Mo Jiuye put his arm around He Zhiran's waist and leapt onto the high wall.","After quickly surveying the surroundings and getting their bearings, Mo Jiuye brought her running swiftly to the outside of the Crown Prince's residence, hiding in the shadows to observe.","The drumming and music sounds were gone. They only saw a youth dressed in gorgeous brocade robes being led out in a huff by a group of servants and guards clustered around him.","He Zhiran and Mo Jiuye were too far away to hear what they were saying. It was nothing more than the Crown Prince's mood being spoiled by the Fourth Princess's death and him being a little unhappy.","The group followed the Crown Prince, heading in the direction of the Fourth Princess's residence as expected.","Taking advantage of this opportunity, Mo Jiuye brought He Zhiran to sneak into the Crown Prince's residence.","This place could be perfectly described as magnificent and opulent. In Mo Jiuye's opinion, its level of luxury was comparable to the Great Shun imperial palace, showing that this Crown Prince knew how to enjoy himself.","The two avoided the sight of some of the servants, searching around. Of course He Zhiran would not miss the chance to fill her own little treasury, not letting a single thing slip by that she could take away.","After searching for a while, they did not find the bottle containing Gu worms here. The mother Gu worm was probably being carried on the Crown Prince's person.","After some discussion, they guessed that the Crown Prince would not return too quickly to deal with the Imperial Concubine's matters. As long as they could smoothly find the Seventh Elder Brother and remove the larval Gu worms from his body, the Seventh Elder Brother would not be in danger.","In order to accurately locate the dungeons, Mo Jiuye grabbed a servant and asked him before knocking him out and swiftly bringing He Zhiran in that direction.","The dungeons were located in the northwest corner of the Crown Prince's residence. The entrance was guarded by four guards.","The two of them were still wearing servant uniforms, so they could just stroll casually over.","The guards thought they were coming over to say something. Caught off guard, they were all stupefied by the anesthetic medicine scattered by He Zhiran.","Mo Jiuye swiftly dragged them to one side before they carefully walked into the dungeons.","The dungeons were dim, damp, and accompanied by a pungent musty smell.","Mo Jiuye gripped He Zhiran's hand tightly as the two had just walked to a brighter area when they heard the sounds of gambling by throwing dice and drinking coming from inside.","Judging from the sounds, there were four people inside.","He Zhiran took out another pack of anesthetic powder, holding it in her hand. When they walked closer, she swiftly scattered it at the few people.","The four guards who were grinning widely immediately lost consciousness.","Mo Jiuye swiftly searched them and finally found a set of keys. Only after confirming there were no other guards in the dungeons did he pull He Zhiran along to walk around the gambling table and continue deeper inside.","These dungeons were not big, only containing six rooms for imprisoning people, but they were all empty.","Only the innermost one, facing the entrance, had a disheveled person chained by iron chains to a rack.","After Mo Jiuye confirmed there was no danger, he pulled He Zhiran to quickly stride towards that person."]},{"number":269,"title":"Chapter 269: You Are Really Here","paragraphs":["That person lowered his head, as they walked closer, still no reaction, like a dead person. Mo Jiuye's heart suddenly raced faster, he went ahead and gently raised that person's head.","\"Seventh brother, you're really here.\"","Mo Yuance's eyes were tightly shut, already in an unconscious state, visible blood stains could be seen from the corners of his mouth, nose and eyes.","He Zhiran reached out to check his breath.","\"He's still alive.\"","Seeing Mo Yuance's miserable state, Mo Jiuye's eyes turned red again, at this moment he wished he could immediately kill those who persecuted the Mo family men.","He Zhiran knew he felt upset, went ahead and patted his shoulder to remind: \"Don't feel sad, first take Seventh Brother away from here.\"","Mo Jiuye struggled to calm his thoughts: \"Okay.\"","After he finished speaking, he took out the key and opened the lock chaining Mo Yuance, He Zhiran waved her hand, and sent the person into the space, also lying in the operating room.","The two swiftly left the dungeon, found a hidden place to enter the space.","Without caring about Mo Yuance's other injuries first, the first thing He Zhiran had to do was to help him remove Gu.","Mo Jiuye was now very familiar with the Gu removal process, without He Zhiran's instructions, he did the assistant's job.","He Zhiran skillfully helped Mo Yuance remove the Gu worms and collected them in a container.","After the Gu worm was successfully removed, He Zhiran started checking his body.","After some examination, his condition was somewhat better than Fourth Brother, at least he didn't reach the point of having his hands and feet cut off, but his body was as weak as Fourth Brother’s.","Also that whole body of skin injuries, using the words skin and flesh torn was an understatement, and new wounds covered old wounds, it was visible how much inhuman torture he suffered here.","Although Fourth Princess was kind-hearted, wanting to keep Mo Yuance here to avoid him becoming a dead warrior endangering his life.","With her status in the Residence of the Crown Prince, she was simply unable to keep Seventh Brother safe, but ended up making things worse instead.","Mo Jiuye assisted He Zhiran, together they treated Seventh Brother's wounds, He Zhiran also gave him some IV fluids.","After all they were still inside the Residence of the Crown Prince, they couldn't stay in the space for too long. After He Zhiran injected Mo Yuance with another tranquilizer, the two left the space.","By now, the Residence of the Crown Prince was already in chaos.","The Crown Prince who originally went to deal with matters regarding the Crown Princess Consort, after hearing that his own bedroom treasures were lost, without discovering any traces of the thieves, was furious.","Not only did he mobilize all the guards in the residence, he also ordered people to mobilize the Imperial Guards from the palace to jointly search.","At present, not only was the Residence of the Crown Prince under high alert, even the entire capital had Imperial Guards everywhere.","Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran's outfits walking in the Residence of the Crown Prince didn’t raise others’ suspicion, the two still held their night watch tools roaming everywhere, no one came to make trouble for them.","What they were more anxious about now was to find Concubine Xiao as soon as possible and leave this place early.","The two soon found Xiao Concubine's residence. With such a big incident happening in the Residence of the Crown Prince, Concubine Xiao naturally hadn't gone to bed yet.","At this moment, she was sitting in the main hall with several maids waiting for news from outside.","In the flicker of time, He Zhiran and Mo Jiuye knocked out all the people including Concubine Xiao, then quickly started searching.","This Concubine Xiao was indeed favored, her bedroom was furnished with all kinds of precious antiques, paintings and jewelry. There was also a medium-sized treasury in her yard.","Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran broke into the door, scanned for a moment, then Mo Jiuye said, \"Most of these are Fourth Princess’s dowries.\"","He had seen the list of Fourth Princess’s dowries that year, so he was not unfamiliar with the items before him.","With the current chaos in the Residence of the Crown Prince, they still didn’t know the situation outside, and didn’t dare to delay here for too long.","Especially for Dan Pi, according to Mo Jiuye, it was originally kept in a small wooden box at that time. Wanting to ascertain whether that small wooden box was among these many items, they didn’t have enough time.","They could only wait until it was safe to check it again in the space. Anyway, as Fourth Princess said, Dan Pi was with Concubine Xiao, as long as they took everything from her, it surely wouldn’t disappoint them.","After ransacking everything in Concubine Xiao’s yard, taking advantage of the chaos, they found the treasury of the Residence of the Crown Prince again and collected all the items inside the space.","Anyway Seventh Brother's Gu was removed. Even if the Crown Prince held the mother Gu worm in his hands, it would no longer endanger Seventh Brother’s life. They would find another chance to settle accounts with him later.","At present, they had to hurry back to the yard they rented, as there were many officials who came into the city to search places under the orders of the furious Crown Prince. Once Fourth Brother encountered danger, it would not be worth it.","The two jumped over the wall to leave the Residence of the Crown Prince. As expected, the streets were full of armed officers everywhere.","To avoid trouble, Mo Jiuye led He Zhiran over the roofs and walls all the way back to the yard they rented, avoiding those officers’ sight.","Although Mo Xiuyan didn’t have much strength and spirit yet, after Ninth Brother and Sister-in-Law had been out for so long, especially in Nanjiang territory, it would be false to say there was no risk.","He tried his best to pull himself together and waited for them to come back, half-leaning in bed.","Mo Jiuye brought He Zhiran back without entering through the front door, but jumping over the wall, because there were already many officers outside, going from door to door searching houses.","After entering Fourth Brother’s room, Mo Jiuye sent Shun Zi away before speaking, “Fourth Brother, there are many officers outside searching.”","At this moment, Mo Xiuyan also heard some movement.","\"Ninth Brother, take Sister-in-Law to hide away, don't bother about me.\" He had already become disabled, he didn’t want to drag down Ninth Brother and his wife.","It was impossible to abandon Fourth Brother alone here. He Zhiran hurriedly took out her acupuncture kit, quickly pricked his fainting point when Fourth Brother was not paying attention, and casually sent him into the space.","As for Shun Zi outside, they weren’t worried that he would be in danger. Shun Zi could read lips and communicate with gestures. If the searching people came in and obtained clues from him, that would be troublesome.","With this thought, Mo Jiuye went out with a hand chop and knocked out Shun Zi, bringing him into the space together with Fourth Brother to hide temporarily.","After entering the space, He Zhiran took advantage of Fourth Brother’s unconsciousness and transfused another bag of plasma into him.","Not long after they entered the space, the searching officers outside broke in, of course the result of the search was nothing.","The two were in no hurry to go out either, after simply eating something to fill their stomachs in the space, He Zhiran went to the farm to check on the status of the two maidservants.","The two maids were still unconscious at the moment, but He Zhiran knew clearly that including Fourth Brother, they would wake up after about another hour.","As for Seventh Brother, he remained unconscious, and He Zhiran couldn’t determine when he would wake up.","In order not to expose her space to more people, He Zhiran flashed out alone to check things out.","It was obvious that the door of their yard had been forcibly broken open, the house door was wide open too, and the bedding on the bed was also messed up, clearly this place had already been searched by those officers.","Since it was searched, it meant it would be safe for the time being.","So she turned back to space again and brought everyone out."]},{"number":270,"title":"Chapter 270: Don't you want to avenge her","paragraphs":["Shun Zi was the first to awake. He was suddenly knocked out and found that there were several more people in the room now. He was a little confused.","But seeing his master was also there, he felt at ease.","Shun Zi got up, massaged his sore neck, gestured that he would go outside to take a look, then left.","Mo Xiuyan and Mo Yuance needed to recuperate. The yard they rented now only had two rooms. Fortunately the beds were big enough that two people lying on them did not feel crowded.","As for Lan Er and Yu Er, after they woke up, Madam Ninth would ask them some questions. If they really had nowhere to go, she would bring them together to the northwest.","The family had already found so many sons alive. This news could not be kept secret even if they wanted to. Besides that, there was nothing else to worry about being leaked out, so there was no need to be concerned that these two would divulge secrets.","Lan Er and Yu Er were both healthy. They woke up faster than the Mo brothers.","Seeing the two gradually wake up, He Zhiran took the initiative to walk up to them.","Lan Er reacted the fastest. Realizing the environment was not right, she immediately stood up, completely ignoring He Zhiran. She started scanning the entire room.","\"The princess, where is the princess?\"","Yu Er also got up and asked suspiciously, \"Where is this place?\"","He Zhiran knew they were not feeling well at the moment, so she softened her tone a lot when speaking.","\"You've left the residence of the Crown Prince.\"","Upon hearing this, Lan Er turned around and ran outside.","\"I'm going back. The princess is still lying there alone.\"","He Zhiran blocked the door: \"The Fourth Princess is gone. Do you think the Crown Prince will spare you if you go back?\"","Lan Er stubbornly said, \"We don't need anyone to spare us. We just want to be with the princess.\"","At this point, He Zhiran could no longer describe whether these two were loyal or ignorant.","She helplessly advised, \"It's obvious that the Fourth Princess was killed by the Prince of Southern Borderlands. Don't you want to avenge her?\"","\"Take revenge?\" Lan Er let out a self-deprecating laugh. \"How can we two weak women avenge the princess?\"","\"You can send a message to Emperor Shunwu that his daughter has died. Would he really remain indifferent?\" He Zhiran was trying her best to dissuade them from thoughts of suicide.","Even if she couldn't make them change their minds, she wouldn't force it. After all, she had done what she could.","Unexpectedly, her words not only failed to make Lan Er change her mind, but also made the disappointed expression on her face grow heavier.","\"After the princess was taken to that place by the Prince of Southern Borderlands, we tried many times to send letters to the imperial capital, but it was like throwing a rock into the sea.\"","He Zhiran raised her eyebrows in surprise: \"Could it be that your letters did not make it out?\"","Lan Er shook her head: \"More than a dozen letters. I don't believe not a single one made it to His Majesty.\"","He Zhiran was even more puzzled: \"Could it be that Emperor Shunwu does not care about his own daughter's life and death?\"","By now, Lan Er no longer had any need to conceal things.","\"We grew up with the princess in the palace since childhood, and have long seen through the cold-bloodedness and ruthlessness of the imperial family.","A daughter married off to consolidate the country, who would care about her life and death?\"","\"What about the Empress then?\" He Zhiran was increasingly confused.","Lan Er sneered coldly: \"The Empress's mind is all on Prince Heng. And we heard recently that Prince Heng has gone missing. Where would she have any thought to care about the princess's suffering?\"","He Zhiran...","Alright!","It was because she had lived in the harmonious Mo family circle for too long that she had forgotten the lack of kinship in the imperial family.","\"Even if Emperor Shunwu is unwilling to seek justice for the Fourth Princess, would the next emperor also turn a blind eye?\"","The next emperor?","Lan Er had not thought that far.","Now that He Zhiran had brought it up, she had to think deeply about it.","The only two princes with the most hope of inheriting the throne in Da Shun were Prince Heng and Prince Qi.","Now Prince Heng's whereabouts were unknown. The only one left was Prince Qi.","Since childhood, Prince Heng had been instilled by the Empress that there was only the throne in his eyes. He had no kinship with his sister born of the same mother. In fact, he had always resented the Fourth Princess for being a girl and unable to help him compete for the throne.","Prince Qi was different. He was gentle and courteous since childhood and extremely respectful to his sister the Fourth Princess.","He would even help the Fourth Princess when she suffered grievances.","If Prince Qi ascended the throne, would he help the princess seek justice?","Thinking of this, Lan Er seemed to see a glimmer of hope.","\"But I don't know when Prince Qi will succeed to the throne.\"","Hearing her say this, He Zhiran knew her persuasion was working.","\"There is a saying, it's never too late to take revenge even after ten years. Moreover, Da Shun and the Southern Borderlands are often at war. Who knows, maybe someday, the Southern Borderlands will be completely conquered by Da Shun. By then, when you make offerings to the princess, you can tell her this news, won't that comfort her spirit in heaven?\"","The more Lan Er listened, the more reasonable she felt it was. If she died, the princess's suffering in the residence of the Prince of Southern Borderlands would never see the light of day. She had to live well and look for opportunities to burn incense and tell the princess that her great vengeance had been reported.","\"Madam Ninth, thank you for reminding me. Lan Er is willing to serve by your side. I only want to wait for the day the Prince of Southern Borderlands falls, and then tell the princess this news. Then Lan Er will have no regrets in this life.\"","As Lan Er spoke, she had already knelt down before He Zhiran.","Yu Er was obviously someone without much independent thought. She basically felt whatever Lan Er said made sense.","Therefore, after Lan Er knelt down, she also knelt down together.","He Zhiran did not hurry to help them up. She had to make clear the ugly truth before bringing them to the northwest.","\"You must have heard about the Mo Family being raided and exiled. At that time, only one Mo son was left alive, my husband Mo Jiuye.\"","As she spoke, she glanced at the two still unconscious on the bed.","\"Today we sneaked into the residence of the Crown Prince and successfully rescued Seventh Brother. This matter probably can't be kept secret for long. But I hope this news does not come from your mouths.\"","Lan Er immediately promised: \"Madam Ninth, rest assured, Lan Er swears she will never speak of this.\"","To protect this person, even the princess had lost her life. Even for the sake of the princess, she had to help conceal this matter for the Mo Family.","Seeing her sincere attitude, He Zhiran went on: \"We now live in the countryside of the northwest. If you can't get used to such hard days, I won't force you to go there.","Moreover, we don't keep idlers in our family. Not to mention you, even my mother-in-law and sisters-in-law work every day.\"","He Zhiran was worried that no matter how the Fourth Princess was not favored, she was still a princess of the country. The palace maids who could accompany her to the Southern Borderlands must be the highest class of palace maids.","In her mind, first-class palace maids in the palace basically did not need to work, only needed to help their masters with some trivial daily matters.","She kindly wanted to bring them along, but what if she brought back two people who could not lift a shoulder or lift a hand? Wouldn't that be a burden?"]},{"number":271,"title":"Chapter 271: How can a body like this get revenge","paragraphs":["Lan Er had already changed her mind about committing suicide, especially since she would be staying with the Mo Family in the future and naturally had to behave herself well.","\"No, no, no, the two of us can do all kinds of rough work. When we go to the Mo Family, the Ninth Lady can order us around like lowly maids if she wants.\"","Lan Er didn't have any great skills. No matter who she followed, she could be loyal. \"Please don't look down on me, Ninth Lady.\"","Yu Er also promised: \"Ninth Lady, I can also work. I guarantee I won't make things difficult for you.\"","After finishing reprimanding them, He Zhiran spoke again: \"As long as you don't have ulterior motives, I won't mistreat you either.\"","With the two maids' matters temporarily settled, He Zhiran went to the bedside to check on the Fourth and Seventh Brothers.","Mo Jiuye guessed his wife might use some special methods to wake the two brothers, so he waved his hands at Lan Er and Yu Er to let them leave first.","Since the Seventh Brother had been unconscious when he was rescued, He Zhiran carefully inserted silver needles at several acupoints on his body.","After about five minutes, the Seventh Brother first showed signs of reaction, with his eyelids twitching slightly, followed by a slight pained expression on his face.","Mo Jiuye anxiously went forward and shouted: \"Seventh brother, Seventh brother, wake up!\"","Mo Yuance felt dizzy. He thought he was dead, yet strangely heard the Ninth Brother's voice.","He didn't open his eyes voluntarily, but mumbled: \"Ninth brother? Ninth brother, tell Mother that her unfilial son couldn't fulfill his filial duty by her side as she sends off her black-haired son.","\"Seventh brother, it's me Jiuye. Mother is very well. If she knew you were still alive, she would definitely be very happy,\" Mo Jiuye said.","\"You said I'm still alive?\" Mo Yuance clearly didn't believe it was true.","\"Seventh brother, you really are still alive,\" Mo Jiuye affirmed.","Hearing this definite statement, Mo Yuance struggled to open his eyes.","He didn't recognize the person in front of him at all. He subconsciously thought this must be the Southern Borderlands people playing tricks, wanting to get something out of him by finding someone with the same voice as his Ninth Brother to trick him.","\"Heh... You Southern Borderlands people really stoop to any means,\" Mo Yuance sneered.","Only then did Mo Jiuye realize his face was disguised by his wife's makeup and he was wearing Southern Borderlands clothing, no wonder the Seventh Brother didn't recognize him.","He hurriedly tore off his fake beard. He Zhiran also timely handed over a wet wipe. Mo Jiuye swiftly wiped off the makeup on his face, then moved closer to Mo Yuance.","\"Seventh brother, look closely at me. I'm Jiuye.\"","To let the Seventh Brother see clearly, He Zhiran even held up the room's only oil lamp next to Mo Jiuye's face, trying to make it clearer for him to see.","Now Mo Yuance could thoroughly see Mo Jiuye's appearance.","\"Ninth brother, it really is you?\"","Seeing his brother recognize him, Mo Jiuye's eyes instantly moistened.","He pulled He Zhiran to his side and introduced: \"Seventh brother, this is my wife, the daughter of Chancellor He's family, He Zhiran.\"","Hearing this, Mo Yuance felt confused.","On the eve of the war against the Southern Borderlands, he and Sixth Brother had also advised Mo Jiuye. They told him he was quite old already, and his marriage had been set for many years. When the war ended and they returned to the capital, he should hurry up and get married to bring some joy to the family.","This had clearly just happened recently. How did the Ninth Brother get married so quickly?","Could it be that the Ninth Sister chased him to the border to marry the Ninth Brother?","The more Mo Yuance thought about it, the more muddled he felt. He simply asked outright: \"Ninth brother, how did you get married so fast?\"","Hearing his question, Mo Jiuye naturally understood the Seventh Brother must have lost his own consciousness due to the Gu worms’ control and didn’t remember what had happened recently.","\"Seventh brother, it’s already been over three years since your accident on the battlefield.\"","\"Over three years?\" Mo Yuance didn't believe it at all.","Mo Jiuye roughly told him about what had happened these past few years, and informed him that his missing memories were caused by the puppet Gu worm.","In order to get the Seventh Brother to accept this fact, Mo Jiuye also specially let him take a look at the Fourth Brother lying next to him.","\"Seventh brother, if you don't believe me, take a look. Fourth brother was rescued a day before you.\"","In Mo Yuance’s knowledge, the Fourth Brother had already died on the battlefield before he himself was captured. Now seeing the person lying beside him, those eyebrows, if not Fourth Brother, then who?","Now Mo Yuance thoroughly believed Mo Jiuye’s words.","\"I didn't expect I was actually muddled for over three years.\" Mo Yuance laughed at himself.","In these three years, he also failed his duty to serve his aged mother. Abandoning his young wife to live as a widow, and now requiring his Ninth Brother and Sister-in-Law to risk danger to come rescue him in the Southern Borderlands.","He felt he was a burden dragging down his family.","Especially just now when he wanted to sit up but couldn't move at all.","For a time, Mo Yuance fell into bewilderment.","At the same time, he also wondered aloud:","\"I remember I inhaled poison powder with Sixth Brother thrown by the enemy, then was taken to a dark place. Why has my body become so weak?\"","It seemed the Seventh Brother didn't remember what had happened at all.","Mo Jiuye could only tell him what he knew.","\"Seventh brother, you were caught and implanted with a puppet Gu worm. At first we all thought you were dead. We found you in the Southern Borderlands Prince's manor. At that time you were locked in the dungeon...\"","Mo Jiuye recounted it very clearly, even telling about the Fourth Princess.","Mo Yuance didn't expect that his current utterly feeble state was caused by the Southern Borderlands Prince's jealousy.","He tried his utmost to clench his fist and say: \"I, Mo Yuance, will take revenge on this grudge in my lifetime.\"","Thinking about his own condition, Mo Yuance gritted his teeth in hatred.","Mo Jiuye also hated the Southern Borderlands Prince, it’s just that when they were at the Prince's manor earlier, they were anxious to save the Seventh Brother, plus the chaotic situation on site, thus letting that Prince slip away temporarily.","But he didn’t dare show too extreme an attitude in front of the Seventh Brother.","The Seventh Brother was fairly hot-tempered. Mo Jiuye worried he would damage his already tattered body from anger, so he urgently persuaded: \"Seventh brother, we will take revenge sooner or later, but you need to recover first.\"","Hearing his Ninth Brother's words, Mo Yuance only just realized that currently he couldn't even get up, so what ability did he have to seek revenge?","He strived to calm himself down and become more sensible.","This sensibility, instead, roused in Mo Yuance a feeling of utter hopeless despair.","He first lifted his bony, scarred hands as thin as firewood to look, then said sarcastically: \"I was really overestimating myself. With this kind of body, what revenge is there to speak of?\"","Seeing the Seventh Brother's despondent mood, Mo Jiuye hurriedly comforted: \"Seventh brother, Rangrang is very skilled in medicine. She will surely cure you.\"","To make Mo Yuance believe his words, Mo Jiuye briefly described the situation the Eighth Brother was in back then, and how Rangrang had cured him and others."]},{"number":272,"title":"Chapter 272: Men and Women","paragraphs":["Mo Yuance had just been in his own decadent thoughts, and only then did he have time to look at He Zhiran.","No matter how low his mood was at the moment, the etiquette ingrained in him since childhood did not neglect, and he struggled to nod at He Zhiran.","\"Sister Nine, you've had a hard time.\"","He Zhiran returned a blessing.","\"Brother Seven, don't worry, I can heal both you and Brother Four.\"","Mo Yuance didn't know what supernatural powers Sister Nine had, but Brother Nine had just said that she had removed the puppet Gu parasites from him and several other brothers, so her skills were clearly extraordinary.","There was hope. Who would want to live in disappointment?","\"Then I'll have to trouble Sister Nine in the future.\" Mo Yuance was still so polite.","He Zhiran also hurriedly replied, \"Brother Seven is too polite. We are all family. What's the trouble?\"","As they spoke, Mo Xiuyan, who was lying in bed, also slowly woke up.","His first feeling was that there was one more person beside him.","Turning his head to look, it turned out to be a person as injured as himself.","Because they were both lying down, Mo Xiuyan's line of sight to Mo Yuance was not very good, so he did not recognize his own brother at first sight.","Seeing that the fourth brother had woken up, Mo Jiuye quickly said, \"Fourth Brother, we just went out and rescued Seventh Brother.\"","Hearing this, Mo Xiuyan struggled to prop himself up with his elbows to check the person next to him.","Mo Yuance excitedly shouted, \"Fourth brother, it's me!\"","The difficult brothers gazed at each other for a long time, unable to hold back their red-rimmed eyes.","Especially Mo Yuance. In his impression, the fourth brother had died in battle half a year earlier than himself, so to see him still alive now was simply a blessing from heaven.","If Mo Jiuye knew his thoughts, he would definitely say, how was it a blessing from heaven? All this was Sister He Zhiran's contribution. Without her, I'm afraid I would have turned into a handful of yellow earth by now, let alone have a chance to find the lost brother and save them from the Gu parasites and treat them.","Thinking of this, Mo Jiuye couldn't help but talk about his precious wife's contribution.","\"Fourth Brother and Seventh Brother, we brothers can still be alive and together, it's all thanks to Sister He Zhiran. Without her, I would have been severely punished by Emperor Shunwu with one hundred strokes, and even if there were no assassins chasing me, I'm afraid I wouldn't have been able to arrive alive in the northwest.\"","There was also a possibility that he would have been caught by that Mr. Si Meng to plant Gu parasites.","This point, both Mo Xiuyan and Mo Yuance had heard Mo Jiuye mention it before, just not in such detail.","They knew Ninth Brother's character and that he would never tell lies. Since he said it was Sister Ninth Sister-In-Law's contribution, then that must be the case.","If their bodies were movable, even if they had to kneel in front of Sister Ninth Sister-In-Law to thank her would not be too much.","Since they could not get up, it was still very necessary to solemnly say a word of thanks.","\"Sister Ninth, on behalf of the Mo family, Fourth Brother thanks you for your great kindness.\"","\"Sister Ninth, from now on in the Mo family, apart from our mother, you are the greatest. Seventh Brother will listen to whatever you say.\"","Being thanked so deeply by two heroic elder brothers, He Zhiran was clearly somewhat embarrassed.","She hurriedly changed the subject.","\"Fourth Brother and Seventh Brother, I am the daughter-in-law of the Mo family. These are things I should do. You can chat with your husband first. I'll go out and prepare some food for you.\"","Having said that, she hurried out.","Lan Er and Yu Er were very sensible. Seeing that the few people in the room had things to talk about, they stood far away in the yard.","At that distance, plus the volume of speech in the room was not large, even Mo Jiuye, who knew martial arts, probably couldn't hear it.","For this reason, He Zhiran's impression of the two was even better.","After all, it was the middle of the night, and the two had just lost the master they had served for many years. He Zhiran could understand their mood at the moment, so she didn't intend to arrange for them to do anything right away, just letting them go to rest in her and Mo Jiuye's room for the time being.","Anyway, they were going to go into the space at night, so leaving the room empty didn't matter.","Shun Zi also came out from the kitchen at this time. Seeing He Zhiran, he gestured with his hands,","meaning to tell her that the fire had already been lit in the kitchen and that he could help prepare some food for everyone.","He Zhiran nodded, \"Okay, I'll cook.\"","If it was the usual meals, she wouldn't mind Shun Zi's lack of cooking skills either. But that wouldn't work this time, given the physical condition of the two elder brothers. They had to eat some nutritious food, but also not too much supplementation.","Therefore, He Zhiran decided to personally cook some food to nourish the bodies of the two elder brothers.","In addition, considering that they were both currently lacking in blood, she also fried a plate of braised liver tips with carrots, which could also replenish some vitamins.","The staple food was sea cucumber porridge with some vegetables added. During their imprisonment, the two elder brothers not only suffered torture but also injured their stomachs. In this case, eating gruel would be easier to digest.","An hour later, when the chicken soup was cooked, He Zhiran personally brought it to their room.","Mo Jiuye patiently fed the two elder brothers spoonful by spoonful.","The fourth brother was fine for now. Since being rescued, this was not the first time he had eaten such good food.","The seventh brother, on the other hand, felt a little uncomfortable. On the one hand, his feeling of hunger was very strong, on the other hand, he felt as if he had never eaten such delicious food before, and the sister-in-law ninth was still standing there watching him, so if he ate too fast, it would obviously be inappropriate.","But he was really hungry. Especially since the food prepared by Sister Ninth was so delicious, he wanted to control the speed but found it difficult. In the end, Mo Yuance ate the meal with a red face.","He Zhiran took the bowls and chopsticks to the kitchen. She had just walked out the door when Shun Zi took them from her.","He gestured that he would clean up himself.","Although Lan Er and Yu Er had entered the room, they didn't dare fall asleep at this time. Hearing the movement outside, they both walked out.","Seeing there was dishwashing to do, they hurried to the kitchen.","This time He Zhiran did not stop them, on the contrary, she hoped that the two would integrate into their lives sooner.","Returning to the room of the two elder brothers, He Zhiran took their pulses again to check on them.","\"The fourth brother's condition has improved a bit. He should be able to have surgery in half a month.\"","This was simply the best news ever.","Mo Jiuye believed that after the operation, the fourth brother would slowly get back on his feet.","He Zhiran also gave the seventh brother a tranquilizer pill, \"The seventh brother is just too weak physically, he can slowly recover.\"","Even if others didn't believe this, the fourth brother definitely did.","Being conditioned by Sister He Zhiran these past two days, he clearly felt much better mentally, and he could still sit up supporting himself."]},{"number":273,"title":"Chapter 273: Mother and two sister-in-law are waiting for you to come back.","paragraphs":["\"Seventh Brother, believe Ninth Sister-in-Law, her medical skills are really good.\"","In order to prove what he said was not empty talk, Fourth Elder Brother deliberately leaned on his elbow and sat up.","\"Look at me, when Ninth Brother and the others first saved me, my body was like a pile of mud, but now I can sit up.\"","Seventh Elder Brother looked at Fourth Elder Brother leaning against the head of the bed: \"Well, I should get better soon too.\"","Seeing the two elder brothers rekindle their confidence, Mo Jiuye encouraged: \"You will definitely get better, when Mother and two elder sister-in-laws see you come back alive, they will definitely be very happy.\"","Fourth Elder Brother and Seventh Elder Brother were originally weak, and had been injected with sedatives by He Zhiran, so they felt groggy after waking up.","If it wasn't for the reunion with their brothers, they probably wouldn't have been able to hold on.","At this moment, after the brothers talked for so long, both of their eyes were gradually unable to stay open.","Seeing this, Mo Jiuye stood up: \"Fourth Brother, Seventh Brother, you two rest for a while, I’ll let Shunzi come in and watch over you.”","The two elder brothers were also worried about Ninth Brother and his wife’s hard work, so they responded and let them go back to rest as well.","Their room was now occupied by Lan Er and Yu Er. The two went directly to a secluded place in the back yard, then flashed into the space.","Although Mo Jiuye was worried about the two elder brothers just now, he didn't forget that his wife was unhappy.","As soon as he entered the space, he pulled her into his arms.","\"Ranran, are you angry?\"","He Zhiran didn’t have the temperament of a young lady. At this moment, if Mo Jiuye hadn't asked, she would have forgotten the little incident at the Prince's Mansion.","Moreover, she believed in Mo Jiuye's feelings for her. He would never have any inappropriate thoughts about other women.","Even if he did, He Zhiran was not afraid. There were so many couples who divorced because of disharmony or the other party's infidelity. When it came to her, she would never compromise.","Of course, this was just her bottom line for marriage. Now that she and Mo Jiuye were in harmony, she didn’t need to think too much at all.","However, since he took the initiative to mention it, He Zhiran still couldn't help but poke at him a little.","\"There is no room for sand in my eyes. If one day you no longer have me in your heart, you can say it directly. \"","I can leave very calmly...","Seeing her say this, Mo Jiuye became even more nervous.","\"Ranran, I, Mo Jiuye, swear that I will only love you in this life. If I ever change my heart, may the heavens strike me with lightning...\"","\"Alright, I know, don't say anymore.\" He Zhiran reached out to cover his mouth, not letting him finish.","Seeing this, Mo Jiuye hugged her even tighter.","\"My good Ranran, you are so understanding.\"","He Zhiran rolled her eyes. She didn't know when this man had become so sweet-talking.","Just as the two were hugging each other and about to become intimate, Rice Ball inappropriately ran over.","The little guy barked towards the direction of the ranch several times, signaling them to look over there.","These past few days, the two didn't have the mood to be intimate because of the elder brothers’ matter. If it wasn't a passionate moment just now, they wouldn't have chosen to do anything at this time either.","Now, Rice Ball's arrival was like pouring a basin of cold water over their heads.","He Zhiran first pushed Mo Jiuye away before he reluctantly let her go.","The two walked together towards the direction of the ranch. Upon getting closer, they saw that the cows had given birth to calves.","These dairy cows were raised by He Zhiran before she came to the Northwest. She had been so busy with everything recently that she hadn't had a chance to check on them.","The cows giving birth meant they would have milk from the space to drink.","In this ancient era, for the two elder brothers whose bodies were severely deficient, milk was definitely a good tonic.","He Zhiran went to the control panel to operate it, squeezing out a large bucket of milk.","Before leaving the space early in the morning, she boiled the milk and brought it out to appear in the backyard.","Lan Er and Yu Er had also gotten up and were cleaning the yard.","Seeing Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran return from the backyard, carrying a steaming wooden bucket, the two thought they had gone to stay at a nearby inn last night, climbed back over the wall early in the morning, and brought back breakfast.","Lan Er put down her broom and guiltily said, \"It's all our fault that Ninth Master and Ninth Madam had to go stay at an inn. \"","He Zhiran waved her hand: \"It doesn't matter, it's the same wherever we stay.\" Immediately after, she asked again: \"It was peaceful last night, right?\"","Lan Er nodded: \"Everything was fine.\"","After she spoke, Lan Er hurriedly called Yu Er to come up and take the wooden bucket Mo Jiuye was holding.","The two had just taken the bucket when they smelled a milky fragrance.","Although cow's milk was a precious thing in this era, the palace maids who grew up in the palace would not find it unfamiliar.","\"Ninth Master, Ninth Madam, did you go out to buy cow's milk?\"","He Zhiran vaguely replied, \"We happened to run into someone selling it on the road, so we bought some.\"","In order not to let them continue to be puzzled by this, He Zhiran urged: \"Take it to the kitchen first. Give Fourth Brother and Seventh Brother a bowl each, and you should each drink a bowl too, as much as you can drink.\"","The two maidservants didn't expect the Ninth Madam to be so generous that she would even share such precious milk with them.","The two suddenly felt warm in their hearts. No wonder the Princess entrusted them to Ninth Master and Ninth Madam before she passed away.","The Princess was an excellent judge of character. The Ninth Madam was definitely not the kind of sour and mean mistress.","Thinking of this, Lan Er and Yu Er were also less resistant to their future life.","He Zhiran didn't know their thoughts. After drinking a bowl of milk, she personally prepared breakfast for the two elder brothers.","It was still a nutritionally balanced meal. Their bodies were too weak. She estimated it wouldn’t take long before they would hurry back to the Northwest.","With so many new members added, they couldn't use the big G anymore. When the time came to travel by carriage and endure the bumps on the road, if their health wasn't improved a bit, He Zhiran worried they wouldn't be able to withstand the jolting.","After preparing breakfast, He Zhiran and Mo Jiuye stayed in the room to chat with the two elder brothers. The topic was mainly about Mo Family finding several brothers and their life in the Northwest.","At the same time,","In the imperial palace of the Southern Frontier.","The Crown Prince stood in the center of the main hall, his face full of helplessness and anger.","\"Father Emperor, I don't know who has such great ability that they actually completely stole the Crown Prince's mansion clean.\"","The Crown Prince had already reported this matter to the Emperor of the Southern Frontier when he sent people to the palace to ask for help last night. However, the ministers present didn't know about it.","Hearing the Crown Prince say this, everyone felt incredulous.","Especially this seemingly useless Crown Prince, who had done a lot of inappropriate things. Few people were willing to believe what he said.","However, seeing the worried look on the Emperor's face, it didn't seem to be false.","Just as the civil and military officials of the whole court were puzzled, someone came to report that a message had arrived from the border."]},{"number":274,"title":"Chapter 274: Mr. Simeng","paragraphs":["If Mo Jiuye were to know, he would say this news came a bit late.","The reason was none other than that the frontier guard commander was worried about being blamed by the Emperor for people sneaking in, so he thought to send someone to find them and wrap up the matter.","He didn't expect that he had dispatched a large number of men, yet was unable to find any traces.","The commander guessed that the intruders had likely already blended into the city. If this matter was hidden any longer and something big happened, he wouldn't be able to get away with it. Thus, he was forced to send someone to the capital to deliver a letter.","When the Crown Prince heard there were intruders at the frontier, he immediately associated it with the strange occurrences at his manor.","\"Father, there must be traitors from Da Shun who have snuck in, that's why someone was able to steal from my manor,\" said the Crown Prince.","The Emperor of Southern Frontier furrowed his brows.","\"The messenger who just came from the frontier said they only saw two infiltrators. What ability would two people have to empty out the entire treasury of the Crown Prince's manor?\"","Hearing the Emperor say this, it wasn't long before the ministers echoed in agreement.","\"That's right, unless those villains were immortals, with the Crown Prince Manor's tight defenses, how could anyone make an entire treasury disappear?\"","This angered the Crown Prince.","\"Are you saying I'm making things up?\"","\"This humble official wouldn't dare.\"","\"Humph! I see you're quite bold.\"","The Emperor of Southern Frontier was already in a terrible mood. Seeing the two argue openly in the hall, he angrily banged on the table.","\"Quiet, all of you!\"","The Crown Prince and minister exchanged glances then immediately shut their mouths.","At this moment, the Emperor of Southern Frontier also didn't know how to deal with this matter. All he could openly do was dispatch more people to continue the investigation.","After making these arrangements, the Emperor of Southern Frontier impatiently ordered the ministers to disperse. Then he hastily departed.","The Crown Prince had complained bitterly in the hall for so long without any results.","Although his father said he would send more men to continue investigating, it was of no help regarding the many items stolen from his manor.","Because his treasury was robbed, the Crown Prince had overlooked the final affairs of the Fourth Princess.","When he returned to the Crown Prince Manor, the servants came to inquire about the next steps regarding the Crown Prince's Consort's funeral.","Only then did the Crown Prince remember that the final affairs for his Consort had not yet been handled.","Although he did not care for the Fourth Princess of Da Shun, she had, after all, come for a marriage alliance.","Her funeral affairs couldn't be handled too simply. After all, there were many eyes watching from outside. Even if just for appearance's sake, it had to be done properly.","So he impatiently arranged for the servants to handle the subsequent tasks.","At the same time, he suddenly recalled that he hadn't seen the two handmaidens who had accompanied the Fourth Princess for the marriage alliance. Could it be...they were the ones who stole the items from the treasury and absconded?","The Crown Prince suddenly felt he had gained insight into the truth. He ordered further searches for Lan Er and Yu Er's whereabouts...","At this time, within the imperial palace of Southern Frontier.","The Emperor of Southern Frontier returned to his study. After dismissing his entourage, he went behind a large screen.","He pressed a switch to open the door to the secret chamber and entered.","The interior of the secret chamber could be described as luxurious and majestic, with furnishings that did not fall short of his imperial study in the slightest.","Moreover, it had all the necessary living facilities, even the chamber pot was gold-rimmed.","As soon as the Emperor of Southern Frontier entered, he eagerly said:","\"Sir, no matter what, you must lend a hand this time.\"","From his tone, it wasn't difficult to hear how respectful and cautious he was, even carrying a trace of fear.","At this time, a person was lazily reclining on the couch. The Emperor of Southern Frontier's arrival did not compel him to stand.","This person wore an ink-colored hat on his head and women's clothing on his body, but his voice when he spoke was that of a man.","Moreover, his tone made people unconsciously feel impatient.","\"What has happened to distress the emperor of a nation to such an extent?\"","The Emperor of Southern Frontier still stood respectfully before that person and said, \"I just heard the report from the frontier. They said two villains from Da Shun snuck in and still haven't been found.","\"Not only that, more strange things happened at the Crown Prince's manor last night. I suspect it has to do with those two villains...\"","Hearing the Emperor of Southern Frontier's words roused some interest in the person on the couch. He slowly sat up straight and asked, \"Do you mean those two villains have abilities that transcend the Heavens, that they were actually able to empty out the entire treasury of the Crown Prince's manor all at once?\"","If this had happened in the past, perhaps he wouldn't have believed such nonsense.","Going back further, the national treasury of Da Shun had been completely stolen clean in one night, and the thief even set it on fire afterwards.","Also, the home of a certain county magistrate of Da Shun had been burgled with the same modus operandi.","Most importantly, just last night he had personally witnessed his own Si Meng Mountain Villa's study emptied out. The few disciples he had left behind were all dead, and Mo Xiuyan had been taken away by someone.","Regrettably, by the time he discovered it, it was already too late and the thief had disappeared without a trace.","If he had not gone to Si Meng Mountain Villa last night and had instead stayed in the capital city, given how big of a commotion occurred at the Crown Prince's manor, he would have been able to rush over promptly to investigate, instead of losing the best window of time to search for clues like now.","He was already furious because of this matter. And now the Emperor of Southern Frontier had come to ask for his help.","Mr. Si Meng did not immediately respond to the Emperor of Southern Frontier. Instead, he carefully analyzed the similarities between these few incidents.","First, the theft of the Da Shun national treasury. That was on the night before the Mo family's banishment.","According to his subordinates' reports, Mo Jiuye was summoned by Emperor Shunwu into the palace on the day of Mo Jiuye's wedding. Afterwards, Mo Jiuye was carried back home after receiving 50 heavy blows with the plaquer.","As someone who practices martial arts, he clearly understood what receiving 50 heavy blows entailed.","If it had been him instead, after taking those 50 blows, he would have likely been bedridden for at least a month.","Even if Mo Jiuye's martial arts were superior to his own, without lying in bed for at least half a month, it would have been impossible for him to move freely, let alone steal from the highly-guarded national treasury. No matter how he looked at it, it didn't seem like something Mo Jiuye did.","But one also could not completely preclude Mo Jiuye's involvement either.","Next was the matter of that county magistrate's family. Some were injured, others were frightened silly, and a treasury full of items had disappeared overnight.","After an investigation by his subordinates, at that time the Mo family's exiled convoy was right nearby.","It was just that their exact location was not found.","Through these two incidents, even if he didn't find evidence pointing to Mo Jiuye, his intuition told him this was certainly related to Mo Jiuye.","Finally, there was his Si Meng Mountain Villa. One must know, there were quite a lot of items in the underground study. Even if one knew Qinggong lightness skill, one would still need to make several round trips to move everything upstairs.","He had carefully examined the location. At most, there were only two sets of outsiders' footprints.","Moreover, judging by the sizes of the footprints, the two people should have been one man and one woman.","He could conjecture the man to be Mo Jiuye. Mo Xiuyan was in such a sorry state, covered in filth. If Mo Jiuye was not his own brother, upon seeing him perhaps he wouldn't even have wanted to save him.","He just couldn't figure out who the woman could be.","In order to break into his Si Meng Mountain Villa, without formidable abilities one wouldn't even have been able to get inside.","But from his understanding, among the Mo family women there was no one who knew martial arts.","The more Mr. Si Meng thought about it, the more he felt he couldn't grasp the crux of the matter."]},{"number":275,"title":"Chapter 275: Nine brothers and sisters, you must go","paragraphs":["Now the Emperor of Southern Frontier said that there was also a theft at the Residence of the Crown Prince, which was similarly emptied out. This made Mr. Si Meng puzzled for a moment.","Since he came here to recuperate, he has received a lot of bad news in succession.","First his disciple Yun Li went missing. And now Mo Yunfeng, which was under Yun Li's control, has also disappeared without a trace.","If Yun Li was dead, he wouldn't worry too much. After all, the mother Gu was in Yun Li’s hands, so Mo Yunfeng wouldn't have any hope of surviving either.","Being dead wouldn't be too bad. It would just be a little earlier than the other people of the Mo Family. He could go apologize to Little Meng down there.","What really gave him a headache were the Fifth Son of the Mo Family and Mo Jiuye.","If the person who caused all this trouble in Southern Frontier this time was really Mo Jiuye, he would definitely seize this opportunity and make sure he never returns.","Upon thinking of this, Mr. Si Meng spoke up.","\"Leave this matter to me.\"","Seeing Mr. Si Meng agree, the Emperor of Southern Frontier hurriedly said, \"I'll have to trouble you then.\"","Mr. Si Meng waved his hand to let him leave first. It looked like he really had to use his trump card this time.","After the Emperor of Southern Frontier left, he got up from the soft couch and went straight out through another passage...","In the rented yard in the capital city.","He Zhiran used silver needles to prick the sleeping acupoints of her two elder brothers, then helped them transfuse blood plasma again and injected them with protein drugs.","An hour later, all the blood plasma was transfused, and the two elder brothers also gradually woke up.","They felt much more spirited now. They both thought it was because their ninth younger sister had prepared nourishing meals for them and they had a good rest.","He Zhiran didn’t explain much about it.","She believed that the Southern Frontier capital must be in chaos today due to what happened in the Residence of the Crown Prince last night. She was going to go out with Mo Jiuye to take a look.","Since the Crown Prince hadn't found the person who had emptied the treasury of the Residence of the Crown Prince and rescued their seventh elder brother, he definitely wouldn't let it go easily.","Moreover, at this point, he must have already attended the early court session. Bringing up this matter at the court, the number of people involved in the investigation would surely increase.","Even though they had narrowly escaped the search last night, they still couldn’t let their guard down now.","If those soldiers who were searching came around again, it would be dangerous for these people at home if they were not around.","Finally, after discussing it, the two decided that only Mo Jiuye would go out while He Zhiran stayed at home. In case of an emergency, she could make everyone unconscious and hide in her space.","Fortunately, they made that decision. Not long after Mo Jiuye left, there was a clamor of noises outside the yard.","Sure enough, those soldiers started going from door to door to search again.","This time, they were better prepared than last night. With the princess dead and her two maids also missing at the same time, it was inevitable to suspect Lan Er and Yu Er even though they were powerless weak women. Having disappeared for so long just like evaporating into thin air, it was impossible not to arouse some suspicion.","They didn't know what the thief who stole from the Residence of the Crown Prince looked like, but they did know what the two maids beside the Fourth Princess looked like. Therefore, the Crown Prince of Southern Frontier ordered them to use the two maids as clues to carry out the investigation first.","At this moment, those people were asking around with the portraits of Lan Er and Yu Er while also searching every household.","In the words of the Crown Prince, they must be thorough and not let even a mouse hole slip by.","When Lan Er and Yu Er heard the movement, they both ran to He Zhiran.","\"Ninth Lady, we heard those officials asking if anyone had seen the two women in the portrait. I guessed they must be asking about us. Let's go out now. We must not implicate Ninth Lady and two Masters.\"","After saying that, Lan Er and Yu Er pulled each other’s hands and were about to walk out towards the main entrance.","\"Stop!\" He Zhiran shouted to stop them.","Just as Lan Er and Yu Er turned to look at her, they saw the air in front of them filled with white powder. At the same time, they both lost consciousness.","He Zhiran quickly sent them into her space.","As for Shun Zi, He Zhiran was not so gentle with him.","After all, there was little left of the anesthetic powder she had prepared. She had to conserve whenever possible.","Therefore, He Zhiran knocked Shun Zi unconscious with a knifehand strike and sent him into the space together with the girls.","As for her two elder brothers in the room, they were martial artists. Even though their bodies were weak, they could still hear the movement outside vaguely.","Neither wanted to implicate their ninth younger sister.","The two brothers discussed and decided to persuade their ninth younger sister to leave by herself no matter what and not care about them.","At this moment, He Zhiran walked in.","\"Ninth younger sister, you hide first and don't mind us.\"","\"Listen to us. Ninth younger sister, leave quickly.\"","Mo Xiuyan and Mo Yuance hated themselves for the first time, for their bodies being so useless that they might even drag down their own younger sister.","When He Zhiran came in, she could already hear the footsteps getting closer and closer to the door. At this moment, she didn’t have time to explain too much either. It was too late to prick the sleep acupoints of the two with silver needles. She simply threw out a bag of anesthetic powder and then quickly brought them into her space.","He Zhiran had just appeared in her space when she was caught by Rice Ball.","Looking at the soft and cute little fellow, He Zhiran's mood instantly relaxed a lot.","She prepared some tasty food for Rice Ball before sending it away to play by itself.","Taking this opportunity while her two elder brothers were unconscious, she helped check their bodies again.","The results of the examination were not bad. Everything was developing as He Zhiran had expected.","Especially for her fourth elder brother, the recovery speed of his heart index was decent. There would be absolutely no problem with surgery in half a month.","Although her seventh elder brother's body was still slightly weaker, there was also great improvement. It shouldn't take too long before he could slowly start walking around.","Looking at the time, the few of them would probably have to sleep for a while more. He Zhiran then used her mind to check the spoils of war from the Residence of the Crown Prince.","Her main goal was to find some lotus placenta.","Luckily, after searching for a while, she finally found the small box.","The lotus placenta was small to begin with. And there was only this one piece of such precious medicinal material. If not for the box looking a bit exquisite, it could even be described as very inconspicuous.","It had been more than an hour since entering the space. The soldiers searching outside must have left already. Only then did He Zhiran bring everyone out together.","Just as they appeared in the room, Mo Jiuye returned.","\"What was the situation outside?\"","Mo Jiuye's expression was somewhat solemn.","\"The streets were full of soldiers. The theft at the Residence of the Crown Prince had flared up. They were still carrying the portraits of Lan Er and Yu Er. I heard that the Emperor of Southern Frontier is continuing to send more men to search.\"","He Zhiran felt it was somewhat funny. If she didn't have her space, she really wouldn't dare to boast. With this space, even if the Southern Frontier people turned the capital upside down, they still wouldn't find them. However, she wouldn't let her guard down because of that either.","\"With such chaos outside, it will probably be difficult for us to act tonight.\"","He Zhiran was also aware of this point. If she hadn't promised the little collector to help him find the Black South Pearl, she would have even considered finding a way to leave this place immediately.","However, she was always true to her words no matter if she could find that Black South Pearl or not. She must go to the Southern Frontier Imperial Palace at least once to be at ease.","The weather in Southern Frontier today was not very good. It was windy during the day. As soon as night fell, there was heavy rain."]},{"number":276,"title":"Chapter 276: I'm not sure Until I Check.","paragraphs":["He Zhiran and Mo Jiuye did not want to stay here any longer, so they ran towards the Imperial Palace of Southern Frontier in the rain.","If everything went smoothly, they would be able to leave this ghost place tomorrow.","This heavy rain was more or less a boost for both of them.","Although there were still soldiers everywhere on the streets, they were also dressed like the People of Southern Frontier. Besides, the People of Southern Frontier had no habit of using rain gear. Wherever there were passersby, they would walk ahead in the rain.","He Zhiran and Mo Jiuye also learned from the Southern Frontier people by covering their foreheads with their hands and ran in the rainy night, trying their best not to blur their vision.","The searching soldiers saw only the Southern Frontier people running past. Besides, they were not comfortable being drenched in the rain either. Naturally, they would not search very carefully.","When He Zhiran and Mo Jiuye ran past those officials, it was like an uninhabited place.","Mo Jiuye was not unfamiliar with the capital city of Southern Frontier. He had specifically checked the route during the day.","Therefore, they arrived near the palace very smoothly.","Mo Jiuye pointed to the west side of the palace wall and said, \"I've checked it out. The guards there are a little weaker. Let's go in from there.\"","He Zhiran nodded. The two held hands again and ran towards the west side of the palace.","Just after they turned a corner, they saw a group of people running towards them.","It was said to be a group of people, only the one leading them was riding a horse, while the rest were running behind the horse.","Mo Jiuye hurriedly hugged He Zhiran and leapt up a big tree. The two held their breath and looked down.","This group had about thirty people. Whether it was the general on horseback or the soldiers running, they all wore a crescent-shaped half mask.","What was most unexpected was that these people looked just like modern well-trained soldiers marching in formation.","This was not unfamiliar at all to He Zhiran, who was a soldier in his previous life.","Although such a formation was not unfamiliar to He Zhiran, its appearance in this alley at night was quite puzzling. What was their purpose?","This made He Zhiran think deeply.","Looking closely at their postures, each of them was holding a shining big knife, raised uniformly to their chests, with the blade pointing forward.","No matter how they ran, that action would not change. The attentive Mo Jiuye even noticed that their hands did not even tremble.","Likewise, the general on horseback was holding a pair of copper hammers in one hand and the rein in the other, looking straight ahead.","It was already dark night and the heavy rain severely affected their vision. They could not see the appearance and expressions of those who showed half of their faces at all.","But seeing that pair of copper hammers, Mo Jiuye felt a strange sense of familiarity.","Among the nine brothers of the Mo Family, only the sixth brother liked to use hammers. He had also used a pair of copper hammers before, simply because the sixth brother was very strong, and his martial arts skills were not as good as his other brothers.","When he went to the battlefield to kill enemies, he mostly took advantage of his great strength.","Although the person in front was also holding a pair of copper hammers, they looked a size bigger than the ones the sixth brother had used.","Mo Jiuye still remembered that the last time he was with the sixth brother, the sixth brother said that his strength seemed to have increased again. After the war was over, he would go back and forge a heavier pair of copper hammers.","Seeing that Mo Jiuye had stared for so long without any reaction, He Zhiran reminded him, \"They are gone. Should we go into the palace, or do you think there is something wrong with these people and want to follow them to see?\"","The reason she said this was that she realized these people were different.","First of all, she could not think of their motive for behaving like this in the alley at night.","Secondly, they walked in exactly the same posture. She did not believe that Southern Frontier could train people like this. Think about the soldiers participating in the parade in modern times, they could not do the same either.","Finally, although she could not see the expressions and faces of these people, she noticed one detail that their chests did not have the kind of rhythmic breathing...","That is to say, He Zhiran suspected that these people might not be alive, or they might be people who lost consciousness controlled by some Gu worm.","The Master Si Meng they were looking for must be a master of Gu techniques. Gu masters usually raised many kinds of Gu worms. Therefore, she was somewhat suspicious that these people might be related to Master Si Meng.","That was why she asked Mo Jiuye.","She knew Mo Jiuye was worried about the safety of his fourth and seventh brothers and did not want to stay outside for too long. Whether to follow them or not depended on his decision.","Although Mo Jiuye did not think as much as He Zhiran did, after seeing the copper hammers of the man on horseback, he inexplicably wanted to take a closer look. To him, this sense of familiarity grew stronger and stronger.","\"Well, let's go take a look.\"","With that said, she hugged Mo Jiuye's waist. Using Qinggong, they secretly followed those people, keeping a distance.","Those people headed straight for the city gate, which was the road they must take when they came to the capital.","Supposedly, when they reached the city gate where there were guards, they would stop to show some kind of token. After all, the capital was under high alert now. It was impossible for people to come and go freely.","However, they did not do that, but continued to move forward in their original posture, without any intention of stopping at all.","At first, some guards at the gate tried to go up and inspect them. Who knew, as soon as they got close, they were hammered to death by the man on horseback.","The guards at the gate were so frightened that they fled everywhere. When faced with such a tough situation, keeping themselves alive was the most important thing.","The group thus left the city unhindered. Taking advantage of the chaos, Mo Jiuye carried He Zhiran and leapt out of the city wall using Qinggong.","When those people were on the official road and there were no soldiers or commoners around, Mo Jiuye gradually caught up with the team.","Logically, when such a rampaging team heard footsteps behind, they should look back. However, they did not, but kept walking forward.","The scene was extremely weird.","Mo Jiuye whispered to He Zhiran, \"Ranran, do you think they are also controlled by puppet Gu?\"","He Zhiran gently shook her head, \"I can't be sure without checking.\"","What she thought was that people controlled by puppet Gu would be manipulated by the caster. There were thirty-one people in this group, including the one riding the horse.","According to the book, puppet Gu was very difficult to raise. Even for masters, at most one mother Gu could only control five people.","And each Gu master could only raise three to four mother Gu at most.","Based on these numbers, a Gu master could control up to twenty people at most.","However, the actions and behavior of these people were exactly the same. Apart from being controlled by one person, it was impossible to be so synchronized.","Therefore, He Zhiran had basically ruled out the possibility that they were under the influence of puppet Gu in her mind.","Just as she was thinking, the man on horseback finally changed his move."]},{"number":277,"title":"Chapter 277: I want to see who the leader is.","paragraphs":["His actions were very stiff, he just raised his hand high, and then increased the speed of the horse.","The leader sped up, and the speed of those behind him rose at the same time. Without using any lightness skills, their speed could be described as sprinting.","Even when sprinting, their actions didn't change at all, without even the slightest wavering.","As those people accelerated, Mo Jiuye's speed naturally had to increase as well. He embraced He Zhiran and used lightness skills to quickly chase after them.","He Zhiran frowned, she seemed to have noticed something wrong.","\"The one controlling those thirty people should be the person on horseback.\"","As she spoke, she had already taken out a sniper rifle from her space ring, loaded it, and aimed at the man on horseback.","Mo Jiuye guessed her intention and stopped her, \"Ranran, use a tranquilizer gun. I want to see the identity of the leader.\"","He Zhiran thought Mo Jiuye wanted to get some useful clues from these people, so she quickly put away the sniper rifle and took out a tranquilizer gun to grasp in her hand.","Mo Jiuye knew his wife was going to aim, so he deliberately sped up. Then, when they were less than fifty meters away from the man on horseback, he stopped.","He Zhiran's body steadied, she immediately fired a shot, precisely hitting the leader's shoulder.","The man struggled for a few moments, then fell off the horse's back.","To be cautious of any changes from the people behind, Mo Jiuye once again embraced He Zhiran and leapt onto the treetops.","The danger he imagined didn't come. After the man on horseback fell to the ground, those people simply stood in place, each like terracotta warriors, without any reaction at all.","He Zhiran breathed a sigh of relief, pointing at the man lying on the ground saying, \"They should be controlled by this person.\"","At this moment, Mo Jiuye also realized this point. Seeing that those soldiers didn't have any actions, he pulled He Zhiran and cautiously approached the leader.","To verify whether those thirty people really had no consciousness, or weren't alive, He Zhiran and Mo Jiuye deliberately probed them as they passed by.","This probe made Mo Jiuye gasp.","What he probed was their breath, but there was none at all...","He Zhiran was different. After all, she was a doctor. When checking if someone still had life, she wouldn't rely solely on their breath, but would check the carotid artery in their neck.","If she hadn't probed like this, she might have also thought they were all dead.","No breath, but a faint pulse in the carotid artery, He Zhiran had never encountered such a situation before.","Before she could tell Mo Jiuye about her discovery, he had already walked up to the leader.","Seeing this, He Zhiran immediately took out a flashlight from her space ring and shone it on the man's face.","Mo Jiuye lifted the man's mask, instantly shocked still as he sat on the muddy ground, completely disregarding the filth on his hands.","\"Sixth elder brother, it's sixth elder brother...\"","He Zhiran was equally shocked. She had guessed earlier that these people were very likely related to Mr. Si Meng, but hadn't considered the side of the Mo family men.","After all, the Mo brothers they had recently rescued looked miserable.","Especially the fourth and seventh elder brothers, it was simply a miracle they were still alive.","But the sixth elder brother before them was completely different. Not only was he not emaciated, but his complexion didn't look unhealthy either.","No matter what, since he was a Mo family elder brother, He Zhiran didn't have any reason to let him continue getting rained on here.","With a wave of her hand, she brought the sixth elder brother and Mo Jiuye into her space ring together.","The two paid no mind to their own rain-soaked clothes, and hurried into the operating room to examine the sixth elder brother.","After examination, it was confirmed that the sixth elder brother had indeed been infected with puppet bugs.","To prevent any changes, He Zhiran and Mo Jiuye removed the bugs from him in the fastest speed possible.","At the same time, Mr. Si Meng, who was sitting cross-legged in the secret room of the Si Meng Villa, suddenly spat out a mouthful of blood. At the same time, the bottle containing the puppet master bug in his arms also shook incessantly.","He paid no mind to wiping the blood from the corners of his mouth, and hurriedly took out the porcelain bottle to inspect it.","He first placed the master bug in his palm. The master bug fluttered its wings, wanting to fly out of his palm.","Mr. Si Meng completely disregarded his own physical condition, and quickly followed it.","He was a genius at raising bugs, and the best bug raiser in southern borderlands. The bugs he raised, especially this puppet bug, had been by his side for many years and developed some intelligence. Whenever an abnormal situation occurred with the host of a child bug, his master bug would react in time.","He just didn't know which child bug's host had run into trouble.","If it was on the western border, it would be troublesome. Even if he grew wings and could fly, he was afraid he still wouldn't make it in time.","The only thing reassuring him was that in the whole world, no one could remove the bugs he had planted in someone.","At most, the infected person would die, and he would lose a Mo family man. As for those medicine men he had carefully nurtured over the years, before he could even utilize them, losing them like this was quite a pity.","Although it was a pity, since he could no longer control the person, dying was the best outcome for them.","Of course, if something happened to Mo Liu, Mo Jinyean, who had just left the capital, he still had a chance to go save him.","Therefore, Mr. Si Meng hurriedly utilized his lightness skill to chase after him, hoping he could still catch up to Mo Jinyean's footsteps.","When he chased to the city gate, he specially asked the soldiers guarding the gate, confirming that Mo Jinyean had already left the city with people, so he directly chased out after them.","At this time, He Zhiran and Mo Jiuye had already removed the child bug from Mo Jinyean's body.","This child bug was a bit different from the ones they had seen before when saving his elder brothers.","The bugs taken out from the bodies of the elder brothers they had saved earlier were all transparent blue, but the bug in the sixth elder brother was somewhat purple-blue.","It was a bit like the unhealthy color a person's skin takes on when poisoned.","Mo Jiuye also noticed the difference with this child bug. He carefully observed the bug still struggling inside the glass bottle in his hand.","\"Ranran, look, it's still using its head to hit the bottle stopper.\"","He Zhiran's attention was not actually on this.","\"Its color looks very strange, like it was steeped in poison.\"","Only then did Mo Jiuye notice the color of the bug.","\"Indeed, just what is going on here?\"","If it was a human, He Zhiran could take some blood samples to test, but for a bug, she really couldn't.","And there were still so many unknown people outside.","Thinking of the people outside, He Zhiran suddenly realized something.","\"Husband, I suspect those people outside are the legendary medicine men.\"","\"Medicine men?\" Mo Jiuye had also heard of this term, it's just that he had only heard of it.","Moreover, according to his knowledge, the secret technique for creating medicine men had been lost for hundreds of years already, so why would medicine men appear again?","In order to verify all this, and also because He Zhiran didn't want to leave any traces, she instantly left the space ring and brought all those people inside.","Anyway, they had no consciousness, so there was no need to worry about the space being exposed at all."]},{"number":278,"title":"Chapter 278: They're just like the Moos.","paragraphs":["At this moment, Sixth Brother was still in a coma. The two of them might as well go check on the situation of these poisoned people.","The light inside the space was completely different from the outside. Although there was no sunlight shining down, it still gave people a feeling of sunshine and warmth.","As a result, when Mo Jiuye removed the mask of one of them, he was stunned in place...","He Zhiran saw his expression was off, and hurriedly asked: \"What's wrong?\"","Mo Jiuye pointed at the person in front of him and said: \"This is my father's deputy general, Tao Ran.\"","After he finished speaking, Mo Jiuye impatiently went to check the identities of the others.","Upon looking, more than half of them were people whose names he could call out, and they were all good brothers who had followed his father through life and death for many years.","As for those whose names he couldn't call out, Mo Jiuye could still vaguely recognize their faces. He could basically confirm that these were all soldiers from the army.","Seeing so many brave men who defended their homes and country here, and all of them had become like living dead, Mo Jiuye was filled with complex emotions for a moment.","He Zhiran didn't need to ask. She could tell from Mo Jiuye's expression that these people were all Da Shun's soldiers and generals.","They shed blood for Da Shun on the battlefield, but ended up in such an outcome in the end.","They were also someone else's sons, husbands or fathers. When their families received news of their deaths, how heartbroken must they have felt?","Mo Jiuye slowly stood up, grief and indignation on his face, and said: \"Here, many people died in battle when I was the one who sent people to inform their families. I didn't expect that they, like the Mo family men, are still alive after all...\"","He Zhiran could understand Mo Jiuye’s feelings.","In her previous life, she had also gone on missions with her comrades. When they left, her comrades were still healthy and lively, but in the end they never came back.","As a result, He Zhiran spent a long period of time in remembrance and longing for those comrades.","Mo Jiuye was the same. He watched his comrades leave one by one before his eyes, so only he himself knew the sourness in his heart best.","\"Don't be sad. Let me check their condition first.\"","She first did a full body check on Tao Ran.","The results were not optimistic. It was obvious that he was poisoned, and not by just one type of poison.","Among the poisons she could name, there were only a few that she was familiar with. These poisons would not kill a person, but would gradually paralyze one's nerves and make them lose self-awareness, turning into something like a living dead. This was where the problem lay with these \"poisoned people\".","These were indeed the legendary poisoned people.","The characteristic of \"poisoned people\" was that they had no autonomous consciousness, could not perceive bodily pain, and as long as they still had a breath left, they would act like machines, ceaselessly carrying out the commands issued by their controller.","Speaking of controllers, the first person He Zhiran thought of was Sixth Brother.","The Gu worms taken out of Sixth Brother's body were of an abnormal color, she didn't know if it had anything to do with the special offspring Gu inside his body.","In order to verify all this, He Zhiran took out the bottle containing the offspring Gu from Mo Xiuyan's body. She shook it a few times, and the Gu worm inside immediately became restless.","The Gu worm first charged around violently, then flew to the bottom of the bottle. If one looked closely, one could see that it had even raised its front two feet.","Next, a bizarre scene occurred.","All the people lying on the grass stood up at once and quickly lined up neatly.","Both Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran were shocked for a moment.","He Zhiran experimentally moved the Gu worm further away, and looked at those people again. Their bodies gradually went limp.","At the same time, Mr. Si Meng, who had chased out of the city, once again felt an anomaly from the mother Gu.","He quickly took out the mother Gu to check, and saw that the mother Gu had inexplicably become restless for some reason.","For a Gu raiser, such a situation was all too familiar.","It was nothing more than the offspring Gu having encountered some kind of shock or accidental situation, which led to this kind of reaction.","In most cases, it was when the host of the offspring Gu died and the offspring Gu itself escaped and encountered some danger on the way back to the mother Gu.","Thinking of such possibilities, sweat appeared on Mr. Si Meng's forehead.","He didn't know which host had died. The mother Gu he owned had given birth to offspring Gu that controlled a total of three Mo family men. No matter which one, their current positions were all very important.","Especially Big Brother Mo and Second Brother Mo. If something happened to them, everything he had planned over so many years might come to naught.","Sixth Brother Mo was also the same. He had just been sent out by himself, with the purpose of intercepting the road from the south to Da Shun, while also helping the southern border soldiers attack Da Shun.","The offspring Gu inside his body was the only one that could control those poisoned people through the mother Gu to pass on information.","If Mo Sixth Brother died, not only would his poisoned people face the danger of seeing sunlight, it would also be a complete waste of his many years of hard work.","One must know, it took great effort to produce these poisoned people.","The combat power of these poisoned people could match a hundred men. At present, they were his biggest trump card.","If he hadn't guessed that the people who broke into the Southern Border Prince's Mansion to steal things and went to kill his disciple at Si Meng Mountain Villa were likely to be Mo family members who also rescued Mo Xiuyan, he would never have revealed his trump card so early.","The more Mr. Si Meng thought about it, the more anxious he became in his heart. He only hoped that the offspring Gu could return to the mother Gu's embrace sooner, so that he could determine exactly who had died.","Although the offspring Gu would bring him definite news, Mr. Si Meng still rushed in the direction of the border between the two countries.","If the dead host really was Sixth Brother Mo, by hurrying over earlier, he might still be able to keep those poisoned people. As a last resort he could always find another powerful host at that time...","Inside the space.","Mo Jiuye stared at those poisoned people, heartbroken, because his wife had not yet found a way to detoxify them for the time being.","Indeed, He Zhiran had not found a way to detoxify them. Not to mention there were several poisons she hadn't even seen before, even for those poisons which she knew the names of, with several poisons combined together, it wouldn't be so easy to detoxify them.","Whether it was poison or antidote, there existed mutual promotion and restraint. Helping those people detoxify, if she used the wrong medicinal material even once, it could lead to death.","Therefore, He Zhiran did not dare to rashly help detoxify those people.","Fortunately, both she and Mo Jiuye knew clearly that the poisoned people did not need to eat, and would not suddenly wake up either, so keeping them inside the space for a while longer was nothing to worry about.","Under normal circumstances, He Zhiran could buy some books related to poisoned people and study them carefully before formulating a detoxification solution.","But now they were in the Southern Border, they didn't dare be the slightest bit careless or relaxed.","Especially since Fourth Brother and Seventh Brother were still healing from injuries in the capital city, they even more so did not dare remain outside for too long.","In case those soldiers searched the place once more with extra scrutiny while they were not by their side, it would be dangerous for the two elder brothers.","Mo Jiuye was also worried about the external situation. Seeing that his wife had not expressed any opinion for a while, he reminded: \"Ranran, or should we return to the capital first?\"","He Zhiran was of the same opinion.","\"Mm, Sixth Brother probably won't wake in the next few hours. Let's go back now.\""]},{"number":279,"title":"Chapter 279: Can't Be reconciled without Checking it out.","paragraphs":["When they left the space, it could be said that Mr. Si Meng arrived just in time.","Mr. Si Meng was riding a horse and happened to chase here at this moment. He was currently looking around.","This heavy rain more or less helped him a little.","He went out of the city and walked on the official road. He could still vaguely see the neat and muddy footprints and hoof prints. Mr. Si Meng could be sure that these prints were left by Mo Jiuye when he passed by with his men.","From the neat traces of those prints, he could be sure that everything went smoothly when they got here.","Mr. Si Meng followed the prints all the way and happened to get here. The prints disappeared, so he got off his horse to check and hoped to find some clues.","Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran had just appeared on the official road and almost bumped into a white figure.","Mr. Si Meng had always been vigilant. After noticing something wrong, he hurriedly threw out a package of poisonous powder at the two.","Seeing this, He Zhiran reacted quickly as well, pulling Mo Jiuye to dodge again and enter the space.","In such an emergency, no one dared to guarantee that they would not be poisoned by the powder.","\"Did you see what that person looked like?\" He Zhiran only saw that the man was dressed in white, which looked a bit conspicuous in the rainy night.","Mo Jiuye shook his head, \"No, it was too fast, I didn't have time to see.\"","\"Whoever can search there must be related to Sixth Elder Brother and these drug dealers.\" This was the first possibility He Zhiran thought of.","\"Ranran, pay attention this time and take me out again to see.\"","It was hard to get a clue, and Mo Jiuye didn't want to give up so easily.","He Zhiran also had this intention. The two covered their noses and mouths and appeared outside the space again.","Going in and out of space only took a dozen seconds, but where was the figure in white? What caught their eyes was only boundless emptiness and the pitch dark night.","The rain had stopped at this time and no longer affected Mo Jiuye's perception.","He listened carefully to the surrounding sounds. He could be sure that the person had walked away.","At this moment, Mr. Si Meng was already on his way back to the capital.","The two people who had just appeared were the most skilled in lightness martial arts he had ever seen. Even his poisonous powder could be avoided. They disappeared in the blink of an eye...","When encountering such masters, the only thing he could do was run, the farther away from there the better.","After Mo Jiuye searched in vain, He Zhiran said, \"The larva will look for the mother gu worm on its own after leaving the carrier. Why don't we let the larva out and follow it?\"","Although this was a bit risky, they didn't want to give up so easily after finally finding a clue.","Whether the person they found was Mr. Si Meng or not, even if not, it was the person who controlled Sixth Elder Brother. It wouldn't be a waste of their efforts to avenge Sixth Elder Brother.","\"Well, I think this is feasible.","If the larva runs towards the border, we'll give up tracking. We can't go too far from the capital city. We must go back before dawn to check on the situations of Fourth Elder Brother and Seventh Elder Brother.\"","He Zhiran also agreed to this. She immediately took out the larva from the space.","At this moment, Mo Jiuye had already embraced her waist, ready to follow the larva closely at any time.","Seeing that Mo Jiuye was ready, He Zhiran opened the bottle and released the larva inside, then quickly stuffed the bottle back into Mo Jiuye's hand, so that he could quickly catch it back if the larva ran in the wrong direction.","The larva, free again, flew towards the direction of the capital city.","Mo Jiuye and his wife looked at each other, then quickly followed.","All the way until the outskirts of the capital city, the larva flew over the top of the wall.","Mo Jiuye also increased his speed to the maximum. On one hand, the higher speed meant a greater possibility to dodge the guards' sight. On the other hand, it prevented losing track of the larva.","Smoothly, the two quickly crossed over the city wall without attracting the guards' attention.","All the way following the flying larva, they finally saw it flying straight towards the imperial palace.","The imperial palace guards were by no means comparable to the city gates. Mo Jiuye was not sure he could follow the larva in unimpeded.","Therefore, when the larva was about to fly into the imperial palace, he quickly chased up to it and put it back in the bottle.","Although this approach could not completely determine the specific location of the Gu Master, at least they knew the person was in the imperial palace.","At worst, they could release the larva again after entering the imperial palace to continue searching.","Although the rain had stopped, the sky was still covered with dense clouds.","He Zhiran glanced at the big clock in the space and saw that it was one o'clock in the morning.","In principle, this was the best time to sneak into the imperial palace. Except for some guards, everyone else should be asleep.","\"Shall we go in now?\" He Zhiran asked.","Mo Jiuye pondered for a moment, then nodded heavily.","\"We've come this far, I'm reluctant not to go in and take a look.\"","The two reached a consensus and circled back to the alley on the west side of the imperial palace.","Mo Jiuye found a hidden place, picked up He Zhiran, and jumped over the wall.","The imperial palace in the Southern Territory was not unfamiliar to Mo Jiuye. When he led his troops to attack the capital years ago, he personally led people to ransack the National Treasury.","Although he could not accurately state the locations of each palace, he had a general idea.","The two avoided the patrolling soldiers and came to a heavily guarded area.","Whether it was because the treasury of the Crown Prince's residence had been emptied, the number of guards here was much higher than Mo Jiuye remembered.","Mo Jiuye whispered, \"This is the National Treasury of the Southern Territory. Behind it a little is the private treasury of the Emperor of the Southern Territory. I have visited both before.\"","At that time, they had carried away all the items in the treasury bright and clear.","Visiting this old place again, Mo Jiuye had a trace of expectation.","He wondered how much wealth the Southern Territory could accumulate after recovering for a few years.","Mo Jiuye did not intend to enter the National Treasury through the main gate. He pulled He Zhiran around to the side, where the guards were relatively weak.","Even so, there were guards every two steps.","There was not much of that magical potion made from the silver ring snake left. He Zhiran was reluctant to take it out before the critical moment.","Especially with so many guards in front. The small amount of potion was of no use.","He Zhiran decisively took out two repeating crossbows from the space.","There were two windows behind the treasury, with four guards in total. Each person would take out two guards, and the speed must be fast to avoid detection.","At the same time, He Zhiran was also prepared to fail. Once they failed, she would pull Mo Jiuye into the space together.","Fortunately, neither of them missed. In the blink of an eye, four delicate crossbow arrows shot into the foreheads of the four people.","Mo Jiuye quickly moved the corpses to a hidden place, while taking out the feathered arrows from their foreheads, leaving no traces behind.","After handling everything, the two broke in through the window.","The National Treasury of the Southern Territory was not as rich as that of the Da Shun Dynasty.","Of course, this was related to the geographical environment and national strength of the Southern Territory. More importantly, it had been looted by Mo Jiuye a few years ago.","In just a few years, being able to accumulate so much again was not bad."]},{"number":280,"title":"Chapter 280: One Step Too Slow","paragraphs":["He Zhiran swept around and waved to collect all the items into his space. Then the two returned the same way and ran to the private treasury behind the imperial treasury.","That was where He Zhiran had to go because the black Southern Pearl might be there.","Using the same method, they entered the private treasury without hesitation and moved everything out empty.","Next, their goal was to continue releasing the gu worm from the space to find the gu master's whereabouts.","All the way hiding sneakily, the two followed the gu worm to the study room.","The gu worm kept hovering around the study, obviously trying to get in.","At this time, the Emperor of Southern Frontier had already returned to the bedroom to rest. There were only two guards at the door of the study room, and they looked half asleep.","Using the same method again, the two guards were dealt with. Mo Jiuye went up to open the large door of the study room.","As soon as a gap appeared in the large door, the gu worm drilled in.","Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran also quickly entered and casually closed the door.","I saw the gu worm bypass the screen and fly towards a bookshelf, wandering around again.","Mo Jiuye guessed that this should also be some kind of secret entrance.","While staring at the gu worm, he worked with He Zhiran to start looking for the switch to enter the secret room in the room.","In the secret room, Mr. Si Meng thought more and more something was wrong.","He had just discovered that it might be the traces of those drug dealers and Mo Family Six Lang, and more than one hour had passed.","If Mo Family Six Lang had died there, the gu worm looking for the mother gu should have come back long ago with the speed of finding the mother gu.","He had been waiting outside the study for a long time just now, but did not see the gu worm come back.","This made him feel more and more uneasy in his heart.","In this case, unless the gu worm died, it would not take so long to fly back here.","If this was the case, the other party must also be a master of raising gu worms, and could even relieve the puppet gu worm.","In his understanding, there was no such master in the gu breeding world. Was it because he was poorly informed?","If there really was such a person who could catch his son gu worm, it would be easy as pie to find his location with the mother gu.","His body had not recovered yet. When he encountered danger and escaped just now, he used his inner power, and his body, which had recovered seven or eight parts, returned to its original state. If he met a master of gu breeding, he might not be able to deal with it.","Just as he was thinking about countermeasures, he suddenly heard movement at the door of the secret room.","Mo Jiuye had successfully found the switch to the secret room. The bookshelf against the wall was slowly moving away.","Mr. Si Meng felt bad. This secret room was only known to the Emperor of Southern Frontier and Yun Li. Now Yun Li had been missing for a long time. The only person who knew about this place was the Emperor of Southern Frontier.","He could determine that the person who came to find him at this time would never be the Emperor of Southern Frontier.","Because when he came back, he had already explained that he would practice qigong again in the next few days to heal his injuries. Even if the sky collapsed, he should not be disturbed.","He believed that the Emperor of Southern Frontier did not have the courage to come here rashly.","What’s more, there was an agreement between him and the Emperor of Southern Frontier that whenever the Emperor of Southern Frontier came, he would knock on the door panel three times the moment he opened the secret room door.","However, at this moment, the door of the secret room had obviously been opened, but he did not hear the sound of knocking on the door panel.","When he thought of this, Mr. Si Meng hurriedly stood up, carrying a package and ran towards the other direction of the secret room.","There was a passage there that could lead to the outside of the palace. It was just farther away from his hiding place. Most of the time, he would enter from the study room. If it wasn't an emergency, he wouldn't choose to leave from this passage.","The door of the secret room opened. Seeing the gap, the gu worm immediately flew in.","The two also strode to follow, but unfortunately, they were one step too late.","Seeing that there were still lights on in the gorgeous secret room, Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran both intended to observe it for a while.","In order not to let the gu worm fly away, Mo Jiuye put it back in the bottle again.","He Zhiran touched the bed, which was still a little warm.","\"It feels still a little warm here. The person should have just left not long ago.\"","Mo Jiuye pointed in the direction the gu worm was about to fly to just now.","\"There should be another exit over there.\"","He Zhiran waved to collect all the items in the secret room into the space.","Mo Jiuye released the gu worm again and chased it out.","Mr. Si Meng came out from the secret passage and faced the forest not far from the palace.","He had always been vigilant and worried that he might not be able to deal with it when he encountered danger due to his current physical condition.","He also thought that the only way for the gu breeding master to find him was through that gu worm.","After thinking twice, his own safety was the most important. Even though he escaped from the palace, he could not guarantee that he would always be safe in the future.","Finally, he made up his mind and released the mother gu from the porcelain bottle, and then chanted a few spells to make the gu worm that had entered Mo Jinye's body choose to commit suicide.","It had to be said that Mr. Si Meng's brain reacted very quickly. In order to ensure his own safety, he was willing to give up such a precious gu worm.","It should be known that the gu worm was raised by him in a special way since childhood, feeding it all kinds of poisons to eat, so as to use the person who was parasitized by the gu worm to control those drug dealers.","After a set of operations, Mr. Si Meng's painful expression was quite obvious.","There was no way. In the last year and a half, he felt nothing had gone well. The people who were sent to search for Mo Family Five Lang had not come back yet.","Similarly, there was no news from the people who went to investigate Mo Jiuye in the northwest.","Next July would be the deadline he swore to avenge Menger. Now there were still so many Mo family men wandering outside. Today he had lost a Mo Jinye again.","For a while, Mr. Si Meng's emotions were extremely low. At the same time, he secretly swore that he would send more people so as to achieve his goal.","He could no longer stay in Southern Frontier. Only Da Shun could allow him to be temporarily safe.","After collecting the mother gu into the porcelain bottle with a painful expression, Mr. Si Meng hurried towards Da Shun.","It had to be said that Mr. Si Meng’s decisiveness and ruthlessness temporarily preserved his life...","He Zhiran and Mo Jiuye chased the gu worm to the woods.","The gu worm, which was flying fast chasing the mother gu, suddenly stopped, then flew towards a big tree and crashed into it.","\"That’s bad. The gu worm is going to commit suicide.\" Mo Jiuye saw the anomaly and exclaimed, then rushed over immediately.","Unfortunately, his actions were still a step slower. The slender body of the gu worm had slammed heavily into the big tree and slowly slipped to the ground.","Such a situation was not unfamiliar to both of them.","They had not read the books about gu breeding in vain.","The two could determine that the man in white they met on the official road just now was the gu breeding master.","He was worried that the gu worm would find his whereabouts, so he chose to let the mother gu manipulate the gu worm to commit suicide. This way, it would be difficult to find him again.","Mo Jiuye gritted his teeth angrily, \"He's really cunning.\"","He Zhiran also felt very regretful. They finally got a little new clue with great difficulty, and now it was cut off. From now on, finding the person holding the mother gu would be like looking for a needle in the sea.","Since it had already happened, she and Mo Jiuye did not consider it carefully enough, which led to this.","\"Since this clue is broken, I believe he can be in the secret room of the study room of the Emperor of Southern Frontier. He must know his identity. Let's go back through the secret passage before dawn and interrogate the Emperor of Southern Frontier. At least it counts as some gain.\"","Mo Jiuye nodded, \"That's all we can do now.\"","Although the gu worm had committed suicide by hitting the tree, He Zhiran did not intend to let go of its corpse either.","It might come in handy later when making antidotes for those drug dealers in the space.","So she took the bottle from Mo Jiuye's hand and put the gu worm back in.","The two returned to the Southern Frontier Imperial Palace by the original road.","Mo Jiuye took her straight to the bedroom of the Emperor of Southern Frontier."]},{"number":281,"title":"Chapter 281: You know he's bad, don't you","paragraphs":["The guards outside the bedchamber were stringent, but none of these could stop Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran.","The two took care of the guards outside and entered the bedchamber of the Emperor of Southern Frontier together.","Perhaps it was because there had been too many things happening in Southern Frontier recently. The Emperor of Southern Frontier was not in the mood to dote on his consorts. On the spacious bed, only he himself laid.","Mo Jiuye's hatred towards the Emperor of Southern Frontier came from the bottom of his heart. If it wasn't for the Emperor's repeated attacks against Da Shun, the men of Mo Family would not have fallen into such dire straits.","He had already decided that if there was a chance today, he would definitely put the Emperor to death.","Doing things like this had become effortless for He Zhiran. While the Emperor of Southern Frontier was sound asleep, she sealed his sleeping acupoint and then threw him into her space.","The two of them searched around in the bedchamber and took everything they could get their hands on.","After the entire bedchamber was left empty, the two slipped away without anyone noticing.","The goal for sneaking into the palace had been fully accomplished. Dawn was approaching soon and they did not dare to linger any longer. While avoiding the guards, the two left the palace.","They first went back to check on the house they rented and saw that their two brothers were safe and sound. Then they quietly went to the backyard and slipped into the space with a flash.","The moment a bright light shone before their eyes, Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran were also stunned by what they saw.","They saw Rice Ball hugging a large bamboo shoot while sitting on the chest of the Emperor of Southern Frontier, eating it with great delight. At the same time, his little butt kept farting out green gas...","Upon seeing such a scene, the tension He Zhiran felt throughout the night was instantly relieved.","She couldn't help but laugh. \"Rice Ball, you also know he is a bad person, right? That's why you deliberately bullied him?\"","\"Mm...mmhmm...\" Rice Ball let out a series of chirps and rolled off the Emperor's body. He trotted towards his master on his little short legs.","He Zhiran first hugged Rice Ball and kissed him, then checked on Sixth Brother's condition.","If her estimate was correct, Sixth Brother would probably wake up after about an hour.","They had to interrogate the Emperor of Southern Frontier quickly while he was here.","Mo Jiuye had already strode forward eagerly and kicked the Emperor of Southern Frontier viciously several times.","He Zhiran did not intend to let the Emperor of Southern Frontier sleep for too long to begin with. Awakened by the pain from the kicks, the Emperor came to his senses after blanking out for a few seconds. Seeing the scene before him, he first froze for a moment before seeing a strange man and woman looking down at him.","\"You...How dare you not bow in the presence of This King...\"","Hearing this, Mo Jiuye couldn't help letting out a cold laugh.","Facing his archenemy, he didn't even want to waste his breath on pointless words.","\"Tell me, who is hiding in the secret chamber of your study?\"","Hearing such a question greatly alarmed the Emperor of Southern Frontier.","He examined Mo Jiuye carefully, trying to find some familiar traces.","However, he had never seen the two people before him at all.","Moreover, the fact that they were able to ask such a question meant that they must have discovered the secret chamber in the study.","Furthermore, he himself was sleeping in the bedchamber with stringent guards outside. How could he have been brought here without even realizing it?","The more the Emperor of Southern Frontier thought about it, the more afraid he became. He felt a chill run down his spine, as if cold air was erupting from the top of his head...","\"Just who exactly are you people?\"","\"To let you die with understanding, I'll show you who I am.\"","With that said, Mo Jiuye tore off his fake beard and took off his hat covering his forehead. Then he used his hands to simply wipe off some of the makeup on his face, revealing most of his original appearance.","Seeing the person before him, the Emperor of Southern Frontier reacted as if he had seen a ghost. His body recoiled violently backwards.","\"You...you are Mo Jiuye...\"","Mo Jiuye closed in on him step by step. \"It's me.\"","If there was anyone the Emperor of Southern Frontier feared the most, it would be the Mo Family men.","He had exhausted almost all of his resources to attack Da Shun, only to be thwarted by Mo Jiuye's father and son each time.","Although there was only one Mo Family man left now, Mo Jiuye was valiant and skillful in combat. He still did not dare to let his guard down.","Not long ago, he even thought that heaven was helping him when the Mo Family was ordered by an imperial edict from Emperor Shunwu to have their assets seized and exiled.","He had finally gotten a chance to win, but in the end, he was captured by the person he was most wary of.","The first thought the Emperor of Southern Frontier had was that the exile order on the Mo Family must have been fake. It was Emperor Shunwu deliberately making him relax his vigilance before sending Mo Jiuye to Southern Frontier to capture him alive.","He had been too careless and fallen for Emperor Shunwu's trickery.","If He Zhiran knew the Emperor of Southern Frontier had imagined so much, she would certainly say it was a waste for him not to write fantasy stories.","Of course, the two of them did not know what the Emperor of Southern Frontier was thinking. Mo Jiuye had no time to dawdle with him here.","\"If you want a quick death, tell me, who is the person hidden inside the secret chamber of your study?\"","At this moment, the Emperor of Southern Frontier's attention was not even on the crux of the question. All he heard was \"a quick death\"...","\"This King is the ruler of a nation. You cannot kill This King.\"","No killing? That was impossible. Mo Jiuye sneered inwardly and stepped forward to grab the Emperor of Southern Frontier's hair, lifting him up.","The Emperor had been captured from his bedchamber and was currently naked above the waist, only wearing a flimsy loincloth below. When Mo Jiuye jerked hard, his loincloth nearly dropped off.","He was heedless of the stinging pain in his scalp and hurriedly reached out to hold onto the only remaining piece of \"cover\" on his body.","Mo Jiuye also saw this scene and subconsciously blocked his wife's line of sight.","Such an unsightly scene would surely sully his beloved wife's eyes...","He Zhiran also felt speechless. Although she was a doctor who had seen many naked men, the Emperor of Southern Frontier's dark, fat physique really made one lose their appetite.","Speaking of losing one's appetite, she didn't know if it was because she had been through too many things these past few days, but looking at food made her somewhat nauseous.","The Emperor of Southern Frontier had grabbed onto his loincloth, but his hair was still being yanked violently by Mo Jiuye. He wailed loudly in pain.","\"Mo Jiuye...Let This King go...\"","However, Mo Jiuye still had no intention of releasing him. For a gutless coward like this, as long as he suffered more, it wouldn't be difficult to get the information he wanted.","Even so, to be prudent, He Zhiran decided to hypnotize the Emperor of Southern Frontier.","Not only would the answers be authentic, but it could also save a lot of time.","Just as the Emperor of Southern Frontier was still about to say something, a swinging pocket watch appeared before his eyes.","\"Have you seen this thing before? It was bought from Westerners.\" While speaking, He Zhiran swayed the pocket watch in her hand.","The Emperor of Southern Frontier blanked out for a moment as he stared at that pocket watch. Soon, as his gaze became more and more vacant, he quickly fell into a state of hypnosis.","Experienced as he was by now, Mo Jiuye also knew how to check if the hypnosis had worked.","He knew it was time to ask questions now.","\"Who is the person hidden inside the secret chamber of your study?\"","Emperor of Southern Frontier: \"Mr. Si Meng.\"","Hearing this name, both Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran gasped."]},{"number":282,"title":"Chapter 282: Gu can seal you as the King of Southern Xinjiang","paragraphs":["Mr. Si Meng, whom they had been desperately looking for, was actually there.","But they were one step too late, and someone had already helped him escape.","This feeling was not good.","Although they did not directly interact with Mr. Si Meng, all the signs he displayed showed that this person was extremely cunning.","Mo Jiuye was extremely annoyed that Mr. Si Meng had escaped just like that.","At the same time, he also suspected that the person who had thrown the poisonous powder at them on the official road was Mr. Si Meng.","Whether that person was Mr. Si Meng or not, Mo Jiuye was very clear in his heart that this was not the time for him to be annoyed about these things now.","He needed to further confirm whether the man in white they met on the official road was Mr. Si Meng.","\"Was he wearing white clothes and a hat yesterday?\"","Emperor of Southern Frontier: \"Yes.\"","Now, it could be completely confirmed that the man was Mr. Si Meng.","It was just a pity that this person was too cunning and had escaped twice when they had the chance.","Since he was hiding on purpose, it would be even more difficult to find him in the future.","Seeing that Mo Jiuye was hesitating and did not continue to ask the next question, He Zhiran wanted to cherish the time under hypnosis.","Just now when she had hypnotized the Emperor of Southern Frontier, she discovered that she didn't know if it was because she hadn't rested well these days, but she felt a little dizzy during the hypnosis, and she was worried that this hypnosis would not last very long.","Therefore, it was best to hurry up and inquire about the things that needed to be asked.","\"Do you know the whereabouts of the Mo family's father and son?\"","Emperor of Southern Frontier: “Didn’t Mo Qing die long ago? His head was still hung at the head of the city by the assassin to show the public.","I only know that the Sixth Son of Mo Family has been with Mr. Si Meng all day long, and the Seventh Son is detained in the Prince’s mansion, and the rest have died from his poison.”","Hearing this, He Zhiran looked at Mo Jiuye and said softly, \"A hypnotized person cannot lie. He really doesn't know.\"","Mo Jiuye also understood this principle. He did not get any useful information from the Emperor of Southern Frontier, and was clearly very disappointed.","However, he still planned to hurry up and ask more useful things while he had the chance.","“Why was Mr. Si Meng hiding in the secret room of your study?”","Emperor of Southern Frontier: \"He is my Empress's master. My Empress said that after he had recovered from his injuries, he could serve my Southern Frontier, and might even give me a big surprise. I know his abilities and thought that he might be helpful to me in the future, so I kept him there.\"","From this, there was no doubt that the master whom Yun Li absolutely refused to reveal during the interrogation was Mr. Si Meng.","While Mo Jiuye was quickly organizing this information in his mind, he continued to ask:","“Did the raid on the Mo family happen under your orders?”","Emperor of Southern Frontier: “My empress has some relationship with Prince Heng of Dashun. It was she who gave some forged letters to Prince Heng at first, to serve as evidence that the Mo family was colluding with the enemy and betraying the country.”","At the time when they hypnotized Yun Li, they did not think in this direction, so they did not ask about it.","Now it seemed that the Mo family being raided and exiled really did have something to do with Yun Li and Prince Heng of Southern Frontier. Thinking of the persecution suffered by the Mo family, it really was too cheap to just let them die like that at the beginning.","Although the Emperor of Southern Frontier did not directly participate in this matter, the plight of the Mo family was also inextricably linked to him.","If he was not still trying to continue asking some questions, Mo Jiuye would have wanted to skin and torture him now.","He Zhiran knew he was feeling upset, and gently held his hand.","\"Don't get angry. The person is in our hands. After you’re done asking questions, you can vent your anger however you want.\"","Mo Jiuye solemnly responded with an \"hmm\". He continued to ask:","\"Where is that black Southern Pearl?\"","Although he was angry, he had not forgotten about his wife’s affairs. After all, the original purpose of them sneaking into the Southern Frontier Imperial Palace was for this reason. As a result, they had unintentionally rescued the Sixth Son.","Emperor of Southern Frontier: “It’s in my private treasury.” He still didn’t know that his private treasury had already been emptied out.","He Zhiran was shaking the pocket watch in her hand when she suddenly felt dizzy in the head, and could no longer concentrate to continue the hypnosis.","The frequency of the swinging pocket watch became more and more irregular, to the point that she as the operator herself felt a little drowsy.","Mo Jiuye noticed her abnormality as soon as it happened. Thinking it was fatigue caused by the hypnosis, he quickly snatched the pocket watch from her hand.","\"Ranran, are you feeling uncomfortable somewhere?\"","\"I probably haven't rested well these past few days and am just a little dizzy. It's nothing!\"","As the two spoke, the Emperor of Southern Frontier had gradually woken up.","The originally expressionless face immediately revealed a look of horror.","He did not know what had happened just now. He only remembered a strange thing appearing in front of him, and then he started to feel drowsy.","\"Mo... Mo Jiuye, as long as you spare me, I can make you a Prince Consort of Southern Frontier from a different surname, and it will be passed down hereditarily and irreplaceably for generations, allowing the Mo family to enjoy endless glory and wealth.\"","As he spoke, the Emperor of Southern Frontier stared closely at Mo Jiuye's expression. Seeing that the other party did not react at all to his huge temptation, he immediately became anxious.","“Also, I can marry my most beloved daughter to you, so you don't have to worry about me going back on my word either.\"","He thought that by saying this, it would be a great temptation to Mo Jiuye. Unexpectedly, he was greeted with a violent beating...","This move caught the Emperor of Southern Frontier somewhat off guard. He instinctively used his elbows to protect his wrinkled face.","\"Mo Jiuye... you can make any request, as long as I can do it, I will agree.\"","Mo Jiuye simply ignored him and continued to vent his anger.","Of course, the best way to vent was to beat the man in front of him until even his own mother could not recognize him.","Although the Emperor of Southern Frontier had practiced martial arts before, after becoming emperor, he had been thinking about how to conquer Da Shun all day long, so his martial arts skills had basically fallen into neglect. Now he could only be beaten.","The more Mo Jiuye beat him, the more vigorous he became. The Emperor of Southern Frontier could not protect his head. Several of his teeth were knocked out.","With a mouthful of blood, he spit out several teeth.","Seeing this, He Zhiran suddenly felt her stomach churning.","She didn’t care to continue watching her husband deal with the villain. She hurriedly turned around and ran to the bathroom in the medical office.","Although Mo Jiuye was beating someone, he kept a constant eye on his wife's actions.","Seeing his wife covering her nose and running towards the medical office, he didn't know what had happened to her.","He cleanly chopped the back of the Emperor of Southern Frontier's neck to knock him unconscious, and then chased after her.","\"Ranran, what's wrong with you?\"","He Zhiran couldn’t answer him at all. She quickly ran into the bathroom and squatted in front of the toilet to throw up.","Seeing this, Mo Jiuye was shocked.","In his impression, although his wife looked rather frail, her health had always been very good. For her to be like this today, it must be because she hadn't rested well these past few days.","Thinking that his wife had worked hard to help him, Mo Jiuye suddenly felt a trace of guilt in his heart."]},{"number":283,"title":"Chapter 283: Are You Pregnant","paragraphs":["To find clues in southern Xinjiang was what the Mo Family men were supposed to do, but he was so incompetent that he could only bring his delicate wife on this trip.","Mo Jiuye felt more and more guilty the more he thought about it. He went up and gently helped He Zhiran smooth her back.","\"Ranran, this trip to southern Xinjiang has really tired you out. We'll arrange to leave here as soon as it's light.\"","He Zhiran was extremely uncomfortable at the moment and had no way to respond to his words.","After vomiting a large pile of gastric acid, she finally felt a little better and slowly stood up.","Mo Jiuye hurried up to support her and thoughtfully handed her a cup of clear water.","\"Ranran, I'll take you to the city to see the imperial physician when it's light.\" Mo Jiuye knew the saying that doctors don't heal themselves. He Zhiran probably thought the same.","He Zhiran shook her head: \"I'm fine, I can check it myself.\"","After she finished speaking, she had already been helped by Mo Jiuye to sit on a chair in the dining room. Then she placed several fingers on her wrist pulse.","This check was unexpected. He Zhiran was stunned herself.","She had originally thought it was gastroenteritis caused by the unfamiliar environment in southern Xinjiang. Unexpectedly...","She was pregnant!","Moreover, judging from the pulse and time, it should be almost two months.","At this moment, He Zhiran didn't know whether to laugh or cry.","The Mo Family had been hoping for the next generation, but this child had chosen this time to come.","They were currently in southern Xinjiang and would take the opportunity to leave soon.","It was not easy to bring along Sixth Elder Brother, Seventh Elder Brother and the two maids of Fourth Princess. Now she was also pregnant.","There was also the matter of July. It has now been confirmed that the person who persecuted the Mo Family men was Mr. Si Meng. He would go to the Western Border in July.","This might be the only chance to rescue Grandfather and Eldest and Second Elder Brothers.","Mr. Si Meng was a master of Gu techniques (poison techniques). To rescue people from his hands, she needed to know how to surgically remove Gu herself.","By then, she would probably have already given birth. How could she help Mo Jiuye rescue them?","The more He Zhiran thought about it, the more her head hurt. For a moment, she actually forgot to tell Mo Jiuye about this news.","Seeing her frowning expression, Mo Jiuye thought something serious had happened to her body.","He went up and grabbed his wife's hand with obvious anxiety in his tone that could not be faked.","\"Ranran, what's wrong with you? Let's go out now and I'll take you to see an imperial physician.\"","Seeing his changed expression, He Zhiran hurriedly said, \"I should be pregnant.\"","\"What? Ranran, you're pregnant?\" The worry in Mo Jiuye's eyes was instantly replaced by a flash of light.","Heaven knew how happy he was.","After becoming intimate with Ranran, he had been looking forward to them having the fruit of their love soon.","Now Ranran told him that there was already their child in her belly, and Mo Jiuye was happily stunned on the spot for a while.","Seeing his lack of reaction, He Zhiran thought that he, like her, felt that this little life had come at the wrong time.","\"I didn't expect him to choose this time either. Anyway, I will try my best to protect him well.\"","Hearing his wife say this, Mo Jiuye finally regained his composure.","\"Ranran, this is our child. Protecting him is my responsibility as his father. Don't worry, we'll figure out a way to leave southern Xinjiang today and go back home. You just focus on nurturing the fetus well.\"","The attentive He Zhiran noticed that when Mo Jiuye said these things, he stuttered a bit, apparently very nervous. He probably hadn't prepared to be a parent yet like her.","\"The child did come a little suddenly, but don't worry. I will definitely help bring Father and Eldest and Second Brother back safely.\"","Hearing his wife say this, Mo Jiuye felt that she must have misunderstood something.","\"No no no, your body is the priority now. The matter of rescuing my father and brothers will be handled by me and the other elder brothers. You just stay in Xi Ling Village and focus on nurturing the fetus when you go back.\"","His father and brothers were important, and so was his and Ranran's child. This kind of thing was originally something they men should undertake. Now getting his pregnant wife involved made Mo Jiuye feel very sorry. He should not let his pregnant wife take risks in the future.","Mo Jiuye's nervous emotions were very obvious. He Zhiran didn't want him to be too nervous and comforted:","\"Don't worry, I'm not that delicate.\"","\"No, you've already suffered a lot following me. Now that you're carrying our child, I must protect you well as your husband.\"","He Zhiran knew that her previous life in the army had made her not have the temperament of a little woman. Now that she had a man who doted on her, she should pretend to be more delicate. People always said that women who were too strong had no blessings.","\"Alright, I'll listen to you.\"","Mo Jiuye felt a warmth in his heart. He hugged his delicate and gentle wife into his arms and gently patted her back.","\"Let's try to set off back northwest today.\"","\"Okay.\" He Zhiran agreed with a sound and got up to go to the operating room to check on Sixth Elder Brother's situation: \"Sixth Elder Brother will wake up soon. After we've dealt with the Emperor of Southern Xinjiang, let's go out.\"","Originally, Mo Jiuye was still planning to torture the Emperor of Southern Xinjiang severely. The grievances in his heart for what he had done to the Mo Family could not be resolved even if he was skinned alive.","One reason now was that he was in a hurry to leave here and didn't have too much time to torture him. Another reason was that his wife was pregnant with his child, so he wanted to accumulate more blessings for his child and didn't plan to use those bloody methods.","So Mo Jiuye went to the front of the Emperor of Southern Xinjiang and broke his neck with a strong twist, while he looked on in horror.","Although he didn't torture the Emperor of Southern Xinjiang, he didn't intend to let him go just like that either.","Although the severed heads hung at the city gate back then were not really the Mo Family men, the Emperor of Southern Xinjiang was unaware. He deliberately hung the Mo Family men's heads at the city gate to make an example. This humiliation had to be avenged.","Therefore, when the two of them left the space, Mo Jiuye did not take the corpse of the Emperor of Southern Xinjiang out with them.","He carefully supported He Zhiran over the courtyard wall, preparing to bring Sixth Elder Brother in through the main entrance. This would make Sixth Elder Brother's appearance perfectly reasonable.","Unexpectedly, as soon as they walked out of the transfer station, they saw Shun Zi leading three officers and gesturing about something as they walked.","Seeing that the officers were holding drawings of Lan Er and Yu Er in their hands while Shun Zi pointed to their location.","\"This is bad, Shun Zi has led the officers here,\" He Zhiran said. Before she finished speaking, she had already taken out two repeating crossbows from the space.","Mo Jiuye took over the repeating crossbow. The two of them shot at the soldiers at the same time.","The three soldiers all fell down dead, while only Shun Zi was left with eyes and mouth wide open in shock.","Mo Jiuye pulled He Zhiran to Shun Zi with anger and disappointment written all over his face.","They never expected that the servant they had bought would try to sell them out so quickly.","Seeing them, Shun Zi's body shuddered instinctively. He immediately knelt down and kept kowtowing while making vague sounds from his mouth."]},{"number":284,"title":"Chapter 284: There Are Men on the Wall","paragraphs":["Shun Zi could read lips, but Mo Jiuye did not intend to communicate with him.","Because he already understood why Shun Zi was doing this.","Under the portraits of Lan Er and Yu Er, big words were written clearly, offering a reward of one hundred taels of silver for those who provided clues.","Presumably Shun Zi was doing this for the one hundred taels of reward.","Originally they had planned to return his contract of servitude when they left Southern Xinjiang, but unexpectedly, he did such a flattering trick.","It seemed that Shun Zi could not be kept either.","Mo Jiuye took Shun Zi's life with one palm strike, then carried his corpse together with several officials' corpses into the yard.","As long as no one discovered anything before they left, it would be fine.","After taking care of everything, the two brought the still unconscious Mo Jinnian into the house.","The appearance of Mo Jinnian shocked both the Fourth Elder Brother and the Seventh Elder Brother.","Especially the Seventh Elder Brother, who had been in the accident with the Sixth Elder Brother back then. Now that the brothers were reunited again, it was such a scene.","\"Ninth younger brother, where did you find the Sixth Elder Brother?\"","Mo Jiuye briefly recounted how he found the Sixth Elder Brother and how he killed the Emperor of Southern Xinjiang. He then said, \"Fourth Elder Brother, Seventh Elder Brother, now that the Emperor of Southern Xinjiang is dead, Southern Xinjiang will definitely be in chaos. We must take advantage of the chaos to leave here.\"","Both the Fourth Elder Brother and the Seventh Elder Brother agreed with his idea. It's just that when they thought of their current situation, they immediately lost confidence.","The Seventh Elder Brother sighed and said, \"Ninth younger brother, although Southern Xinjiang will be in chaos, you and Ninth Sister-in-law can leave, but if you bring Fourth Brother and me, I'm afraid it won't be so easy, let alone that it will drag Ninth Brother and Ninth Sister-in-law down.\"","In fact, He Zhiran and Mo Jiuye had already figured out a way to leave, mainly relying on her space. But this method could not be explained to the two elder brothers.","Mo Jiuye did not give too much explanation.","\"Don't worry, Ran Ran and I have figured out a way to take you away.\"","Since he said it like this, the Fourth Elder Brother and the Seventh Elder Brother did not object anymore.","There was no time to delay. They had better leave before the chaos in Southern Xinjiang.","Now the Fourth Elder Brother and the Seventh Elder Brother were sober. When He Zhiran took out the silver needles, she said, \"Fourth Elder Brother, Seventh Elder Brother, let me treat you first.\"","Before the two elder brothers could respond, He Zhiran's needles had already pricked their acupoints.","Soon, the two fell into a deep sleep. He Zhiran pricked the Sixth Elder Brother's acupoints as well and sent them all into the space together.","She then called Lan Er and Yu Er over, and did the same thing by pricking them unconscious and sending them into the space.","She and Mo Jiuye also re-dressed in the space before simply eating some food and preparing to leave the city.","At this moment, it was the early morning court in Southern Xinjiang.","All the civil and military officials of Southern Xinjiang were facing each other in the main hall.","They could not figure out why the Emperor did not come to the early morning court today.","At the same time, the harem of Southern Xinjiang was already in chaos.","The Emperor's personal guards and eunuchs gradually woke up, only to find that their master had disappeared.","The Empress was missing, and now the Emperor was missing too. Everyone did not know who to report the news to.","Helplessly, the head eunuch could only grit his teeth and go to the morning court.","It was a major issue, and the eunuch did not dare to widely publicize it. He could only tell the Crown Prince about it.","When the Crown Prince heard that His Majesty had disappeared, he was overjoyed in his heart, but he did not show it.","He only hoped that His Majesty would stay disappeared forever, so that he could inherit the country in name and substance.","Just as the Crown Prince was calculating his future in his heart, people had already come to inquire impatiently.","\"Your Highness the Crown Prince, how about His Majesty?\"","The Crown Prince didn't even think about it before announcing to everyone that His Majesty had disappeared.","Only in this way could he become the real person in charge.","Sure enough, after he announced this, everyone demanded that His Highness the Crown Prince take control of the situation.","Although the Crown Prince did not want His Majesty to come back, he still had to keep up appearances.","He immediately ordered all the soldiers in the city and the Imperial Guards to seal off the capital, absolutely not allowing the villain to escape.","...","Fortunately, Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran acted quickly. As the two reached the city gate, a large number of soldiers rushed over.","Seeing this, the guard soldiers at the gate knew that something big might have happened. They hurriedly sealed off the city gate.","Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran looked at each other, knowing clearly that it was no longer possible to leave the city openly.","But they had to get out while a large number of soldiers were guarding the city gate, only then would they be safe and sound.","\"Ran Ran, I'll hold you carefully and we'll jump over the city wall.\"","He Zhiran subconsciously glanced at her flat belly and nodded, \"Okay.\"","Now she also had someone to protect, she had to be extra careful in everything she did.","After all, it was broad daylight. Even with Mo Jiuye's excellent qinggong, such a big movement would attract the soldiers' attention.","He had just hugged He Zhiran and jumped onto the city wall when someone shouted, \"Quick, shoot arrows, someone is on the city wall!\"","Hearing the shouting, Mo Jiuye's first reaction was to protect He Zhiran, while speeding up at the same time.","Seeing the situation going badly, He Zhiran moved her thoughts and brought Mo Jiuye into the space.","With such means, she didn't want to take any risky actions.","The Xinjiang soldiers watched with their own eyes as the two people on the city wall disappeared in the blink of an eye. They all thought they were having hallucinations, and kept rubbing their eyes.","Two living people just disappeared like that in broad daylight. At this moment, if it wasn't daylight, they would have thought they saw ghosts.","Having been pulled into the space, Mo Jiuye was also very surprised, but at the moment he was most concerned about his wife's well-being.","\"Ran Ran, are you uncomfortable anywhere?\"","\"I'm fine, don't worry.\" He Zhiran said gently.","This was the critical point for them to leave. They absolutely could not have any accidents.","When they were on the city wall just now, they had already been seen by many officers and soldiers. So He Zhiran changed their outfits again.","Mo Jiuye's original gray coat was changed to green, and He Zhiran also changed into a brightly colored dress.","The two stayed in the space for about ten minutes before leaving again.","Their previous actions had already alerted more soldiers to chase outside the city.","When they appeared on the city wall again, there were not so many guards left. The two swiftly jumped off the city wall and walked naturally among the crowds.","Changing outfits was indeed a good way to hide their identities.","When the soldiers saw them on the city wall, they only saw the colors of their clothes. Now when searching outside the city, they could only use this clue.","There were some commoners on the official road outside the city. But because a large number of soldiers appeared, the commoners hid one after another.","They didn't know what had happened, and were afraid of getting involved. Without any important business, they didn't dare to stay any longer.","Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran kept their heads low, imitating the panicked fleeing appearance of the commoners as they moved forward.","On the way, they encountered soldiers interrogating them several times, but passed safely each time.","The two rushed for more than an hour before finally arriving at the entrance to the next city."]},{"number":285,"title":"Chapter 285: Our Kids are Healthy.","paragraphs":["Perhaps the South Xinjiang officials did not expect them to escape so quickly. The blockade order had not yet reached here, and this place still looked quite peaceful.","Neither of them had expected that the journey from the capital city would go so smoothly all the way.","With more people on the return trip, their SUV could no longer be used. Fortunately, He Zhiran had already raised horses in her space, and they came in handy now.","As for the carriages, as long as there was wood, the operating table could make them.","She made two carriages according to the style of carriages in this era, and Mo Jiuye harnessed the horses.","The carriages were rather special. They looked very low-key on the outside except for having no windows. The carriage doors could be locked to prevent people from looking inside. But there was a whole world inside the carriages.","Considering the physical condition of the fourth and seventh brothers, it was not suitable for them to travel long distances to begin with. If the carriages were uncomfortable as well, it would be hard to say whether the two of them could safely make it to the Northwest.","Therefore, she deliberately wrapped the entire interior of the carriages with thick cotton padding, so that lying on it would be as comfortable as a big bed in the modern world, which would make the ride much more bearable.","The lack of windows and the locks installed on the doors were also carefully considered countermeasures by He Zhiran.","If they encountered danger on the road, or when passing through city gates and got questioned, she could lock the carriage doors early and withdraw them into her space.","That way, the people inside would be unable to see the outside environment, directly solving her dilemma of exposing her space.","And then there was Rice Ball. They had all seen the little guy go out with them with their own eyes. With more people on the return trip, they could not leave behind any excuses that would arouse suspicion. He had to be taken out as well.","The carriages were ready in the blink of an eye.","He Zhiran used her mind to send the three brothers into one carriage, and Lan Er and Yu Er into the other carriage.","She then picked up Rice Ball and said softly, \"Rice Ball be good. We're going home. You'll have to squeeze in with those two sisters for a few days.\"","Upon hearing its master's words, Rice Ball rubbed hard against her in her arms, clearly unhappy.","But it had to obey its master to get delicious bamboo shoots and formula milk.","So the little guy looked at its master with aggrieved eyes, and reluctantly burrowed into the carriage.","With everything ready, He Zhiran was about to leave the space to get on the road as soon as possible.","Mo Jiuye looked at the two carriages, troubled.","Seeing him standing there with no intention of leaving, He Zhiran asked, \"Is there anything else that needs to be handled?\"","Mo Jiuye pointed at the two carriages and said, \"Two carriages. We need to go out and hire a coachman.\"","\"No need. I can drive too. We'll each drive one carriage,\" she disagreed with hiring someone. She was already afraid after a close call.","What if the coachman they hired was an unscrupulous person? Wouldn't that be asking for trouble?","Mo Jiuye knew this reasoning all too well. But at the moment, his wife was pregnant, and it was simply inappropriate for her to travel long distances. If anything went wrong on the way, he would probably never forgive himself in this lifetime.","At that moment, the guilt in Mo Jiuye's heart had already overflown. But under the current circumstances, if he didn't do as his wife said, he would be at a loss.","\"In that case, let's take it slow. If there's any discomfort, you must tell me right away.\"","Seeing that he agreed, He Zhiran hurriedly sat in the carriage.","\"Alright, I know. We have to hurry.\"","As soon as she finished speaking, the couple had already appeared outside the space with two carriages.","The husband and wife looked at each other, then started the carriages in unison. The carriages moved quickly and soon arrived at the city gate.","The blockade had not been completely implemented there yet, presumably because the news of the disappearance of the South Xinjiang Emperor had not spread here yet.","However, the theft at the Crown Prince's mansion had already caused a huge uproar in the city. Therefore, routine inspections of passersby were essential.","At this time, the few people in the carriages were still unconscious. The couple drove the carriages to a remote place and withdrew them into the space. Then they walked towards the city gate nonchalantly on foot.","Their makeup was no different from that of ordinary commoners in South Xinjiang. At the city gate, the guards only asked them a few simple questions before letting them pass.","Having easily passed the first city, the couple did not relax their vigilance.","The disappearance of the Emperor of South Xinjiang was such a huge incident that the news would surely spread quickly everywhere. They only hoped that they could travel faster so that they could return to Dashi territory before South Xinjiang was completely under blockade.","After finding a secluded place, He Zhiran took the two carriages back out of the space to continue on their way.","About an hour after setting off, He Zhiran heard Lan Er and Yu Er talking inside the carriage.","\"Sister Lan Er, where exactly are we?\"","Yu Er had just finished speaking when there was a shriek from inside the carriage, \"Ah... Sister Lan Er, there is a furry ball moving. What is this?\"","It was pitch black inside the carriage. Rice Ball was sitting next to Yu Er. So Lan Er did not know what furry ball Yu Er was talking about.","Besides, she had always been calm by nature. In such a place of unknown danger, even if there really was some kind of furry ball, she would not scream like Yu Er did.","To keep Yu Er from screaming further, Lan Er hurriedly covered her mouth and said in a low voice, \"Don't make any noise. We should be in a carriage.\"","Lan Er had already sensed that swaying feeling and determined that they must be in a carriage.","Yu Er's eyes were wide open as she tried her best to calm herself down.","Hearing their voices, He Zhiran quickly responded, \"Don't be afraid. That's my pet. And you're very safe in the carriage.\"","Hearing He Zhiran's voice brought some relief to Yu Er's startled heart.","He Zhiran went on to explain, \"We're on our way to Dashi. To prevent any danger on the road, I specifically bought two carriages without windows. And the furry ball you mentioned is my pet. It's very well behaved and won't hurt you.\"","Lan Er understood the urgency of the situation. Besides, she could feel that it was He Zhiran driving the carriage.","What virtues and talents did she and her sister possess that they were not only saved by this husband and wife, but that the couple was also taking such great risks to bring them away from South Xinjiang.","She, Lan Er, would remember this kindness.","As long as she still lived, she would stay by the side of Madam Jiu to serve her in the future, with loyalty befitting service to a princess."]},{"number":286,"title":"Chapter 286: Mo Jinnian Wakes Up","paragraphs":["Yu Er naturally did not need to say much, she did not have that many thoughts, and had always listened to Lan Er. When the Fourth Princess chose to bring her along for the marriage alliance, it was because she was obedient.","He Zhiran did not know what Lan Er was thinking, he explained things clearly, then continued on the road.","On Mo Jiuye's side, the first to wake up was Seventh Elder Brother. His surroundings were similarly pitch black, but for someone with martial arts skills, this kind of darkness was nothing at all.","Realizing the environment had changed, he did not ask questions right away, but looked around.","The slightly bumpy feeling and the sound of horse hooves told him he was in a carriage.","Fourth elder brother and Sixth elder brother were by his side.","He first pushed Fourth elder brother.","\"Fourth elder brother, wake up.\"","Fourth elder brother was already showing signs of waking up, and was fully awake after Mo Yuance pushed him like this.","Mo Jiuye also heard the movement in the carriage, and quickly explained: \"Fourth elder brother, Seventh elder brother, don't worry, you are very safe now.\"","Hearing their ninth younger brother's voice, the two brothers were completely at ease.","Although they did not know the specific situation, and did not know why they would wake up in a carriage, in any case, with their ninth younger brother present, they must be safe.","By now it was almost noon, and the carriage had entered the next city.","According to his understanding, this was the largest city in the Southern Borderlands, and it would probably take them until nightfall to get through it.","Even if they were in a hurry, they had to take care of his wife's health.","He discussed with He Zhiran for a while, and decided to rest in the city for a while first, and eat something before continuing on their way.","It would be best to leave the city after dark. Even resting in the carriage would be safer than in the city.","After all, there was no knowing when the news of the Southern Borderlands Emperor's disappearance would reach this place. It would be troublesome for them to want to leave again later.","According to plan, the two drove the carriage to a more remote place. Mo Jiuye pretended to go out to buy food, when in fact He Zhiran was buying some instant food in her space.","The husband and wife opened the carriage compartments separately, first took care of personal matters, then ate ravenously.","From last night until now, this was the first meal they were eating, and they were hungry even without much exertion.","Seeing its master, Bao Dan immediately climbed into her arms to act coquettish.","The soft bleating melted He Zhiran's heart, and she quickly hid to the side to prepare its favorite food.","After eating her fill, just as He Zhiran was getting ready to urge them to continue on their way, there was movement from Mo Jiuye's side.","\"Ninth younger brother, ninth younger sister-in-law, come quickly, Sixth elder brother is awake.\" Mo Yuance was clearly somewhat excited.","Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran hurried over.","Sixth elder brother's condition was much better than Fourth elder brother and Seventh elder brother's. At this time he was already sitting up, it was just that his eyes still seemed a little dazed.","\"Sixth elder brother.\"","\"Sixth elder brother.\"","\"Old Six.\"","The three brothers called out to Mo Jinnian at the same time.","Mo Jinnian met his brothers' eyes, and was still a little confused, especially when looking at Mo Yuance.","\"Seventh younger brother, have we been saved?\" He remembered that he and Seventh younger brother had been poisoned together on the battlefield, and after waking up, they had been locked in a pitch-black underground prison cell where he couldn't see his fingers.","The guards would come daily and beat him routinely, grasping the force precisely so that he was badly mangled but couldn't die.","This kind of torture continued for about a month, until finally one day, a mysterious person came and cast a gu worm on him while he was only hazily conscious.","But now he was with his brothers, could everything in his memories have been a dream?","Since he couldn't figure it out himself, he could only ask Seventh younger brother, who had the same experience as him that year.","Seeing his brothers awake in this state, Mo Xiuyan felt his heart ache.","\"Sixth younger brother, we brothers all went through the same ordeal, falling into the hands of a man called Mr. Si Meng from the Southern Borderlands. You and Seventh younger brother were both controlled by his puppet worm gu. It's normal that you don't remember what happened during that time.","Fortunately Ninth younger brother and Ninth younger sister-in-law noticed something amiss, and came to rescue us brothers, so we have lived to see this day.\"","After listening to Fourth elder brother say so much, Mo Jinnian noticed the speaker.","The voice was clearly Ninth younger brother's, but the person wasn't...","\"Who are you?\"","At this time Mo Jiuye could not reveal his identity, he could only explain: \"Sixth elder brother, we are currently in the Southern Borderlands' territory. I disguised myself like this to facilitate traveling.\"","Seeing the situation, Fourth elder brother also helped explain: \"Sixth younger brother, this really is Ninth younger brother, there's no mistake.\"","Mo Jiuye was in a hurry to get going, and could not explain much to Sixth elder brother.","\"Sixth elder brother, let Fourth elder brother and Seventh brother tell you what happened. We'll continue on our way. Call me immediately if you feel any discomfort.\"","If it were normal times, seeing Sixth elder brother awake, Mo Jiuye would definitely have talked with him at length. But the current situation did not allow him to do so. He had to get out of the city before nightfall.","The carriage slowly started up, and he could hear the conversation inside the carriage compartment.","Fourth elder brother and Seventh brother told Mo Jinnian everything they had learned from Ninth younger brother.","After listening, Mo Jinnian's temples bulged with rage, and he fiercely punched the carriage compartment.","Mo Jiuye only felt the carriage behind him make a creaking sound, and looking back, the compartment had cracked open a little...","Fortunately his wife had chosen good quality wood to make the compartment, otherwise with that punch from Sixth elder brother, the compartment would probably have been smashed to smithereens.","Mo Jiuye slowed down the carriage and spoke towards the inside of the carriage: \"Sixth elder brother, everything is already in the past. No matter what, now that us brothers can meet again, we should think about how to live well in the future.\"","Mo Yuance also persuaded: \"That's right Sixth elder brother, we are all men, we need to learn to accept reality.\"","It wasn't that Mo Jinnian couldn't accept reality, it was that the more he thought about it, the angrier he got.","He, an eight foot tall man, had actually been controlled by a bug, and that wasn't enough, he had even foolishly sold his life for others.","As a Mo family man, he felt it was all too humiliating.","However, just now Fourth elder brother and Seventh younger brother had told him that he could reunite with his brothers mostly thanks to Ninth younger brother and Ninth younger sister-in-law's efforts.","Ninth younger brother and Ninth younger sister-in-law had risked their lives coming to the Southern Borderlands to rescue them, no matter what he would treasure this second life he had been given."]},{"number":287,"title":"Chapter 287: I will protect you and our child.","paragraphs":["\"I understand everything you said, I'm just a little annoyed,\" Mo Jinnian said, seeing that the Sixth Elder Brother was no longer so agitated.","Only then did He Zhiran feel a little more at ease. She had just increased the speed of the carriage a little when the carriage door behind her was opened from the inside.","\"Ninth younger brother, I'll go catch up with Ninth Sister-in-Law's carriage to let her rest for a while,\" Mo Jinnian said, and he was about to jump off the carriage.","He Zhiran also noticed his action and quickly said, \"Sixth Elder Brother, I can do it. Your body has not fully recovered since you just relieved the Gu poison, so stay in the carriage these days to rest and take care of the Fourth and Seventh Elder Brothers at the same time.\"","It wasn't that she was determined to drive the carriage herself, she and Mo Jiuye had already agreed that if they encountered an emergency on the road, they would lock the carriage door and send the carriage into the space together.","If the Sixth Elder Brother came to drive, she wouldn't be able to continue operating like this.","In order for everyone to safely leave Southern Frontier, He Zhiran had to grit her teeth and persevere no matter what.","In fact, Mo Jiuye was happy to let his elder brother replace his wife in driving the carriage when he saw that the Sixth Elder Brother was fine.","But thinking of the dangers they might encounter on the road, it would be easy if it was just him alone, but with two carriages and seven people, without his wife's space, it would be impossible to resolve the crisis.","Mo Jiuye looked at his wife distressedly and persuaded her forcefully, \"Sixth Elder Brother, Zhiran understands medicine, you should listen to her.\"","When the two of them mentioned his physical condition, Mo Jinnian only then carefully sensed it.","Except for some dizziness and discomfort, he was fine.","Besides, he didn't know about Ninth Sister-in-Law's pregnancy. Seeing that the couple insisted, he had no reason to be stubborn.","\"All right, I'll rest first in the carriage. Ninth Sister-in-Law, call me if you get tired to switch.\"","\"Okay, I'll call Sixth Elder Brother when I'm tired,\" He Zhiran responded and continued to drive the carriage forward.","The journey went smoothly all the way and arrived at the city gate on time.","It seemed that Southern Frontier had been shocked by the two people sneaking in from the border recently. There was no inspection when they came in, but there were obviously many more checkpoints when going back.","As before, the two found a secluded alley according to plan.","Mo Jiuye could hear the conversations of several elder brothers in the carriage. In order to prevent them from having doubts, he felt it necessary to explain.","\"Fourth Elder Brother, Sixth Elder Brother, Seventh Elder Brother, the city gate is not far ahead, and there are guards guarding it. Zhiran and I will change our looks so we won't be recognized. We plan to temporarily park the carriages here and go to the city gate to take a look. Please try not to make any noise in the carriage so as not to attract unnecessary trouble.\"","\"You and Ninth Sister-in-Law just go ahead and be extra careful,\" the Fourth Elder Brother responded. Then the carriage instantly quieted down.","Seeing this, He Zhiran waved her hand and put both carriages into her space.","She and Mo Jiuye then headed towards the city gate without any cover.","By this time, the sky was already dark. Ordinary people basically wouldn't leave the city at night unless they had something important to do. Therefore, apart from a group of guards at the city gate, you could rarely see civilians.","Naturally, their arrival was subject to some interrogation, but Mo Jiuye managed to get through smoothly, and they successfully left the city.","The first thing after leaving the city was to immediately take out the carriages.","Fortunately, the Mo family brothers trusted Ninth Younger Brother and Sister-in-Law enough. Even if they felt something was a little off, they did not doubt anything.","After all, they were still in Southern Frontier Territory. They couldn't stay at an inn at night, and since they were already on the official road, it would take a long time to travel to the next city. Sleeping outdoors was inevitable.","Fortunately, although Sixth Elder Brother would occasionally get dizzy, taking care of Fourth and Seventh Elder Brothers was not a problem.","Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran found a secluded place at the foot of a mountain to rest. He Zhiran helped Sixth Elder Brother with acupuncture to alleviate his dizziness.","In fact, Sixth Elder Brother's dizziness was not difficult to solve. He had just had his consciousness sealed for too long, and his brain was a little unaccustomed to being suddenly restarted again. Even without acupuncture, he would recover after some rest.","Without talking all night, everyone set off again before dawn the next day.","Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran were already prepared to encounter trouble on the road, but whether it was because the Emperor of Southern Frontier was missing and no one issued orders, or some other reason, in short, their journey was smoother than they had imagined by countless times.","After four days of travelling, the group finally arrived at the border of Southern Frontier.","It was already night time. In Mo Jiuye's opinion, it would be much easier to pass the border checkpoint at this time of poor visibility than during the day. Besides, he still had something important to do that was most suitable for this dark night with obscure vision.","It might take longer to get through the checkpoint this time, so Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran did not dare to be careless. They sent the people inside the carriage into the space only after everyone had fallen asleep.","Mo Jiuye looked at his wife guiltily and said solemnly, \"Ranran, let's go.\"","\"Okay.\"","Mo Jiuye gently put his arm around her waist, leapt up high, and then began to observe the situation at the border checkpoint.","There were two teams of patrolling soldiers at the checkpoint, rotating back and forth to exchange shifts.","There would be a gap of about ten seconds during the shift change.","Mo Jiuye planned to take advantage of this ten-second gap to use their superior lightness skill to leap over with his wife.","He Zhiran was nervous at this moment. After all, the situation was different from when they sneaked in.","The two of them still hadn't been found after the infiltration. The Southern Frontier barracks must be on high alert now.","Mo Jiuye felt her nervousness and gently comforted, \"Trust me, I will definitely protect you and our child at all costs...\"","As he was thinking, the two had already leapt up high, heading straight for the checkpoint.","They landed more than 50 meters beyond the Southern Frontier checkpoint.","Seeing the patrolling soldiers turning back and possibly spotting them soon, He Zhiran took Mo Jiuye straight into the space.","Mo Jiuye did not idle either, as he had to prepare for that important matter.","\"Ranran, don't look this way.\"","He Zhiran knew what Mo Jiuye was going to do. Just thinking about that scene made her want to vomit.","\"Okay, I'll go to the medical room. Call me when you're done.\"","Seeing his wife walking away, Mo Jiuye swiftly cut off the Southern Frontier Emperor's head.","When they left the space again, Mo Jiuye took He Zhiran and continued using their superior lightness skill, running several hundred meters away to stand under a thick big tree.","At the same time, He Zhiran also used her mind power to take out the Southern Frontier Emperor's corpse and severed head.","Mo Jiuye casually picked up the corpse and head from the ground.","\"Ranran, just hide here and wait for me. If there's danger, go into the space in time. If something happens on my side, I'll also withdraw as soon as possible to meet you here, then you just need to come out and check occasionally.\"","He Zhiran knew that since she didn't know lightness techniques and was pregnant, following him would not be helpful but a burden instead.","However, letting Mo Jiuye take such risks alone, she really couldn't stop worrying."]},{"number":288,"title":"Chapter 288: I'll be right here waiting for you.","paragraphs":["Suddenly, she thought of the bulletproof vest from her previous life. Bullets that were so powerful could be blocked, let alone the cold weapons of this era.","\"Wait a minute,\" He Zhiran softly called out to stop him.","Mo Jiuye didn't know what his wife was going to do, but he obediently listened and didn't move.","He Zhiran purchased a top-of-the-line bulletproof vest on Taobao Online Mall.","\"Wear this,\" she said.","Mo Jiuye looked at the strange garment in front of him and asked, \"Why?\" Although he asked, he still obediently put on the bulletproof vest.","\"This is called a bulletproof vest. You can say it's knife and gun proof,\" He Zhiran explained quickly.","Mo Jiuye had never heard of such a wonderful thing before.","However, now was not the time for him to be too curious. After putting on the bulletproof vest, He Zhiran also hung a bag full of grenades on him.","Naturally, there was no need to explain in detail how to use the grenades. When Mo Jiuye had nothing to do in his personal space, he would often study them. Although he had never actually used them before, he knew how to use them by heart.","Feeling the heavy sensation on his body, Mo Jiuye felt a warmth in his heart. He instructed He Zhiran again before taking the Southern Frontier Emperor's corpse and leaving.","He Zhiran watched his figure run away quickly, and said softly:","\"Be sure to stay safe. I'll be waiting right here for you to come back.\"","Mo Jiuye carried the Southern Frontier Emperor's corpse, used his lightness skill to leap over the heads of those Southern Frontier soldiers, and landed on the highest point at the pass.","He quickly hung the head there, and randomly threw the body below.","Mo Jiuye's series of actions would inevitably attract the attention of the Southern Frontier soldiers.","He had just thrown the corpse on the ground when someone pointed to the top and shouted, \"There's a spy up there!\"","The soldiers swarmed up, arrows aimed at Mo Jiuye.","Outnumbered, Mo Jiuye had no intention of lingering in battle. He threw a grenade towards the area with the most people.","With a loud boom, the Southern Frontier soldiers were blown high into the air.","At the same time, a deep large pit was blasted into the ground.","The soldiers who continued to chase Mo Jiuye didn't react in time, and many of them fell into the deep pit.","Mo Jiuye took advantage of the chaos to use his lightness skill and ran towards He Zhiran.","The Southern Frontier had a large number of soldiers. After some of them reacted, they chased after him again.","Mo Jiuye threw out two more grenades, blowing those soldiers away.","With just three grenades, the Southern Frontier had already suffered heavy losses. The surviving soldiers were frightened and didn't dare to recklessly give chase. They could only keep shooting arrows in his direction.","Arrows rained down towards Mo Jiuye. Even with his agile figure, he couldn't completely avoid so many arrows.","He was careless for a moment, and two arrows fell on his shoulder and back.","Mo Jiuye knew that this injury was inevitable, but the location was still good, and it wasn't fatal.","However, the expected pain did not come. Mo Jiuye glanced back at his shoulder, where his outer garment was already damaged, but there was no arrow piercing it like before.","He moved his arm, and it was still flexible without any sign of injury.","He curiously touched his back again. Similarly, he could feel his clothes were ripped but there was no arrow stuck in it, nor was there any pain.","Mo Jiuye suddenly realized that this must be due to the effect of the garment his wife gave him.","No wonder she told him to wear that piece of clothing before leaving. It really could save lives.","Accompanied by cries of grief, Mo Jiuye easily escaped from the pass.","Seeing the flames and smoke rising into the sky in the direction of the pass, He Zhiran knew that Mo Jiuye had successfully hung up the Southern Frontier Emperor's head.","Now that she didn't see him coming back, her heart was in her throat.","He Zhiran could confirm that in her two lifetimes, this was the first time she felt such nervous emotions.","She subconsciously looked at her still flat belly and murmured softly, \"Baby, pray with Mommy for your Daddy to come home safely.\"","Fortunately, as soon as she finished speaking, a tall figure appeared before her.","\"Ranran, were you very anxious waiting for me?\"","Seeing him come back, He Zhiran took the initiative to throw herself into his arms for the first time.","\"Not anxious. As long as you're safe, that's good enough.\"","Now she had one more feeling - how anxiously the sisters-in-law waited at home when the Mo Family Men went to battle in the past.","Mo Jiuye could feel her tension. He held her in his arms and comforted, \"Don't worry, I'll be fine.\"","He Zhiran felt the familiar warmth and her reason did not disappear.","\"We can't stay here long. Let's leave quickly.\"","\"Okay,\" Mo Jiuye agreed and carried He Zhiran towards Da Shun.","Entering Da Shun's territory, this place was more familiar to Mo Jiuye than anywhere else.","When he led troops to garrison here for many years, he had memorized the terrain extremely clearly. Therefore, he didn't need to exert any effort to smoothly leave the border.","At this time, the eastern sky was already brightening. He Zhiran felt it was about time and quickly took out the carriage from her personal space.","Mo's brothers woke up to find it was already bright outside, and they could also feel the swaying of the carriage as it moved.","The slit in the broken carriage let in a ray of light.","When Mo Jinnian woke up from this nap, he felt his dizzy problem was instantly cured.","He knocked on the carriage door, \"Ninth brother, where are we? Have we encountered any danger?\"","\"Sixth brother, we've already entered Da Shun's territory. Everything is going very smoothly,\" Mo Jiuye's reply could be described as understated.","\"You said we've already entered Da Shun?\" The sixth brother was clearly very surprised.","With the current tense situation in the Southern Frontier, how did the ninth brother and his wife manage to get out smoothly?","The more Mo Jinnian thought about it, the more he felt something was wrong.","\"Ninth brother, how did you manage to return to Da Shun without making any noise at all?\"","The fourth and seventh brothers were also curious and wanted to hear the ninth brother's explanation.","At this time, Mo Jiuye had already stopped the carriage at the roadside and opened the carriage door.","His explanation was a bit far-fetched. After all, it was impossible to make this kind of thing sound reasonable.","\"Last night the Southern Frontier Emperor was killed. His head was hung at the highest point at the pass. The Southern Frontier army camp was thrown into chaos, so I took the opportunity to escape.\"","As the carriage door opened, the sixth brother jumped out.","He didn't expect such a big thing to happen in the Southern Frontier.","If Mo Jinnian didn't know that the ninth brother had been on his way to Da Shun, he would have suspected that he did it.","\"I don't know which righteous hero did this, but it's extremely gratifying.\"","The reason why the Mo Family Men kept rushing onto the battlefield was all thanks to this Southern Frontier Emperor.","If it wasn't for him repeatedly launching wars, they could have spent more time together in the capital.","Moreover, because of one battle after another, they faced the pain of losing loved ones and comrades countless times. Although the ninth brother had found so many brothers back, Mo Jinnian still hated the Southern Frontier Emperor.","Although the Southern Frontier Emperor’s death was gratifying, Mo Jinnian still couldn't believe the reason given by the ninth brother.","\"Ninth brother, I'm a light sleeper. Even if the Southern Frontier army camp was thrown into chaos, it’s impossible there wouldn’t be any noise at all.\"","Just as Mo Jiuye was thinking about how to explain, He Zhiran also released the other two from the carriage. She hurried over to explain.","\"Sixth brother doesn't know that the needles I gave you have a sleeping aid effect. It's not surprising you didn't hear any sounds at all.\"","\"So that's how it is. Ninth brother's wife's medical skills are truly amazing. I woke up today feeling my body was very relaxed and my dizzy problem was cured.\"","Now, Mo Jinnian believed it.","Recalling when the ninth brother's wife gave him acupuncture, he did feel sleepy.","No wonder he didn't hear the big commotion outside."]},{"number":289,"title":"Chapter 289: Shoot Yourself in the Foot","paragraphs":["Mo Jinnian felt that his body had no discomfort at all, so he could not let his ninth younger sister-in-law, a woman from a fallen family, continue driving the carriage.","\"Ninth younger brother, ninth younger sister-in-law, my body is fine now, so let me drive the carriage!\"","\"Well, since sixth older brother's body has recovered, let He Zhiran rest in the carriage.\"","Mo Jiuye had almost worried himself to death these past few days. If it wasn't to safely leave Southern Xinjiang, he would never have let his pregnant wife work so hard under any circumstances.","Now that they were safe, the carriage driving should naturally be handed over to his sixth older brother.","He Zhiran would not be stubborn at this time. Although she did not have much reaction in her early pregnancy, after driving all night until now, she could feel her body was somewhat overwhelmed.","\"Then I'll have to trouble sixth older brother.\"","After He Zhiran finished speaking, she drilled into the carriage. What she needed now was to rest well.","Lan Er and Yu Er were also very perceptive. Seeing her come in, they hurriedly made room for her to sit in a spacious spot.","\"Ninth young madam, you look a little unwell. You must be too exhausted from driving all night. Please rest here and tell us if you need anything.\"","As Lan Er spoke, she had already covered He Zhiran with a thick blanket.","Rice Ball cleverly snuggled up at the top of its owner's head, incessantly acting cute.","He Zhiran reached out and patted its furry little head, \"Rice Ball, be good and let me rest for a while.\"","Rice Ball seemed to see its owner's fatigue. It murmured an agreement and obediently lay there to sleep.","The carriage continued on its way. Passing through towns, they no longer needed to hide. At night everyone entered an inn to rest, and traveled during the daytime.","Ten days later, the group finally arrived safely in Yunchéng.","The carriage slowly drove towards Xilin village. As soon as they entered the village, they heard a commotion.","\"Official, what I said is all true. If you don't believe me, go take a look at the Mo family home.\"","\"Humph! Daring to offend the Mo family, it seems your Cui family really doesn't want to survive in Yunchéng anymore.\"","\"Official, that ninth young master Mo and his wife haven't shown their faces for over half a month. If they didn't leave the city, why wouldn't they have appeared by now?\"","Hearing someone mention the Mo family, Mo Jiuye instinctively sped up the carriage.","Walking closer, he saw two Cui family members leading several yamen runners heading into the village.","From the earlier conversation, it was not difficult to hear that the Cui family resented them. Discovering that he and He Zhiran had not appeared for half a month, they had secretly observed and then reported it to the authorities.","The reason was simple. Exiled criminals could never leave this place without the emperor's special pardon.","The Cui family had wanted to take this opportunity to get revenge for their whole clan...","Hearing the sound of hoofbeats behind them, the yamen runners turned around.","At a glance, Mo Jiuye recognized Ma Junshan.","\"Magistrate Ma, what brings you to Xilin village today?\"","Seeing Mo Jiuye, Ma Junshan's face immediately showed joy.","\"So it turns out to be Ninth Young Master. Where have you been?\"","As he spoke, Ma Junshan glared fiercely at the two Cui family members.","The Cui family members' hearts tightened when they saw Mo Jiuye.","They had observed around the Mo residence for several days and hadn’t seen Mo Jiuye or his wife at all. Only then did they dare to report it to the authorities in order to get revenge for the Cui clan.","Who would have thought that after all their coaxing to get the yamen runners to come, the person in question would show up instead! Wasn't this shooting themselves in the foot?","In fact, the Cui family had really overestimated their abilities. They didn't even think about the relationship between the Mo family and the county magistrate. Besides, the Mo family had Mo Chuhan working as a subprefect at the county yamen. What were the chances that going to report it would accomplish anything for them?","If it wasn't for the Cui deliberately making a loud fuss outside the yamen gates, Meng Huaining wouldn’t even have sent people over.","He had been visiting the Mo residence very frequently recently, so he naturally knew about Mo Jiuye and his wife's absence.","It was something that even the county magistrate didn't want to get involved in, yet the Cui family insisted on making it a big issue.","The Cui family righteously told the yamen that the Mo family were exiled criminals. Now they actually dared to privately leave Yunchéng, which could easily cause trouble for other places.","The common people were soft-hearted. Hearing the Cui family's reasonable-sounding words, they echoed along in agreement.","Meng Huaining had no choice but to first send Mo Chuhan back to Xilin village and pretend that Mo Jiuye was sick in bed. That way, when he sent over some yamen runners, they could just say whatever they wanted after taking a look.","In any case, the Cui family couldn't enter others' private chambers to check. The yamen runners could just say whatever they wanted after taking a look.","He didn't expect that Mo Jiuye would return at this time, so they didn't need to keep up the act.","Mo Jiuye disdainfully glanced at the two Cui family members, then said to Ma Junshan: \"I asked someone to buy two carriages. I just went into the city to retrieve them.\"","Ma Junshan had originally planned to give Mo Jiuye a hint in front of the Cui family, but unexpectedly, Mo Jiuye smoothed it over himself.","\"No wonder. I heard the magistrate mention a few days ago that the Mo family wanted to buy horses. I didn't expect them to buy them back so soon.\"","Seeing Mo Jiuye chatting happily with the yamen runners, the two Cui family members wanted to slip away.","But before they could, they were stopped by the runners who had been standing in place.","\"You two, you think you can run away after falsely accusing someone?\"","\"Official, it's a misunderstanding, a misunderstanding...\" The Cui family immediately pleaded for mercy.","Although they still firmly believed that Mo Jiuye and his wife had not been in Xilin recently, the current situation was already very clear.","These yamen runners were obviously biased towards the Mo family to begin with. Now that Mo Jiuye had appeared, they had no argument left.","The yamen runners came forward and mercilessly whipped the two men several times. \"You say it's just a misunderstanding so casually. Come back to the yamen with me and report to the county magistrate for punishment.\"","Hearing they still had to go to the yamen, the two Cui family members were so scared their legs went soft and they knelt down.","\"Official, spare our lives! We know we were wrong and won't dare do it again.\"","The yamen runners completely ignored them and tied up both men without another word.","Seeing this, Ma Junshan cupped his fists towards Mo Jiuye, \"Ninth Young Master, we will take these two back to the yamen for handling.\"","Mo Jiuye returned the gesture. \"Very well, thank you all for your hard work. When you have time, please come to my humble home for a drink.\"","Speaking of drinking, the yamen runners couldn't help swallowing.","They had tasted the Mo family's cooking once before. Even the best restaurant food in town couldn't compare.","\"Alright, when we brothers have time, we will certainly come to bother you.\"","Whether they would truly be able to come still depended on if their boss allowed it.","Now that they all worked under Eighth Young Master, it was not common for just anyone to have the qualification to come eat at their superior's home.","Mo Jiuye saw the group off before driving the carriage on towards home.","On the road, Mo Jinnian asked, \"Ninth younger brother, what exactly happened back there?\"","The brothers had hurried on their trip, only resting at night at inns, with hardly any conversation. It was not surprising that Mo Jinnian was unclear about the situation in Xilin Village.","Mo Jiuye briefly recounted what had happened when they first arrived at Xilin Village.","Mo Jinnian angrily banged the carriage panel, \"Truly horrible people! Just wait until I take care of them!\""]},{"number":290,"title":"Chapter 290: It's Good to have You All Alive.","paragraphs":["Mo Jiuye knew that Sixth Elder Brother had a fiery temper, and advised: \"These ordinary commoners are not worth getting angry over, Sixth Elder Brother, don't get angry.\"","\"Humph! This is truly a case of when the tiger falls in Pingyang it is bullied by dogs.\" Sixth Elder Brother felt more and more uncomfortable the more he thought about it, remembering what an impressive presence the Mo family used to have in the capital.","That dog emperor had no eye for talent, My Mo family's men shed blood on the battlefields to protect the great lands of Dashun, yet he was still unable to tolerate us.","Mo Jiuye could understand Sixth Elder Brother's feelings. He too had felt similarly indignant when they were first sentenced to exile.","There was no use in talking too much about these things, you could only slowly become accepting on your own.","\"Sixth Elder Brother, we're almost home, don't let Mother see you in low spirits.\"","Sixth Elder Brother nodded: \"I know.\"","Soon, the two carriages arrived at the front gate of their home.","The first to run out at the sound of hooves and take a look was Second Sister-in-Law.","With one glance she spotted Mo Jiuye sitting in the carriage at the front.","Second Sister-in-Law excitedly shouted loudly: \"Ninth younger brother is back...Ninth younger brother is back...\"","Her voice was louder than the other sisters-in-law to begin with. This loud shout made the whole family hear it clearly.","In an instant, some people ran over from the back yard, others came out from the kitchen. Mo Chuhan no longer needed to pretend to be Mo Jiuye inside the house. He rushed out in one leap.","Mo Jiuye had already gotten off his carriage and entered the yard first, everyone's gaze was focused on him, and they neglected Mo Jinnian behind him.","While Mo Jiuye was surrounded by family members, Mo Jinnian jumped off his carriage and squeezed into the crowd. The instant he saw Old Lady Mo he knelt on the ground, knocking his head: \"Mother, your son is unfilial and made you worry.\"","The family's attention had originally all been on Mo Jiuye. With Mo Jinnian's kneeling, they were suddenly at a bit of a loss.","It was still Sixth Sister-in-Law who reacted the fastest. With one look she recognized her husband.","\"Husband, is it really you?\"","As Sixth Sister-in-Law spoke, she had already thrown herself into Mo Jinnian's arms, clinging tightly to his arm as tears streamed down her face.","The instant Mo Jinnian saw his wife, his heart was filled with complex emotions.","The two people he wronged the most over these years were his mother and his wife.","Seeing his wife now, she had gotten darker and thinner. She was dressed in ordinary commoner's clothes with no makeup on her face at all. Her whole being looked several years older.","No wonder, which young woman who loses her husband early can live well?","\"Xue'er, it's been hard on you these years.\"","As Mo Jinnian spoke, he had already pulled his wife into his embrace. Husband and wife held each other tightly as they wept.","When Old Lady Mo saw her son, her body shook from the excitement.","\"Jinnian, is it really you?\"","Mo Jinnian held his wife as he crawled forward a few steps closer to Old Lady Mo and heavily knocked his head to the ground.","\"Mother, it's your son, your unfilial son.\"","Old Lady Mo could no longer hold back the surging tide of tears. She went forward and pulled Mo Jinnian up.","\"As long as you're alive, it's so good that Mother can see you again in this lifetime.\"","Inside the carriage, Fourth Elder Brother and Seventh Elder Brother heard the voices outside. Their hearts were anxious but their mobility was restricted so they couldn't immediately come out and reunite with the family.","Mo Xiuyan could only summon his full strength to shout loudly from inside the carriage: \"Mother, Seventh younger brother and I are here too.\"","Fourth Sister-in-Law, who had been standing to the side watching Sixth Elder Brother and Sixth Sister-in-Law's reunion, was secretly extremely envious. She even thought for a moment that she was having auditory hallucinations when she suddenly heard this extremely familiar voice.","\"Third Sister-in-Law, did you hear that voice too? It sounds a lot like my husband.\" Fourth Sister-in-Law asked Third Sister-in-Law as she pulled on her arm.","Of course Third Sister-in-Law heard this voice. She also felt it was a bit unreal, but she was much more rational than Fourth Sister-in-Law.","\"Fourth younger Sister-in-Law, that voice does sound a bit like Fourth Elder Brother.\"","Mo Chuhan reacted the fastest. Hearing the voice his first reaction was to rush to the carriage and fling the door open. What he saw inside were two emaciated figures.","He was stunned in place.","At this time, Mo Jiuye also walked over.","\"Eighth elder brother, my trip to the Southern Border this time yielded quite a bountiful harvest. I found three elder brothers, but Fourth and Seventh elder brother's physical condition isn't great.\"","Without Mo Jiuye needing to say, just looking at how skinny they were, barely making it home and unable to get out of the carriage, of course they weren't well.","\"Fourth elder brother, Seventh elder brother, how did your bodies become so pitiful?\"","When he himself had been saved by Ninth Younger Sister-in-Law, although he had become a bit thin and weak, that was because Nanrui had deliberately starved him. Other than that there was nothing seriously wrong with his body.","The current state of these two elder brothers could simply be described as miserable.","Fourth Elder Brother was even worse off than Seventh Elder Brother. Seventh Elder Brother could at least prop himself up with some effort when he saw Mo Chuhan come over. But Fourth Elder Brother showed no intention of moving at all.","\"Fourth elder brother, Seventh elder brother, it's so good that you're alive.\" When Mo Chuhan spoke, his eyes glowed red as he struggled to keep the tears from falling.","At this time Old Lady Mo was also being supported by Mo Jinnian as they came to the front of the carriage. The others followed closely behind.","When Fourth Sister-in-Law and Seventh Sister-in-Law heard from Mo Jinnian that their husbands were still alive, the two were so agitated they could barely stand. Their sisters-in-law supported them as they came to the carriage.","Old Lady Mo walked at the front. She was the first to see her two sons who were skin and bones.","\"Xiuyan, Yuanze, how did you become like this? How exactly did they torture you...\"","As Old Lady Mo spoke, she simply couldn't go on. Both sons were born from ten months in her womb. To see them become like this now, how could she, as their mother, bear it?","Old Lady Mo wept bitterly. The women also cried. Especially Fourth Sister-in-Law and Seventh Sister-in-Law, upon seeing their husbands' miserable states their hearts were bleeding.","Since the Old Lady was in front, constrained by proper etiquette, the two did not step forward and could only stand on tiptoes to check on their husbands.","\"Husband, is it really you?\" Fourth Sister-in-Law barely managed to get out a complete sentence.","Hearing her voice, Old Lady Mo quickly made way for her daughters-in-law.","Fourth Sister-in-Law and Seventh Sister-in-Law hurriedly ran up.","Seeing their husbands up close made them choke up even more.","\"Hus...husband...as long as you're alive that's good enough. I'm willing to serve you for a lifetime.\" What Seventh Sister-in-Law said was sincere. As long as someone was around, even if he couldn't move as freely as before, she was willing.","Moreover, now they were earning plenty of silver from making dolls with Ninth Younger Sister-in-Law. She had no issue providing for her husband.","The silver Fourth Sister-in-Law's maternal family gave her when she left the capital was still with her. She rarely was willing to part with a penny. But having taken one look at her husband, she immediately went to find He Zhiran.","When she got to He Zhiran, Fourth Sister-in-Law moved to kneel. He Zhiran reacted extremely quickly to stop her.","\"Fourth Sister-in-Law, speak slowly if you have something to say. We sisters-in-law don't need to stand on ceremony.\"","Fourth Sister-in-Law choked up for a long time before taking out a money pouch from her bosom and handing it to her.","\"Ninth Younger Sister, Fourth Sister-in-Law knows your medical skills are extraordinary. Use all of this silver to buy medicine, do everything you can to heal Fourth Elder Brother.\"","He Zhiran knew that aside from taking the initiative to cover some expenses while traveling, ever since leaving the capital Fourth Sister-in-Law had not been willing to part with the silver her maternal family gifted her for anything else."]},{"number":291,"title":"Chapter 291: I'll do what I can to help.","paragraphs":["Later, she followed her ninth sister-in-law in making dolls and saved some money. Perhaps she felt that since she had no husband and no descendants, she would keep this silver for her old age.","In a frugal manner, Fourth Sister-in-law handed over all the silver to her, to be used for her husband's treatment, showing how deep her affection was for Fourth Brother.","As he watched his wife's actions in the carriage, Fourth Brother, this tough man, couldn't help but feel tears welling up in his eyes.","At this moment, he deeply regretted himself, realizing that he had become a burden to his wife upon returning home.","However, he was completely unable to move his body, unable to even comfort his wife.","He Zhiran quickly supported Fourth Sister-in-law, while returning the purse to her hand.","\"Fourth Sister-in-law, rest assured, we are all family. I will do my best to treat Fourth Brother's injuries.\"","Mo Xiuyan's injuries were too severe, and He Zhiran didn't dare to make any absolute promises in front of so many people. In case they encountered any difficulties that couldn't be solved, it would only give everyone false hope.","Fourth Sister-in-law felt somewhat reassured by what Ninth Sister-in-law said. She firmly believed that with Ninth Sister-in-law's medical skills, she would definitely be able to cure her husband's illness.","On the side of the carriage, the five sons of the Mo family, Mo Xiuyan and Mo Yuance, were carried into the house.","Fourth Sister-in-law and Seventh Sister-in-law immediately followed. Since their own husbands had suffered such serious injuries, they wanted to ensure they had a comfortable resting place.","They took out all the quilts and made a thick bedding, then went out to heat up the kang stove, making the room even warmer.","Old Lady Mo had just shed tears of joy. Now that she saw her two injured sons settled down, she took Mo Jiuye and Mo Jinnian with her and went to the main hall.","\"Jiuye, was your trip to the Southern Frontier dangerous? I'm sure it must have been,\" she asked.","Indeed, it was somewhat dangerous, but Mo Jiuye didn't plan to explain it too clearly and worry the elderly.","\"It was fine. We first went to Si Meng Mountain Villa and found Fourth Brother in a secret room there.\"","Upon hearing that Mo Xiuyan was found in Si Meng Mountain Villa, Mo Yunfeng immediately stood up.","\"Jiuye, did you say Fourth Brother was found in Si Meng Mountain Villa?\"","Thinking of this, Mo Yunfeng clearly felt regret. He was the first one to find Si Meng Mountain Villa. But he didn't discover any secret rooms, which resulted in his Fourth Brother suffering for even more days.","If he had been more careful, if he had found where Fourth Brother was earlier, perhaps Fourth Brother's condition would have been better.","Mo Jiuye understood Mo Yunfeng's thoughts. He and Ruan Ruan personally went down that dry well. If it weren't for Ruan Ruan's help, he probably wouldn't have been able to enter smoothly.","In that place filled with poisonous substances and gu insects, even if Mo Yunfeng went, not only would he not have been able to rescue Fourth Brother successfully, he might have ended up trapping himself.","\"Yunfeng, don't blame yourself. Fourth Brother was locked in a secret room underground. If I hadn't accidentally triggered a mechanism, I wouldn't have discovered it either.\"","Seeing that Mo Yunfeng still wanted to say something, Old Lady Mo raised her hand to stop him.","\"Yunfeng, sit down first and listen to Jiuye talk about what happened during their trip to the Southern Frontier.\"","Since the matriarch had spoken, even if Mo Yunfeng had a lot to say, he could only obediently keep quiet.","Mo Jiuye continued his narration, \"Fourth Brother fell off a cliff while being chased by soldiers from Southern Xinjiang, resulting in both his legs being broken. Even if he was cursed, the other party couldn't control him to do anything, which is why he was imprisoned there.\"","Upon hearing that her son fell off a cliff and broke both his legs, Old Lady Mo couldn't contain her grief.","\"Jiuye, are you saying that your Fourth Brother will be paralyzed from now on?\"","Her son... Why did fate take such a turn? After finally reuniting with his family, his body became like this.","Seeing her mother-in-law heartbroken, Mo Jiuye quickly comforted her, \"Mother, Ranran said she will find a way to cure Fourth Brother.\"","Old Lady Mo nodded repeatedly, \"Ranran's medical skills are excellent. I believe she will be able to heal your Fourth Brother.\"","She had witnessed Mo Xiuyan's condition herself, especially upon hearing about his broken legs. As a military family member, she knew very well about this type of injury. Most soldiers who had broken bones on the battlefield couldn't be completely cured, and even if they were, they would be left disabled.","Moreover, Mo Xiuyan had been injured for so many years. Even if Jiuer's daughter-in-law had exceptional medical skills, it was probably impossible to fully heal him.","She couldn't express her true feelings in front of everyone. As an elder, if even she lost faith, wouldn't the children feel even more hopeless?","Mo Jiuye continued his narrative, briefly recounting the process of finding Sixth Brother and Seventh Brother while skirting the main issue.","Finally, when he mentioned killing the Emperor of Southern Xinjiang and hanging his head at the highest pass, envy shimmered in the eyes of all the men of the Mo family present.","The Mo family had fought for the prosperity of Da Shun and suffered many hidden losses at the hands of the people from Southern Xinjiang.","Especially their father, the late Duke Mo Qing, who died on the battlefield. The Southern Xinjiang Emperor ordered his head to be hung high on the city walls as a display.","Now, they finally had a day of revenge. May the spirit of their father find solace.","No one in the Mo family expected that their late father was still alive in this world. What Mo Jiuye said next shocked the entire family.","\"Mother, during my journey to Southern Xinjiang, I discovered a massive secret.\"","\"What secret? Ninth Brother, please tell us, don't keep us in suspense.\" Mo Chuhan, being impatient by nature, hurriedly urged him when he mentioned a secret.","\"I found out that Father and our older brothers are most likely not buried in the tombs of the Mo family.\" Mo Jiuye said slowly.","Now, not only his older brothers but even Old Lady Mo couldn't remain calm.","\"Jiuye, are you serious about this?\" As for how Mo Jiuye discovered that the people buried in the tombs were not members of the Mo family, Old Lady Mo no longer had the heart to ask. At this moment, she was most concerned about the outcome.","\"If Father and our older brothers are alive, where are they?\" This question was one that Mo Jiuye couldn't answer definitively at the moment.","Both he and He Zhiran felt that they couldn't speak too firmly until they found the people they were looking for.","\"Based on the clues, Father and our older brothers are most likely in the western region. Unfortunately, we missed the opportunity twice when encountering Mr. Simeng.\" Mo Jiuye's words made Mo Yunfeng slam the table in excitement.","Based on the account of Mother about the past events, combined with the investigation of Ninth Brother, Mr. Simeng is undoubtedly the person who persecuted the men of the Mo family.","Mo Chuhan also stood up and said, \"I will request leave from the yamen tomorrow and go to the western region to find out their whereabouts.\"","Fifth Brother, who had been silent all this time, stood up and patted Mo Chuhan's shoulder.","\"Little Eighth Brother, we need to discuss this matter carefully. Besides, with so many brothers in the family, you don't need to take leave.\"","Mo Chuhan knew that Fifth Brother was more thoughtful than him. He glanced at Mother, who had been silent all along, and sat back in his seat, feeling disgruntled.","Everyone else also looked at Old Lady Mo and Mo Jiuye. Old Lady Mo was the elder of the family, so her words naturally carried weight. Moreover, Ninth Brother and Ninth Sister now supported the entire Mo family. Furthermore, the credit for finding the lost men belonged to Ninth Brother and Ninth Sister, so they naturally had to listen to their opinions."]},{"number":292,"title":"Chapter 292: My husband took good care of me on the road.","paragraphs":["Old Lady Mo sorted out her thoughts for a moment, and looked at Mo Jiuye: \"Jiuye, what do you think about this matter?\"","She had long seen that on the surface, it was the Ninth Son and his wife who found the other sons, but the one who really had the ability was the Ninth Son's wife. By asking Mo Jiuye, it was equivalent to indirectly asking He Zhiran.","Even though there were only mother and son in the room at the moment, Mo Jiuye's words could completely represent He Zhiran.","Mo Jiuye was a little embarrassed at the moment. He knew that in the face of Mr. Si Meng, He Zhiran would have to be present in order to be of help. Finding his father and brothers could help undo the Gu poison as soon as possible. However, He Zhiran was currently pregnant, and he absolutely could not let her take such risks.","\"Mother, He Zhiran is currently pregnant, so I plan to go to the Western Regions alone.\"","\"Is this true?\" When Old Lady Mo heard the news that the Ninth Daughter-in-Law was pregnant, she couldn't even express the excitement in her heart.","The so-called \"ice and fire dual heavens\" feeling was probably like this. She had just heard that the old Duke and two sons were still alive, and she was happy in her heart. However, soon it was replaced by a surge of inexplicable anxiety.","Now hearing again that the daughter-in-law was pregnant, she was so happy that tears streamed down her face.","Mo Jiuye knew that his mother would be happy to hear this news. He had been back for so long, and finally he could make the old lady happy.","\"Mother, it's true. He Zhiran is already two months pregnant.\"","After confirming the news, Old Lady Mo could no longer sit still.","\"The bumps along the way must have been hard on her. Let mother go take a look.\"","As Old Lady Mo spoke, she had already stood up, leaving her several sons who also had happy expressions on their faces behind.","He Zhiran had indeed suffered a lot along the way, especially since she had recently developed morning sickness. She had no appetite when looking at anything, making her look somewhat weak all over.","Lan Er and Yu Er already knew she was pregnant. The two had taken care of the pregnant Fourth Princess before, so they were not unfamiliar with this.","They knew He Zhiran had a bumpy ride all the way, and must have been uncomfortable all over, so they stayed by her side to take care of her.","At the moment, the two had already laid out the bedding to let He Zhiran lie down and rest first.","Lan Er even took the initiative to go to the kitchen to boil hot water to help wipe her face.","He Zhiran felt that Lan Er and Yu Er were very thoughtful. Her face felt much more relaxed after being wiped with the hot towel. Just as she was feeling a little drowsy, there was a knock at the door.","Yu Er opened the door and saw that it was Old Lady Mo coming over. She hurriedly bowed politely.","Mo Jiuye had just briefly explained about meeting the Fourth Princess, so she had some understanding of the two unfamiliar faces, knowing they were both people around the Fourth Princess. She nodded slightly, then walked straight to He Zhiran.","Seeing her mother-in-law coming, He Zhiran wanted to get up, but was pressed down by Old Lady Mo with one hand.","\"Lie down, pregnancy is tiring in itself, plus you rushed such a long way by boat and carriage.\"","\"Mother, you already know?\"","Old Lady Mo smiled and sat down next to her, \"I just heard Jiuye say it. This boy really should have mentioned such a big thing earlier.\"","This was the first time He Zhiran had seen her mother-in-law smile so happily. It was evident how eagerly she had been waiting for a grandson.","\"Mother, I'm fine. My husband took good care of me on the road.\"","At this time, Mo Jiuye also followed along. This was also the first time he had seen his old mother act so anxiously.","\"Mother, I will take good care of He Zhiran from now on. Just wait to hold your big fat grandson!\"","Seeing her son's silly appearance, Old Lady Mo couldn't help laughing. \"Alright, Mother will wait to help you take care of the baby.\"","When Mo's sons heard that the Ninth Younger Sister-in-Law was pregnant, they were equally delighted.","However, it was not appropriate for those elder brothers to come over and visit. Each went back to call their own wives over.","The sisters-in-law came over one after another when they heard the news. In addition to joy on their faces, there was also envy, without the slightest hint of jealousy. This showed how pure their dispositions were.","Especially those sisters-in-law who had found their husbands again, they all subconsciously lowered their heads to look at their own flat bellies.","This was because He Zhiran had not explicitly mentioned the fact that they were infertile due to being poisoned.","The sisters-in-law were still very puzzled. In the past when their husbands were away campaigning in the capital for years, that was one thing. But in recent months, being with their husbands day and night, why was there no sign of pregnancy?","Now that the antidote Pei Pi had been found to help the sisters-in-law detoxify, He Zhiran no longer intended to continue concealing it. After discussing it with Old Lady Mo, she told them the truth.","The sisters-in-law were somewhat unable to accept the fact that after being married for many years without children, it turned out to be the fault of Empress Dashun when they heard they had been poisoned.","The Second Sister-in-Law had lived with her husband the longest after marrying into the Mo family. She had seen countless doctors and drank stomachs full of bitter medicine for this reason, yet still failed to conceive successfully. It turned out it was all because of the poisoning by the Empress.","\"It's really too much, what offense did our Mo family commit against her that she would treat us this way, depriving us of the right to be mothers.\"","Although the other sisters-in-law did not speak out in righteous indignation like the Second Sister-in-Law, they also clenched their fists tightly, showing the anger in their hearts.","The reason why He Zhiran did not tell the truth after discovering they were poisoned was that she did not want to add unnecessary troubles to the sisters-in-law.","Now it was different. She had found the Pei Pi that could help make the antidote for the sisters-in-law. After detoxification, she would slowly help them recuperate. And the elder brothers had also been found one after another, so children would come sooner or later.","Moreover, although the present days were somewhat arduous, there was none of the deceit and scheming of the capital. The sisters-in-law liked it too. In the future, with children around, they would have no regrets in this life.","\"Sisters-in-law, don't worry. My husband and I went to the Southern Border this time and found the medicinal materials to help detoxify you. In the next few days I will make the antidote for you to take. You must make every effort afterwards to give birth to more nephews and nieces for me.\"","If it were in the past, the sisters-in-law would definitely have been shy hearing He Zhiran tell them to make more effort.","At the moment, they couldn't care less about embarrassment, focusing all their attention on the antidote.","The Eighth Sister-in-Law was one of the earliest to reunite with her husband. She excitedly went up and grabbed He Zhiran's hand.","\"Ninth Younger Sister-in-Law, can our poison really be cured?\"","He Zhiran smiled and patted the Eighth Sister-in-Law's hand. \"Eighth Sister-in-Law, don't worry, this poison can definitely be cured.\"","\"That's wonderful, Ninth Younger Sister-in-Law. You don't know how much I want to have my own child.\" The Eighth Sister-in-Law was already crying with joy.","The other sisters-in-law had the same feelings.","Back then, when they heard that their husbands had died in battle, they had completely lost hope for the future.","Without their husbands, and no children around, they were destined to grow old alone.","Some sisters-in-law even felt despair, and had once thought of ending their lives when hearing that their husbands had died in battle.","Now it was completely different. Their dead husbands had come back to life, and they might have their own children in the future. The sisters-in-law suddenly had great hopes for the future.","Moreover, although the present days were somewhat arduous, there was none of the deceit and scheming of the capital that they liked. In the future, with children around, they would have no regrets in this life."]},{"number":293,"title":"Chapter 293: Both men and women add blood to the Mohist School","paragraphs":["Although He Zhiran had not yet been completely assimilated by the thinking of ancients, she could understand a woman's thirst to become a mother.","To reassure her sisters-in-law, she promised, \"Sisters-in-law, rest assured, I will strive to produce the antidote in these next few days and administer it to everyone.\"","Eighth Sister-in-Law excitedly grabbed her again.","\"Ninth Younger Sister-in-Law, once our poison is cured, can we have our own children?\"","He Zhiran took the opportunity to check Eighth Sister-in-Law's pulse. Her pulse was no different from Sixth Sister-in-Law's, and everything else seemed normal. This meant that Eighth Sister-in-Law herself had no issues. If she had not been poisoned, she would have had children long ago.","Therefore, she replied with great certainty:","\"Eighth Sister-in-Law, once the poison is cured and you recuperate for a period of time, you will be able to have your own children.\"","Upon hearing He Zhiran’s words, Eighth Sister-in-Law wept tears of joy, “Wonderful, as long as we can give birth, whether boy or girl, it will be adding bloodlines to the Mo family.”","Seeing this, the other sisters-in-law who had found their husbands also came up one after another to ask He Zhiran to check their pulses.","After checking each of them, He Zhiran informed them that there were no issues with any of their healths, and they would have children sooner or later.","Eldest Sister-in-Law and Second Sister-in-Law looked upon this scene with envy, truly hoping their own husbands could come back alive, even if they were paralyzed in bed like Fourth and Seventh Younger Brothers for the rest of their lives. They would be willing to take care of them.","As for children, Eldest Sister-in-Law and Second Sister-in-Law did not dare to hope for too much. After all, among the sisters-in-law, they were the oldest and had been poisoned the longest.","Their only wish now was for their husbands to return safely.","Seeing the sisters-in-law rushing up to He Zhiran to get their pulses checked regardless, Old Lady Mo quickly scolded, afraid that He Zhiran would get tired and affect the fetus in her belly,","“You few stop crowding around to watch the fun. Ninth Younger Sister has said she can cure it, so she definitely can. Right now she needs more rest. Everyone should disperse if you have nothing to do, just go about your business.”","Reminded by their mother-in-law, the sisters-in-law realized they had indeed been somewhat rude.","Ninth Younger Sister had just gotten pregnant and endured a long journey by boat and carriage. They had originally come over intending to show care, but instead ended up asking Ninth Younger Sister to check their pulses.","The sisters-in-law were clearly somewhat embarrassed. They quickly came up to say some reassuring words before dispersing one by one.","After all the daughters-in-law left, Old Lady Mo gave some more instructions to He Zhiran before leaving as well.","With everyone gone, only Lan Er and Yu Er remained in the room. The two of them seemed to have already acknowledged He Zhiran as their future mistress, not leaving her side for a moment after arriving at the Mo family home.","He Zhiran knew these two maids were loyal. Having them by her side to serve her was indeed comforting. However, it would be inconvenient when she needed to enter her personal space.","Moreover, as a modern military officer, she was simply not used to being waited on constantly like this.","\"Lan Er, Yu Er, the Mo family nowadays is just an ordinary farming household. We no longer have those rules of wealthy households. You two can relax a bit more around here. There's no need to keep following me all day.\"","Hearing her say this, Lan Er became a little uncertain in her heart.","\"Ninth Lady, it was you and Ninth Master who saved us initially. We are your people now. Especially since you are pregnant now, you naturally need people around to care for you. If there is anything wrong with how we behave, you can point it out. Yu Er and I will surely amend according to your wishes.\"","She assumed Ninth Lady found them not thoughtful enough in their service, hence was disgruntled with them.","If this was truly so, they would not know how to live in the Mo family in the future.","He Zhiran knew Lan Er had misunderstood her meaning. Regardless, she did not plan to beat around the bush to explain. She directly voiced out her thoughts,","\"Don't misunderstand. If I was unhappy with you two, I would not have brought you back with me. From when we were exiled until now, I've been used to relying on myself to get by. This goes the same for the rest of the Mo family. We have always depended on our own labor for self-sufficiency. In the future, you don't have to keep following at my side all the time.","The womenfolk in the family all have things in their hands to do. You can go find Eldest Sister-in-Law and ask her arrange tasks for you. Of course, if I have need for anything here, I will still call for you two.\"","Having grown up navigating danger with Fourth Princess since a young age, Lan Er thought differently than normal people.","She could understand Ninth Lady's meaning. Ultimately, it was that Ninth Lady did not wish for her and Yu Er to remain by her side attending to her.","It was understandable. Before her last breath, Fourth Princess had wanted to entrust them to Ninth Master. Although they harbored no such intentions, as Ninth Master's wife, it was inevitable she would overthink when seeing them all the time.","Lan Er walked forward a few steps and knelt to solemnly vow,","\"Ninth Lady, I, Lan Er, hereby swear I harbor absolutely no improper thoughts toward Ninth Master. If I go back on my word, may heaven strike me down with five thunders.\"","Seeing Lan Er act this way, Yu Er also knelt down to swear an oath and make a wish.","He Zhiran looked at the two's actions and rubbed her temples helplessly.","Forget whether Lan Er and Yu Er harbored such thoughts, Mo Jiuye would never have ideas like that himself. Even if these two frolicked before him all day, he would not be swayed.","For some reason, He Zhiran simply had such faith in Mo Jiuye, believing he would never do anything to betray her.","Even if she was wrong about the man and Mo Jiuye did end up fickle, so what?","She, He Zhiran had her own abilities and money. The national treasuries of Great Shun and Southern Frontier were in her hands. She had her own flesh and blood. And she had the gold fingers given by the transmigration god.","With so much at her disposal, no matter where she was, she could make a thriving life for herself and had utterly no need to worry about such matters.","Although she held no concerns, things still had to be clarified since Lan Er and Yu Er would be staying here for some time.","\"You've misunderstood my meaning. I already said it very clearly back when I brought you two out. In the Mo family, we do not support freeloaders. If you want a good life, you have to work for it yourself.","As for you two, you’re already of age to be married. If there are suitable matches, I will certainly help arrange.\"","He Zhiran was one to worry over others. When Liang Hao and the others came over earlier, she had considered that they were following the Mo family, so they could not possibly remain single all their lives.","If suitable girls came up, she intended to help keep an eye out.","She had such plans since bringing Lan Er and Yu Er back, but interactions with them so far had been limited. She still needed to understand their personalities better before making any decisions.","Hence He Zhiran did not hurry to bring up the matter of marriage, as she was still observing their conduct.","Even if Lan Er's thoughts diverged greatly from He Zhiran's, her words were stated plainly. If Lan Er still could not understand, she would have to be an idiot.","Lan Er shuffled forward on her knees a few steps and sincerely spoke, \"Ninth Lady, Yu Er's and my lives were saved by you and Ninth Master. By rights, we should obey all your arrangements. It is just, we only wish that when the day comes Fourth Princess' great revenge is accomplished, during offerings of incense we can notify her. Once this matter ends, we will have no more regrets for our whole lives. As for things like marrying off, we harbor no such thoughts.\""]},{"number":294,"title":"Chapter 294: The South Pearl You Want has been found.","paragraphs":["He Zhiran knew that the two of them were still in grief at the moment. She had just mentioned it in the hope that they would have a clear direction for the future.","If they really did not want to, He Zhiran would not force them.","\"I will respect your thoughts, and I also hope you can understand my meaning. You have also seen the environment of the Mo family. Now it is just an ordinary farming household. The family does not need any servants. It is good for everyone to work together.\"","Lan Er nodded repeatedly: \"Ninth Madam, don't worry. We will definitely work hard.\"","He Zhiran raised her hand to the two of them: \"You can both get up now. From now on, just speak, no need to keep kneeling down.\"","Hearing this, Lan Er obediently pulled Yu Er up to her feet.","\"Ninth Madam, rest assured, we will try our best to get used to life here, and will never become a burden to the Mo family.\"","Lan Er's attitude made He Zhiran very satisfied. She waved her hand at the two of them: \"I want to rest for a while. If there is nothing, do not come to disturb me. As for your residence, go find sister-in-law to arrange it. There are still a few empty houses in the family.\"","After Lan Er and Yu Er bowed, they turned and left.","The room was left with only He Zhiran. It was still daytime, and she was pregnant, so the whole family was very concerned about her. She could not guarantee that no one would come over again later.","Therefore, she only used her mind to enter the space and take a look.","At the moment, what she cared most about was the black Southern Pearl.","At that time in the private treasury of the Emperor of Southern Frontier, she had taken many things, but she and Mo Jiuye did not have time to check them out.","Now that she finally had free time and was not very tired, it was a good time to take a look.","He Zhiran's consciousness wandered back and forth among those items, and saw several small boxes opened one by one.","As those small boxes were opened, it suddenly gave her a feeling of having her eyes opened wide.","Of course, the black Southern Pearl was also there.","In addition, there were also two fist-sized Night Pearls and a palm-sized jade Buddha statue.","The most striking thing was not these, but a dark red Southern Pearl.","Compared with the black one, the dark red Southern Pearl was quite rare. She had only heard people mention it, and had not heard of any place where it was treasured.","Now, a dark red Southern Pearl the size of a chicken egg appeared brightly before her eyes. He Zhiran's first thought was that she had struck it rich.","Although she was already very rich, who would dislike having too much money that it was troublesome?","Not to mention that dark red Southern Pearl, any one of those other items taken out alone was a priceless treasure that could rival the black Southern Pearl.","He Zhiran used her mind to store these things separately. She would contact Little Collector later.","There was also the Dan Pi to detoxify her sisters-in-law. This was a very complete Dan Pi. Making eight doses of the antidote would be enough.","Since she had already promised her sisters-in-law, she was going to take action as soon as possible.","The antidote required many medicinal materials, in addition to Dan Pi. Others could be purchased from the Taobao Mall.","She prepared all the medicines completely according to the prescription, then directly made them into pills in the medical room container.","It took a few hours to make the pills. He Zhiran simply opened the Taobao Treasure app to contact Little Collector.","[Are you there? I found the Southern Pearl you wanted.]","Very soon, Little Collector responded.","[Found it?]","He Zhiran: [Fortunately not in vain.]","As she spoke, she took a picture of the Southern Pearl with the product upload function and sent it to Little Collector to see.","Little Collector: [Yes, this is the black Southern Pearl, exactly the same as the one that was lost.]","He Zhiran: [How do you know it's exactly the same?]","Little Collector marked a spot on the original photo with a red line and sent it to her.","[Look here, if you look closely, it bulges out a little.]","He Zhiran picked up the Southern Pearl and looked closely. The spot marked by Little Collector did have a not very obvious bulge.","It seemed that the Southern Pearl that Little Collector had lost was indeed a product of this era.","She suddenly had an idea.","[If this Southern Pearl gets into your hands, the person who stole the Southern Pearl will surely not have it anymore. You can use this clue to find the thief.]","Hearing this, Little Collector's eyes suddenly lit up.","[Your idea is good. I will contact the relevant personnel to pay more attention and find the thief.]","At this point, He Zhiran also had a doubt. She had sold so many ancient calligraphy and paintings on Taobao, and these things were unique.","She wondered if modern collectors of these antiques would lose their artifacts?","If this was true, she could no longer sell these antiques casually. Would this not disrupt modern law and order?","Thinking of these, He Zhiran asked about it.","[The Da Shun antiques I sold before are all unique pieces. I wonder if there are any lost treasures among the collections of people over there?]","Little Collector: [You can rest assured about this. Historical records show that due to frequent wars, almost no antiques from the Da Shun Dynasty and surrounding smaller countries were able to be passed down.","That Southern Pearl is just one of them. Its high price is partly due to the value of the treasure itself, but mainly because it is a product of the Da Shun era and has high collectible value.]","I see, if it was really her selling an item that caused someone in modern times to lose one, then she could no longer sell these antiques casually, otherwise it would disrupt modern law and order.","[So you mean that the goods I sold to you before did not cause any problems, right?]","Little Collector: [That's right. Most of the Da Shun era antiques have not been passed down, so the antiques I bought from you are very precious.]","Hearing Little Collector say this, He Zhiran was relieved. Even so, she did not dare to be as careless as before.","In case the antiques she sold appeared in modern times and disrupted order, it would not be good.","[If you are a professional antique dealer, I hope we can cooperate long-term. Let me show you the antiques I have, and if there are no issues, I can list them for sale. How about that?","Even if you don't buy them yourself, just help me determine if they are okay to sell.]","She hoped that the antiques she sold would not run into such problems.","Little Collector: [No problem. As long as I can turnover the capital, I can buy all your antiques.]","He Zhiran: [That is unnecessary. You just need to help me see if they are suitable for sale.]","She did not want to disrupt modern antique collecting or take advantage of anyone.","Especially Little Collector. For this trip to Southern Frontier, he had helped her obtain so much fuel oil. She would not go back on her word in doing business. Even though she had helped him get the black Southern Pearl, she was still going to list it for sale to him, and not mix personal favors into it.","Of course, she could also sell some good things to Little Collector at a low price to compensate for his favor.","For example, the few good things she had just picked out were absolute treasures in modern times."]},{"number":295,"title":"Chapter 295: Eight Pills","paragraphs":["Little Collector did not have enough money on hand for that black nanzhu, but since He Zhiran had said so, he did not insist on showing off.","\"Alright, I'll listen to you. Let me know if you need anything.\"","After discussing the main points, He Zhiran listed the black nanzhu for sale.","Taobao only appraised the black nanzhu at 20 million yuan, probably because the nanzhu was an antique of Da Shun, so Little Collector had a higher price over there.","The 20 million yuan was the reserve price given by Taobao. He Zhiran did not intend to increase the price at all, and directly listed it in the store at the price of 20 million yuan.","She was not worried that someone would snap up the nanzhu after it was listed. After all, something so expensive, anyone who wanted to buy it would have to weigh it carefully.","After the product was listed, He Zhiran immediately notified Little Collector.","Little Collector had already started preparing the money when he heard from He Zhiran that she had gotten the black nanzhu.","The funds he could mobilize at the moment only amounted to 50 million yuan. If it was not enough, he might have to embarrass himself and discuss installment payments with the other party.","As a result, when he saw the listing price, his first feeling was that his eyes were blurred. The other party only sold him the nanzhu for 20 million.","To prevent being snatched by others, Little Collector didn't think too much about it. He paid immediately to buy it.","After receiving the item, he sent He Zhiran a message.","\"Did you deliberately sell this item to me at a low price?\"","Seeing this message, He Zhiran felt somewhat amused.","Because she was not greedy, all the items she listed for sale were based on the lowest price estimated by Taobao. Even though she knew the value of this nanzhu in modern times, she did not want to raise the price when sitting on the ground.","She did not have much business sense. In her previous life, she only thought about protecting her family and country and saving the dying. Now that she had crossed over to ancient times, her concept of money had not become much thicker either. It was fine as long as it was enough to spend.","\"My prices here are all normal.\"","Little Collector was deeply moved. The moral character of this crosser was too good. She had helped him so much without asking anything in return from him.","No wonder she could be chosen by the crossing god. With such moral character and values, she would be fine wherever she went.","Little Collector did not want to say too much. He remembered this favor.","\"In the future, you can let me take a look at the items before you list them. I will give you tips if there are any issues.\"","With a modern antique dealer to help, He Zhiran was more than willing.","\"Okay, nice to cooperate with you in the future.\"","Little Collector had received the black nanzhu by now, and was absolutely overjoyed. He was going to immediately look for clues about the theft and bid He Zhiran goodbye before hastily going offline.","After He Zhiran sorted out the new items in her space again, the antidote had been successfully produced.","Not more or less, there were exactly eight pills, one for each of the eight sisters-in-law.","After they took the antidote, then carefully conditioned themselves for about a year, there would be no problems at all.","After getting the pills, He Zhiran did not go to give them to her sisters-in-law immediately. After all, these antidotes were not openly produced. Bringing them out now would surely lead to questions about this and that.","She just waited for Mo Jiuye to go into the city at some point, using the excuse of purchasing some medicinal materials to bring back, and then she could justify producing the antidote.","The most difficult matter at the moment was that there were still dozens of Mo Family's former subordinates in the space.","He Zhiran had drawn some of their blood for testing and obtained the same results.","They carried at least dozens of poisons in their bodies, and these poisons were basically in a mutually antagonistic state. However, dozens of mutually inhibiting poisons aggregated together naturally numbed their consciousness and even changed many of their own functions.","The most obvious was that they would not die even if they did not eat for a lifetime.","This baffled He Zhiran. Even in the medical age of the later generations with highly developed medicine, a clear explanation could not be made for such a situation.","Not only that, after they turned into human medicine slaves, they would obey the driving force of the person with the special worm in them.","Judging from this, the only way to find a way to deal with the poisons in their bodies was to start from the dead worm.","That worm was obviously raised with medicine, and the efficacy in the worm's body had a restraining effect on these human medicine slaves.","He Zhiran looked at the clock on the wall. There was still some time before dinner. She simply took out the worm for research.","The best way to study was to use medical equipment to extract everything, medicines and poisons, from the worm.","After an hour of testing, He Zhiran found that there was only one poison in the worm's body.","She was also seeing this poison for the first time. To confirm, she flipped through some books about poisons.","The final result was that the poison in the worm's body, in simple terms, was a kind of material that could absorb physique and absorb hundreds of poisons.","At the same time, this absorbent material medicine could also become a panacea for solving hundreds of poisons.","It seemed that this could explain what was going on.","The absorbent physique of the worm could attract those human medicine slaves.","As long as the operator of the parent worm kept manipulating Mo Jinnian all the time, those human medicine slaves would naturally obey his commands.","There were too many kinds of poisons in those human medicine slaves. Rash detoxification might trigger other poisons to spread in their bodies, which would be like casting off new troubles after getting rid of the old ones. Not only would it be impossible to save them, but it would also accelerate their death.","The only way was to use the dead worm and extract all the efficacy from the worm's body, and then combine it with other medicines to detoxify.","This was a very complicated matter.","It was already extremely difficult just to extract the medicines from such a tiny worm, and the resulting extracts would be pitifully little. They would also need to be combined with hundreds of other medicines for processing.","From the current look, those human medicine slaves only had this one chance for detoxification. He Zhiran did not dare to be careless at all.","Although she had already figured out the approach to deal with the poisons in those slaves' bodies in general, she did not dare to take action rashly.","This matter had to be done at the safest time, otherwise even a little deviation would ruin the previous efforts, not to mention taking the lives of so many people.","Although she could not immediately detoxify those people for the moment, He Zhiran felt that her harvest this time was not small.","At least she had figured out the direction for detoxification. Over the next few days, as long as she studied it carefully, she should be able to save those people.","Seeing that it was about time, she recalled her consciousness from the space.","Mo Jiuye thought she was asleep and had been sitting by her side to keep watch. Seeing her wake up, he stepped up to support her up to sit.","\"Ranran, did you rest well?\"","How could He Zhiran have rested?","\"I did not rest. Just now my consciousness was in the space. I gave the nanzhu to Little Collector and also checked their bodies for those subordinates."]},{"number":296,"title":"Chapter 296: I can't believe I got a nice wife like you.","paragraphs":["He Zhiran saw that Mo Jiuye was tired after working hard for so many days without properly resting after returning home, and felt distressed as he helped massage her shoulders.","\"Now that you're pregnant, you shouldn't overexert yourself. If there's anything that needs doing in the future, let me handle it.\"","What he meant was that even if he didn't understand medicine, he could still follow instructions. This way, his wife would feel a bit more relaxed.","While enjoying her husband's thoughtfulness, He Zhiran said, \"I've basically figured out the situations of those poisoned guards. I'm just waiting for a good chance to detoxify them.\"","Mo Jiuye was anxious to detoxify his subordinates, but was even more concerned about his wife.","\"There's no rush with this matter. Wait until you've rested well and feel better before doing anything.\"","He Zhiran knew he had been quite worried about her throughout the journey, and had felt very guilty the whole time.","\"I'm feeling alright now, much more relaxed than when we were traveling. After a good night's sleep tonight, I'll be fine tomorrow.","Also, I've finished making the antidotes for my sisters-in-law too. I'll find an opportunity to deliver them.\"","The more Mo Jiuye listened, the more distressed he felt. He had thought his wife was sleeping in the room and didn't even dare disturb her. But who knew that in just an afternoon, she had done so many things, and every task was for the Mo Family's benefit.","He gently pulled her into his embrace and gently patted her back.","\"Ranran, I, Mo Jiuye, do not know what virtues or abilities I possess that allowed me to marry such a good wife as you.\"","\"We're all one family. And now that I'm carrying your child, isn't it a bit distant of you to stand on ceremony with me?\" Seeing Mo Jiuye get emotional, He Zhiran didn't know how to respond.","Mo Jiuye hugged her and nodded. \"Mm, I won't stand on ceremony with you.\"","...You've given me the most precious thing a woman has, and are even willing bear children for me. I will spend my whole life pampering you to make up for it.","These were Mo Jiuye's inner thoughts, but he didn't say them aloud to avoid his wife accusing him of being distant again.","The two of them just held each other, neither willing to be the first to let go.","At this moment, the door was rapped on inopportunely.","\"Ninth brother, ninth sister-in-law, have you rested well? It's time for dinner.\"","Hearing eighth sister-in-law's voice, Mo Jiuye reluctantly released his wife...","After dinner, He Zhiran went to check on Mo Xiuyan and Mo Yuanze's conditions before going back to rest.","That night, she could finally comfortably rest inside her space.","After being away in Nanjiang for so long, this was He Zhiran's first time sleeping so soundly. She woke up early the next morning.","She and Mo Jiuye were in no hurry to leave the space. Instead, they studied again the antidote for detoxifying those poisoned guards.","In addition to the medicinal essence extracted from the gu worm, He Zhiran still needed to purchase other medicinal materials from Taobao Treasure.","What surprised her was that one very common medicinal material was not being sold in Taobao Treasure.","Moreover, this medicinal herb had been passed down from the West in later generations, so it would definitely not be found in the Da Shun Dynasty.","This gave He Zhiran a headache.","As she sat holding her phone pondering, the avatar of Little Collector shook a few times.","He Zhiran decisively tapped open the chat box to check.","[I'm truly very grateful to you this time. Not only did you resolve my urgent problem, you also successfully caught the thief.]","He Zhiran was currently worried about the issue of medicinal materials. She only briefly registered the good news brought by Little Collector.","[I'm glad it's resolved.]","Seeing her response less enthusiastic than usual, Little Collector asked, [Did something come up over there?]","It's said that pregnant women lose their edge for three years. And He Zhiran had only just gotten pregnant, so her mind wasn't as sharp.","Seeing Little Collector's inquiry, she suddenly slapped her forehead.","There was a modern person right here. How could she have not thought of asking him for help?","[I urgently need a medicinal material called crane bamboo. Back when I was in the modern times it was very commonly seen. I just searched all over Taobao Treasure but couldn't find any. It would be best if you could help me get some. Of course, I would provide adequate compensation.]","Judging by Little Collector's occupation, he wasn't lacking in money. But she had plenty of nice things that could certainly satisfy him.","Little Collector: [You might not know, but over ten days ago crane bamboo was explicitly banned from sale. They said the mercury content in crane bamboo is too high and extremely harmful to the human body.]","[I see, no wonder I can't buy any on Taobao Treasure. Do you have a way to get your hands on it?] He Zhiran already knew earlier that crane bamboo contained some bad components. But its efficacy was something no other medicinal herb could compare to.","For instance, mercury can reduce lead. Those poisoned guards had very high lead levels in their bodies after testing. Therefore, crane bamboo was essential to counteract it.","Little Collector: [No problem. I have a friend in the medicinal materials business. After the crane bamboo ban, he secretly kept some stock. I can help you get it from him!]","[Wonderful, please help me acquire the crane bamboo as soon as possible. I'll give you a nice surprise too.] He Zhiran happily replied.","As long as she could get the crane bamboo, she could start configuring the antidote.","Closing her phone, He Zhiran and Mo Jiuye washed up and left the space together with their buns.","She had gotten used to getting up early to help her family prepare breakfast with her sisters-in-law. Today was no exception as she headed straight for the kitchen.","But she had just entered when eldest sister-in-law chased her back out.","\"Ninth sister-in-law, just focus on nurturing the fetus from now on. Leave the cooking to us.\"","Second sister-in-law also chimed in, \"That's right. From now on, you're not allowed in here anymore. Giving birth to a big fat son for the Mo family is most important.\"","The sisters-in-law were even more adamant than each other, leaving He Zhiran no choice but to return to her room.","Just like that, days passed where food and clothing came without her lifting a finger. After three days, Mo Jiuye finally finished arranging the household affairs and used the excuse of taking her along into the city.","The purpose of their trip to Yun City was nothing more than to pave the way for the antidotes for her sisters-in-law. There was no real business to handle.","The previous mule cart had been switched out for a stately horse carriage. The carriage slowly made its way through Yun City's streets.","They had just entered a prosperous commercial area when the carriage was forced to stop.","He Zhiran opened the carriage door and looked outside while asking, \"What happened?\"","Mo Jiuye pointed at the crowd ahead.","\"It looks like there's a fight happening over there.\"","A fight?","Meng Huaining had already brought such good order to Yun City. And with eighth brother's iron fist, who still dared make trouble openly fighting?","Out of curiosity, He Zhiran wanted to go take a look at the front.","Knowing his obstruction would be futile, Mo Jiuye hurriedly tethered the carriage at the roadside and came over protectively.","There were no small number of onlookers. The circle they formed was quite large. From the gaps, one could see the situation inside.","A ragged man was being dragged out of the circle by his hair in the grip of two thuggish figures, who kept cursing and swearing.","\"You worthless self-selling slave, you actually dared try to run away. I'll make you regret even being alive!\"","As he spoke, the thug's leather whip lashed fiercely across that person."]},{"number":297,"title":"Chapter 297: Mind your own Business.","paragraphs":["That person struggled desperately, mumbling some unclear words to argue.","\"You're talking nonsense. You took advantage of my drunkenness to force me to press my handprint on the contract to sell myself. I'm going to report this to the magistrate to arbitrate fairly for me.\"","If that person didn't have disheveled hair, He Zhiran and Mo Jiuye wouldn't have recognized him. But when he started talking, his voice was quite familiar.","The two looked at each other.","\"Is it Hu Cong?\" He Zhiran wanted to confirm his guess.","Mo Jiuye nodded, \"It's him.\"","According to reason, Mo Jiuye was not the kind of person who liked to meddle in other people's business. But he quite approved of Hu Cong's character, especially since he and the Mo Family were fellow sufferers.","Meeting this kind of thing on the street, he would intervene no matter what.","Mo Jiuye sent his wife to a place a little further away from the crowd, then stepped in front of the two thugs.","\"Stop it.\"","At his shout, the two thugs who were still swaggering there were stunned on the spot.","However, they quickly reacted. After carefully looking over the person blocking their way, he was just a handsome farmer. The two didn't take him seriously at all.","The thug with slightly darker skin impatiently whipped at Mo Jiuye.","\"Get lost. Don't meddle in other people's business here.\"","He thought a whip would be enough to frighten away the blocker. But when he swung his whip, it was grabbed by the opponent.","What's more, Mo Jiuye used a little force and sent the thug flying to the side of the road along with the whip.","This action caused the onlookers to exclaim involuntarily.","Ordinary people had seen people being beaten at most like what those two thugs did to Hu Cong. Where had they seen someone able to swing another person away just by grabbing his whip?","Stunned for a moment, the crowd was completely agitated.","Some even cheered in a low voice, \"Well played!\" It showed how unpopular those thugs were.","Mo Jiuye paid no attention to the spectators' discussion and strode towards Hu Cong.","The remaining thug still held Hu Cong by the hair. Seeing Mo Jiuye coming over, he was so scared that he didn't even think to let go and run away. He was lifted aside by Mo Jiuye like a little chicken.","As Hu Cong's body relaxed, he slumped to the ground instantly. But he didn't forget to look at his lifesaver's appearance.","\"Master Mo the Ninth?\"","\"It's me. Elder Hu, why were you bullied by these people?\" Mo Jiuye asked.","When asked, Hu Cong was obviously a little angry. He pointed at those two thugs, \"They are from the pier shipping firm. A few days ago, I went there to help people repair ships. They said I snatched their business and had to hand over the silver I earned.","I didn't agree, so they sent people to burn down my house, then forced me to sign a contract to sell myself so that I could only repair ships for their shipping firm in the future.","I took the opportunity to escape when they were not paying attention and was going to report this to the authorities. But I was caught by them on the way...\"","The thug who was thrown away by Mo Jiuye just now walked back with his whole body in pain. Although he was a little afraid of Mo Jiuye, he was still aggressive towards Hu Cong.","\"Hu Cong, don't forget your status. Your contract is now in our hands. If you don't know the right thing to do, beware of suffering.\"","After speaking, he looked at Mo Jiuye again. His attitude was completely different from how he treated Hu Cong.","\"And... and you, I advise you not to meddle too much. Be careful or Master Liu will make sure you can't stay in Yuncheng.\"","Facing such a bluffer, Mo Jiuye didn't even bother to give him a glance.","\"Big talker.\" Mo Jiuye said as he had already helped Hu Cong up.","Although he didn't take those two thugs seriously, it was still best to let the government resolve this kind of thing.","\"Elder Hu, let's go to the government now.\"","Relying on Mo Jiuye's support, Hu Cong got up with difficulty and followed him, preparing to leave.","Seeing this, the two thugs nervously stood in front of Mo Jiuye.","\"We have his contract in our hands. If you forcibly take him away, we can also report this to the authorities.\"","Mo Jiuye glanced obliquely at them, restraining his urge to hit them, \"Then you report to your official and I report to mine.\"","The two thugs had already experienced Mo Jiuye's prowess. Seeing that he was taking the man away just like that, they didn't dare to stop him. After exchanging glances, they fled towards the pier quickly.","Mo Jiuye supported Hu Cong to He Zhiran. He let He Zhiran sit in the carriage while he supported Hu Cong and sat outside with him. The carriage slowly drove towards the county government.","Recently, Meng Huaining hadn't been to the Mo Family. He was just troubled by the matter of Yuncheng Shipping Firm.","He had been secretly sending people to investigate evidence of the shipping firm's illegal activities. Today, he finally got some clues. He was about to take action to arrest the bosses of the shipping firm in one fell swoop.","At this moment, an officer came to report that someone was staging a protest at the entrance by beating drums and shouting grievances.","Meng Huaining was a diligent and caring official. Even if he was busy with things at hand, he would not delay justice for the common people.","Thanks to his integrity and diligence, the lives of Yuncheng commoners were getting better day by day. Obviously, those kinds of bullying men and women had almost disappeared.","His yamen had also become peaceful for a period of time.","Earlier, during the New Year, he had received a letter from his family strongly approving his intention to marry the young lady from the Mo Family. If it wasn't for the tricky matter of the shipping firm, he would have wanted to hang out at the Mo Family long ago to become familiar with Mo Hanying.","Meng Huaining brought several officers to the lobby. Unexpectedly, the one staging the protest turned out to be the Mo Jiuye couple. As for the one accompanying them, he didn't know him.","Seeing his future brother-in-law, Meng Huaining couldn't stay still.","He didn't care too much about the rules, and hurried out from behind his desk.","\"Brother Mo the Ninth, Sister-in-Law, what happened?\"","Looking at this scene, Hu Cong kept cursing inwardly.","In his many years as an official in the imperial capital, he had watched and participated in hearings in court halls. This was the first time he saw an official take the initiative to come out and ask questions. Even if they were acquaintances, it shouldn't be so exciting...","The Mo Jiuye couple were familiar with Meng Huaining so they didn't think too much about it.","Mo Jiuye pointed to Hu Cong beside him, \"This is Hu Cong, the former Vice Minister of the Ministry of Public Works who, like the Mo Family, was exiled here. He has a grievance to complain.\"","Only then did Meng Huaining carefully look over Hu Cong.","Hu Cong's wretched state at the moment couldn't be described in words. It would be fair to say that he looked like a beggar standing here.","Meng Huaining was not the kind of person who only looked at the surface. Although he hadn't seen Hu Cong before, he had heard his elders mention that this person was ingenious and skilled with his hands.","As for why Hu Cong was exiled to the northwest, he didn't probe too much into it. After all, it was indisputable that Emperor Shunwu was muddle-headed, and losing talents like Hu Cong was a loss for the court.","\"Elder Hu, please tell this official what happened.\"","Although Hu Cong looked disheveled, he still retained the grace of a scholar.","He respectfully saluted Meng Huaining neither humbly nor arrogantly, \"This commoner has already been dismissed and exiled. County magistrate, it would be better to address me by my name.\""]},{"number":298,"title":"Chapter 298: Thank you for standing up for the people.","paragraphs":["Shortly after, Hu Cong recounted in detail to Meng Huaining what had happened to him.","After listening, Meng Huaining slammed the alarm bell violently.","\"In the eyes of those boat gang people, there really isn't a shred of royal law.\"","Regarding Hu Cong's matter, Meng Huaining did not intend to inquire too much, because in the evidence he had in hand, there was a lot that was similar, and the evidence was conclusive.","Hu Cong's matter could be handled together with the evidence he had collected.","Meng Huaining called the attendant to bring Mo Chuhan over. It was said that the head of the boat gang was a master of martial arts. Sending those attendants who only knew some boxing skills would be at a disadvantage.","Not long after, Mo Chuhan, who was patrolling outside, was brought back.","In front of Mo Jiuye and his wife, Meng Huaining directly ordered Mo Chuhan to lead twenty attendants to rush to the boat gang and be sure to arrest the head of the boat gang.","Mo Chuhan left with the people. What Meng Huaining had to do now was to wait.","He greeted Mo Jiuye and his wife as well as Hu Cong to chat in the back hall, sent someone to fetch hot water for Hu Cong to wash away the filth on his body, and found a set of clean clothes for him to change into.","When Hu Cong came back after changing his clothes, he was like a different person.","The kind of scholarly temperament he inherently had was undeniable.","Meng Huaining asked casually, \"Master Hu, don't be impatient. After the people from the boat gang are arrested and brought to justice, this official will definitely destroy your deed of sale, and give you corresponding compensation from their confiscated property.\"","Hu Cong stood up gratefully and bowed: \"Thank you, sir, for standing up for me.\"","Meng Huaining waved his hand to indicate that he should not stand on ceremony.","Mo Jiuye was also very concerned about Hu Cong's situation: \"Older brother Hu, now that your house has been burnt down, do you have a suitable place to live?\"","Hu Cong shook his head helplessly: \"I don't want to go back to the fishing village anymore, and I don't want to fish anymore. I might as well find another village to be an authentic farmer.\"","When she heard that Hu Cong wanted to be a farmer, He Zhiran suddenly had some thoughts.","She had heard from Mo Jiuye that Hu Cong was the number one craftsman in Datong. It was just that he had always been low-key, and after arriving in the northwest, he had never publicized his talents.","Such a talented person, not to mention in ancient times, even in modern times, would be like a top-level engineer.","She and Mo Jiuye had bought so many abandoned houses and land in Xiling Village, not only to build houses for their family to live in, but also to build some small workshops.","The workshops would inevitably need some advanced tools. Although she could buy such tools on Taobao, they would definitely not see the light of day.","It would be different with Hu Cong there. She could provide some blueprints and then ask Hu Cong to help make them so that they could be used openly and completely solve her troubles.","In addition, she personally felt that Hu Cong was a man of great talent, and it would be a pity if he continued to be buried.","\"Since Older Brother Hu doesn't plan to go back to the fishing village, would you consider going to Xiling Village to be Mo family's neighbor? After all, we are all from the capital city. Living closer would allow us to take care of each other.\"","Mo Jiuye immediately saw what was on his wife's mind and helped persuade: \"The villagers of Xiling Village are very simple, and there is a lot of farmland there. It happens that we are about to build houses right away. If Older Brother Hu doesn't mind, you can join us.\"","After being taken away by the boat gang, Hu Cong had already had the idea of feeling hopeless about life. He thought his life was over like this.","He didn't expect that after escaping from the boat gang, he would be rescued by Mo Jiuye. He had just mentioned his plans for the future on a whim without any detailed plans.","What's more, he didn't have a penny in his pocket at the moment, not even a place to stay.","If what the county magistrate said was true, he would be able to get some compensation from the boat gang. At that time, he could indeed consider going to Xiling Village to be Mo family’s neighbor.","\"I have no objection to this, it's just that...\"","When he spoke, Hu Cong's eyes couldn't help glancing at Meng Huaining, hoping to get confirmation from him that he would be able to get compensation from the boat gang.","Unexpectedly, Meng Huaining did not look at him, but stared blankly at the tea in his hand.","Even if Hu Cong didn't say so, Mo Jiuye could clearly understand his current predicament.","\"Older Brother Hu doesn't have to worry too much. I can lend you some silver first to settle down in Xiling Village.\"","Hu Cong didn’t have a penny in his pocket. Now was not the time to pretend to decline courteously.","\"Since that’s the case, Hu will not stand on ceremony with Master Mo. If I’m fortunate enough to get compensation from the boat gang, I will return it immediately. If not, I also have skills. As long as you give me some time, I will definitely be able to pay back the silver.\"","Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran had the resources of two national treasuries in their hands. How could they care about a little money?","The reason they were willing to help Hu Cong was purely because they valued his skills and character.","It could be said that both were indispensable.","\"Older Brother Hu doesn't have to consider too much. Just settle down in Xiling Village.\"","Hu Cong's matter was temporarily arranged. After some casual chat, He Zhiran felt somewhat restless after about half an hour.","Suddenly, an attendant ran in in a panic, even forgetting to knock on the door in his hurry.","\"Sir, bad news! The head of the boat gang knows poison. Just now when Mo Chuhan took us there to arrest them, we couldn't even get into the yard. The few people in front were poisoned and fainted.\"","Upon hearing this, Meng Huaining jumped up.","\"What? You said the head of that boat gang used poison, what about our people?\" What he cared most about now was the lives of his subordinates.","The attendant wiped the sweat from his forehead and continued to report: \"The few brothers walking in front have lost consciousness, and Mo Chuhan is also a little dizzy.\"","Now it was Mo Jiuye's turn to panic.","Eighth Brother had narrowly escaped death. He couldn’t let the villain injure him again.","Moreover, he and He Zhiran had the same thought that for Wucheng, the boat gang could only be regarded as local tyrants. Most of them were just some gangsters.","However, someone who knew how to use poison and dared to use poison against the attendants must be extraordinary among those gangsters.","Through brief analysis, they both determined that the leader of this boat gang was not ordinary.","The situation was urgent. Mo Jiuye got up and said to Meng Huaining, \"Brother Meng, I'm going over there to take a look now.\"","He Zhiran knew that Mo Jiuye was worried about Eighth Brother's safety. He didn't know anything about poisons either. It would be very easy for him to suffer a loss if he rushed over recklessly like this.","She also stood up, \"Husband, take me with you.\"","When He Zhiran spoke, her eyes were extremely determined.","This time, Mo Jiuye didn't even consider rejecting her.","\"No, you're pregnant now. I can't let you take risks.\"","He Zhiran subconsciously glanced at her belly. Indeed, she couldn't be too brave at this time.","After thinking twice, she followed Mo Jiuye out of the county government office gate.","At the street corner where no one was around, she handed Mo Jiuye an invisible anti-poison mask.","This thing was a disposable item and extremely thin. It was a military item in her infirmary that she had used during missions to prevent toxic gases from entering the body."]},{"number":299,"title":"Chapter 299: Somebody in this boat knows how to use drugs.","paragraphs":["He Zhiran knew that although this thing could not prevent others from being poisoned, she could not care about so much at this moment. When Mo Chuhan was in trouble, it was impossible not to let Mo Jiuye go to save him. She could only protect him from being poisoned first, and then take those people to a safe place before treating them in time.","According to the official report just now, Brother Eight had only felt a little dizzy after coming into contact with the toxin. This was enough to show that the poison used by the ship owner was not highly toxic, and there was still time to save him.","Seeing that his wife listened obediently this time, Mo Jiuye felt much more at ease.","He took the anti-poison mask and quickly followed the reporting officer to fly towards the direction of the ship owner, using his lightness skill.","Fortunately, the anti-poison mask was only a simple version, with only a thin layer. It would not be too abrupt for He Zhiran to suddenly take out something like this from her arms.","Mo Jiuye was used to using foreigners as an excuse for these things. If no one asked, then forget it. If someone inquired, he would push it to the foreigners.","Although He Zhiran was unable to follow Mo Jiuye to the scene, she did not dare to stay too far away, after all, the poisoned people needed treatment, and she had to try to reduce the time on the road.","She was settled by Mo Jiuye in a nearby teahouse, and gradually watched him disappear from her sight.","Mo Jiuye was worried about the situation on Brother Eight's side. After settling He Zhiran, he grabbed the official's collar and used his lightness skill to rush towards the direction of the ship owner.","When he arrived at the ship owner's place, the scene was even more serious than when the officer had reported.","Four officials were lying on the ground, their bodies had begun to show slight convulsions. Mo Chuhan was also supported by two people to barely stand still.","Mo Jiuye did not care about the others. He ran to Mo Chuhan first.","\"Brother Eight, how do you feel? Ruan'er is in a nearby teahouse. Let someone take you there first for her to treat you.\"","Mo Chuhan's state was extremely weak. If it wasn't for his firm willpower to support him, I'm afraid he would have collapsed too.","\"I'm fine. Little Nine, there is someone using poison in the ship owner's place. Don't get too close.\"","With one glance, Mo Jiuye could see that Brother Eight was just pretending to be strong. He said to the officials supporting him, \"Take my brother and those officials to the teahouse. Leave this place to me.\"","Seeing that the chief and so many colleagues had been poisoned, the officials no longer had the courage at this moment. Now finally someone was taking charge, so they carried the people away without saying anything more.","He Zhiran was anxiously looking out the window. Not long after, she saw a group of officials carrying unconscious people running towards the direction of the teahouse.","She put down her teacup and walked out.","\"Put them down first and let me take a look.\"","The officials obediently put the people down. Before they could say anything, He Zhiran had already walked up to Brother Eight.","At this moment, Brother Eight had fallen into unconsciousness, and his complexion looked a little pale.","He Zhiran first took his pulse and quickly determined his condition.","This was simply an anesthetic. The efficacy was extremely similar to the anesthetic she had made with the Silver Ring Snake.","It was just that using the Silver Ring Snake's venom to extract anesthetics was a very advanced method. If it wasn't for He Zhiran relying on the advanced medical equipment in her space, I'm afraid she would not be able to complete it either.","Therefore, she could be sure that the anesthetic Brother Eight had ingested was definitely not an extract of the Silver Ring Snake, and the biggest possibility was the Seven Color Frog.","What was worrying was that the toxins of the Seven Color Frog were several times more potent than those of the Silver Ring Snake. Although it was an anesthetic, if the antidote was not administered in time, the toxins would spread to the five viscera as time passed.","To put it bluntly, if this kind of anesthetic stayed in the human body for too long, it would also become a lethal poison. It would just not kill the poisoned person so quickly.","At this time, the officials had already talked to the boss inside the teahouse and asked him to vacate two private rooms for those unconscious colleagues to rest temporarily.","Facing the officials' request, even if the boss was unwilling, he could not refuse.","Mo Chuhan was the head of these officials. Without He Zhiran saying anything, he was directly sent to a separate private room.","Taking advantage of the officials taking care of the other colleagues, He Zhiran quickly extracted some of Mo Chuhan's blood for testing.","Sure enough, the anesthetic Brother Eight had ingested was extracted from the Seven Color Frog.","Since it was the Seven Color Frog, it would be easy to handle.","She and Mo Jiuye had caught so many Seven Color Frogs at the Simeng Mountain Villa, and they were still kept in her space now.","Although the Seven Color Frog was highly toxic, it would also produce a kind of antibody against its own toxins. Therefore, to obtain the antidote, it had to be extracted from the Seven Color Frog itself.","He Zhiran pretended to go to a nearby pharmacy to buy some medicinal materials. Then she borrowed the back kitchen of the pharmacy to brew the antidote, and added the extract from the Seven Color Frog when others were not paying attention.","After the antidote was brewed, she let the officials administer it to everyone. If nothing unexpected happened, people would gradually wake up after about an hour.","...","After seeing Brother Eight being carried away, Mo Jiuye walked straight to the main entrance of the ship owner's place.","The officials who had not been anesthetized hurriedly came up to stop him.","\"Young Master Nine, you can't get close to that door. There will be people throwing poison powder out from inside.\"","Mo Jiuye waved his hand. \"You guys stay farther away. I'll go in alone.\"","As he spoke, he had already put on the anti-poison mask his wife had given him and strode towards the door.","Sure enough, as the official had said, a puff of white powder came rushing at him as soon as he approached the door.","Mo Jiuye ignored it and kicked the closed door open.","A man dressed like someone from the Southern Borderlands inside was staring proudly at the direction of the door.","The door was suddenly kicked open and he was instantly at a loss.","This medicinal powder was carefully prepared by him. No matter who came into contact with it, they would be anesthetized.","Just as the man was puzzled, he looked up to see someone wearing a strange thing standing in front of him.","\"Who...who are you?\"","Seeing this person's outfit, Mo Jiuye first thought to find out about his identity.","\"And who are you?\"","The Southern Borderlands man put one hand into his clothes, seeming to take something out, while also trying to frighten the incoming person with momentum.","\"Humph! I am a poison master from the Southern Borderlands. Get lost if you don't want to die, otherwise I'll make sure you never come back.\"","Mo Jiuye ignored his ugly face and quickly walked up to clamp the arm he had put into his clothes. With some effort, he broke it.","The man from the Southern Borderlands cried out in pain.","\"Ah... you dare to hurt me?\"","As he spoke, his other hand was about to reach into his clothes.","Mo Jiuye knew he was going to use poison against himself. Although his wife had given him this anti-poison mask, he did not want to be careless.","With the same method, he broke his arm.","Seeing things going badly, the man from the Southern Borderlands wanted to escape.","Mo Jiuye took a quick step forward and kicked him to the ground, then shouted outside towards the officials:","\"Tie him up and watch him closely.\"","Although the officials did not follow Mo Jiuye into the ship owner's place, they had seen his actions just now very clearly.","Seeing that this poison user had been injured by Mo Jiuye and would no longer pose any threat to them, they swarmed in like bees and tied the man up tightly.","The commotion just now was quite loud. Reasonably, it should have alerted other people inside the ship owner's place, but no one came."]},{"number":300,"title":"Chapter 300: Yes Man","paragraphs":["This phenomenon was obviously somewhat strange. He stared at the People of Southern Frontier and asked, \"Where are the people on the boat?\"","At this moment, the People of Southern Frontier was still a little distracted. His poison powder had not been sprinkled out before he was injured by someone, and he was also tied up so quickly in five flowers.","Suddenly being asked, he did not react for a while.","Just then, several unaware thugs ran back. As soon as they entered the yard, they were stopped by the officers.","Mo Jiuye's eyes also immediately turned to those thugs.","Among the thugs were the ones who had beaten Hu Cong in the street. Seeing Mo Jiuye, they instinctively wanted to run away, but they had already been controlled by the officers and could only stand still in place, staring at Mo Jiuye in horror.","Mo Jiuye turned his head and asked the thugs, \"Where is your leader?\"","The thugs had already experienced his power before, and now they were still being controlled by the officers. They clearly knew that they were finished.","At this point, behaving better might result in a different ending.","\"He is our leader.\"","When the thug spoke, his eyes had already looked at the People of Southern Frontier.","Hearing this, the officer walked up and kicked the thug heavily.","\"Be honest. How could I not recognize the leader of your boat gang? You still dare to talk nonsense when facing death.\"","The thug felt very wronged by the kick.","\"Official, the little one did not lie. This man came a month ago to our boat gang. The original leader voluntarily gave up his position to him.\"","\"What exactly is going on?\" Mo Jiuye asked.","He was curious why the People of Southern Frontier would come to Yun City's boat gang to become the leader, and this poisonous man made him suspect that his purpose might be related to his own family.","He knew that asking these thugs would not get any results, so his eyes turned to the People of Southern Frontier who was tied up in five flowers.","The eyes of the People of Southern Frontier were obviously a little evasive, but his answer was still righteous.","\"It was because the leader of their boat gang owed me money and mortgaged the boat gang to me.\"","Not to mention Mo Jiuye, even those thugs did not believe it.","The boat gang had been operating in Yun City for more than ten years, and had always done uninsured business. How could it possibly owe others money?","Mo Jiuye sneered, considering that this was not the place to inquire about these things. He ordered the officers to go forward and ask where the original head of the boat gang was.","Although he was not an official, he had just heard Meng Huaining mention it a few times.","Recently, Meng Huaining had been busy collecting evidence of crimes by the head of the boat gang, which were things that happened over the past decade. Even if this People of Southern Frontier had done something illegal, it had only been more than a month after all.","Mo Jiuye guessed that the original head of the boat gang was most likely controlled by this person, and Meng Huaining must interrogate the People of Southern Frontier.","He went forward to grab the People of Southern Frontier and walked out in big steps, while saying to several officers, \"I'll take him to the yamen first.\"","Meng Huaining could interrogate this person, but before that, he wanted to find out what he wanted to know.","Besides, he left his wife alone in the teahouse, and he was not at ease either. He would feel more secure after seeing the person sooner.","In Mo Jiuye's hands, the injured People of Southern Frontier was like a dead dog, with no resistance at all, and was carried all the way to the teahouse by him.","He Zhiran was currently observing the situation of several poisoned people when she heard the officer come to inform that Mo Jiuye had brought back someone.","She hurried out of the teahouse to check. At this time, Mo Jiuye had already thrown the People of Southern Frontier into the corner, intending to ask some questions.","He Zhiran first looked at Mo Jiuye and saw that he had returned unharmed. She was much more at ease immediately, and then looked at the person he had thrown on the ground.","\"Is he the People of Southern Frontier?\"","Mo Jiuye nodded, \"Mm, the poison that hit Eighth Brother was released by him. He also took over and became the leader of the boat gang...\" He told her everything he knew.","What He Zhiran thought of first was the same as Mo Jiuye, which was the origin of this People of Southern Frontier.","\"Who sent you here?\"","Seeing that a woman was asking him questions, the pupils of the People of Southern Frontier shrank instantly, revealing his sinister appearance undoubtedly.","\"As long as you let me go, I will tell everything I know.\"","Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran sneered at the same time. Even ghosts would not believe such words, yet he still dared to say them.","Mo Jiuye walked up and kicked him right on his broken arm.","The People of Southern Frontier screamed in pain again and again, attracting the passing pedestrians to stop and watch.","Seeing this, Mo Jiuye picked up the person again and walked away with He Zhiran.","\"Ranran, let's find a quieter place.\"","The two turned into a small alley. Mo Jiuye threw the man on the ground again.","This time, the People of Southern Frontier was really scared. Just now he thought that there were so many pedestrians passing by on the street, this person would not dare to do anything to him.","But it was different now. The location here was remote. Even if someone killed him, no one would know.","\"Good...good sir, spare my life.\"","Mo Jiuye walked up with an expressionless face and said coldly, \"If you want to live, tell me your origin honestly.\"","Now that his wife was pregnant, he didn't want her to use hypnosis anymore. It was not worth it if she hurt her body for this.","Moreover, the People of Southern Frontier in front of him was obviously a coward. He estimated that he would not need much coercion to make him tell the truth.","As expected, the People of Southern Frontier was a greedy and fearful person. In order to survive, he confessed everything.","\"I am the People of Southern Frontier.\"","\"I know that, say the key points.\" Mo Jiuye was obviously a little impatient.","Seeing his eyes as sharp as blades, the People of Southern Frontier was so frightened that his whole body was wet with sweat. Sweat beads kept flowing down his forehead involuntarily.","But his hands and feet were tied so tightly that he couldn't wipe it off at all.","\"It was my master who sent me here to investigate the situation of Duke Mo's Family in Da Shun.\"","As expected...","Mo Jiuye continued to ask, \"Is your master Mr. Si Meng?\"","\"How...how do you know?\" The People of Southern Frontier seemed to understand something. He stammered and asked, \"Could it be that you are Mo Jiuye?\"","Although he had never seen Mo Jiuye with his own eyes, he had heard people say that the men of the Mo family were handsome, and they also had superb martial arts.","He himself was also a martial artist. He was beaten just now without fighting back at all. A person with such skills in Yun City could only be Mo Jiuye.","Mo Jiuye did not hide it either, \"It's me.\"","Seeing him admit it, the People of Southern Frontier shrank back instinctively in fear.","\"Master...Master Mo, it was an act of helplessness that made me come here. Please spare me this time!\"","Mo Jiuye did not answer his words, but urged, \"If you don't want me to send you on your way personally, then tell me everything I want to know.\"","Fearing that he would be killed if he spoke too slowly, the People of Southern Frontier hurriedly said after Mo Jiuye had finished speaking:","\"My master asked me to come here to find out news about the Mo family and report it to him truthfully.\"","Mo Jiuye had already heard this answer earlier. Seeing that the People of Southern Frontier was beating around the bush for a long time, he simply asked."]}]);
